    {
        "review": "Really happy with this product They hold a charge forever. Sound great. I’ve had more expensive Ear buds and these are better than the Jaybird’s I had for half the price. I’d recommend these. They also have good base and you can adjust the eq to your liking and listening preferences."
    },
    {
        "review": "After more than 3 years of continuous use of these headphones, I have decided to make this review. They are the best I have had to date, and not by spending more will we always be happier. To begin with, the sound is quite good and the bass is not bad at all, but above all the noise cancellation is very good, not recommended if you are going to turn the volume to full and someone is going to scare us by touching us on the shoulder, you are completely isolated. The battery lasts what it really says, 45 hours for the box, about 6/7 hours for each earphone depending on the volume. I have used them almost all my working day with the volume turned up under protective helmets and they have saved my life from monotony and repetition. They resist falls quite well, I have had them fall several times, even on surfaces with dirt and rocks and they have continued to work perfectly. They are water resistant and not just the typical IPX5 (splashes), even if they fall into the sink no water gets into them and they carry on as if nothing had happened. After all this time my only drawback is the box, it has a somewhat fragile hinge and the ideal is to buy a silicone protective case, if it comes with a carabiner to hang it even better, yes, it is worth a third of what the headphones cost. Today I have them in that case because I dropped the box and the hinge broke, but since it has a magnet it stays closed even then and with a case much better. On calls I have noticed a somewhat annoying backfire but it is something recent and it can happen, with music or podcasts it is not noticeable. They capture all the ambient sound so between that and the noise cancellation it is not highly recommended that you talk on the phone with them in the middle of the street because you will shout and the person on the other end of the line will even hear the buzzing of the flies. I would also not recommend them for exercising on the move such as going for a run, it will depend on your hearing, although it comes with ear pads of various sizes. For exercising there are other models that are fixed over the ear and do not fall. The touch controls usually work even with gloves, if they get wet they continue to work but I don't know to what extent because I usually store them when it rains. In short, they are an alternative to other headphones with higher prices and cache but these are not far behind in terms of performance. To listen to music, podcasts or watch videos they are perfect. I recommend them and I have even bought them as a gift. 100% satisfied."
    }
