    {
        "review": "I really like these earbuds. The charging case is compact and looks modern, and the earbuds feature a comfortable design that fits well in the ear. Connecting them is simple, and the sound is quite clear for listening to music, watching videos, or making calls.I also appreciate that they are wireless and easy to carry around. Overall, I think they offer good value for money and are a practical choice for daily use."
    },
    {
        "review": "I like them because they connect easily and quickly, have incredible sound, the volume isn't annoying, they're very comfortable and don't bother you if you want to wear them all day; they adapt very well, the charge lasts a long time, definitely a good buy, good quality and a good price, They are easy to use and very durable. and they're very comfortable."
    },
    {
        "review": "After my Apple Airpods stopped working (loud buzzing that the Apple store said was a known defect but I missed the refund or replace date by two months because, who knew), I decided to save money and try these. They actually last much longer than my Airpods did and are a great replacement. The cut off button on the sides though are sensitive and I frequently accidentally touch and click the button making them cut off, but I just tap and back on again.Also, these cut off my phone calls when their battery is dying and I remove to put back in case and switch the call from airpod audio to phone or speaker on phone, which is the most annoying feature, but I eventually learn to just leave the airpod out and not try to place into case and the call doesn’t drop.Overall for the money these are great, I just suspect the radio frequency is way over legal limit."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m really impressed with these wireless headphones! The sound quality is clear and the noise reduction works really well, especially when I’m listening to music or podcasts. They are lightweight, comfortable to wear, and stay securely in place during workouts. The charging case is also very convenient and easy to carry around. Overall, these are a great pair of headphones for the price and I would definitely recommend them"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought these BX30 sports headphones and I really liked them. They have a very secure fit thanks to the ear hook, so they don't fall off while exercising. They connect fast and I love that the case clearly shows the battery level and the battery lasts a lot. Super recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "They were working fine  for the first few months. One day they would not disconnect so I had to  turn off the device they were connected to to disconnect them, after that they would not connect again no matter what I tried.  Only 20 buck so I guess  I got what I paid for.  update: I was able to connect them again after a week of trying. how? I just kept hitting the disconnect button repeatedly out of frustration and it finally disconnected so I was able to re-pair them. So basically treat them like a toddler with a broken toy , that seemed to work. The next time they did not disconnect until I turned off the device they were connected to but unlike last time I was able to connect them again. they have been ok for the last few days. I will keep you updated if there is any change"
    },
    {
        "review": "I was looking for a pair of headphones that could help block out the noise in my office, and I absolutely love these! They’re comfortable, sleek, and the sound quality is fantastic. I highly recommend them if you’re looking for comfortable headphones for the office, traveling, or even working out.I also really love the battery life. I was able to use them for a long time without having to constantly recharge them, which is a huge plus compared to other headphones I’ve used. Overall, I’m very impressed with this product. Love, love, love!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought these headphones only after a long research and evaluation. Since there are so many on the market, and I didn't want to spend crazy amounts of money, I also found these headphones at a discount, and I took them. I would say excellent purchase. Top quality/price ratio. Convenient because they come with 3 plugs to adjust the size to insert it into the ear! Try it both at home while moving and during a run and never go out! Which many other headphones did! They recharge in a very short time and have a long battery life! Simple but very beautiful design! I highly recommend them, excellent audio and call quality"
    },
    {
        "review": "Hello, before buying this earphone I read the reviews, afterwards I trusted my onion, I admit that the reviews helped me conclude my purchase. I use them when I listen to music in the metro to isolate myself from the noise, or at home. It isolates well from surrounding noise, the sound is clear and the bass too. Easy to pair with the bleutouth 5.3, just activate it and it pairs automatically. The first use when in terms of its great I admit that I made a good purchase at this price the best is that I got them with a coupon of - 20% that's great, without going into too much technical detail in a word I recommend it to youPs: I sent the link to my daughter she bought the same and her companion too. Reception deadline respected with bonus thank you amazon"
    },
    {
        "review": "A very nice headset. I was using the iPhone's wired headset, I bought this one, the sound quality is the same, and another beauty is that it has a long battery life. You can buy it without hesitation. Thanks amazon."
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered these headphones because of the good reviews, but I was doubtful as to whether they were all really genuine. But you can't go wrong on Amazon; if they were junk I would have sent them back. I kept them and even ordered 2 more in pink and black so that there are always some within reach. I've actually been a fan of the Samsung Buds and own one pair of each generation. My Buds Pro 2 are great in themselves, but unfortunately they always slip easily when I go for a walk and with every correction I activate the touch control.So I borrowed the JBL tws 230 from my husband to see if it would work better with a bridge on the headphones.From now on, the JBLs were my companion when walking the dog.I like to listen to podcasts, dance charts and the occasional \"Malle Musik\", but I'm not a sound fanatic.For me, headphones simply have to have a clear sound, fit well and work reliably.My 12-year-old daughter is now getting into that age too I wanted to have such headphones and often borrowed my JBL. However, I didn't see the point of giving her headphones for €80 every now and then and started looking for headphones that had a similar shape. I didn't pay much attention to the technical data, I was concerned with the fit in small ears - she just couldn't fit all the existing Galaxy Buds (which I would have liked to pass on to her) in her ears. So I had to find something similar to JBL at a reasonable price. When the headphones arrived, I was More than pleasantly surprised.The sound is hardly inferior to the two comparison models (at least for my ears).I think that the bass is a bit too \"buzzy\", but my daughter is very happy - which is what counts in the end.And since I listen to podcasts 80% of the time anyway, that hardly bothers me.The noise reduction is absolutely fine.Some people will be bothered by the fact that there are no different levels - that doesn't bother me. I hardly used this function with the other headphones. The running time is absolutely sufficient. They have been in use for 4 days now, were fully charged once at the start and the case still has 98% - so no or hardly any self-discharge. The touch control is absolutely precise and also has a very pleasant confirmation tone. I paid €19.99 for the offer, which I consider to be an absolute bargain and that's why I ordered 2 more. Then my daughter can lose one. 😉"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love them, good sound, good battery life and very nice design and color. I am delighted with them, they are worth it and their price is incredible. Great purchase. I would buy them again"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Good god, what a mouse. I mean, it's not perfect; nothing is. But it's so good.I came from years of the G502 Hero; the grips on it were wearing out. I first decided to try a G502 X, as it was supposed to be an improved version of the Hero, essentially. For $25 more than the Basilisk, it pretty much sucked in my opinion. The only thing I could imagine picking it over the Basilisk for is weight. But if you care that much about weight, there are much lighter mice on the market.---I'll review it as compared to the Hero (and a bit to the X), as that's what I know. They're pretty common, so maybe this will help people out if they're thinking about converting:Initially I wasn't so sure about the grip and the main mouse buttons. The mouse buttons have a rough texture, and I found with my Hero that when my fingers were slightly tacky/damp, they would stick slightly to the surface of the buttons in the same way a clean basketball shoe does to a court (i.e., not \"sticky\", but grippy). I liked that. But after using it for a while, I think it's totally fine and maybe even better.The feet seem the same to me as the G502 X, which is good. They're white PTFE. Very smooth.The scroll wheel is *fantastic*. Like, it's perfect. It seems to control the mode with an electromagnet, so it makes a cool click sound when the computer is restarted and such. And it even has a setting in the software where you can have it tactile by default, but with a quick flick, it switches to free-spin temporarily. Awesome. And when I move the mouse quickly side to side, there is absolutely no play in the wheel. Nothing. That was one of my annoyances with the Hero. The scroll wheel would wobble audibly and tactilely when in free spin mode with even moderately fast mouse movements.The click noise isn't as nice as I expected, but it's totally fine and better than the X (which was super loud and piercing). I'd put it somewhere between the X and the Hero. It's kind of like if someone built the X and then was like, oh, that sucks, and then made adjustments like a sane human. I believe the Basilisk switches are optical (the Hero is mechanical and the X is hybrid mech/optical), and so maybe that's approximately what happened. In short, I think the Hero is a pretty quiet click, and I think the Basilisk is a very standard click. Sounds like what I'd use as a mouse click if I were a foley artist.The Basilisk's weight is listed at 101g, and it feels quite nice. Not hard to control. I'm sure I'll get even better as we go, though. The palm section is actually quite high! Like, even more than the Hero. It feels pretty good so far.The Basilisk's cable is an absolute work of art. I mean, it's perfect. It's got a soft woven sleeve and is not stiff at all. I had the same kind of reaction to it as I did when I got my current massage shower head and found that no, the tube connecting the head to the spigot doesn't actually have to be stiff at all to do its job.The software is slightly annoying because there's a separate program for the lighting and the mouse (though they're styled identically and could ostensibly be packaged in one app). But its functionality is nice. There are 9 RGB zones around the bottom edge of the mouse, plus one on the scroll wheel and the logo under the palm. They seem rather infinitely adjustable. Neat!---Hope this helps somebody!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I used the Razer Mamba Elite for many years and absolutely loved it, so I was hesitant to switch. This mouse was recommended to me as a replacement, and I have been pleasantly surprised. It feels comfortable in the hand, responds quickly, and the customizable buttons and RGB lighting are excellent. The scroll wheel is especially smooth and versatile. Overall, it has been a great change and I am very happy with it."
    },
    {
        "review": "This mouse is just incredibly smooth. Even with its high weight the skates make it super easy to move around and the weight gives it control, resulting in superb aim. The material can make your hands a bit sweaty when death gripping it, but it’s very solid matte surface. You can grip test and throw this mouse across a room without it breaking. The shape this mouse has just fits right in your hand, and the rubber side grips make it super comfortable and easy to use, it’s basically great with any grip type. The skates are super glidey and quiet even when under the weight of this chunker of a mouse. It’s better for bigger hands of course, it’s harder to use with smaller hands but it’s doable. The scroll wheel is the best of any mouse, even the Logitech g502. It has a setting in the software where it can be a tactile scroll wheel when scrolling slowly, but becomes a freely spinning wheel when flicked fast. You can even switch between spinny wheel mode and tactile mode with the click of a button. I loved this mouse so much I upgraded to the wireless version, and I wasn’t sacrificing much leaving wired because the battery life was great on that one. 10/10 mouse."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve genuinely liked using the Razer Basilisk V3. The first thing I noticed was how comfortable it felt. Some mice are fine for about 20 minutes and then they start feeling like a weirdly shaped brick. This mouse has been much better for longer use, whether I’m gaming or just clicking around online doing whatever nonsense I got distracted by.What I like most is that it feels like someone actually thought about how a hand works. The buttons are responsive, the movement is smooth, and the scroll wheel feels so nice that it almost made reading comment sections worth it. Almost. While this mouse has not been life changing in a dramatic movie soundtrack kind of way, it has changed my expectations enough that going back to a cheaper mouse would feel like using a shopping cart with one bad wheel.Oh, and the customization. I am not out here trying to launch a space mission from my desk, but it is nice being able to set things up in a way that actually fits how I use it. Once everything is dialed in, it just feels easy.Overall, it has been a genuinely solid mouse and one of those upgrades you stop thinking about because it just quietly does its job well. Which, for a mouse, is honestly the dream. It just sits there, minds its business, and makes me slightly more powerful than I probably deserve."
    },
    {
        "review": "Best mouse I've ever used. Every surface is comfortable to touch & adds to its controllability. The RMB & LMB are soft & responsive, and have a quick reset. Easy to hold & thumb rest allows for greater control during long use."
    },
    {
        "review": "To be honest they don't make mice like they used to. I remember a time where you would buy gaming mice and they would last 5 years minimum. Now a days they last a year if you are lucky. So far this mouse has worked pretty good and seems like it is holding up quite fine. I also want to point out I haven't had this for a very long time and I suspect the build quality of the mouse should last a year if this was anything like my old razor mouse.The scroll wheel is pretty solid. I like how responsive it is. I have never seen a mouse scroll wheel quite like this. Scrolling speed is pretty good. Was able to do a lot of jagged movements and noticed the mouse handled it very well in minecraft.Ergonomic of the mouse are probably the best part. I haven't used a non trackball mouse that felt this great in maybe ever. The programmable buttons I haven't used for anything since I literally have nothing to remotely use them for whatsoever.RGB is decent. Not a selling point for me that is a selling point for some people I guess.With that said I am not sure if I can recommend this just because it seems pretty good but the way gaming mice have been going I don't see this lasting more than a year. I remember a time where mice would last like a decade now they break if you look at them the wrong way. I will say the big pro to a gaming mouse is the fact it is meant for gaming. Yes you are paying a lot of money for something that will break within a year but you pretty much have no choice just because these mice have a sensor in them that is significantly way better than most mice."
    },
    {
        "review": "The Razer Basilisk V3 is hands down one of the best gaming mice I've ever used. It's super comfy even during long gaming sessions thanks to its ergonomic design, and the customizable buttons are perfect for both gaming and getting stuff done. The RGB lighting looks awesome, and the HyperScroll wheel is surprisingly handy for switching between precise and fast scrolling.The sensor is super accurate and responsive, and the mouse just glides across my mousepad. I also love how easy it is to customize everything through Razer Synapse. Whether I'm playing FPS games, MMOs, or just browsing, this mouse works perfectly.If you want a top-notch gaming mouse with tons of customization and excellent comfort, the Basilisk V3 is totally worth it. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This mouse is basically the “I’m him” of gaming mice. It’s super comfortable, the buttons feel crisp, and the 26K DPI sensor tracks like it’s reading your mind. The RGB lighting goes full rave mode (in a good way), and the HyperScroll wheel is clutch whether you’re swapping weapons or doom‑scrolling.The 11 programmable buttons give you all the customization you could want, and the whole thing just feels premium. It’s fast, smooth, and honestly makes every other mouse feel a little mid."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good quality"
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm an avid PC user and rarely replace my accessories. My mouse especially was hard to replace, as every top end mouse seems to get lighter and lighter. However, after using the Basilisk V3, I can safely say this mouse has been a perfect upgrade from my 2013 Deathadder. It weighs roughly the same, being on the heavier side for a mouse, and that's perfect for me. It's built great, has a fantastic braided cable which is smooth to the touch, it doesn't catch on corners like the older Razer cables, and the RGB is stellar. I really like the ring of RGB that goes around the base, and it's incredibly easy to edit in Razer Synapse.The mouse is also extremely comfortable. I didn't expect a thumb rest to do much, but I'll honestly miss it if I ever have to upgrade.For the price, you really can't go wrong. This mouse is incredible for its price point and well worth investing in if you like to 'feel' your mouse movements."
    },
    {
        "review": "real razer mouse not a scam works perfectly fine and great quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been using this mouse for about a month now.It's my first gaming mouse.It's lighter than I expected but that does not impair the use at all.The greatest strength is it's smoothness of operation. The cursor glides smoothly with small and large gestures."
    },
    {
        "review": "Deathadder v2 pro broke down so I bought a new one. I generally don't play games, but I often switch DPI on a 4K monitor, so a gaming mouse would be perfect if I could switch between them at hand and have enough buttons to assign a certain amount of macros. Since it was originally a wireless mouse, I was reluctant to switch to a wired mouse, but the thick-looking cable is lighter and softer than I expected, so I don't feel any discomfort when operating the mouse. It has a suitable weight and is easy to grip, so personally, I made the right decision to buy a new one. Since there is one more button, I assigned Alt+F4 (close window) to the backmost button, which I personally find very convenient and use frequently. One negative thing I noticed right after purchasing it (which has already been resolved) is that the scroll wheel feels too light. Even when I turned the deathadder v2 pro, it felt like it was turning one step at a time, but this product spins so lightly that I thought it was almost free, so I thought it was a little strange, but I was a little impressed when I found out that you can change the feel of the wheel mechanically by setting it on the SYNAPSE side. I felt the evolution of the mouse."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’ve owned and tested many gaming mice over the years, and the Logitech G Superstrike X2 is, without question, the best one I’ve ever used. I don’t play competitively—I mostly enjoy adventure games, action titles, and other immersive experiences—but this mouse has made every gaming session more enjoyable. It combines incredible comfort, premium build quality, and features that genuinely stand out.The biggest highlight for me is the haptic switches. They feel amazing, providing a tactile, satisfying click that makes every input feel deliberate and precise. The feedback is unlike anything I’ve experienced on another mouse, adding a level of immersion that you don’t realize you’re missing until you try it. Combined with the outstanding responsiveness, every click feels fast, consistent, and incredibly satisfying.Another thing I absolutely love is how lightweight it is. It glides effortlessly across the mousepad and never feels fatiguing, even after hours of gaming. The shape is comfortable, the weight is perfectly balanced, and it almost feels like an extension of your hand.The wireless connectivity has also been flawless. It’s fast, stable, and completely reliable, with no noticeable latency or dropouts. It truly delivers the freedom of wireless without any of the compromises that used to come with it.Logitech has once again delivered a premium product. From the build quality to the innovative haptic switches, lightweight design, and rock-solid wireless performance, everything about the Superstrike X2 feels refined and thoughtfully engineered. It’s a mouse that makes you appreciate the little details every time you use it.Overall, this is easily the best mouse I’ve ever owned, and I couldn’t recommend it more. Whether you’re a competitive player or, like me, simply want the best possible experience while enjoying your favorite games, the Logitech Superstrike X2 is absolutely worth it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve had this mouse for almost a week now, and I can confidently say it’s hands down the best mouse I’ve ever used. It’s incredibly lightweight, the wireless performance has been flawless, and it just feels high quality overall.I am 35 years old and don't have the best reaction time but this mouse dropped my Human Benchmark reaction time average from 190 ms to around 160 ms. I wasn’t even planning on testing this, but one of my friends told me to try it and see if there was actually a difference. I tested on my old mouse, a Model O, and then back to the Superstrike X2 just to make sure it wasn’t in my head. The difference was still there. Everything just feels quicker and more in control, and the speed and click feel really make a difference.The feeling when you click it is incredibly responsive and smooth. The only thing I can compare it to is clicking an iPhone sleep button.Battery life has been very good also. After about six hours of gameplay, the battery only went from 82% down to 75%, which is impressive for a wireless gaming mouse.Can't recommend this mouse enough to everyone"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using it daily for about a month and a half now. First thing you notice is how insanely light it is, my hand doesn’t get tired even after long sessions.The buttons feel really nice to press. The magnetic analog switches are smooth and the fact that there are basically no loud clicks is actually pretty cool and satisfying. You can adjust the haptic feedback and trigger stops which is a nice touch.It’s comfortable tracks perfectly and the wireless connection has been rock solid. Battery life is good too.No major complaints so far"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Logitech PRO X2 SUPERSTRIKE is easily one of the best gaming mice I’ve used. The first thing you notice is how incredibly lightweight it is—it glides effortlessly, which makes a huge difference during long gaming sessions. The responsiveness is top-tier, and the Lightspeed wireless connection feels just as fast and reliable as a wired mouse.The build quality is excellent, with a clean, minimalist design that looks great on any setup. The clicks feel crisp and precise, and the customizable haptics add a nice touch for those who want to fine-tune their experience. Battery life is also impressive, and the USB-C charging is a welcome upgrade."
    },
    {
        "review": "I gave this mouse 5 stars simply because of the haptic triggers. Ive only ever used the razer viper pro mouse and for my large hands its the only one that fits comfortably. The superstrike is a bit smaller in my hand but nothing that would make me stop using it. Its heavier than the razer and to my surprise I actually like and prefer that. The battery life on the mouse is great. The settings you choose for the haptic triggers does affect battery life but its nothing major. Now the main reason I bought this mouse was for the haptic system it uses and ill be blunt and say its the best thing ever and I hope more companies adapt this. Being able to adjust the actuation points is fantastic. It will take a few days to get used to the sensitivity if you go all the way to one but once youre used to it you'll never want a regular mouse again. Overall I think its a fantastic mouse its a bit spendy but in my opinion the haptic system by itself is worth the price. The only issue i have with this mouse is the side buttons they are extremely squishy they barely click its very unsatisfying I would give the side buttons a half a star."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this mouse for a while now and honestly I’m really impressed. It’s super lightweight and feels very comfortable in hand, even during long gaming sessions. The response time is excellent — everything feels smooth and precise, especially in FPS games.Battery life is also really good, I don’t have to charge it often which is a big plus. The wireless connection is stable with no lag at all.The only small thing is that it might feel a bit too light if you prefer heavier mice, but for me it’s perfect.Overall, definitely worth it if you’re looking for a high-performance wireless gaming mouse."
    },
    {
        "review": "I absolutely loves this mouse. I usually have stuck to only using razer mice in the past. However I made the switch to this one and its honestly so great. I only really have one complaint and the rest is amazing.Pros: Battery life is honestly amazing. Its really quiet because it no longer clicks, its just haptic feedback like the ps5 controller. You can adjust when it actually clicks which is super cool just like a Hall effect keyboard, because it's the same tech. Mouse just feels great and the included grips are nice, but they do take some getting used to as they aren't what I was expecting. However I have come to like them.Cons: It's vey expensive for a mouse, there's a lot of competition and a variety of mice esp way cheaper. The stock skates are absolutely terrible, that's why I changed them jade's and now its perfect. No complaints after that. However for a mouse this expensive, I was hoping for better skates. I also don't really like the scroll wheel, to be fair I do come from razer mice so that might be why I hate it. It also takes some getting used to as the mouse is front heavy because of the switches on the mouse, but I bet you can fix that if you have a powerplay to balance it out.However I have this mouse for 2 months now and I absolutely love it and I wouldn't switch for another. The only thing I would change if you were buying this mouse today is to also order skates so you can replace them. Would be a 5/5 if it weren't for the terrible skates.TL;DR: Great mouse if purchasing, buy skates as well."
    },
    {
        "review": "After just a week of using this mouse, I can confidently say this is the best peripheral purchase I have ever made.I initially wasn't in the market for a new mouse, until my scroll wheel broke on my razer mouse. I decided to just pull the trigger on the X2 Superstrike instead of purchasing another razer mouse.The mouse material feel is excellent, and the wheel is great as well. I've also seen some reviews disliking the skates on the X2 Superstrike, however I personally found them to be great.The haptic feedback mouse click seemed a bit gimmicky before I actually used it. Right off the bat, the mouse click feels incredibly responsive and similar to that of any high quality mouse. You get enough feedback and it doesn't feel that much different from a regular mouse click. But, you also have optionality to adjust a ton of settings, like accuation, feedback strength, etc. For gaming, with the right settings, this genuinely feels amazing, and that's before the performance upgrade. As many other reviewers have noted, it noticeably decreases latency on top of all of this.Another huge perk with this mouse I found, was that it's almost dead silent as well. No more loud clicking!My only critique with the mouse are the side buttons and the size. The side buttons are the only part of the mouse that feel \"cheap\". Because I use the side buttons often in competitive games, I notice it a lot more than probably most people would. I also have large hands, and this is the smallest mouse I have used. I got used to it pretty quick, but the mouse is on the smaller side.Nonetheless, if you are looking to upgrade your mouse and have the money, I would 100% recommend. This feels as impactful as going from a 60hz monitor to a 144hz+."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought it and the mouse had problems"
    },
    {
        "review": "A good mouse, encanto me"
    },
    {
        "review": "Mostly got for the reason that it’s basically silent in terms of clicking the main left and right mouse buttons. When paired with the mousepad Amazon recommends, this combo is great in terms of feels and responsiveness. Also comes with grip tape which has a nice texture but a really strong smell of fake cheap leather.The software is top tier you can customize a bunch of things, I have the haptics for the mouse (the vibration/feeling of when you press down a button) set to almost the lowest possible and it still feels better than any mouse I have used.I haven’t really messed with changing the speed of how fast the button presses down or whatever, but superb mouse although it is a tad overpriced ( kind of reasonable as this is one of if not the only mouse with this technology )"
    },
    {
        "review": "I recently picked up this mouse as my first step into wireless gaming, specifically the Superstrike X2, after using a wired Razer Basilisk V3 for a long time. I’d been thinking about making the switch for a while, and overall I’m glad I did.The main buttons (left and right click) feel excellent — responsive, solid, and satisfying to use. This is clearly where the mouse shines, and it delivers exactly what you’d expect at this price point in terms of core performance.However, the side buttons (the two next to the left click area) are a noticeable weak point. They feel cheap and somewhat out of place, especially when compared to competitors like Razer. Considering the price of this mouse, I expected a higher-quality feel across all buttons, not just the main ones.That said, since the primary clicks and overall performance are what matter most in actual gameplay, I would still recommend this mouse. If you can overlook the side button quality, it’s a strong option for anyone looking to move into wireless gaming.Sorry for the messy mousepad :)"
    },
    {
        "review": "I spent a long time shopping around for the right mouse, and the description of this one immediately caught my attention. What ultimately convinced me was the adjustable haptic feedback.It feels wonderful in the hand, without being overloaded with unnecessary buttons. The scroll wheel feels excellent and reminds me of my old Microsoft Optical mouse, which I used for 22 years.I’m very happy with my choice. I would never go back—I’m definitely keeping it! JFN Quebec, CANADA"
    }
]

