        "review": "I had to find a fast affordable replacement after my cat suddenly decided that my previous mouse was actual prey and absolutely demolished it. This one is a pretty good weight, which will hopefully save this one from an early demise. It goes to sleep fairly quickly to extend the battery life if you're using it wirelessly like I am, but there's no noticeable delay when you move it again and it wakes up. I have arthritis and typically use a palm grip as opposed to a claw grip on the mouse and it fits in my hand perfectly, plus the little grippy side where the thumb sits helps with control pretty well. The RGB default lighting actually matches the setup I have now, so I don't feel the need to change it unless I decide to change my lighting theme for my whole desk, but there's a little program on the redragon website that's pretty easy to set up and change what the buttons do and the lighting if you so choose.RIP old mouse, long live the redragon.Edit: Purchased July 2024 — Currently August 2025. For the past month or so, the mouse battery has been dying faster and faster. In the beginning, I really only had to charge it once a month with VERY heavy, daily use. Now, I've rarely been playing video games, mostly just using my computer for email and school, and I have to charge it at LEAST once a week. It's such a shame, it was such a good mouse. On the bright side, my cat can't knock it off very easily.RIP redragon too, I guess."
