        "review": "So far so good. Will update review if anything changes - have audio interface and few devices plugged in, external hard drive, sd card reader - no issues.For anyone curious about the chipset used, it's VIA Labs:VIA Labs VID_2109 PID_0822 (USB 3.2 hub) Primary 3-port hub + 1 downstream port (USBC)VIA Labs VID_2109 PID_0822 (USB 3.2 hub) Secondary 4-port hub off that downstream port (USBA)VIA Labs VID_2109 PID_2822 (USB 2.1 companion hubs)This was the only information I couldn't find before purchase, and was exactly what I was looking for - previously purchased a Amazon Basics 7 port usb3.1 hub and kept on getting errors in device manager. Seems like they just daisy chained a bunch of crappy hubs together to make it 7 port, and was bottle necked for throughput."
