    {
        "review": "Well worth the money spent. Allows for more usb slots now that newer computers are downsizing the number of slots that they used to come with. No degradation in picture quality through hdmi, doesn't appear to slow down data transfer. Powers on with the computer it attaches to. Plug and play, no driver installation or software. I've only used on Windows computers, but I'm sure if whatever computer has a USB C, it would work. There are slots for charging devices. I bought a lot because there are a lot of employees needing to use it because their hdmi slots are not providing enough power to the output device they are using. They use a SMART board/tv that had a hard time reading the signal from the regular hdmi port. But once plugged into this hub, it had no issues recognizing it and broadcasting a signal."
