[
    {
        "review": "⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Six ports done right — everything works at full spec simultaneouslyBeen through enough USB-C hubs to know that the spec sheet and the real world performance are two different conversations. Hubs that claim 4K HDMI but throttle to 1080p under load, or PD charging that slows to a trickle the moment you plug in a display — these are the failure modes that make hub shopping frustrating. The UGREEN Revodok delivers on every spec simultaneously without compromise.4K HDMI output is clean and stable — no signal dropout, no resolution negotiation on reconnect, just a solid 4K signal from the moment the hub is plugged in. Color accuracy and refresh rate are correct without any manual display configuration needed. Drives a 4K monitor without any of the flickering or handshake issues that plague cheaper hubs.100W PD charging passthrough is the other critical spec and it holds up under real load. Laptop charges at full speed while simultaneously driving the HDMI output and pushing data through the USB ports — no thermal throttling, no charge speed reduction from splitting duties. The hub handles the power budget correctly which is not a given at this price point.Gigabit Ethernet is a legitimate gigabit connection — ran a speed test to confirm throughput matches a direct connection without the bottleneck that USB-C Ethernet adapters sometimes introduce. Stable link with no dropped packets under sustained transfer load.Build quality is classic UGREEN — aluminum housing, tight port tolerances, USB-C connection to the host that seats firmly without wobble. Compact enough for travel without sacrificing the port selection that makes it useful at the desk. Six ports, full spec, no compromises. Highly recommended."
