        "review": "I have a 13-inch MacBook Air, M4, 2025, and I use it for everything: work, watching videos and series, and occasionally gaming. I also regularly attend court hearings and professional meetings through Zoom, Google Meet, and similar platforms, so I cannot afford connection issues.This adapter, especially with its LAN port, has been very useful. It gives me more confidence when attending hearings online because I can rely on a stable wired connection. It also works well while connecting other devices, such as microphones or pen drives, which makes it very versatile.The finish and materials feel solid and high-quality. I used to have a white plastic adapter from another brand, but it ended up changing color with use. This one stays cleaner, looks more professional, and is easier to keep in good condition.It is easy to carry, practical, and very efficient."
    },
    {
        "review": "Works perfectly for my use! I bought one for my Desktop PC when the Ethernet jack wasn't functioning correctly. My Ethernet has had no problems since.I ended up buying another one for my ROG Ally as my old dock was having issues with the screen flickering. After switching to this hub, no more screen flicker! It powers my keyboard, mouse,and displays.A versatile hub for many uses."
    },
    {
        "review": "I had bought this for a new Dell Pro 14 Plus laptop that I use for work in the office and at home. Rather than having to connect power, monitor, LAN cable and D-Link USB 2.0 hub each time I brought the laptop home, I was hoping to have just one connection to deal with. The issues I ran into are: 1) the laptop complained about the power lever coming from the UGREEN hub, saying the laptop would work, but could run slow. So I ended up not using the new hub for power (my laptop has 2 USB-C ports). 2) the mouse dongle appears to have interference with the USB 3.0 ports and I had to continue to use the old D-Link 2.0 to get the dongles away from the YGREEN hub (I daisy chained it). So I now only have two USB-C connections to make, which is better, but not perfect."
    },
    {
        "review": "Many of today's thin laptops don't have LAN ports (holes for plugging in wired LAN), which is a problem when you're working from home or want a stable internet environment. So I purchased this \"UGREEN Revodok 1061\". As a result, I am very satisfied! [Good points] Peace of mind when using wired LAN: Since it supports gigabit, communication is more stable than wireless Wi-Fi, making online meetings and large downloads more comfortable. Abundant ports: With 3 USB 3.0 ports and an HDMI port, you can integrate a mouse, keyboard, external HDD, and external monitor all into one device. Keep your desk clean and easy to carry: If you plug all the cables of your peripherals into this hub, you can simply unplug one Type-C cable from this hub when you take your laptop out. When you get home, just plug in one and you'll be back to your comfortable desk environment, so it's really convenient. It also supports Power Delivery (100W), which is useful because you can charge your PC at the same time. The price is reasonable, and I highly recommend this item to anyone using a thin PC such as a MacBook or Surface."
