[
    {
        "review": "(3 years now I have had this and today is July 12th 2025. I literally love this thing so much I came back yet again to tell you after 3 years it works just as good as the day I originally got it. It is scuffed and scratched, has the remnants of tape and stickers i applied over the years, it has seen much wear, tear, and abuse by me, and works perfectly! ANKER makes great products, but especially nowadays when there is so much cheap garbage out there, everything i have brought by ANKER just works everytime. The only time I have had an issue? Is when I broke something, or dropped it under a car wheel (I actually did this with the first one I bought, not from Amazon, but a few months beforehand, it still worked until I started messing with it to see if it still functions lol), because I tend to be extremely irresponsible with my portable electronics. If you do buy this, and you forget to order a power supply, I bought a 100w power supply from Walmart for it, that is also three years old and works great as well.  If it makes it 5 years, I'll be back to tell you about it. Now, keep reading to see the first review i left awhile ago)This thing is so awesome. I had to come back and write another review first off. You will need a 100 watt power supply to go with it separately just get that out-of-the-way. You can get one at Walmart for fairly cheap. That’s what I did and after about six months, I actually glued the hub permanently to the power supply so they would never be separated now let me tell you how versatile this thing is you can take your iPad plug it into the little USB-C sticking out of the end of it then you could take an HDMI cord from the hub and plug it into your TV. If you have a splitter, you can do it into several TVs or several monitors. It has a microSD card for all your pictures. It has a not as micro a little bigger memory card can’t remember what they’re called but they go in like cameras and stuff SD cards? It reads those two it’s got a USB-C out so you can charge your phone if you have an iPhone and an iPad like I do it connects your iPhone into your iPad together so you can play video games on your phone on your giant screen of your iPad running an HDMI cord to your TV now you’re playing on your phone on your monitor and your TV and your iPad all at the same time and see how awesome I’m saying this is you can plug a keyboard into it and a microphone and a mouse and now your live streaming your gaming on your iPad your monitor your TV your projector I’ve even hooked mine to a projector! I’ve literally spent hours trying to see how many items I could plug into this thing and run at the same time just so I could put it on my YouTube channel and show off and have people give me no props, shake their heads, and say I’ve got way too much free time on my hands. Doesn’t that sound amazing? That could be you. One guy who made fun of me relentlessly in the comment section a week later asked me where I could get one and guess what I told him I could get one for twice the amount that I paid for it and he paid me so I win guess what I do with the money? I bought a midi cord that I plugged into my MPC so I could play music on GarageBand on my phone. Had another cord going from the hub to a monitor where I could watch OBS for studio live streaming as a third cord projected the entire image on a wall, 6 feet across while I produce this music a microphone that I also had plugged it into the hub was recording me freestyle horribly because I cant rap, but all of those magic moments captured on a small SD card also plugged into the hub at the time I just left in the hub and when I was done, all I had to do was unplugged the USB-C from my phone into my computer and transfer all the information over i’ve plugged my GoPro into it from my GoPro. I was able to power a light and a microphone this thing is endless possibilities. Do yourself a favor and get one anchor products are amazing and guess what I’ve stepped on this thing countless times my dog thrown it across the room. It’s fallen downstairs. I dropped a puddle of water put it in a bowl of rice it still works. I should be selling these things man they’re incredible."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this to use with my MacBook for work, and it’s been a really useful all-in-one hub. One of the biggest advantages is not having to carry separate adapters for HDMI, USB devices, and SD cards. It makes it much easier to connect everything I need at my desk or when working away from home.The HDMI connection worked well with an external monitor, and the USB ports have been useful for keyboard/mouse and flash drives. The pass-through charging is also a big plus since it lets me keep my MacBook powered while still expanding the number of ports available. That makes a big difference if your MacBook already has limited ports to begin with.I also like that it’s compact and easy to keep in a laptop bag, so it works well for both a desk setup and travel. It can get a little warm during longer use, but that seems pretty normal for a small hub doing multiple things at once. Overall, this has been a helpful and convenient accessory for turning a MacBook into a more practical work setup."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this years ago but never had the time to review..anywho, this is GREAT! I love allll Anker items and have multiple from power banks to chargers to cables to this. It’s reliable, works great and hasn’t failed me yet. It’s slim so easy to bring with you anywhere."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good hub though the SD card reader not fast does the job. Primarily bought for the power PD through and USB-C connection which perform ok for travel with iPad."
    },
    {
        "review": "What I likePlug-and-play. One USB-C cable in, several ports out. No drivers, no setup, no configuration.HDMI output for plugging into a hotel-room TV or conference projector without an adapter.SD card reader for moving photos off a camera. The microSD reader is a bonus.Two USB-A ports are enough for a mouse, a USB stick, or a card reader I already own.85 W pass-through charging means I can keep my laptop charged through the hub when I have a USB-C charger handy.Lives in the laptop bag and is ready when I travel. It is the kind of accessory that pays for itself the first time you really need it.Compact and light. I forget it is in the bag until I need it.What annoys meNot a daily driver on my home desk. My home computers already have the ports I need, so the hub sits in the bag most of the time.Bus-powered. No battery, no separate power input. I am not trying to power a hungry external device through it, so this is fine, but it is not a “real docking station” with its own power supply.One HDMI output. If I wanted to drive two external monitors, I would need a different hub or a dock with display-multiplication support. The transcript says “second HDMI port,” and this hub gives me one, not two.No Ethernet port. Wireless works almost everywhere I travel, but a wired Ethernet jack would be a real bonus on hotel networks that block Wi-Fi or charge for it.I do not actually use it on my Mac mini. It would work, but I have not built the habit of plugging the mini through the hub. That is a me problem, not an Anker problem.Who it is for, and who should skip itIf you travel with a laptop and need HDMI, an SD card reader, extra USB-A, and the option to charge the laptop through a single cable, this is the right tool. It is small enough to leave in the bag and useful enough to justify its weight.Skip it if you want a full desktop dock with its own power supply, multiple display outputs, Ethernet, and the ability to drive a multi-monitor workstation. That is a different product class, and a single USB-C hub with bus power will not do that job.Skip it if your laptop already has every port you need. The hub is solving a missing-port problem, and if you do not have one, it will just sit in your bag.VerdictThe Anker USB-C 7-in-1 hub is a small, useful travel accessory that lives in my laptop bag and earns its place every time I take a trip. It is not exciting. It is not a daily driver. It is the kind of thing that disappears into your workflow and then you are grateful for it when you need it.Grade: A—if you want a single-cable travel dock for a laptop or Mac mini. Buy the linked listing if your use case matches mine."
    },
    {
        "review": "Highly impressed with the build quality of this hub. All the ports work seamlessly, connection is solid, and it doesn't get overly warm during use. Excellent value for money!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent product as I have come to expect with all Anker products I have purchased, BUT...I attempted to hook up this hub with the external power pass-through configuration to my Dell Latitude 5430 laptop, but the hub uses 15 Watts of power so the Dell-supplied external charger was reported as insufficient for charging.But, there are 2 USB-C ports on the left side of the laptop, so I'll connect the charger directly to one of the USB-C ports and use the other one for data exchange and the HDMI monitor connection.Just a heads-up if you see the same notification like this that I received."
    },
    {
        "review": "As a tech enthusiast and someone who's always on the go, I'm constantly looking for ways to streamline my setup and maximize productivity. The Anker USB-C Hub has become an indispensable tool in my arsenal, transforming my laptop into a versatile workstation wherever I am.Here's why I'm giving it a five-star salute:Connectivity Powerhouse: This compact hub packs a punch with 7 ports: 4K HDMI, 100W Power Delivery, USB-C, 2 USB-A, microSD, and SD card reader. It's like having a mini docking station that fits in the palm of my hand.Crystal-Clear Display: The 4K HDMI port allows me to connect my laptop to an external monitor for a crisp, high-resolution display. It's perfect for presentations, streaming movies, or just expanding my workspace.Blazing-Fast Data Transfer: The USB-C and USB-A ports offer impressive data transfer speeds, making it quick and easy to move files between my devices. No more waiting around for those large files to transfer!Pass-Through Charging: The 100W Power Delivery pass-through charging ensures that my laptop stays powered up while I'm using the hub. This is a lifesaver when I'm working remotely or traveling.Sleek and Portable: The hub's compact and lightweight design makes it incredibly portable. It easily slips into my laptop bag, so I can take it with me wherever I go.A Few Minor Considerations:While I'm extremely happy with the Anker USB-C Hub, there are a couple of minor drawbacks that I've seen mentioned in other reviews:Limited Ethernet: Some users have expressed a desire for an Ethernet port on the hub. While it's not a dealbreaker for me, it's something to consider if you require a wired internet connection.Can Get Warm: A few reviewers have mentioned that the hub can get a bit warm during use, especially when transferring large files or using the HDMI port. I've noticed this as well, but it hasn't caused any performance issues.Overall:Despite these minor points, the Anker USB-C Hub is an excellent addition to any tech enthusiast's arsenal. It's a versatile, reliable, and portable solution that expands the capabilities of your laptop and simplifies your workflow."
