[
    {
        "review": "I've used a lot of inexpensive, no-name USB-C hubs over the years. In my experience, they never quite do everything they claim to do. There always seems to be something that doesn't work correctly, whether it's the video output, charging, or random disconnects.A while back, I replaced the two docking stations I use at home with Plugable products, and for the first time, everything just worked. Because of that, when I decided I wanted a small travel hub to keep in my laptop bag, I wasn't really interested in trying another bargain brand.This is exactly what I was looking for.I use it with my Dell Latitude laptop at work. It gave me an HDMI output for a second monitor, enough USB ports for my keyboard, mouse, and flash drive, and everything worked immediately. No drivers, no troubleshooting, no wondering why one feature wasn't working. It was truly plug and play.I didn't test the pass-through charging because my laptop has a second USB-C port that I use for power, but everything else worked exactly as expected.Compared to my full-size Plugable docking station, this obviously doesn't have nearly as many ports or capabilities. It also costs about one-tenth as much. That's the point. It's small, lightweight, inexpensive, and easy to throw in a laptop bag when I travel.I'm getting to the point where working from a laptop screen all day just isn't enjoyable anymore. This gives me an easy way to connect another monitor and enough USB ports for the peripherals I need without carrying around a bulky dock.At around $20, I think this is an excellent value. If you're looking for a compact travel hub and don't need a full docking station, I don't think there's much more you could ask for."
    },
    {
        "review": "I picked up this Plugable hub to consolidate multiple cables into one connection for my laptop, and the 5-in-1 functionality has genuinely streamlined my desk setup, no more juggling separate adapters for HDMI, USB-A devices, and charging. The 4K@60Hz HDMI output has delivered crisp, smooth video to my external monitor without any lag or resolution downgrade.100W PD charging has been convenient, powering my laptop through the hub itself rather than needing a separate charging cable plugged in alongside everything else. The 3 USB-A data ports have handled my keyboard, mouse, and an external drive simultaneously without any connectivity drops or slow transfer speeds.Build quality feels solid, no overheating during extended use even with multiple devices connected and charging happening at the same time. Compatibility with my MacBook worked exactly as expected, plug and play with no driver installation needed.For anyone wanting to reduce cable clutter and simplify connecting multiple peripherals and displays to a single laptop, this hub has performed reliably and made my daily desk setup noticeably more organized and efficient."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is exactly the kind of hub I want when I only want to bring one thing and trust it to behave. It handles the usual day-to-day tasks without drama, and that matters more to me than chasing big numbers that look nice on a box. The ports all work the way I expected them to, which is honestly the best compliment I can give a hub.I’d call this a medium-duty option rather than something meant to do everything at once. It’s not trying to be a powerhouse, and that’s fine. For me, it feels more like the practical choice you keep around because it is dependable, not because it is flashy. All the ports work as expected. When isolated, the ports work to just under maximum, but the bandwidth limitation is 10Gbps for all ports together.That said, I was a little surprised by that from this brand, since I usually think of them as being on the more premium end. But as an everyday Essentials-style hub, it makes sense. It is the kind of device that quietly does its job, stays out of the way, and works when I need it to. I trust the Plugable brand (I admit I'm a fan and have LOTS of their stuff going back a decade) and I have no problems taking this as my only hub. If it was TB4/5 or USB4, I'd be much happier, but I wouldn't want to pay 4 times more for that capability in this case.Absolutely RECOMMENDED."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am a fan of Plugable products.  This will be my fourth Plugable  hub that I have acquired in the past two years.  It's a solid product.  You get the typical USBC 100W PD port, 5GGPS USB 3.0, USB 2.0, 4k 60HZ HDMI.  When it's connected, you see a small blue LED turn on , I like this small feature, it tells me the hub is being powered.  It packs a big punch.  It is 100W input and 85W output, sufficient to power my peripherals all day long.  It powers a full 4K 60HZ monitor with ease.  It's compact and fits easily in my backpack.  This is my go to travel hub when I'm out of town.  I have not had any issues with this hub.  It's a sharp steel gray color and blends in well with my high end Dell laptop and monitors.  I observed no defects whatsoever.  This is a sharp looking device.  It has a solid feel to it and a high quality build to it.  I am very pleased with this device.  It is value priced.  Highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have always been impressed by Plugable's products and this USB-C hub does not disappoint. With usb-c quickly becoming the new standard and replacing what I think of as \"regular usb\", this hub expands your capacity. It is very versatile, with data, power, and display capabilities. Speeds are as advertised, with blazing fast data transfers. It gets a bit warm while charging with a charge cable plugged in but nothing to worry about. The display out works great as well, and adds to the versatility of this hub. Overall it's a good value for the money, and I plan on keeping it in my laptop bag to have on hand. Especially considering how modern devices are giving fewer and fewer ports this helps save space and make the most of the ports that are there.This is a recommend from me!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Overall Thoughts…This is a small, compact data port hub, with a hard wired USB-C connection (3.0) upstream port cable, an USB-C port, for primary power delivery (only), three other USB-A ports and HDMI port at the end. SEE PHOTOS. The casing is of a solid metallic construction and appears well made. NOTE: There are no additional cables or storage case included within the package. The hub also arrives with a product design and operational manual, along with a usage tips card. 5 stars."
    },
    {
        "review": "Brilliant (as long as you acknowledge it’s limitations) little mini hub with all the basics, and the typical Plugable flair.It may not be the most technically advanced, but for most people looking for a little hub to bring in their bag it covers all the basics. Plugable has always had excellent customer service and their products are always well documented. It’s also way more solidly built than any other hubs I’ve seen in this price range.This little hub has a controller from Terminus Technology in it, which is a bit odd since they’ve never released a chipset that supported usb 3 to my knowledge. Despite this, I haven’t noticed any slowdown using the port over any other adapter.PD pass through works as expected, and charges just as fast as it would have without the hub.If you get it for the low price, great. If you pay full price, it’s still worth a look."
    },
    {
        "review": "Plugable USB C Hub - I have been running a 4K monitor, keyboard, mouse and a drive off this all at once and it has not hiccuped. HDMI does 4K60 and the picture is clean.Pass through charging works while everything else is plugged in, which was the main thing I wanted out of it.Read the port list first though. Only one of the three USB A ports is 5Gbps. The other two are USB 2.0, so put your SSD on the fast one and the keyboard and mouse on the others.It does get warm under load, but the aluminum shell is doing its job."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this USB-C hub as a simple way to add more connectivity to my laptop, and so far it has worked well. The compact design makes it easy to carry around without adding too much bulk, and the aluminum housing feels solid and well made.The HDMI output has been reliable for connecting to an external monitor, with a sharp image and smooth 60Hz performance. I also like having three USB-A ports available, since it lets me connect things like a mouse, keyboard, and USB drive without constantly swapping devices around. The mix of one USB 3.0 port and two USB 2.0 ports is worth keeping in mind, though, especially if you need fast transfer speeds from multiple devices.The 100W USB-C power delivery passthrough is another useful addition. It allows me to keep the laptop charging while the other ports are being used, which makes the hub practical for a desk setup without needing a larger docking station.The short attached USB-C cable keeps everything compact, although the length can be a little limiting depending on where the laptop's USB-C port is located. Overall, this is a well-built and convenient little hub that adds the ports most people are likely to need without taking up much space."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've always found this brand to be very reliable with their computer electronics, and this hub is no different. There's never enough ports on a laptop, and this splitter that turns to 1 to 4 was nice. It's simple, just straight forward type C to another type C then 3 more usb A. It basically uses to your normal charger port and turns it into a extra USB ports, but you don't get extra C's. The hub itself is very compact although that does mean that it can't easily fit usb items that have wider sides that will block the adjacent ports. The only fancy thing about it is the one port at the end is a hdmi for display connection.Speeds wise seem okay, transferred a large number of music files in the USB 3 speeds, I think. They were fast enough that I was satisfied anyway. Also used this on my android phone and it worked fine, even the hdmi display to a portable monitor. That's the good thing about having a Type C plug in.[ This is a review for:Plugable USB C Hub, 5-in-1 USBC to HDMI Adapter 4K@60Hz, 100W Power Delivery, 3 USB A Data Ports, Laptop Docking Station, Type-C Dongle for MacBook Neo/Pro/Air, iPad Pro, iPhone 17 Pro Max -Dark Grey]"
    },
    {
        "review": "Sytem -> Display -> Advanced display -> \"Choose a refresh rate\"! When I firrst plugged it in, I was dissapointed to see on my 2K Ultrawide bars on the top and bottom of the screen, even when I changed the resolution, the image would not fill the entire screen. Only once I checked checked the refresh rate, I found that Windows kept setting the detault to 29 HZ! After trying a few different, I was able to get full 3440 x 1440 resolution with 85 Hz.Using it during long work sessions made an immediate difference in my display clarity. Scrolling through long documents and editing videos on my external monitor feels smooth thanks to the crisp hight refresh rate, avoiding the slight delay or blur I used to see with basic hubs. Plugging my laptop charger straight into the 100W power delivery port keeps my workspace uncluttered, supplying reliable juice to the computer while powering a mouse, keyboard, and external flash drive simultaneously.This multiport hub is ideal for students, office workers, and frequent travelers who need a dependable port expander for ultra-thin laptops. It gives you the necessary video clarity and charging capability without forcing you to carry a bulky desktop dock.I did take 1 star off as when waking my Thinkpad up from sleep my Ultrawide display would scramble and lose the input. I would need to reseat the dogle in my USB C port. It has a Ryzen pro with DP Alt Mode,. so it shouldn't have an issues. I'm still trying to determine if the issue is with my Thinkpad, the dongle, or the resolution/refresh rate combo. but honeslt, I just like when adapters like these work out of the box without having to play around with the settings each time."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this as an HDMI adapter for my Galaxy S25. The box has CE, FCC, and WEEE markings, which is good. However, there is no USB-IF certification.The adapter works correctly with my 1080p60 monitor although I did not test 4k60. The light on the adapter lights up if plugged to power or to a device, which is somewhat annoying as I wanted to leave this plugged into power 24/7 but don't want the light. I didn't test if the USB 3.0 port was able to negotiate those speeds but the ports do appear to work fine for a mouse and keyboard.What's nice is that the PD passthrough actually charges my phone, when plugged into a 60W PD charger.Note that \"Plugable Essentials\" appears to be a different brand or manufacturer compared to the regular \"Plugable\" - the support email linked in the support QR code in the box is identical to a completely unrelated brand, \"acer gadget\".Overall, this is a pretty good price for especially this type of adapter."
    },
    {
        "review": "Pros:- Premium metal build- Stable 4K60 HDMI output- Runs cool- One fast 5Gbps USB-A port- Three total USB-A data ports- Works without external power- Flexible USB-C cableCons:- PD port does not work with 5V chargers- Only one high-speed USB-A port- Two USB-A ports are slowThe Plugable USB-C hub has premium build quality with a compact metal shell and a flexible eight-inch USB-C cable.I tested the hub on a laptop with a Thunderbolt 4 port. The HDMI output looked solid at 1080P and UHD at 60 fps without artifacts. The two slow USB-A ports worked well with a keyboard and a mouse. The single high-speed USB-A port reached 257 MBps upload and 370 MBps download with my SSD, which was slightly faster than many 5Gbps ports I tested before.The PD charging port did not work with 5V USB-C power supplies. A higher voltage source might work, but I did not test this. The hub does not need external power to function well. The hub runs cool, which matches my past experience with Plugable products.In summary, this hub offers strong build quality, stable HDMI output, and one fast USB-A port, though the PD port is limited and two USB-A ports are slow. It is a reliable compact option for laptops and tablets that need extra ports without extra heat or bulk.  I like this brand and was happy with the order."
    }
]

