    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the AULA F75 keyboard as my main keyboard, and it has been a great upgrade from my previous one, especially considering the price. I mainly use it wired, but I also tested the Bluetooth connection and it worked perfectly fine with no issues. The overall connectivity has been excellent, and I haven’t had any problems using it with my games.The RGB lighting looks really nice and adds a lot to the keyboard’s overall appearance. I do wish there were more RGB customization options and selections available, but the included effects are still enjoyable and look great.The Reaper switches feel and sound amazing. In person, the keys have a really creamy sound profile, while in videos they seem to come across as a bit more thocky. The typing experience feels smooth, satisfying, and enjoyable.The multifunction knob is one of my favorite features. I mainly use it for controlling volume, and having quick access without needing keyboard shortcuts is extremely convenient. It’s a small addition, but it makes everyday use much easier.For gaming, this keyboard has been great for me. Everyone has different preferences when it comes to switches and keyboard feel, but personally, I really enjoy using it while gaming. The responsiveness, comfort, and connectivity have all been solid.Overall, the AULA F75 is an excellent upgrade at its price point. I’m very happy with it so far, and I’m definitely interested in trying out other versions of this keyboard in the future. For now, this has been a fantastic choice, and I would recommend it to anyone looking for a quality mechanical keyboard without spending a lot."
