        "review": "This keyboard is beautiful, it’s very easy to use, and sounds so creamy! Some of the videos including one I tried to make myself, make the sound appear a bit more “clicky” than it really is. The keys actually do have a very full bodied and creamy sound. It’s easy to type with for work or gaming really. The RGB lights are easy to navigate even if you don’t have the driver. And it’s build allows for easy typing and less tension in your hand. It has a pretty solid build, and for what you pay I’d say it’s more than worth the price!"
    },
    {
        "review": "⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ 5/5 StarsThe AULA 99 Wireless Keyboard has been an amazing addition to my setup. The tri-mode connectivity is incredibly convenient, allowing me to switch seamlessly between Bluetooth, 2.4GHz wireless, and USB-C wired mode depending on what I need. Pairing was quick and easy, and the connection has remained stable with no noticeable lag.The keyboard feels premium and well-built, with responsive keys that provide a satisfying typing experience for both gaming and everyday work. The compact 99-key layout saves desk space while still keeping all the essential keys easily accessible.Battery life has been excellent, and I love the flexibility of being able to connect multiple devices. The customization options and overall design give it a modern, high-end feel that stands out from other keyboards in its price range.For anyone looking for a reliable, versatile, and comfortable wireless keyboard, the AULA 99 is a fantastic choice. Great quality, great performance, and absolutely worth the purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Keyboard is amazing, has all of my needs met. It's a full keyboard with NUM pad, has a backlight that can be adjusted either by color, by pattern, or by brightness, AND connects to multiple devices simulataneously. The keyboard is *NOT* quiet. But it's a \"thocky\" sounding keyboard. The taps are thick, muffled, and soft. I do wish the booklet that came with it had better instructions. I couldn't find in it how to switch the backlight pattern and had to ask Alexa on the product listing after it arrived. But the booklet does show how to program the buttons, install the software, and switch between connection modes. I'm definitely a fan for the price. Other keyboards with these features can be up to $70+ so this is basically a steal and such a great product for the value.I'd get more but because it connects to multiple devices, I only need one!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This keyboard is adorable, has great soft (not super quiet, but soft feeling) key presses, its responsive, and it has great connectivity options. Its a happy medium between a full size keyboard versus a compact layout, and it's so easy and smooth to type on.That said, the RGB backlighting does not work for me. I've followed the instructions sent with the keyboard, followed the troubleshooting instructions from AULA and from Amazon, used AULA's software for this keyboard, tried factory resetting, and googled for help videos or anything I could find. Reached out to AULA's support, and they were unwilling to assist and just directed me to Amazon. All I could find on Amazon was the seller's support information. At this point I'm just accepting that it's a defect and something must be wrong within the keyboard, and I'm not savvy enough to diagnose their hardware issues nor do I have the time or will to demand a refund or replacement.The keyboard works great without RGB, but it was a big feature for me when purchasing this as it was mostly an aesthetic purchase. Yeah, I could have picked other options, but I chose this because of the price and I wish I hadn't. So, knocked two stars off for me.TL;DR - it's just a keyboard that you can use on multiple devices. If you just want simple for a good price, this is for you, cause it's a solid option. Don't expect support from the seller or be surprised when the extra functions don't work."
    },
    {
        "review": "This keyboard is pretty amazing. It's very easy to set up and use. I use it for both office-type work and online gaming. It is not a quiet keyboard, typing makes some sound, which I personally prefer.I love the extra controls like the dial for volume. The LED lighting has a lot of customization, even including adding a custom color, if you install the \" AULA S99 三模RGB版 \" software, but there are also shortcut keys to just quickly flip through the preset modes/colors.It has multiple options for connection(BT/GHz/USB), and they all work smoothly & without error that I've encountered. I like that there is the option to keep it on consistently if it's plugged in(USB), but I wish there was the option to do that while running on its charge too(BT/GHz). If it isn't plugged in, it will go to sleep with inactivity, but that's really my only complaint.I have not noticed any type of lag or input errors when using it. If anything, it's a little extra sensitive and, when first using it, I was typing some double letters by accident, so it is very responsive. I found it to be perfect even for fast-paced online competitive gaming, which says a lot for a small and affordable company/product. For the price, it's a no-brainer.AULA, PLEASE MAKE A MOUSE TO GO WITH THIS THAT HAS CUSTOMIZEABLE LEDS AND A COUPLE BUTTONS ON IT PRETTY PLEASEEEEEE. <3"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this keyboard. It’s surprisingly sturdy. The keycaps and comfortable and they make a bit of a blend between creamy and clacky but they’re still quiet enough for a shared office space.I wish I had more options for the color of the backlight without installing the software as I use this keyboard with a work computer that I cannot install that on, so my choices are basically a terrifying red or rainbow.The Bluetooth connection to my computer is *fast*.The USB C connection only works if the cord is USB-C to USB-C, but the cord provided is USB-A to USB-C so that’s annoying.It also doesn’t seem to hold its charge and I don’t know why. I always have it plugged in to power so it’s fine, but I get a lot of “battery 0%” notifications and if I do unplug it it stops working immediately. I may test if charging is for some reason a USB-C to USB-C requirement as well.My keyboard in the picture is up on a keyboard riser so it isn’t actually that tall or angled. I do recommend a riser if you want a better angle for typing."
