        "review": "feels nice and colors are great super durable and size is amazing not too heavy and typing feels so smooth and connects perfectly like any other keyboard love the fact that you can change how little you have to press in order for it to register. 10/10"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very silky smooth, sounds absolutely amazing and feels even better, the software drivers were kinda hard to find n looked like a scam but were not and work perfectly, though you don't need the software for much unless you care about the actuation points and all that special stuff, which you probably do since you're getting a HE keyb, came with everything in box everything works, very high quality feel its heavier (In a good way) than my old keyb I bought for around 60 usd. Got just the standard black keyb but the rgbs all show through the keycaps really good and none of them are buggy or broken. All in all its very worth it if you're a gamer or just care about hall effect keybs in general. It's a 60% so you obv don't have all the keys of a 100% but it's definitely good for saving space. But that's why I mainly recommend to gamers or people who are looking for specific features."
    },
    {
        "review": "Perfect for Gamers! My son has a 200.00 keyboard and actually prefers this one. Great price and quick clicks."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the AULA WIN68 HE keyboard for a while now, and it’s been a great experience overall. The compact size is small enough to save desk space but not so small that it feels restrictive—everything is still right where you need it. The function key functionality is seamless, making it easy to access all the extra commands without breaking your flow. The typing sound is crisp and satisfying without being too loud, and the build quality is excellent—solid and heavy enough that it won’t slide around, even if you accidentally bump it. The RGB lighting is another standout, offering a wide range of patterns and configurations to match any setup. While the software initially seemed a bit sketchy, after doing some research and testing I was able to find a great actuation point that feels perfect for my typing style. One thing I’m still unsure about is the “different switches” option in the software—it’s visible, but I’m not entirely certain what it changes, if anything. Considering the overall quality, sound, build, lighting, and features, this keyboard delivers an impressive experience for such a budget-friendly price.Overall, I highly recommend this keyboard to anybody looking for a budget-friendly gaming keyboard!I've attached a picture with my Logitech G305 mouse for a scale reference."
