[
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the RK Royal Kludge R98 Pro for a little over a week, and I’m honestly impressed with how much value this keyboard delivers. The moment you take it out of the box, it feels solid and well-built definitely not your typical budget keyboard.Typing Experience (5/5)The gasket mount design combined with the pre‑lubed linear switches makes typing incredibly smooth and quiet. It has that “creamy” feel everyone talks about. No pinging, no rattling just clean, soft keystrokes. The MDA profile PBT keycaps are thick, durable, and comfortable to type on.Design & Layout (5/5)I love the 96% layout. It saves desk space but still includes a full number pad, which I use constantly for work. The addition of the volume knob is a nice touch and works great for quick adjustments.RGB & Customization (4.5/5)The RGB is bright, vibrant, and offers a ton of effects. Customizing it is easy once you get familiar with the shortcuts. I only wish the software was a bit more intuitive, but it’s definitely not a deal‑breaker.Performance (5/5)For gaming, it’s responsive and stable with zero noticeable latency. Hot‑swappable sockets are a big win if you ever want to switch to different switches later.OverallIf you’re looking for a keyboard that feels like a premium custom build for a fraction of the price, the RK R98 Pro is a fantastic choice. Great for both work and gaming, excellent build quality, and a super satisfying typing experience.Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "So, i dont usually write reviews, but i felt i had to for this keyboards. the creamy clicks are AMAZING (its my first time having it so im super impressed.) the tiny screen is actually pretty simple and easy to use, you can customize the backlight color and style, speed, etc. the knob works perfect. feels great. it came with extra keys, a usb-c to plug in if you prefer wired, and a key remover. everything feels amazing, very high quality. its obviously not 10 pounds, but carries some heft that feels super secure. its got little folded stands to prop your keyboard up if desired, which i think is super nice. i love the color variety (i got the brown, for reference.), it can be hard finding a nice keyboard that is still stylish and pretty. im extremely satisfied, especially with the price being only 70 usd for this nice of a keyboard. i still have yet to use it, but im pretty confident it will be nice. ill update if anything happens!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I recently purchased this item a couple of weeks ago and so I think it was a good purchase. First of all, they keyboard is super smooth and because of the switches, you do hear some clicks but they're not that loud, just enough to be satisfying. The product feels well-crafted with quality in mind. The keyboard stands; are the perfect size, not freakish large so typing for long periods of time is comfortable. I also like how they send you the \"end\" key in the box so if you don't like the volume knob, you can put the \"end\" key back in. I type 80 words a minute, especially when I am writing programs, I pleased on how well the keys on this board respond and the entire feeling of when a key is pressed. When I type superfast on things that are super important, I don't want my keyboard to fail me.Now, there are a few things I don't really like about it but overall, like I said, this is a great keyboard.- The volume knob: Hey, it works but personally, I feel that it is too close to the \"pgdn\" key so you really can't grip it like a knob. I kind of wished it had groves or something on the dial making it easier to turn. Right now, I just got to try and turn it little by little by spinning the know from the top down to the \"-\" key. That's about all the room you got.- Key position: This one is more of my fault. I am more used to full sized keyboards and not the space saving ones with less keys. The part that messes me up is where the arrows, shift, and enter is all smushed together. If this might also, be you, check out the S98 model instead.- Drivers and App: I can't really download this because the website is blocked at work for gaming lol. I don't know if the site is listed as gaming or if it is just because of their name. I know, this is totally not their fault haha."
    },
    {
        "review": "I upgraded my home gaming setup with this keyboard after considerable research, and it’s been a joy to use for both gaming and typing.Strengths:Premium typing experience: The pre-lubed cream linear switches and gasket mount deliver a “thocky” feel and satisfyingly smooth keystrokes. Typing and gaming are both quiet and comfortable, with five layers of foam dampening any hollow sounds.Customization: The included software lets me remap keys, create macros, and adjust more than 20 dynamic RGB lighting modes quickly. I loved being able to easily tweak the look and functionality.Build quality: PBT double-shot keycaps with an MDA profile feel sturdy and resist wear; they’re grippy and comfortable for long sessions. The detachable aluminum volume knob is a treat for instant control.Layout: The 98-key layout keeps the numpad and arrow keys but eliminates wasted space—a space-saving solution perfect for both gaming and work.Universal compatibility: Works perfectly with Windows and Mac out of the box, and includes both a 2-in-1 keycap/switch puller and extra switches for future customization.Bottom Line:This is an exceptional value for anyone who wants a customizable, quiet, and responsive keyboard for gaming, work, and creative projects. The smooth switches, full-featured software, and premium build make it a standout in its price range. Highly recommended for enthusiasts and everyday users alike."
    },
    {
        "review": "So I upgraded my desk setup to include this keyboard. I did minimal research but I knew I liked the color and the number pad.After having it for several months:1. The keyboard is indeed \"creamy\" and smooth2. The lighting is fun and the quality of the board is very nice.3. It has a good weight and the volume knob is very helpful.4. I am glad I didn't go smaller5. The key swap capability is nice but I don't use it a whole lot.Overall a good keyboard to replace my Bluetooth work one. I definitely think this a worthy upgrade if you're in need of one."
    },
    {
        "review": "I was looking for a keyboard that had a nice compact profile, looked nice, has a volume control knob, AND sounds great when typing.THIS keyboard literally hits everything I was looking for.It's just the right size and weight - it looks and feels premium.The keys have that creamy/clacky sound I was looking for.The colors of the keys are great - but that being said - the backlights don't seem as bright as other keyboards I've owned, but that's not really a big deal to me - but it might be to some people.Overall - I love this keyboard - now I just hope it lasts.  I've read some reviews that make it seem like it might not, but I'm hoping it's durable.As of this review, I've only had it for about an hour, so I'll update this review if anything changes with time."
    },
    {
        "review": "Absolutely worth the money, and even got it on sale! As I was looking for a replacement for my Logitech G512 that had finally started to show its age, after nearly 5 years of daily wear and tear from both games and general typing, I stumbled upon this board after seeing the shop it was inside of.I've been using it now for close to a week, and it has sealed the deal for my desire to build a keyboard once I have the means to do such. Each keycap having a small variance in its elevation by just a few millimeters may not sound like much, but it allows for a much smoother flow in typing and touch feel as you move through the keys. Additionally the sound the keyboard makes with the lubed switches below each key, effectively a quiet thunk-click is just beautiful. Its also much quieter than the G512 was, and is less noticed by people when I am speaking with them over the phone for work. So major win there!Solid 5/5 stars, if you need a keyboard for a good price and solid function - fully recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "This keyboard is great, little heavy and only connects via USB, but as far as everything else you'll be pressed to find a better keyboard at this price range that is as satisfying to type on, cause the \"creamy\" switches sound like something that punches WELL above its weight.Nothing necessarily ergonomic about it but it does have a satisfying color to it and the lights aren't exactly offensive in terms of \"too bright\"If you're looking for wireless don't get this one, look at RK's other offerings but if you're okay only hooking up wired for work or other reasons this is going to be the one you want."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good & my son loves his new keyboard"
    },
    {
        "review": "\"+\"- Qualitative injection of key plastics,- Flattering appearance and robust chassis,- Not aggressive branding,- Super responsive,- The definition of the RGB backlighting is excellent and the LeD scenarios are good,- Really cool 98% format.- Little parasitic vibration,- Excellent quality/price ratio,- Replacement set of a few switches and wheel replacement key if necessary.\"-\"- Some keys (Shift, Caps Lock, Tab) wiggle a little,- Wheel its is smooth and difficult to turn. However, it is equipped with a high quality mechanism. - The keyboard is high, without wrist rest fatigue is inevitable. - Any attempt at cleaning is in vain: dismantling the keyboard by layer is difficult.\"i\" - The activation distance is very short, my hand resting above the keyboard can be enough to trigger commands. This is an effective way to make the keyboard responsive but reduces the comfort of use in my opinion. - The \"creamy\" sound is not to everyone's taste, but it is a good compromise between mechanical feeling and discretion. It is noisier than cherry brown or the \"brown\" keys of Logitech mechanical keyboards. I really like the aesthetics and sound of this keyboard, I recommend it to informed buyers! :)My rating was 4/5, but the brand spontaneously contacted me to better understand my feedback. I think they have absolutely exemplary customer service."
    },
    {
        "review": "The RK ROYAL KLUDGE R98 Pro convinced me from the first moment. The workmanship is of high quality, the keyboard appears stable and the compact 96% layout offers all the important keys including the number pad without taking up an unnecessary amount of space on the desk. I am particularly impressed by the pleasant typing experience. The already lubricated switches run smoothly and sound pleasantly rich. Thanks to hot swap, the switches can be easily replaced if necessary. The RGB lighting is bright, can be adjusted in many ways and ensures a great look. The rotary control is also very practical in everyday life, for example for controlling the volume. Overall, the R98 Pro offers features that are often only found on significantly more expensive keyboards. It is an excellent choice for gaming, home office and daily use. The price-performance ratio is excellent – ​​I would buy them again at any time."
    },
