[
    {
        "review": "Great Value!I’m honestly very impressed with this smartwatch! The screen is beautiful and clear, it looks elegant on my wrist, and it has so many features that I expected to find only on much more expensive smartwatches.I love the heart rate, sleep, SpO2, steps, calories, and activity tracking. It also has tons of sport modes, and the battery life has been great so far. It feels comfortable and lightweight, too.For the price, I really don’t think you can ask for much more. It looks stylish, works great, and gives you many of the features you would expect from a high-end smartwatch without the high price tag.Very happy with my purchase and definitely recommend it! ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have always been an Apple Watch person. I’ve had one since probably 2017 and I was sick and tired of the horrific battery life Apple Watches have. Let me tell you on battery life alone this watch is leaps and bounds ahead. It’s been 8 days since I got this new watch, it came 96% charged and it currently has 45%. My Apple Watch battery wouldn’t last me 12 full hours. It’s overall  easy to use, coming from Apple there was a slight learning curve but it’s not bad. Very easy to setup. It seems accurate steps wise. I have a very small wrist so I wish it came with a smaller band. This one fits but the left over strap wraps around almost all the way. I still get the needed notifications from my phone and can control my music. This is an incredibly functional watch. My husband kept telling me just to buy a new Apple Watch because I use it for work primarily but I couldn’t bring myself to pay that high of a price again for just a slightly better battery and I know Garmin is worth it but I’m not active enough to make the price worth it. I was skeptical with this only being $45 at the time but it has definitely proved its worth. We shall see how long it actually lasts though. Crossing my fingers for at least a year because I love this thing."
    },
    {
        "review": "I wasn’t expecting much from this smartwatch since it’s not a big-name brand, but I’m honestly impressed with everything it can do for the price.The feature that surprised me the most is the Find My Phone function. I use it way more than I thought I would, and it’s already saved me from searching the house countless times. It works great!The watch also tracks my steps, heart rate, sleep, and workouts, and the battery lasts several days before I need to charge it. Notifications come through clearly, and it’s comfortable enough to wear all day and while sleeping.If you’re looking for an affordable smartwatch without paying for a premium brand, this is definitely worth considering. It has a lot more features than I expected, works reliably, and has been a great value for the money. I’m very happy with my purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I was honestly considering returning this, but now I’m a bit undecided. Maybe I’ll write this review and it’ll help me decide.For context, I’m a big watch person - especially for workouts - so I set a budget of $50 max and decided to give this one a try. It was right on the money. When it arrived, I’ll admit the packaging made me a little skeptical. Usually, presentation says a lot about the product, and this didn’t give the best first impression. AT ALL.After opening it, the watch itself did feel a bit flimsy at first (see photos), but surprisingly, the actual build quality turned out to be better than expected. It feels fairly sturdy, which was a nice surprise.I tested it at the gym this morning for the first timr, and it definitely held its own. The workout tracking exceeded my expectations - it offers a wide variety of activities you can easily select, which is a great feature!The battery life is exceptional! It lasts for a very long time which is ALWAYS a plus!I also liked that I could customize the watch face with a personal photo. However, there’s a downside: if you upload your own image instead of using one from the app’s store, you’re very limited in what data can be displayed. Instead of showing time, date, steps, calories, etc. all together, it only allows you to display one or two items. In my case, I could only show the time and date, which was disappointing.Cons:The app is probably the weakest part of this product. There’s a “Find My Phone” feature, but it disconnects every few minutes. You have to reopen the app to reconnect before using it again, which defeats the purpose - especially if you’re trying to locate your phone when it’s lost. Not sure how someone is supposed to find their lost phone but need their phone and watch need to be connected to the app before using this tool. Make it make sense??? You can’t lol.It also claims to support notifications from apps like Snapchat, Facebook, and Instagram, but despite enabling everything, I haven’t received any of those. Not a single one. I only get basic notifications like calls, texts, and a few random apps.I work in software, so I’m prettyyyy comfortable with tech. If I’m having trouble getting these features to work properly, that’s something to keep in mind if those functions are important to you. Please be aware of this if you’re searching for a watch solely for this reasoning.Another downside is that the wristbands aren’t interchangeable - there’s no easy way to swap them out, which is limiting. Which really sucks.Overall, for $50, it’s decent. But honestly, for an extra $20–$30, you could probably find something much better without all the disconnection issues this one constantly gives you.I’ll give it a few more days before deciding whether to keep it or return it. More than likely I’ll be returning to get something more reliable but I’m writing this review for those who wants to stay in a reasonable price range, while giving them the honest review they deserve before spending their hard earned money.Hope this helps!!EDIT 5/24/26: I ended up keeping the watch. The more I used it, the more features I was discovering both in-watch, and in-app. However, I’m still keeping it as 3 stars because of the Cons I’ve listed still being an issue. I’d say give it a try yourselves and see how you like it. You can read all the reviews but it’ll affect everyone differently."
    },
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love this smartwatch! It has a beautiful, elegant design that looks much more expensive than it is. The display is bright, crisp, and easy to read, and the touch screen is very responsive.It pairs with my phone quickly, the battery lasts a long time, and it tracks my daily activity accurately. I also enjoy receiving notifications right on my wrist without constantly checking my phone.Overall, it's stylish, comfortable to wear, and offers excellent value for the price. I highly recommend it to anyone looking for a reliable and attractive smartwatch!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I LOVE this watch for so many reasons!Package came on time, as expected and with all parts. I set it up immediately with no problems. Downloaded the app with no issues at all and the watch synced the first try!I am using this for the health benefits of keeping track of my steps and calories, but to my surprise there are so many other cool features I wasn't expecting.The watch has an option to set a reminder to drink water, I have mine set every hour and it is so cute! The battery live exceeds my expectations! I wore it a full day and night as I slept and it was only at 82% battery.The sleep feature is pretty cool as well!Watch is aesthetically pleasing, fits great and is comfortable. The face features are cool as you can choose between a nice selection of freebies. I ordered the circle watch and it is large, which I like because I can see everything I want to see by glancing at it.The price of this is well worth the purchase, without any doubt at all!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This will be the only review needed to know this is the Smart Watch to purchase!!I have at this point probably purchased and returned more than 50 smart watches because I wanted notifications to have an audible tone and not just vibrate. With Bluetooth 5.2 it was an automatic with most of the accompanying apps you had to partner the watch with but when 5.3 came out, it became vibrate only on all apps with the exception of ONE…VeryFit. Additionally, VeryFit is the ONLY one which will register notifications from LITERALLY EVERY SINGLE APP you have which sends banner notifications to your phone, not just the 10-15 options typically seen in the other apps like Gloryfit, DaFit, FitCloudPro, HBand, etc.In order to receive these Push Notifications on an iPhone, which is what I have, you need to go into Settings, Bluetooth, touch the “i” in the circle and check off “Show Message Notifications” and “Share System Notifications”. You must then go to the App List, find VeryFit, make sure Background App Refresh is checked and Notifications are mirroring the ones I’ve captured in my images.The other important piece of info is the watch volume is set low when it first arrives. Make a phone call from the watch and touch the speaker icon key to allow for raising the volume.In the VeryFit app itself, go to Device, click Notifications, be patient and wait a few seconds and the screen will expand - check off “Sync Phone Notifications” and this is where all the excitement is!As notifications come to your phone, they will also become listed here on this page (and your watch will get the alert for them at the same time) and this is where you can Allow or Turn Off the specific notification. I have also captured this in my images for reference. As you can see, I get notifications for everything I receive on my phone. If you need more assistance, do as it says and tap the “i” in the circle on that page and you will get the detailed instructions just as I have given you now. I have also captured those in my images for you to reference as well.This tracks sleep, stress, energy, blood oxygen level, heart rate, gives you weekly averages on all. It can track your cycle for females and ones weight. It has suggested programs to help with better sleep habits, managing weight, stress, breathing exercises etc. It has every possible physical exercise activity one could imagine. It’s waterproof, has excellent options for watch faces - many are free or you can opt to pay for some if you choose not to become a Community member and if you do, those become free then as well. You can share your progress within the community to help stay motivated if needed. You can contact customer service if you have additional questions at anytime by tapping the little blue operator floating on the page within the app as well.There are screen protectors available, watch cases are shown available but they are too big, so don’t bother, you can change out the bands - there’s nothing you can’t do with this watch and the battery life is also fantastic, lasting me a week so far, even with all the many notifications I receive!!Obviously, I highly recommend it!! You won’t regret the purchase! The only thing I am now in need of is finding its twin in rectangular form because I like to switch between that and round; should I find it, I will update this review with the information! I hope this review has helped!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Update 6/3/26, company responded to my email and sent a new watch asap. I will report back in a couple months if it keeps working.Update 4/20/26, just short of 2 months. My watch has been acting up, the screen has not lighting up for me and the charge going from 100% to zero in just a couple minutes, and now the screen won’t turn on and Bluetooth will not connect to my phone. I have added a video of the issue that is causing me to update my review. Not the update I wanted to give as I loved this watch, but I felt compelled to come back and give an update to others so they were aware of what i experienced.I typically don’t write reviews, but I had to for this product. I used to be a Fitbit owner and very much enjoyed the fitness tracking. I was ready to move to a different style, I wanted one that looked more like a watch. I searched and reviewed garmin and nowatch. I didn’t love garmin due to the size of the watch face on my smaller wrist and the one I liked the best was around $500. The nowatch brand is beautiful but along with the expensive price, I didn’t love that you couldn’t look at the watch and see steps. So I landed on, why not give this product a try?? The watch face size was smaller which was better for my wrist size, the price was better than right and it had all the features I wanted, plus more. Once I got this watch I wore this watch and my Fitbit together to compare stats, believe it or not, this watch was closer to the miles walked measured on my treadmill compared to the Fitbit, the sleep stats were similar. Love the ability to answer calls and make calls in this watch. The weather tracking and all notifications come through well. And the screen is amazing. I did swap out my band (20mm), just for personal preference, the one that came with it was durable. Battery lasted 7 days, I used a decent amount and tracked fitness each day. 100% would recommend!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I loved my watch, the size is big as I wanted, the horn when you make a call is heard very well, it is clear and easy to configure. I recommend it, I just need to test how long the battery lasts."
