[
    {
        "review": "Excellent battery life paired with one of the brightest screens. OS is snappy and rich in useful features. 3000 nit screen is great for viewing in bright daylight. The flashlight function is one of the most used features on my watch. The light can be toggled to red as well. The sleep tracking is improved over the balance model. Find my phone is another feature that I use daily. I prefer this to apple or popular android brands. The watch itself has a nice sporty look but can also be dressed up just by changing the clock face. This is my 3rd amazfit and they just keep getting better. The price is a steal. This is a legitimate high end brand with some fantastic budget watches. Lastly, there are many accessories from 3rd party manufactures available."
    },
    {
        "review": "This watch is awesome! I’ve used Apple watch for years and the battery life on that is terrible. Very different story for the Amazfit Active Max! I’ve had it for a month now and haven’t fully exhausted the battery life on this one yet. I have charged it back to full a couple times, but I’m on my 9th day now, attempting to drain the charge completely to cycle the battery, still at 27%. The Zepp app syncs with IOS health and it has so many features! I was looking at $500-$600 Garmin watches before this, but this watch does everything they do. I’ve also inadvertently banged the bezel on the countertops in my home several times, no scratches! Went for a jog the other day and the watch started a workout and mapped my run! There’s a lot of free watch faces to load to it, and very simple and quick updates. I’ve also used the phone feature to receive a call and the voice and sound were crystal clear! This is a great watch, I absolutely recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I previously had the Amazfit Active 2, but felt it was a bit small for my wrist. This however is perfect. Easier to see the heart rate info and whatnot with the larger screen. Plus the battery life is way longer than the 10 days claimed on the Active 2 and while it's not a huge deal to charge, it's still much more convenient to have extra battery life.One thing I was a little unsure of was the thickness. The photos kind of make it look like a beast. While it is thicker than the Active 2 it's not obnoxious and it's given me no pause whatsoever in terms of look and feel. Brightness is excellent, though I haven't had it long enough to test it on a sunny day outdoors. **Edit** Have been out in full sun with it and no problems seeing the screenThe strap is very comfortable and is the same type of quick release strap with the pins that other smart watches have. Doing some googling it's a 22mm strap which shouldn't be a problem to find. One thing worth mentioning is some peoples skin is sensitive to silicone straps. My skin is not, but I've also had nylon with velcro and can recommend that if you want to use a different strap. Also there's no more tucking the tail of the strap down between your skin and under the strap, it's now routed the way most other straps are, on the outside.I'll update this review if I have any issues, but if you're up in the air between this and the Active 2 and you don't have tiny wrists I'd definitely go with this.Edit 1/22/26: Zero issues to report. One thing worth mentioning is that the face is not completely flat. The edges at the bezel curve down slightly. This means a flat 1.5 inch screen protector won't work; the edges would come off or there would be bubbles that you can't remove. I'm currently using the same screen protector I had for my Active 2. It doesn't cover everything but it does cover the flat part and vast majority of the screen completely and without any raised edges or bubbles. You can view my profile to see which I used. There seem to be some tempered glass screen protectors here on Amazon that curve down at the edges (with the bezel markings to match), but since this is so new I haven't bought one yet."
    },
    {
        "review": "Stunning 1.5\" AMOLED display with sharp, vibrant colors even in direct sunlight, 25-day battery life is genuinely impressive and delivers as advertised, built-in GPS maps work reliably without needing your phone nearby, lightweight and comfortable for all-day wear. Cons: App ecosystem feels limited compared to Garmin or Apple Watch, some advanced health metrics lack accuracy during intense workouts. Overall a fantastic value smartwatch — the battery life and display alone justify the purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "It’s been a week now since the purchase and I can honestly say this is an excellent smart watch!Build Quality: Excellent, well thought out and very good quality controls. Arrived well-packaged with good protective packaging. There is a very small font but well written manual. The screen is of very high definition and very bright.Functionality: Excellent and very responsive. Easy to pair with my IPhone and the alerts are instantaneous, both the phone and the watch receive, emails, alerts etc at exactly the same time and the watch doesn’t show any lag at all. I would say, it beats my Apple watch in receiving the same alerts from the phone!If you’re very active and do all kinds of sports, you’re in luck. The watch is loaded with functions for any sport imaginable. These functions can be turned on or off / customized to suit your life style.Zepp app: The Zepp app is used to set up / pair / customize the watch and it is an excellent app actually!Customization: Also excellent. The watch can be customized in dozens of ways. There are countless watch faces that are free as well as ones that one could purchase. But honestly, the free ones are truly good!Cons: Nothing serious. The band would be much better if the connections are like Apple’s (slide in and lock in place)  instead of using pins.The instructions manual really requires a magnifying glass. But it is so intuitive that one may not need the manual and the magnifying glass!In summary: This is a terrific smart watch. I am wearing it more frequently than my Spple watch that cost 3x more!I highly recommend it , especially when on sale!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Best smart watch I have used by far. Have been using it for over two weeks now and it has been great. It was bought to be a \"work watch\". One I used for my work phone so I didn't have to pull it out every time my coworkers or boss buzzed me. Very quickly I swapped it out for my main smart watch (new Google 3 that came with my phone). This watch is so easy to use, has a huge display, fits snuggly, looks great and holds up in my job, working with my hands.I really can't say enough, I have tried several other smart watches for long periods of time and this in two weeks is by far superior. This is my first review for any watch I own. I use my watch and phone for personal communication as well as fitness tracking and it uses maybe 5% battery life a day, max.It was an excellent purchase. Glad I did. Would buy again. Wish It was around sooner."
    },
    {
        "review": "Amazing !!!!!!!!!!!! I’ve had the Apple Watch SE the Apple Watch Ultra 2 . The bip active max it’s beyond better I actually get all my notifications messages with sounds alert, massive days without charging truly a smart watch that everybody should have I could not stand charging my Apple Watch every day. The active Max does all the vitals track steps like a track dog. It’s really amazing. I’m so happy I got it really high-quality .  170 dollars is extremely good for all you get !!! It’s great and highly recommend . Big round interactive face makes it very resourceful with interactive icons and multi function .."
    },
    {
        "review": "Had it for about 3 weeks now. Set up was a little tricky but not too bad. The pulse reading seems pretty accurate but I'm not sure about the sleep yet. Sometimes it seems very accurate and sometimes not, so time will tell. The steps count differs quite a bit from that on my phone but I'm not sure which is the more accurate I'll test it when I get a chance. The standing time is totally off. If I stand for one hour and sit for seven it shows me standing for seven or eight hours. The worst part was the wristband. It was very uncomfortable and actually gave me a pretty bad rash so I replaced it with a flexible one."
    },
    {
        "review": "I used coros pace 3 for almost 2.5 years until there was hardware issue with crown and touchscreen. I had two amazfit watches previously, GTS and BIP. But I liked my coros pace 3 the most because of its accuracy, battery life and training modes. I didn’t expected it would end this way.It was an expensive watch so I decided to go with a budget watch this time and purchased crossbeats armour pro. I returned it the next day as it wasn’t able to sync with Strava.Next I decided to go with Amazfit watch because i had good experience with my GTS and BIP. Scrolling around I came to know about newly launched Active Max. I just ordered looking at the reviews and ratings on amazon although I didn’t expected much from this one. After using coros pace 3 i was not expecting much from this watch but to my surprise it surpassed my expectations. It did everything what my coros pace 3 did and at not so expensive price tag. It is pretty accurate in distance, heart rate, calories tracking. The calling feature is amazing and speaker and mic are crystal clear. So many good features like quick notifications, bt calling, offline and online music control, AI coaching, Always on display and not to forget it has a very strong gps connection. Gps locks up very fast, within few seconds and doesn’t loose signals throughout the run.16K is Great value for money for this all in one accurate and precise, premium, feature rich bundled watch."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am pleasantly impressed by this watch especially since it's replacing my Garmin Forerunner 945 which has lost its bezel seal. I'm going to start with the negative: The watch doesn't have built-in golf recognition. I believe that other models from Amazfit do. That's about it as far as negatives go. I track my sleep, my runs and my swims. For me, the watch provides the same type of metrics as the Garmin. If anything, this watch tracks my swimming way better than my garmin. I get the real distance from a swim at the lake. When the Garmin would have me finish in the middle if the lake. The battery last longer than the once impressive 945. I have my music via mp3 upload to the watch, but I can also make phone calls and answer them using the watch microphone and speaker. Really pleased with this Amazon Warehouse Deal!"
