[
    {
        "review": "I love this OtterBox phone case! It’s super cute, and I absolutely love the glitter design. The durability is great it offers solid protection while still looking stylish. I know OtterBox makes even tougher cases, but this one was perfect for what I needed. I also like that I can still use my magnetic charger with it, which is a huge plus.The only downside is that after using it for quite a while, the edges have started to discolor, and the case has become a little loose on my phone. However, I’ve had it for a long time, so I think that’s just normal wear and tear. Even with that, it’s been one of my favorite phone cases, and I would definitely buy it again."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've used OtterBox cases before, so I had pretty high expectations, and this one didn't disappoint. It keeps the phone slim while still feeling sturdy enough to protect it from everyday drops and bumps.I like that it's clear because it lets the color of my phone show through instead of covering it up. The buttons are easy to press, and the raised edges give me a little extra peace of mind around the screen and camera.The MagSafe connection is strong and works well with my charger and accessories. It's a little more expensive than some clear cases, but the quality feels worth it. Overall, it's a great choice if you want protection without adding a lot of bulk."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve always trusted OtterBox for reliable phone protection, and the Symmetry Series case for the iPhone 15 Pro Max doesn’t disappoint. It fits the phone perfectly — snug but not bulky — and the buttons are easy to press with great tactile feedback.The slim design still offers serious protection. The raised edges around the screen and camera lenses provide extra peace of mind without adding unnecessary weight.I’ve been a big fan of the OtterBox Strada case since my iPhone 6, but I used to have issues with the cover leaving an imprint on the screen. After a few days of using the Symmetry case, I actually prefer it — it feels lighter, simpler, and seems to work better with wireless charging than the Strada.I also love the finish — it’s sleek, feels great in the hand, and slides easily in and out of my pocket. It looks professional enough for work but stylish enough for everyday use.Overall, a perfect balance of protection, function, and style — exactly what I expect from OtterBox."
    },
    {
        "review": "You just can’t go wrong with an OtterBox, it’s very durable and looks great. Would recommend to anyone."
    },
    {
        "review": "Have had this since March and the stickies constantly get stuck on my phone. It’s an okay case - I am very careful with the phone so I believe it does its job but have not tested it.7/31 - UPDATE:(Increased from 3 to 4 stars)See new photos from today. Cons: **The mag safes constantly remove on phone and I have to unpeel, on the occasions I remove my phone. **No OtterBox indication anywhere on case (that I’ve seen). Flimsy or flexible for a (depending on sales) $30-something - to - $40-something case. **Concerned with how much protection is provided from elements — The inside of the case and that part of my phone ended up with salt all over it even though I left it by the door to a salt spa/float therapy. I had to scrub my phone (have camera and screen protectors), in the nooks and crannies. Pros: the camera lip and screen edges are raised very much, although you cannot tell from the photo. **The case is very light - new case is like 2x heavier with phone in it. Has protected my phone - never have had a cracked screen. I’ve used a variety of screen brands (to try them out, to find one I like best) so I attribute it to the case. At 36, I have tried tons and tons of cases. I have a toddler. I am clumsy. And yet - this one has stood up pretty well. No scratches or really anything - easy to clean, only slight yellowing. If not for the mag safe peeling, I would stick with it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been using the Otterbox symmetry series for years on all my iPhones and when I went to buy one for my new iPhone pro max I was surprised by some of the bad reviews so wanted to share my experience.I think a lot of people looking for a phone case don't realize that this is a different model than other Otterbox options. The case is designed to be less bulky, and doesn't curve over the screen like some of the other, larger options.However, having had this case on two past iPhones, I can tell you the protection is incredible, I've never so much as even had my screen protector crack, and I tend to drop my phone a lot.When I received this case, it fit exactly as expected based on my past experience with the symmetry models. It rises above the case, so if the phone were to fall on its face, no part of the screen would actually touch the ground, which is how it can offer such good protection without feeling bulky. It lines up perfectly in the charging areas and the buttons, and also offers raised protection in the back around the camera lenses, so that in case of a fall again they won't actually hit the ground.My favorite part about the symmetry cases is that they are so pretty and have fantastic designs. This one is bright and matches the product photos perfectly!Like I said, I've had these cases for three iPhones now, each phone lasted 3+ years without any damage and the cases lasted that long too. I'm thrilled to have a new one and looking forward to the next few years with this beautiful phone case."
    },
    {
