[
    {
        "review": "When i plug my phone to charge it says super fast charging which ive never seen before. Ive seen fast charging never super fast. Cool 😎 but it only shows 7.7 watts on the display. 🤔 but i like this charger. It does what I need it to do. There's no its taking to long or overheating issues etc. The size form factor and display all nice. 3 ways to charge nice and price wasn't bad though could be lower. Happy with the purchase. Ugreen may become the new Anker having better prices for quality products."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the UGREEN Nexode 20000mAh 130W Power Bank with my ROG Ally, and it has been outstanding. It easily doubles my gaming time, turning the Ally into a truly portable handheld instead of something that constantly needs to be plugged in.The 100W output is no joke — it keeps up with demanding devices without throttling, and fast charging works exactly as advertised. I can game while charging without noticeable slowdown or excessive heat. The TFT smart display is also a great touch, giving clear info on power usage and remaining battery, which is very helpful.Build quality feels premium, it’s compact for its power capacity, and having multiple USB-C ports makes it versatile for charging other devices like phones, tablets, or even a laptop.If you own a ROG Ally or any high-power handheld, this power bank is absolutely worth it. Reliable, powerful, and well-designed."
    },
    {
        "review": "The battery life on this is what makes this product so worth it. You can charge this, and it will keep the battery life for months even when it’s not in use. Every other power bank I’ve had would lose its charge if it was idle or not in use. It does have some weight to it, but it’s very compact for the most part since it fits in the palm of my hand. It’s great for traveling and hiking long distances. Even on hikes in the heat it has no gotten warm or overheated."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a somewhat heavy (weighs about a pound), but powerful battery. I don't mind the weight, I expect that from a 20k battery. It feels solid and well built. I like the display and how it shows the negotiated voltage and amps so you can see what it is doing.I also like that it has a trickle charge mode for lower power devices like my watch and earbuds. Most batteries will shut off because there isn't enough of a power draw, in trickle charge mode the battery will not shut off for 3 1/2 hours.Please note that they recommend that you use a minimum 65 watt charger to charge the battery. You can use less power, but the battery will take longer to charge. With the more powerful charger it takes a little over an hour to fully charge.One day my M4 MacBook Air was down to around 25% and my phone was around 40%. I plugged both into the battery at the same time. I charged my phone to 80% and computer to 100% and the battery was down to about 10% remaining charge. The computer was drawing around 60 watts the majority of the time.One thing that has left me curious is that I have yet to see it either receive or draw more than 3 volts @ 20 amps since it says it is capable of 5 volts. Both my charger and computer should be capable of 100 watts, but I also know that devices negotiate with the charger so it doesn't bother me that it is less."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a really awesome power bank. It has extra features like a setting for lower power draw for older devices that wouldn't work with higher wattage output. It also has a great display that shows power draw from attached devices. It's a solid feeling compact brick but not too heavy. It'll fit in a pocket but you'll definitely notice it and will look awkward. The included cord and carrying pouch are a plus. It charges relatively fast if using a fast charger. Just note only 1 port outputs 100W and the other two will split the remaining 30Ws between the two.Another thing would be the outside plastic may be susceptible to dents if dropped.Overall, it's a great power bank and I recommend getting this one if you are looking for this form factor & a pretty high capacity."
    },
    {
        "review": "The UGREEN Nexode 20000mAh: Seriously, Ditch Your Old Power Brick Okay, let's be real. Nobody gets excited about a power bank. But the UGREEN Nexode 20000mAh is the one exception that actually makes charging your gear feel... well, fun. The Dashboard You Didn't Know You Needed Forget those four little blinking lights that leave you guessing. The absolute best part of this power bank is the built-in Smart TFT Display. It’s like a tiny, high-tech dashboard for your charging life. You can instantly see: Real-time Wattage: Is your laptop actually pulling 60W or 100W? The screen tells you exactly how fast the juice is flowing. No more guessing games!Battery Percentage: The precise percentage remaining, not just \"half-full-ish.\"Time Remaining: This is the MVP feature. It estimates exactly how long the power bank has left before it dies, or how long it’ll take to charge itself back up. Pure genius for planning your day.Power to Spare (For Your Laptop, Too!)This isn't just for topping up your phone. The 20,000mAh capacity paired with the high output means you can fully charge a MacBook or another hefty laptop while you’re stuck waiting at the airport or working remotely. And since it has multiple ports, you can charge your laptop, phone, and earbuds all at once without breaking a sweat. If you’re a digital nomad, a student, or just someone who uses their gadgets a lot, you need this. It’s reliable, it’s fast, and the smart display turns a boring chore into an easy, informed process. Grab one—you won't regret it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "if you need a power bank charger that can last long, charges fast, and can quickly charge multiple devices at one time, this is worth it, especially if you get it on sale like I did (usually 89.99, I got mines for 69.99). Functionalities are amazing on this unit, durable and long lasting, can take with you anywhere, highly recommended!*one year later and it’s still here, very reliable and helped me out in plenty of situations, especially when I’m on the go, I will say that it will drain more when you connect the more power hungry devices, but it’s still a winner in my book"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great power bank! It charges my devices quickly and lasts a long time. The only con I have with this device is that it's hard to achieve the max wattage of recharging without it thermal-throttling quite a bit to only around 30-40w. Overall, this has a very high-quality feel and build quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good product, I charge several devices at the same time, fast charging"
    },
    {
        "review": "ESSENTIAL.... I tested some power banks, but this one....To begin with: Total recharge in less than 2 hours which is rather quick given the capacity. In fact... I needed something efficient and powerful to accompany me during long drone hikes. I have a mini 4 Pro 3 battery combo, and no need to explain to those who do it at some point the batteries can melt in the sun at high speed and we can remain frustrated to miss a last shot due to lack of battery. I left on a 12Km hike quietly, 1 first empty battery, which I plugged directly into this power bank: Charged at 35W (+- 35min of charging, identical to my charger at home) time to walk around, to empty a second battery, the first was already at 100%...final result, I returned home less having consumed the equivalent of 6 drone batteries... there was still 33% left on this one which also allowed me to recharge my phone. Well it is still 450gr; but I highly recommend it for this type of use. I came back happy to have really enjoyed this walk, my drone shots, without frustration of having missed a single one"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this portable battery from UGREEN and the truth is that it has been a success. It is powerful and charges your cell phone, tablet and even your laptop without breaking a sweat. The other day, with the big blackout, it was my lifesaver: I was able to have all my devices working without worrying about being stranded. What I liked most: • Fast and efficient charging: Charge my laptop and mobile at the same time without losing speed. • Information screen: It shows the battery percentage and charging power, which is very useful. • Compact design: Despite its large capacity, it is easy to transport. However, as a negative point, the price is somewhat high. But honestly, for the quality, the power and the peace of mind that comes with having it, I think it is worth the investment. In short, if you are looking for a reliable and powerful battery, and you don't mind paying a little more for quality, this one from UGREEN is a safe bet."
    },
    {
        "review": "Convenient and insight into your charging process"
    },
    {
        "review": "This UGREEN power bank is one of the best I’ve used—it feels solid, well-built, and the 20,000mAh capacity is perfect for travel since it’s the max allowed for air carry-on. It charges my Galaxy S25 Ultra and MacBook quickly without any issues, and the smart TFT display is a great touch—it shows real-time input/output so I always know exactly what’s happening.The three ports make it easy to charge multiple devices at once, and the top-mounted design keeps cables neat and out of the way. Despite the power, it’s surprisingly compact and comes with a pouch that keeps everything together, which is great for not losing cables on trips.Recharging the power bank itself does take a few hours, but that’s expected given its size and capacity. Overall, it’s a high-quality, dependable charger that gives me peace of mind compared to cheaper brands. Worth every penny, especially when on sale."
    }
]

