[
    {
        "review": "This is the first time I've had a phone that used a magnetic charger, boat suffice it to say, I'm very pleased with this one. It sticks on firmly, yet not so firmly that I can't pull it off. Seems to charge pretty fast and I don't have to worry all the time now about my phone running out of battery. Cord is the perfect length for my needs and the charging unit seems very strong and sturdy. I appreciate the simplicity of the unit has it's very easy to use and I can take it with me without thinking about it. I was worried it would get warm, but it doesn't seem to do that. Would definitely buy this again."
    },
    {
        "review": "This magnetic wireless charger works great! The magnetic connection is strong, charging is fast and reliable, and it keeps my phone securely in place. The design is sleek and compact, making it perfect for both home and travel. Highly recommend for anyone looking for a convenient, hassle-free charging solution."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been very impressed with the Apple MagSafe 25W Wireless Charger. The magnetic connection is strong, making it easy to snap my iPhone into the perfect charging position every time. It charges noticeably faster than my older MagSafe charger, especially when paired with a compatible 30W or higher USB-C power adapter and a supported iPhone.The build quality is exactly what you'd expect from Apple. The braided cable feels much more durable than previous versions, and the charger stays securely attached while I'm using my phone. I also appreciate that it works with my AirPods, making it a versatile charger to keep on my desk or nightstand.While it's a little more expensive than some third-party options, the reliability, strong magnetic alignment, and faster charging make it worth the investment. If you're already in the Apple ecosystem, I highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "This charger works great. Sure, it’ll get hot sometimes, but the charge will pause until the temperature drops. I like the heft and texture of the cord - it doesn’t feel like plastic. This isn’t going to wear out fast. I like the little cord management Velcro that comes with it. Nice fast charge. I’m pleased. Great deal overall."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m really impressed with this magnetic wireless charger. It connectseasily to my iPhone 15 Pro Max and holds securely in place, so I don’thave to worry about the phone slipping off while it’s charging. Themagnetic connection makes it very convenient to attach and remove myphone, especially when I’m using it throughout the day.Charging has been reliable, and I like not having to deal withplugging a cable directly into my phone. The charger is also compactand easy to use, making it convenient for my desk, nightstand, orwhile traveling.Overall, this is a great wireless charger for the iPhone 15 Pro Max.It’s simple, convenient, and works as expected. I would definitelyrecommend it to anyone looking for an easy-to-use magnetic wirelesscharging option."
    },
    {
        "review": "First, this charger is fantastic at charging fast. I have had no problems with charging any phone fully in half the time my old wireless charger took.The caveats: The charger has two states. It is either fast charging, or it is off. It will not work at all in a car because it doesn't supply enough amps. It won't work with wall plugs under 25 watts (5v, 5A). It doesn't just refuse to fast charge, it won't even power up. So this only works if you have a high-amperage adapter, or a high power computer port.The other issue is weight. The device is small and surprisingly light, but that means if you pick up your charging phone, the charger comes with it. Great in a car, but it won't work there. Terrible on a nightstand or desk. I'm constantly prying off the charger just so I can use the phone.So great in any situation where the above two issues don't matter."
    },
    {
        "review": "I highly recommend these chargers for anyone with an iPhone 12 or later who's charging port has become useless.  With this two pack I glued one to the wall in my apartment, the other is attached to a vent clip in the car.  The mag safe feature allows me to slap my phone on the wall or vent and the phone is secure (even works through my off brand silicone case). I haven't had a single failed charge since switching to wireless charging.  So simple but still life changing"
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered this wireless charger because my charging port stopped working.  I didn't expect much from wireless charging, but l was wrong. My phone was charged very fast. I have since had my charging port fixed, but l still prefer the wireless charging pad. I bought the 2-pack and have one on my nightstand and one on my desk at my office.  It worked well with my Samsung Galaxy 24."
    },
    {
        "review": "Does a good job"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve always found charging my phone overnight a bit annoying – constantly trying to get the cable in the right position, and still waking up with a low battery more often than I should.This MagSafe-style charger has completely removed that hassle. Now it’s just a case of placing the phone down and letting it attach magnetically, which feels a lot more reliable than fiddling with cables in the dark. Since using it, I’ve stopped waking up to a nearly dead phone, which is exactly what I wanted from it.It comes as a simple package with the charger itself, a USB-C cable and a USB-A converter, so you’ve got a bit of flexibility depending on what plug or setup you’re using. The magnetic alignment is strong enough that the phone stays in place easily, even if you move it slightly on the bedside table.What stands out with this set is having two chargers. It makes it easy to keep one at the bedside and the other in another room or take it for travel, so you’re not constantly unplugging and moving things around.It also supports faster wireless charging, so it doesn’t feel slow compared to wired charging overnight, especially when paired with the right adapter. It’s more than enough for overnight use and day-to-day top ups.Case compatibility is decent too. It works through most standard slim cases without issue, but for the best magnetic hold you’ll want a MagSafe-compatible case or one with built-in magnets. Thicker cases do weaken the snap-in feel a bit. Price wise seems to be normal for the price of 2.Overall, it’s a small change that makes a big difference in day-to-day use. No more cable faff, no more guessing angles – just put it down and it charges. Exactly the kind of simple upgrade that makes life easier."
    },
    {
        "review": "I use this with my iPhone 8 because sometimes the charge port is finicky so I have to use wireless charging, and I gave the second one in the 2 pack to my cousin who has an iPhone 14 Pro Max. The magnet connection is strong, it snaps on tight and doesn't shift. The slim design is great for when it's stuck to the back of your phone and you're using it so it's not bulky in your hand. For my iPhone 8, there's no magnets in the phone, so it doesn't attach, but it works fine as a normal Qi pad if I centre it and it doesn't make my phone hot.It charges my phone at 7.5W. That's an iPhone 8 limit, not the charger's fault. My cousin's 14 Pro Max gets 15W, since 25W Qi2.2 only works on iPhone 15 and newer. No wall adapters are included so you need a 25W+ USB-C PD brick to get fast charging on phones that support it. With my iPhone 8, a basic 10W brick is enough. If you use a weak adapter with a newer phone, charging will be slow.For the price of a 2 pack, it's good if you need a backup for port issues or want Qi2.2 speeds on a newer phone. The strong magnet is great for MagSafe phones, and it still functions as a standard wireless charger for older models."
    },
    {
        "review": "Set of two magnetic chargers in lemon yellow color. At home, we all have iPhones: 12, 14, 17, and these cats are perfect for all our phones. They replace the old basic chargers with less efficient cables and prematurely wear out the phone's charging socket. This helps extend the life of our old iPhones which are no longer able to charge with the cable. Charging is fast and efficient. The magnet is super effective. And the charger remains discreet, plus I love the color!!!!I recommend ++++"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "These work if your in a jam. When our power went out from the snow storm these literally saved our household. Lol. I have a toddler who loves playing and watching videos on her tablet. Well without power it wasn't possible so these charges came in handy to have. It literally saved the day and made a toddler very happy. So yes they do work and are small enough to carry anywhere. I bought 2 and wil definitely be getting a few more. It's very easy to use. Just put the lithium batteries in and go. It also has a flash light and it's bright. :)"
    },
    {
        "review": "I was not expecting this to be so good"
    },
    {
        "review": "UPDATE: Tested with alkaline batteries. After three hours, my 10k mAh power bank was still at 25% charge, and now the light doesn't work. Will be returning this, regretfully.There's a lot to like about this item. It's compact, with an easy-open top. The LED light is bright and steady. And the price is right. That said, it does seem to be a little slow.I tested it with the only two types of batteries I had on hand, a set of Super Heavy Duty ones from a dollar store, and a national brand rechargeable type. Alkaline batteries are strongly recommended by the manufacturer, and I don't doubt they'd yield better results than what I used. But here's what I found:After one hour, the Super Heavy Duty batteries had charged my older Android from 82% to 88%. After an additional hour, it was still there. Thinking the batteries may have died, I pulled and tested them. They were just about 35% depleted.The second test, with branded rechargeables, yielded similar results. After one hour, it charged to 95% from 88%, and wouldn't go any further. Those batteries tested out at around 30% depleted.Things I think would help yield better results: A faster cable, the proper type of battery, and charging a power bank instead of directly charging a phone. I have a few 10-20k mAh banks I'm going to fool with to see if I get better results.The bottom line? It does the job, albeit slowly, and would probably charge a small flip phone more quickly. With a good supply of AA alkalines, it's a good alternative to solar for an emergency tool kit, and worth the $7 I paid. I would buy it again."
    },
    {
        "review": "LZDICITARU Battery Operated Phone Charger Emergency|USB Battery Powered Power Bank Portable 4 AA Batteries Powered Outlet (White)SIZEThe battery bank is not large but actually somewhat big when you consider the amount of BAttery capacity it provides versus what you get with a purpose built battery bank. The use of AA batteries creates a loss of size efficiency that the product makes up for in powersource availability; the availability of the additional batteries. I doesn't weight much until you place the batteries in it, at which point it does obtain a modestly substantial weight.BUILD QUALITYThis isn't built very robustly. It does feel like something that would break if dropped. Even though I have dropped it before, it does still work. I wouldn't be too rough with this.I used these with lithium ion AA rechargeable batteries. I do seem to have to recharge them quickly after being used in this but i assumed it was a matter of the lower voltage and power capacity of my lithium batteries vs mr previous actual power bank, but it may be that batteries lose efficiency in this device and rechargeables may more of their power lost in heat or something in this device. Its also possible that the warning is supposed to be against NiMh batteries which operate at a 1.2 volts and not lithium which operates at the same voltage as alkaline (1.5 volts). These are a great value if you do use them with a collection of rechargeable batteries because it gives you a battery banks for for a small fee and that same power source can go back to running your game controllers or remote and flashlights when you don't need it. That makes this the perfect device for emergency kits. since this is  appropriately compatible with AA batteries that should or would also be in such emergency kits. Its also great to have in the event you can't charge your phone at an outlet but could purchase batteries."
    },
