[
    {
        "review": "Let me be very clear here, this is truly only an EMERGENCY product, not, \"oh, my phone's at 1% and I'm out with my friends - time to use this!\" It is only 8W, even with fresh alkaline batteries. I had it in for 2 hours and my older iPhone didn't charge even 1%. HOWEVER... DID stave off the drain of my phone. To explain, with wifi on, apps constantly pinging for updates, and my browser open (even if I'm not actively using it), my (much) older model phone uses 4-10% battery an hour. I plugged this in and, though I wasn't actively using it, it didn't drain the 4-10% I was expecting. So it does work, but very, very slowly, and you're probably better off charging a power bank with it and then charging your device with it, instead of going directly to the device, though if the device is completely off and not draining its battery at all when you use this, that may also work better. I tested the batteries before and after using this - 2ish hours of having this plugged into my phone didn't make a substantial dent in the battery's life (they were mid-to-high \"good\" when I first popped them in, and were low-to-mid \"good\" when I stopped using this charger). It's great to have at home in case of a natural disaster, but I'm not sure that having it in your car or work bag would be super helpful because of how long it takes just to squeeze out a couple of percentages of charge. For true emergencies, it's one of only two products I can find that offer true battery-to-USB charge, which might be lifesaving, but it's not for everyday, on-the-go use."
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered the AA batter-operated phone charger hoping to keep it packed with other essentials in case we lost power or had to evacuate with little notice The idea of a portable charger that runs on regular batteries (instead of needing a wall outlet or a pre-charged power bank) seemed smart for true emergencies when electricity isn't available.In practice, it does work as a pure backup option when regular plugs aren't accessible. You load it with AA batteries and it can slowly top off a phone, However, the charging speed is a letdown as it takes closer to an hour than just minutes that you'd expect from a normal charger or power bank.If you're looking for something to keep charged phones going during prolonged outage or off-grid situation and you're willing to wait (and have spare batteries on hand), it fills that niche. Just don't expect fast results."
    },
    {
        "review": "Package is just a clear bag, so first terrible packing. Second, does not work at all and the side was broken with a big hole, it looks small in the photo because we attempted to close it. Still does not work"
    },
    {
        "review": "This LZDICITARU battery operated emergency phone charger will be nice to have on hand as a backup in case of an extended power outage. It operates exactly as described, and I'll be keeping this in my \"battery box\" with my AA battery supply for quick use in case of emergency.I had a little trouble installing the batteries at first. The back panel didn't slide off easily, but after a few attempts it came off. It was easy to install the three AA batteries. I was able to power it on immediately using the black switch on the side of the device. I was pleasantly surprised to find that there is small built-in flashlight. The switch has three modes - off, flashlight and USB, for charging.As for functionality, it has a built-in USB C charging cable that conveniently folds into and secures to the side of the device. Underneath the build-in cable, there is a USB A outlet that can be used for non-USB C devices.Based on three uses to charge my iPhone 17 Pro, this is NOT a fast charger, and I did not expect it to be. It charged my phone about 10% in 20 minutes, which is pretty good for emergency use. I wouldn't rely on this as an everyday charger, but it's not intended for that use. Also, the battery compartment heated up quite a bit while in use, but it cooled off quickly after turning it off."
    },
    {
        "review": "Ehhhh i just don’t like it it works good tho lmao o hate I had to add batteries battery life is long and the charging speed is decent. Lightweight"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this to put in our hurricane emergency stash, thinking it could be a good option since it uses batteries (3 AA). And it would be a good option if it worked. I added the batteries, flipped the switch and my phone (Iphone 16E) showed it was charging. I didn’t use my phone and checked it almost 30 minutes later and it never added even 1%. The device was smoking hot and I didn’t want to let it continue charging (or not charging) my phone so I disconnected it. One note, the ad shows this to be a USB-C in their photos and a USB-A in the info, and to confirm, this is a type C. The device does have a small flashlight (think penlight) but it’s a very tiny, dim light and wouldn’t be much, if any, help in a power outage. Disappointed because this could have been a useful device but as it is, it is not something I would get any use out of at all."
    },
    {
        "review": "This little gadget is made with a hard, brittle plastic so don't expect to toss it around and not break it..I give it a 5star as it works as promised and it's a really cool thing to have in your car or bag.. The batteries charge slowly but give you enough of a charge where you can still talk. I constantly have people asking me for a charger.  For the price you can just give a person the whole charger to keep and pass on to the next person...I grew up in a hurricane zone.. This is a perfect item for your emergency kit.Those are the two uses I see for it-leave it in your bag for days when you need it and give away as a gift to someone who asks you for a charger.As a reminder, always use quality batteries like Duracell or Kirkland as  cheap batteries will often corrode and ruin the inside of the gadget."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is an absolute game changer for hurricane season, tornado kits, blizzards or any other time you might need an emergency charger. I could see it being used in your car, kept in a purse, the uses for this our endless. What I really love about it is it’s not only a USB-C charger. It has the option to plugging in any USB cable and it also functions as a flashlight. You can endlessly replace the batteries which it takes three AAs. You will never be dependent upon having power to recharge your phone again. I have bought for hurricane season a USB-C charger for six dollars that only works once and you cannot charge older iPhone iPhones off of it or any other items plus it does not have a built-in flashlight. I am going to purchase several more of these and recommend them to my friends."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "This Anker 20W USB-C charger set is exactly what I needed. It charges my iPhone quickly and efficiently, and the compact design makes it easy to carry when traveling. The included USB-C cables are durable and work perfectly right out of the box. I also appreciate getting two chargers in one pack, making it convenient to keep one at home and one at work. Anker's quality is outstanding, and everything feels well-built and reliable. Highly recommended for anyone looking for a dependable fast charger at a great price!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I've had these cables and power bricks for about 2 years now, every since I upgraded from an iPhone XS to the S24 Ultra, and I haven't had any issues!The length is great when I'm lying in bed or sitting on the couch and want to use my phone while it's charging.Having a USB A and USB C connector is handy too if I need to dual chargeI try to buy Anker products whenever I can. I'm always impressed with the quality of everything I've used by themI know that you could spend less for similar products but you really are paying for quality!The fast charging works great when I need a little bit of extra charge on phoneDon't hesitate to buy this, it's worth every penny!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve bought these chargers for our iPhones and my kids Amazon kids tablet several times. They work well and charge fast. Plus I like the cute green and purple colors. They work with every case that I’ve tried and they don’t wear out easily like some other top brands. These are a must have imo. They’re very affordable too."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great charger with reliable fast charging! The Anker 20W USB-C Charger Block works great, is compact, and delivers the performance you expect from a trusted brand. One important tip: make sure you are using a fast-charging compatible cable as well, because the charger can only perform as well as the cable allows. Pair it with the right cable and it’s an excellent charging solution."
    },
    {
        "review": "The block is compact, with two ports so two items can be charged simultaneously. The 5 foot cord is very convenient."
    },
    {
        "review": "Used it daily with an anker magsafe charger for my iPhone 13. It worked well for 18 months, now it seems to have gone bad. I don't know if that's a decent life span for this or not, but I'm a tad disappointed."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have purchased this 2-pack probably 3 times now. They work! Fast charging, long and durable cable, thin wall block (helps not to take up 2 plugs with one block), and now the cool colors to choose from."
    },
    {
        "review": "Huge fan of Anker products across the board. I’ve been using their Mac dongles and external batteries for years without any issues, so buying this 2-pack charger set was a no-brainer. They perform great, fast-charge reliably, and customer support is top-tier if you ever need anything. Easily my favorite tech accessory brand!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The charger is very good, it fulfills its function with quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "Purchased for $19.95 in November 2025.This is my third time ordering this charger set—partly because they’re great, and partly because the kids keep “borrowing” them. Anker has always been a dependable brand in our house, and this set just reinforces that. Each charger has both a USB-C and a USB-A port, which comes in handy when you need to top off two devices at once.The included USB-C cables are solid quality. They’re not the most flexible, but based on my past experience, they hold up really well over time and don’t fray or loosen at the connectors like cheaper ones tend to. Charging speeds are excellent—fast, consistent, and reliable.After a long charging session, the brick gets a little warm, but that’s expected with higher-wattage chargers. It’s never hot enough to worry about, just something you notice if you touch it.Overall, these have become my go-to chargers for phones, tablets, and just about anything else. Anker continues to be a brand I trust and look for whenever I need reliable charging gear.TLDRReliable, fast, and durable. Dual ports are convenient, and the included cables last a long time. Gets slightly warm during use, but nothing concerning. Great value and performance from a trusted brand."
    },
    {
        "review": "The chargers worked very well, I gave one to my mother, and I use the other, a Samsung and iPhone and they both charge super fast, one of the best chargers in my opinion"
    },
    {
        "review": "I actually bought this Anker Charger 2-Pack on sale for the second time because my first set held up so well.Why I like this bundle:=> Better cables: It comes with two USB-C cables, and they are 5 feet long. Most cheap chargers only give you a tiny 3-foot cord, so the extra length is a huge plus.=> Dual ports: Each block has both a USB-C and an older USB-A port. I can use the new fast cables but still plug in my older tech without needing new bricks.=> Speed: The 20W charging is noticeably faster than the old standard cubes.No real complaints at all. Anker makes reliable gear, and getting two blocks plus two long cords on sale is a killer value. Highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "This item has in a very short time cemented itself as a foundational piece of daily kit.  Charger can be assembled in mere moments; the flat form allows it to be used in nearly any kind of outlet space availability, and supplies \"fast charging\" to the connected device.  The biggest fault to level is the quite short charger cable.  Said cables length, however, is dictated by necessity for the compact purpose; anything longer than the alleod18 inches and it would not be so portable.Overall this is an incredible price for incredible piece of small but lriority"
