        "review": "This is a great usb c plug.  It's compact and portable and can be attached to a Keychain or bag.  The mini usb cords attached are a nice touch and great for charging on the go with a c cord or adapter."
    },
    {
        "review": "Did charge my phone. Not sure how long it'll last. The actual charger pay got extremely hot and plugged into the wall"
    },
    {
        "review": "excellency"
    },
    {
        "review": "Works great"
    },
    {
        "review": "My wife uses this all the time. She uses it at work to charge her phone, her vapes, her AirPods, and her charging banks. It hooks right to her work keys and doesn't add any bulk or weight to them. It is very durable and extremely easy to use. It charges her stuff pretty quickly. It has both a lighting charger and a usb-c charger which makes it very versatile and very convenient. It functions exactly as it should. It looks sleek. It's made well. The cords aren't long but they're made to go on your keys so it makes sense that they're not. This charging keychain is worth the money."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is indeed a fast, incredibly compact charger that - along with the short USB cord - easily fits into a pocket without creating a bulky bulge. If you're a minimalist traveler, this is about as small and lightweight as it gets.The drawback of a short cord is that your access to the device may be limited while charging - but it charges so quickly that you won't be without for long.I like the \"keychain\" aspect because I can clip this to the internal lanyard in my backpack, the zipper on my laptop sleeve or the clip in my tote bag. It stays on deck for quick access without digging for a tangled 6ft cable.The quick-release connector feels sturdy enough to hang the lightweight charger, but I'd be reluctant to trust it with a heavy keyring until after further testing.In my first test it did get a bit hot - but I in further testing it's stayed surprisingly cool. Unfortunately I didn't note what that first scenario was - will update if it happens again.This is most certainly on the pricier end. I'd think of it is a \"miniaturization tax\" - the premium is for the engineering to make this thin and the cables doubling as lanyards. It also looks pretty cool. Worth it for a zero-bulk setup but probably overkill if you just need a charger for your nightstand. Only time will tell how long it lasts."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’ve used the Ugreen QI2 Power Bank for a couple of days now and it has been a great product for me. I use a lot of Ugreen’s items and this is no different. You pay slightly more than for other products, but you get a high quality item with a trusted brand. It’s very slim and doesn’t bulk up your phone too much. In terms of charging, it wirelessly charged my phone from 25% to 60% in about 30 minutes. I usually recharge it after 2 days of use, which I think is great considering how thin and powerful this device is. If you’re looking for a small and reliable wireless power bank, this is a high quality and high value one."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very slim battery for my s24 ultra with magsafe case. Got fast wireless charging and wired charging, usually can charge my battery to 70-80% while in use. 100% if left to charge with screen off. I would recommend"
    },
    {
        "review": "I didn't see anywhere on the product page that, while the battery is \"5000mAh\", it's rated capacity is just 3000. I actually expected it since many of the ultra-thin batteries are this way, but it would be nice if UGREEN were more upfront about it.The magnets are strong on my iPhone 16 Pro with a thin case. The battery is very small and lightweight, perfect for emergency topups as the evening goes on. But don't expect this to have enough juice to live-stream for 20 hours."
    },
    {
