[
    {
        "review": "I was hesitant to buy one of these because of the reviews about fires. Don't pay attention to those reviews. This little trickle charger keeps your car battery at full and in brand new condition. I read somewhere online that if you put a brand new AGM battery in your car like I did and keep this NOCO Genius10 hooked up, the battery can theoretically last up to 10 years because the NOCO will continuously keep it charged and repaired. It seems that my battery was not the problem with my car as the starter relay on the clutch needed replacing so now my car starts again. But I put in a new AGM battery anyways and won't have to worry about replacing it for another 7-10 years as long as I keep the NOCO attached when not driving the car for long periods of time.As for the NOCO functionality itself it has a couple buttons, one to choose what kind of battery you are using, regular 12V, AGM, or Lithium Ion. The other button I believe is for what kind of charge you want(trickle, decharge, repair) but since I have a brand new battery I simply keep it on trickle charge.The cord length is not very long so in order for my NOCO to reach my car battery and the wall socket in my garage I used a decent gauge extension cord. The instructions say not to use an extension cord but there is no other way since my wall outlet in my garage is too far away from the car battery. I keep a smoke detector next to the NOCO and battery just to be safe. I got the NOCO on sale during Prime Day so it is definitely a good value for the money. So far so good."
    },
    {
        "review": "Purchased the NOCO Genius charger in hopes it would resurrect my battery.  Un fortunately, it did not save my battery, but I cannot blame that on the charger.The only complaint I have is the lack of instructions.  They were not minimal, there were none at all provided with the unit.  Luckily, able to look on line and find plenty of videos, however, this does not negate the need for an instruction and care pamphlet.The unit feels solidly built and works as expected.  While it did not resurrect my battery as it claims it can do (not in all situations), mine was 5 years old, lead acid and probably just to far gone for help.  However, it is doing a great job charging  my marine battery and using it to keep it charged until used again.I like it.  Much more compact than the older styles and easily able to mount to a wall or post as a charging station.  I would definitely buy again."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have a battery charger made in the 1970s, inherited from dad that passed away in 2011. It was time for another one, and I was going to buy another Schumacher that weights about 15 Lbs. Was ready to pull the trigger and decided to see if something better was out there, thus buying a Genius 10 instead based on YouTube reviews.The Genius 10 was much larger and heavier than how it looks in the picture. The build quality is really good in my eyes, looks like tough ABS polymer, very nice cords with that good feeling wire jacket insulation. The new clamps are nice looking and very practical to me. It's heavy and awkward to store, so I bought the Noco case as well; I thought the other case was too small in size.I ran some test with it, on a 12V Honda Lead Acid and Group H8 AGM battery and was happy the results. It was more intuitive than the 1970s version I have with 30 amp boost that is scary to use. What I like with Noco or Genius, it's several tools in one unit, so every 3 or 4 months, I can use the Genius to check the status of all my batteries, well that is the plan at least.  One neat thing, using the 12V output to keep a battery online while changing a battery, so the cars computer keeps running and doesn't reboot from removing the battery causing weird things to happen.I have no regrets in my purchase and bought the case to enhance it more. I think the price is reasonable as well considering what a $100 buys today."
    },
    {
        "review": "EDIT 2/26/24: I am now the blocks \"AAA\".  Been helping people start their cars when jump starts with cables have not worked.  Definitely handy to get other people out of an otherwise expensive pinch.I have a car battery that I purchased around 2016 (date of review 1/3/24).  The car itself does not get driven much, at most 2-3 times a week no longer than 15 minutes one way.Throughout the years I've drained it by leaving the car lights on.  Its always required a jump start after that to get going again.  Recently I've been an idiot and been leaving my lights on more frequently.  Eventually it required me to jump start everytime I wanted to turn on the car.  It was becoming a hassle and I was about to call it quits and purchase a new battery until I came across Project Farm's review on battery chargers.  This was at the top of the list so I figured to give it a shot.I was not disappointed!  I charged it for 4 days straight, put it in my car, and it started right up.  Not surprised considering it was just charged but the real test laid ahead.  I was going to be out of town for two weeks and leave the car sitting.  I came back two weeks later and the car started up, no hesitation whatsoever, as if it was a different battery!The NOCO Genius 10 saved me about $150-200 at least in a brand new battery.  On top of that, I can now use it for other batteries in the event of any similar issues.  The instructions on the other hand are a bit confusing and had to rely on YouTube comments to piece it together.For those who are confused at what to do, I did not do a 12V repair (function which this unit has) as it requires the battery to be completely charged first.  All I did was charge it straight for 4 days uninterrupted.When first put on battery to the charger it will be in standby mode.  You push (or hold depending on what you need) the MODE button to select your desired option.  I was charging a lead acid battery so I selected 12V.  The meter at the top slowly advanceD from each of the four bars until the final bar was pulsing green which indicates its charging to full (over 80% I believe).  The green charging light continued to slowly pulse even on the 4th day but I took a gamble and disconnected it from the battery.  For the battery to be 100% charged, the green light should stay solid.  That means my battery worked 2 weeks later after sitting and it wasn't even at 100%.The unit can also force a charge on batteries that are extremely under voltage.  Thats a separate setting that I haven't had to use yet.  It can also charge AGM and Lithium but I believe the 12V repair function is only for lead acid.Unfortunately I had to go through 3 separate orders because the first two were from Amazon Warehouse and I encountered issues with both, consecutively.  I ended up getting frustrated and just purchased a brand new charger.Pros:Solid build qualityExcellent cable connections with weather coversCompatible with a wide variety of batteriesRepair and Force charge batteriesCons:Poor instructionsCharge is slow BUT I think thats how these chargers workTL;DRTry this first before rushing to get a new battery it is a good investment that can save you a lot of money"
    },
    {
        "review": "Had to replace the charger after 1 year but the warranty process was painless. The quality of the charger seems good but since it quit working after only 1 year I don't know if it will last as long as my 30 year old charger I've had for years. I mostly use this charger to charge my AGM batteries and to repair lead acid batteries, which it seems to do a decent job at in most cases but your milage may vary. Overall I'm satisfied with the charger and for the price it's not bad."
    },
    {
        "review": "Works fantastic! I had the Genius 5 and it worked very well also until my ex got away with it. So this time I ordered the ten and it didn't disappoint.  Had an Interstate Megatron battery that had sat dead for a few months. Charged it in a few hours and its running like new ever since. I also like the recondition setting.  Used it on a deep cycle battery and it brought it back to life as well."
    },
    {
        "review": "I just bought this after researching what is the best battery charger or maintainer for owning a Riptide pool vacuum system. This is for personal use and not running a business. Advice for new pool owners or even existing ones, do not buy a junky 500-1500 dollar pool robot, but a hammerhead or Riptide vacuum. Long story short I bought this maintainer to charge the vacuum battery and maintain it between uses. Charged it in no time and I also use this for my Yamaha 700 ATV. Fantastic unit. Only regret is before I opened this, I didn't test it on an ATV battery that died on me to test it's recovery mode. Chance are that I gave the kid at Advanced Auto parts a free ATV/motorcycle battery because if he had one of these NOCO 10s, chances are he saved the battery and got new life into it. Cant go wrong with this especially for the fast charging, force recharge mode, and versatility to charge, maintain, and breathe batteries back to life. Just one more thing, First time charging the battery after sitting idle for 3 weeks and 2 uses in my case and charged it to full literally in 5 min. I like the unit for keeping the battery at full between uses and not overcharging costing me $300 for a new battery. Well worth the money for less worry and hassle. Hope this helped someone with whatever they were looking to use this for. Also cable length is more than sufficient. Im sure there's an extension option if needed too."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve used this charger for 3 years now and it hasn't let me down once. It’s simple to operate and incredibly compact compared to those giant rolling cart chargers from the past. The optional permanent eyelet leads make maintenance charging on hard-to-reach or detachable RV batteries effortless. Excellent value for the money—I'm buying another one to leave permanently in my RV to keep the house batteries topped off."
    },
    {
        "review": "excellent"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Even I got issue with the item, they sent a new one to. Thanks!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The charger arrived in one day, the price on Amazon is high compared to other sites, however the reception in one day was in my favor. It was recommended to me by a friend who is dedicated to automotive mechanics, my truck barely started, especially on Mondays after not using it on Saturdays and Sundays, the first two photographs show the condition of the accumulator (LTH AGM 48, 760CCA and 70AH) before using the NOCO Genius10, basically it seemed that the accumulator was well charged however it went down quickly and lacked starting power, after connecting it to the Genius10 and letting it perform a full charge (approximately about 4 hours and until the green LED stopped flashing), and then the repairer ran for approximately 4 hours plus the battery was completely restored, as can be seen in the following two photographs. Once installed back in my truck, starting is immediate and effortless. The battery had already been charged before with other different chargers, but it did not work well almost immediately, it gave problems starting again and the SOH (state of health) was still in the 80s, now it is 100%, likewise the state of charge (SOC) never reached 100%... this charge rehabilitated my accumulator with around two years of use, and due to my carelessness it had been allowed to discharge by leaving accessories on in the truck on several occasions. I highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Brilliant bit of kit. Essential for my ancient Range Rover."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’m really happy with this two pack of MagSafe chargers. The magnetic connection is strong and lines up perfectly with my phone every time, making charging simple and reliable. Charging speeds are fast, and my phone stays securely attached while it charges. I also like that each charger has dual ports, which makes them more versatile and convenient to use in different locations. The cables feel durable, and the charging pads are lightweight enough to keep at home, in the office, or while traveling."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good chargersI loved these wireless chargers. There are two in the package, so it's super convenient to have one for different places in the house or even take a spare one. They connect easily and the magnet keeps the phone well placed while charging. I found them very comfortable to charge the cell phone during the night or while I'm using the phone. In addition, for the price of both, I think it's an excellent purchase. The quality feels quite good and so far they have worked perfectly. I definitely recommend them if you are looking for practical, simple and economical chargers."
    },
    {
        "review": "This 2-pack is a great value. The chargers are well made, connect easily, and charge my phone consistently. The magnetic attachment is strong, and the cables feel durable. Everything works as expected, and I’m very happy with this purchase. Highly recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "I picked up this 2-pack of 15W MagSafe-style chargers because I wanted something I could keep by the bed and another for my desk at work. For the price, these actually surprised me. The magnets are noticeably strong — not Apple-strong, but strong enough that my phone snaps into place without having to wiggle it around. Charging speed is about what I expected from a third-party 15W pad. It’s not blazing fast, but it’s consistent, and I haven’t noticed any random disconnects or overheating. The build quality also feels better than some of the cheap plastic ones I’ve tried before; these have a slightly soft matte finish that doesn’t scratch up easily.Day-to-day use has been pretty smooth. The cable is long enough to reach awkward outlets, and the pad stays cool even when charging overnight. One thing I appreciate is how flat the design is — it doesn’t rock or slide around, even on my slippery nightstand. The LED indicator is subtle, too, which is a huge plus for me because I hate bright lights at night. I’ve been able to toss my phone on the charger half-asleep and it just works. That reliability alone makes it better than most of the budget chargers I've bought over the years.My only real gripe — and the reason this isn’t a 5-star review — is that the magnetic alignment isn’t perfect with thicker cases. It works flawlessly on my slim case, but on my partner’s bulkier one, it sometimes charges a little slower or doesn't grab dead-center. It’s not a dealbreaker, just something to be aware of if you use rugged cases. Overall, though, for a two-pack at this price, these chargers do exactly what they claim. Good quality, decent speed, and very convenient. I’d absolutely buy them again."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good quality and affordable magnetic wireless charging discs. Works well and charges fast in an hour.Compact size is great for traveling options. Lightweight and easy to pack. Feels durable. Two for the price of one means I can share with a family member. I definitely recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've had these for a while and they work just fine. They don't charge my phone fast, but I mainly use them to charge my airpods overnight because the charger port stopped working. They stick my my MagSafe phone case well. I don't really get the point in using it to charge your phone unless you need to use the port for something else."
    },
    {
        "review": "Don’t buy it for everyday use. Fire hazard or face burn risk due to overheating of the smartphone and the charger, device battery life might get depleted.ProsAffordableEasy to connectUSB to type c connector in box.ConsNo adapter in boxSlow charging (15W) 4.5 hrs to charge.Gets hot very fast, I am surprised that neither phone or this charger disconnect the charging due to overheating of both the charger and the device."
    },
    {
        "review": "An excellent magnetic charger; the package includes two of them. It is very easy to use—I just place it on the back of my phone and it starts charging, so I no longer need to plug cables directly into the phone. The magnet keeps it securely in place, it doesn't overheat, and my phone charges quickly. It’s a great product; I would definitely buy it again."
    }
]

