[
    {
        "review": "Fully compatible with Windows 11 and a clear upgrade over the built-in camera on my HP computer.The video quality is noticeably better, and the microphone performs well too. Picture and sound are both solid, making it a reliable option for calls and meetings.It also has the little thingy to block the camera for privacy, which is a nice touch. For meetings, programs such as Zoom, Google Meet, or Microsoft Teams include mute controls, adding another layer of privacy and control.Friendly suggestion: mine came with a USB-A connector. It works fine, but it would be even better if it used USB-C or came with both options. I bought it a while back, so by now it may already include USB-C.Overall, it delivers strong performance and dependable quality at a very competitive price point"
    },
    {
        "review": "✅ great value for my money✅ easy to set up with my PC✅ love the video quality and auto focus on my face when I record✅ connects without a problem to my Pc. I just plug in the USB portion"
    },
    {
        "review": "If video streaming is a way you make money, do NOT buy this. This webcam + microphone is not for professional level video streaming.If you need a webcam + mic device that is good enough, and performs better than most/all laptop integration webcams, then just buy this and call it a day. There are a lot of options, but I promise that unless you are a really particular human, you will be happy with this product.a) WfH business person taking video calls for work = YESb) private individual streaming to connect with friends/family = YESc) a recreational streamer = YESDetailed review notes below....**MOST IMPORTANT THING TO KNOW**The camera can only go so far, but a lot of what determines the final video quality is what YOU do to create a good video streaming environment. Read: If you are in a windowless cave 50' below Earth's surface with no artificial lighting, poor video quality is on you, not the device.Lighting and distance of the camera from your face are THE MOST IMPORTANT VARIABLES in determining whether this camera performs well or not. I posted a photo of my specific camera placement and lighting and desk situation, and have tested out four different lighting scenarios (listed below) to show the impact of lighting on the video quality.**REVIEW NOTES**Each number 1-4 below has a matching image that I have attached to this review:1. Only natural light from my office windows (indirect sunlight)2. #1 + clip-on desk lamp with warm colored LED*MY FAVORITE SETUP* 3. #2 + recessed ceiling lights (3\" white colored LEDs with 8' ceilings)4. Natural light from windows + recessed ceiling lights (NO desk lamp)*NOTE*: Each image was taken via Windows Snipit tool while waiting to join a Google MeetingBOTTOM LINE, you have to mess around with your lighting and camera distance to get the sweet spot foryour specific environment, and may require additional lighting sources (e.g. lamp) to get it right.The EMEET app is super easy to install and provides decent enough picture settings to tweak the image quality without being overkill. No login/account/signup required. I recommend keeping the \"white balance\" on AUTO at all times."
    },
