    {
        "review": "I can definitely say, after hooking up this camera, that it does its job perfectly.  The video quality for making video calls was perfectly clear.  The audio aspect was equally impressive.  The microphones seemed to pick up the voice from a couple of feet away from it (sitting at the computer desk) but wasn't overwhelmed by any background noise.  Whether this is a design function utilizing noise cancellation or just a matter of it not being a very noisy environment remains to be seen.The snap down cover for privacy is about as basic as it gets.  A well fitting plastic lens blocker on a hinge, but really what more do you need to achieve those results?The only complaint I would have (and it's being very very picky I suppose) is the way it \"mounts\" on the monitor.  While it initially sat quite still and steady, as soon as I reached up to tweak the positioning it shifted all over the place.  This was very easily rectified, however, with about 5 cents worth of electrical tape to hold the clip solidly to the top/back of the monitor.  So in reality, it's not so much a \"complaint\" about it as a VERY minor inconvenience.In summary, high quality, great sound, great picture, very easy to install and use.  I'd certainly recommend it to anyone looking for an affordable camera with built in mic."
