        "review": "The box for this is quite sturdy although not very visually impressive. Acer should put more effort into their packaging, particularly on a premium product like this.These are my main likes and dislikes for this product:Like:Sony 1/2 “ sensor4K HDRPremium lensesFull metal bodyCompact and portableGood overall build qualityFully Plug & PlayDislike:Expensive at £79.99 rrpLens cover falls off too easilyAs you can see there is a lot I like about this webcam. The image it produces look very natural, being not too colourful or contrasty, with just the right balance. The sharpness at 4K is a noticeable improvement over 1080p or even 1440p, as long as you have a monitor good enough to see the difference of course. The Sony CMOS sensor is good at controlling signal noise, so the fuzziness is kept to a minimum in low light, and is far better than a standard webcam with a generic cheap sensor.The autofocus is surprisingly good, again this is due to the sensor and chip combination. Tracking actually works in most instances, which I have not seen on a webcam before.The dual mics work very well and remove background noise almost completely. Voices are clear, even multiple voices can be heard perfectly within about six feet of the camera.Installation was a few seconds, as it is plug and play. This is being used on Windows 11 but it should also work on Apple Macintosh computers.The lens cap is a bit of a disappointment, it is not strong enough and is easy to knock off when handling the camera. A more powerful magnet is needed.The current price for this is £66 which I think is reasonable, and at that price it’s going to get a solid five stars."
