    },
    {
        "review": "I bought one about 5 or 6 weeks ago and like it so much I just ordered another. They are very bendable in every direction including the head of the lamp.The clamp is sturdy enough to hold the unit securely in place. Plus, after looking at many available adjustable lamps, this inexpensive light has more lumens than more expensive adjustable lamps. As an artist this is a must have. I do very large paintings as well as small drawings, paintings as well as multi dimensional sculptural art and I wanted a second light to use while drawing on a lap desk outside my studio. I didn’t hesitate to buy another one of these.The long bar that holds the lamp can be twisted to focus in every direction. I also use it for applying makeup since it’s just really utilitarian.It’s a weird looking contraption that reminds me of the old War of The Worlds movie’s depiction of the aliens😂 but the two settings are another handy feature.Use the adapter plug it comes with. It’s cheap but different adapters can cause it to not turn on. Make sure the clamp has a flat surface on the underneath part of the clamp - it must be able to fully accommodate the round clamp that moves up and down from below.Packed in a good box, arrived fast and nothing to put together."
