l features ensures complete satisfaction. As a member of the Vine program, I have reviewed this product completely independently and honestly. I remain at your entire disposal to resolve any additional questions or queries that may arise in this regard."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a lightweight desk lamp.  The base of the lamp is covered in a felt material.  The head of the light can be easily rotated so it can swivel left and right and the flexible arm is coated in a soft silicone material and bends easily.  It also maintains the position you bend it into and doesn't sag since the head of the light is relatively light.  The button controls are not individual buttons, they're plastic bubble buttons.  Once the flexible arm is connected, it cannot be removed.  The back of the lamp is just a plastic housing, no metal there to help dissipate heat, but even so I found that the back of the light only got slightly warm even at maximum brightness.  Not even warm enough to be used as a hand warmer.The light has 5 brightness levels and the light is a very even diffuse light pattern and a wide cast area.  The light output at maximum is quite bright, but not bright enough to over saturate printed material which would make it unreadable.  The night light mode provides a much dimmer light output than is achievable with the brightness controls.  It works very well as a night light.  By default when pressing the night light button, the color temperature is warm.  You can cycle through the other color temperatures after selecting night light mode.  In order to get out of night light mode, you need to increase the brightness.  When you turn the light off and turn it back on, it will remember which mode it was in last and use the same mode as it was in when it was turned off, this also applies to the night light mode, not just the brightness and color temperature.  The brightness of the light isn't controlled via PWM, so it is flicker free.  The 4 LEDs on the base illuminate to tell you which timer setting you're on.Due to the fact that the base is very lightweight and doesn't have any heft to it, you cannot move the head of the light too far away from the base.  If you do, the imbalance of the weight will just cause the light to fall over.  Also accidental bumps can knock it over easily.  A heavier weighted base would help a lot here to allow for maximum range of positioning.  I have another old fashioned halogen bulb desk lamp and it has a very heavily weighted base even though the head is lighter than this unit's head and it has very good stability as a result.The remote is a wireless remote and not an IR remote so there's no need to point it at the lamp to use it.  I tested it, and it has very good range, going through 3 walls with ease.The base has a felt layer on the bottom providing some grip to keep it from easily sliding around.  Although there is a USB-A and USB-C ports on the back, you need to provide your own cables.Included is a 12V/2A barrel connector power adapter, however it isn't UL or ETL certified, but then again neither is the lamp."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’m very happy with the this purchase for my son’s dorm room desk. All the different outlets are great, and the multiple brightness/natural light color options are nice. We did use a non-slip coaster under the base so it doesn’t move because it’s light weight, but it also comes with little stickers as well."
    },
    {
        "review": "The first one I bought lasted less than an hour, then the light went out and it stopped charging my phone (that was the only extra thing I had plugged into it).  I switched outlets twice and unplugged it for an hour and tried it again (even though I knew that wouldn't do anything) and it was done. It wouldn't work.  I was disappointed because it was a perfect lamp for my needs.I almost just returned it for a refund but it was too good not to try one more time. I'm glad I did. The second one was sent to me about a month ago and it's worked perfectly since. I use this on my desk at work so on average it's used, either as just a charger or a charger and a lamp, for an average of 40ish hours a week for a month with no issues.The light brightness is adjustable so it's as bright as you want it to be (very bright on its highest setting).  The neck adjusts in 2 spots so you can easily get it to the angle you need.  The charging ports all work great and I use those every work day, as many as 3 at a time (there are 4).  I haven't used the plugs much because I haven't needed them but they all work.If you think this fits your needs then definitely buy it.  Just use it way before the return date in case you happen to get a dud like I initially did."
    },
    {
        "review": "Perfect desk lamp for my son’s college dorm room. He loves the power surge strip on the lamp; with few outlets in his room, this is a great use of space."
    },
