[
    {
        "review": "Love that it has different modes, and very easy to use and store! Works like wonder! I even used it as my night lamp by folding the light up!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my second ine of these. Love it. Can easily get any amount of light I need."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this lamp to use on a grand piano at church. The arm reaches across reasonably well from the side (though it doesn’t extend far enough to be fully centered over the music desk). The multiple color temperatures and brightness levels are very helpful for accommodating the preferences of various users, and all our pianists seem to like it.It works smoothly and perfectly... in most keys.BUT if you like to play in D-flat, beware! I just discovered that the resonance point of the casing appears to be a D-flat (138.591 Hz). The plastic started buzzing quietly when playing strong tonic chords in that key. This was, of course, horrifying.I assume the same disturbing outcome holds true when playing in C-sharp major, since the identical notes are used, but I only had sheet music in D-flat today. More testing would be needed to determine whether the issue extends to enharmonic keys, but this didn’t seem urgent to share here, since:• I didn’t want to go into too much detail that isn’t relevant to the average consumer (because we all hate that), and• Only psychos play in C-sharp major anyway.I realize this acoustic phenomenon may not affect all potential buyers of this lamp, but it seems like this particular harmonic bug could be mentioned somewhere in the description—if not in the product title itself—just so that members of the five-flats-loving community have some warning.Oh, also, the buzzing stopped as soon as I moved the arm slightly, so there’s that."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been using this lamp since July 2017 and it still functioning well.  It's light weight, so it's easy to move around, and does not take much space!  The brightness can be adjusted easily.  I love it and hope it will stay with me for a very long time!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I like the lamp. The controls are easy to see and use. I only wish it seemed more solid and that the horizontal top bar with light could swivel to aim light 45 degrees to a side."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very sleek, modern looking lamp with a variety of lighting levels.  It matches my black glass desktop very nicely, adding a sophisticated modern look. Contrary to what some reviewers said, I think it has a relatively small footprint on the desk, which is nice because I'd rather utilize the desktop space for working instead of a huge lamp. I've wiped it down here for the photos, but do realize that it is a dust/fingerprint/cat hair collector.  Smudges show up, so if you're not willing to wipe it down every now and then you might be disappointed with it's overall aesthetic look. Pro tip: I keep a pack of Pledge multi-surface wipes (Pledge Multi Surface Everyday Wipes Fresh Citrus, 25-Count  (Pack of 4)) in a drawer near my desk to wipe both it and the lamp down - takes a few seconds and looks as good as new.I mostly use this lamp at its lowest setting, as it provides a nice ambience to my work area. Each of the preset light levels can be brightened and dimmed. If I'm going to be doing real work, the light gets bright enough by itself to make reading from a textbook or paperwork comfortable and without strain.  Usually one of the reading or middle settings is  as bright as I'll go for reading actual pages from a book, and I only use the brightest settings if I'm struggling to see something small like jewelry or I'm fiddling with some component or part of my computer. It does get quite bright. I haven't used the timer function, but there is an automatic 60 minute timer included. Overall, it's a versatile little lamp.I got mine on sale at Christmas during a flash sale, for thirty something dollars, and I think it's well worth it. The listed price, however, is complete rubbish - total waste to pay full price regardless of how well it works, as it is simply made up of plastic and LED bulbs.  Wait for a sale and you'll be happy with it.  I've included photos of the lamp with various light levels and in different positions."
