    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered this for better lighting for miniature painting as well as lighting up my desk area. It is a light lamp and has a heavy base, I incorrectly ordered this instead of the mounting one to gain desk space, which is a small foot print so not terrible. The simple minimalist look is sleek and contemporary meeting almost any desk or setup universally.The lamp feels sturdy and solid but you can tell the material is not all metal but some pressed plastic or much cheaper thin alloy material which is non-magnetic, maybe thin aluminum. The buttons are touch sensors not actual clicky buttons so that could put some folks off but non-issue for me.The lighting has color adjustments so you can light to you preference whether warm, cool, or cold and even has an automatic brightness and stepping feature built in. Honestly I though the brightness feature was a gimmick however using it as a back light in my office has improved my eye comfort from long periods at the computer for work.While the lamp is very easy to adjust and stays in place when moved the information presented makes it seem like the lamp head would rotate 180º which it does just not in the direction expected, meaning the lamp must always be parallel to the surface it is placed on no exceptions. I dinged it a star because of this as the image shown seems to be a bit misleading whether intentional or not.It uses a power adapter with barrel socket to the lamp so is not portable and does not charge, has no remote though there are auto stepping and brightness features you must manually activate the lamp."
