        "review": "As a treat to myself I did a work desk refresh and did a purple desk haul. Getting all the same shade of purple is a challenge, but I am picky about what I want out of a desk lamp. I can't lie I was prepared to be disappointed but I found myself pleasantly surprised with this little lamp. I found the size of the lamp to be just perfect. I love that I can change the lamp from a warm light to a cold light. (I prefer warm light most days) You can make the light as bright or as dim as you want, I just have it turned all the way up. Its got a sturdy base and is powered by USB-C so you can give it a longer cord if needed."
    },
    {
        "review": "I like that this desk lamp has a small footprint and can be placed off to the side, out of the way, but then using the gooseneck the light can be brought in where it is needed. I also like that it is quite bright and can be dimmed from low light to full output. The light color itself can be adjusted between 3 levels, warm, cool or a mix of warm and cool. I personally prefer the white cool light as it seems like a better color for a work light. I don’t use the ambient sensor function so can’t comment. The base is heavy and holds the lamp without tipping even when the gooseneck is cantilevered far out. There is a light diffuser on the end of the lamp shade which can be removed if you want the full blast harsh light, which may be more useful in some situations. There is a usb charger port. The dimming control is a little funky and the click stops were not expected. I would rather have a smooth silent dimmer than one with detents. Also the range of lowest light  to highest light is not very wide. Nevertheless, at this price point there isn’t much to complain about. This is a nice bright lamp with more functionality than one would expect at such a low price and seems well made. It is recommended."
