        "review": "This is a 14 inch (measured with the light facing down and neck curved) small desk lamp that provides about 60watts of light [it says 280 lumens but it is much brighter than a 25 watt bulb]. It is very bright at a daylight hue of 5000k.There is no way to change the LED or change the hue of the LED. So once the light dies, the entire lamp is tossed. The lamp has a plastic diffusing cover that seals the lampshade and ability to replace the bulb.The stand flat and you can place decor on it. It has a black protective layer at the bottom to not scratch wood tables.I own a similar sized lamp and have used it for over 2 decades...but the bulb is replaceable.  It seems like a waste to toss this once the LED dies.As a note, all LEDs have a limited life and like everything else, burn out and need replacement."
