[
    {
        "review": "I wasn’t sure how much of a difference such a small air purifier would make, but I have to say, I’m really impressed with this one. It does exactly what I wanted it to do, and I’ve been very happy with it.First of all, it’s really quiet. That was important to me because I didn’t want something that sounded like a fan running all day and night. I can have this going while I’m working, watching TV, or sleeping and barely notice it.It’s also the perfect size. It doesn’t take up much room at all, but it still feels like it’s doing a great job keeping the air fresher. I love that I can just put it on a nightstand, desk, or dresser and pretty much forget it’s there.The controls are super simple, and having three different fan speeds is nice depending on how much airflow I want. I also really like the aromatherapy feature. Adding a little essential oil is such a nice touch and makes the room smell fresh and relaxing.Another thing I appreciate is that it doesn’t feel cheap or flimsy. It has a nice clean design, works exactly like it should, and there really isn’t anything complicated about using it.For me, this is one of those purchases where I thought, \"why didn’t I get one of these sooner?\". If you’re looking for a small air purifier for your bedroom, office, or another smaller space, I would definitely recommend this one.It’s quiet, easy to use, doesn’t take up much space, and does exactly what it says it will do.Very happy with my purchase. Definitely 5 stars!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this air purifier for my bedroom. My dog has a very severe dust mite allergy. He was literally disintegrating. His hair was falling out and his dandruff was like a blizzard. He had full body yeast and it smelled like a dirty gym sock on steroids.Despite having no carpet, rugs and bedding that are washed weekly, and dust mite covers on both of our beds, he was still miserable.  He is so allergic that out of desperation I'm trying everything I possibly can to minimize his exposure while his immunotherapy does its job.The vet said that short of having hospital level air purification I would never get rid of all the dust mites, but I can limit his exposure with air purifiers, so we are giving it a try. There's no way I can accurately gauge how much this air purifier is reducing the dust mites, but it has to be better than it was before I got it.My dog gets 3 medicated baths a week and is about to start immunotherapy, so I can't really credit any progress to the air purifier alone, but there is no doubt it will help reduce the total number of dust mites he is exposed to.I also got a larger air purifier for my living room/kitchen. I live in a camper currently as I recently moved and am building a home. Since we live in cramped quarters with less ventilation than a sticks and bricks home, the dust mites and other allergens are far more concentrated.I've noticed since having these two purifiers running that our home smells fresher and cleaner, any smells do not linger. I've tried my hardest to deep clean any dust collected around the house in all the little nooks and crannies that you can't see and hopefully the purifiers will help keep that to a minimum. For some reason even in the dead of winter we seem to have a lot of dust. Again, probably because the space is so small. It seems the smaller the space, the bigger the mess! Thankfully it doesn't take as long to clean a smaller space.I'm not sure if I'll ever really know how effective these are, but I can say I've noticed a big difference since I got them in the quality of the air. We have wood heat so there's not a furnace constantly blowing air around. They provide air flow in what used to be pretty stagnant areas in the winter when the a/c isn't running.The stinky sock yeasty dog smell has been reduced quite a bit, and any other lingering smells like cooking or flatulence from my gassy teenager don't tend to hang around as long lol. So they have been a win-win! They seem to work very well.I don't use the timer features because I let them both run 24/7, but it's nice to have that as an option if it's ever needed. I really appreciate the small footprint of this purifier because there's not much room in a camper. I have it on my bedside table. You can see in the picture about how big it is next to my 40oz swig.Even on high it's very quiet, but I'm one of those \"can't sleep without a fan\" people so I enjoy the sound lol. Between this and the fan at the foot of my bed pushing air towards it, our air in the bedroom ought to be squeaky clean!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been really happy with this little air purifier. It’s compact enough to sit on a nightstand or dresser without taking up much space, and it runs quietly, especially at night. I’ve noticed the room smells fresher and there seems to be less dust floating around. Simple to use and works well for a smaller room."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent Compact Air Purifier for Small Spaces5.0 out of 5 stars Compact, Efficient, and Quiet – A Game-Changer for Allergy SufferersI’ve been using the Levoit Core 300 Air Purifier for about two months now in my 200 sq. ft. bedroom, and it’s exceeded my expectations in every way. As someone who deals with seasonal allergies and pet dander from my cat, I was looking for an affordable, reliable solution to improve indoor air quality without breaking the bank or taking up too much space. After researching options, I settled on this model, and I’m thrilled with the results.The setup was incredibly straightforward – just unbox, remove the plastic from the filter, plug it in, and you’re good to go. The design is sleek and modern, with a cylindrical shape that fits neatly on a nightstand or floor corner without dominating the room. At around 8.7 inches in diameter and 14.2 inches tall, it’s compact enough for apartments or offices, yet powerful for its size.Key features include a 3-stage filtration system: a pre-filter for larger particles like dust and hair, a True HEPA filter that captures 99.97% of airborne particles as small as 0.3 microns (think pollen, mold spores, and fine dust), and an activated carbon filter to tackle odors, smoke, and VOCs. It has three fan speeds plus a sleep mode that dims the lights and runs ultra-quietly at just 24dB – quieter than a whisper, making it perfect for nighttime use. There’s also a timer (2/4/6/8 hours) and a display lock to prevent accidental changes.In terms of performance, this little unit punches above its weight. It refreshes the air in a 219 sq. ft. room up to 5 times per hour on high speed, according to the specs. I tested it during a smoky day from nearby wildfires, and within an hour, the air felt noticeably fresher – no lingering smells or stuffiness. My allergy symptoms have reduced significantly; I wake up with clearer sinuses and less sneezing. It’s also energy-efficient, using only about 45W at max, which keeps my electricity bill in check.Pros:• Affordable and great value: At under $100, it outperforms many pricier models in small to medium rooms. 3• Quiet operation: Sleep mode is a lifesaver for light sleepers. 1• Effective filtration: Handles pet dander, dust, and odors exceptionally well. 2• Easy maintenance: Filter replacement is simple, and indicators remind you when it’s time (every 6-8 months).Cons:• No built-in air quality sensor or auto mode – you have to manually adjust speeds (though the upgraded Core 300S adds smart features if you need them). 5• On the highest speed, it can get a bit noisy (around 50dB), but it’s still tolerable for short bursts. 3• Best for rooms under 300 sq. ft.; for larger spaces, you’d need multiple units or a bigger model.Overall, the Levoit Core 300 is a fantastic entry-level air purifier that’s reliable, user-friendly, and effective for everyday use. If you’re dealing with allergies, pets, or just want cleaner air in a small space, I highly recommend it. It’s ETL, CARB, and Energy Star certified, so you know it’s safe and efficient. Worth every penny!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great purifiers, customer service is top notch too, did not receive one unit and they were very helpful. I have 4 small units and one large unit for my 1,600 sq ft apt. Not needing to change my hvac filters as often and no more allergies!!! They emit a soothing white noise that actually helps me nod off to sleep. Highly recomend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this going into my freshman year of college (I'm now about to be a senior) and it seriously is one of the best purchases I made. Even though its mini, its powerful and I feel as though I could notably notice a difference. I think this single handly saved me from getting super sick my freshman year. I brought it home over the summer and could notice a difference with pet odors as well."
    },
    {
        "review": "Slight noise, but if you need white noise to sleep, it's a bonus. Cleans air, has aroma, and size is great for dorms. Perfect for college students needing a breath of fresh air. Recommend for compact spaces!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Found this from a general search, and the price was right and the reviews are good, so I picked one up.We got it to sit near our cat box, to see if it helps at all.  Not too sure about odor control, the only way to really tell would be to turn it back off again and see.  But it IS picking up a lot of fine particles.  A LOT.  After only a couple of weeks, the filter had a good coating, and needed to be vacuumed.On low it is SUPER quiet.  We run it on high because, hey why not.  You can hear it running, but it's not loud at all.Very happy with it so far."
