[
    {
        "review": "I received the Mooka air purifier for home/large room 3/23/26 and I am impressed and completely happy with the purifier.  I’m using it in my bedroom which is a nice larger size and it’s the perfect size and doing a fantastic job.  I live on a roadside and have lots of dust, woods in the back, lots of pollen and a small dog and cat and it’s keeping our air pure.  We suffer with allergies and have not doubt it’s going to make a big difference.It’s made great and looks great.  It’s made for people with pets and has about 6 fan speeds including auto and pet mode. The round air indicator on the front display is clear and easy to see plus the dial changes colors accordingly to air purity and the front provides a nice nightlight.I love that it has a washable filter and a True HEPA filter. It filters smoke, pollen, dander, hair, and smell.  And a definite plus for me the air purifier is 100% Non-BPA and Non-Ozone! Also certified for using recycled and healthier materials for pets and peoples health. Plus a good price.  How it holds up in the long run will be my final thought but so far I would buy again and in fact plan to get another in the future.  I have already been recommending and do recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I previously owned one purifier, an AIRROMI purifier. I kept it near the litter box because phew my cats can be stinky.Unfortunately, one of my cats recently started showing symptoms of asthma. And hearing those attacks he has is honestly extremely scary, knowing I cannot offer him direct relief. So I made the decision to get a second purifier, a bigger one this time. But not just one, I got THREE! Maybe a little over kill but I want to ensure my cat is OKAY!I have had them for about a month and there has been ZERO asthma attacks from my cat. So it is fair to say that all the bad allergens in the air have been going straight to the filter. My boyfriend works in HVAC and he said the HEPA filter combined with the activated charcoal works great for catching particles and allergens. I have yet to open it up to see the damage; the purifier has an alert that will show up on the control panel, letting you know when it is time to change the filter. I will come back and update with pictures once I change the filter on at least one of the purifiers.There is about 3 modes on the purifier, Automatic, Speed 1, 2, 3 and Pet mode. Automatic is hardly detectable in terms of noise. Pet mode and the highest mode are very loud though. I don’t mind the white noise, so I could sleep with it no problem, others might have a problem.As for looks, I think she is really pretty! I absolutely love the reader on the front that determines the air quality, all of ours sit at a range of either 5-7. I very interestingly found that my purifier in my room almost hit 400 after a hot shower, and it did not go down, the numbers fluctuated between 150-350. I unplugged it and then it read 005 again…not sure what that was about, but it only happened once, so I did not think much of it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this for my mom. My siblings don’t visit her because they claimed pet hair/dander was severely triggering their allergies. I thought they were making it up because I personally never had any kind of reaction. Well, I recently I went to visit Mom for a few hours as I normally do, and the trifecta of dust, dander, and pet hair hit me like a ton of bricks. For 3 days, I was having coughing fits, wheezing, and my eyes were itchy and felt like there was dust in them 24/7. My mom already has COPD and frequently complains about being short of breath, so realizing that she was casually breathing all of this in 24/7 completely freaked me OUT. That said, I went on the search for an air purifier and ended up pulling the trigger on this one and can finally report on well it works.Even though at first my mom wasn’t happy that I spent money and bought this for her, after I set it up, she allowed me to leave it running on high if it meant there could be a chance that it might make her air quality suitable for my siblings start visiting again. Well, 6 weeks later, I was able to convince my siblings to come with me to mom’s house to visit for Christmas because now there she has a good air purifier. Upon entering my mom’s house with my family, the first thing I noticed immediately was how much lighter the air way. Before this filter, the air was thick, heavy, and DUSTY. Afternoon light filtering through the blinds would reveal clouds of pet hair and dust particles swirling around like smoke. Now? Nothing! No dust in the air when sunshine is coming though the windows. The second thing I noticed was that the smell of litterbox went from 100% to 40-50%. My family had a wonderful, comfortable holiday visit with my Mom, they were shocked how much of a difference this machine made. No one had any of their allergies triggered. YAY!! My mom, who originally wanted to hate this machine, finally confessed that she’s breathing a lot better lately & believes that it’s due to this machine improving her air. She leaves it running on auto now, when she cooks, it kicks into high gear until the numbers go down. She loves it a lot. Highly recommend this machine."
