[
    {
        "review": "The LEVOIT Vital 200S-P Air Purifier is AHAM certified, meaning it has been independently tested by the Association of Home Appliance Manufacturers for air-cleaning performance, safety, and energy efficiency. Products with the AHAM VERIFIDE seal meet strict appliance-performance standards, giving added confidence in their ability to improve indoor air quality. This air purifier is designed with allergy sufferers in mind, helping capture common airborne irritants such as pollen, pet hair, dander, and dust. Its efficient filtration system traps tiny particles to support fresher, cleaner air for you and your family. Built for spaces up to 1,875 square feet, the Vital 200S-P is a strong choice for living rooms, bedrooms, basements, open-concept homes, high-traffic areas, and households with pets. A traditional air inlet works together with an additional U-shaped air inlet to help capture airborne pet hair and odors more efficiently while reducing the chance of clogs, so the purifier can keep air moving smoothly.Verified CADR RatingsThe Vital 200S-P has been tested with the following Clean Air Delivery Rate ratings:• Smoke: 250 CFM• Dust: 254 CFM• Pollen: 289 CFMAfter looking at several air purifiers, this LEVOIT looked to be exactly what I was looking for. It received complimentary reviews and was reasonably priced. It is very quiet and comes with the option to turn the control panel lights off, perfect for bedroom use during the night. This has been a great purchase for my family."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this LEVOIT air purifier for a while now, and I’m very happy with it. It was easy to set up, and it runs very quietly, even at night.I noticed the air feels fresher, and it does a great job reducing dust and everyday odors. I also like that it has different fan speeds, so I can adjust it depending on what I need.The build quality is excellent, and the controls are simple to use. Overall, it’s been a great addition to my home, and I would definitely recommend it to anyone looking for an effective and reliable air purifier."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this air purifier because with all the animal hair, dust, and seasonal allergens floating around, I was coughing constantly- night and day. I happened to get it a little on sale, and while the cost is a little high, it has proven its worth to the penny. It comes with multiple speeds, modes, and most importantly the sleep function. When its in night/sleep mode, its still releasing air but there is no light pollution or any sounds. It is so quiet I forget its on. I also see a vast improvement on my air quality and I no longer wake up the whole household at night with my coughing. It does its best work in one room, but I have noticed that the room its in has less dust. Ive also noticed it is a little if a deoderizor, which is great for someone who has a sensitive nose. Overall, yes its a little expensive upfront but the design of it, the quality of its work, and being able to finally sleep through the night is priceless. I dont know about its longevity but I did buy a very small and older version from this manufacturer 3 years ago and its still going."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've not had the purifier for a full 30 days yet, but so far it is excellent! I did thorough research when replacing my MedifyAir purifier and found that Levoit is one of the few that is actually 3rd party tested and thus markets the correct numbers of how much space it can cover, unlike MedifyAir and some others brands. I am very impressed with the packaging, the ease of set up, and that you don't have to use the app unless you want to. Though the app is very nice. It has some nice smart features, but again, you don't have to use them if you don't want. You can literally plug it in and turn it on and go. I also like the fact that the filters are cheaper than what I have been used to buying and they last longer! So more efficient, longer lasting, cheaper filters, covers more space, WIN-WIN!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been using the Levoit 200S-P in a bedroom, and it's been a great balance of performance, noise level, and convenience.Setup took just a few minutes, and pairing it with the VeSync app was straightforward. I like being able to check the air quality, adjust the fan speed, create schedules, and turn it on before I get home.Auto mode works well and usually keeps the fan quiet unless it detects a noticeable change in air quality. It's nice when I'm cooking and the lights will blink red indicating the air quality has changed and it will kick on high speed.For everyday use, it's very quiet on the lower settings, making it easy to sleep with. On the highest speed it moves a lot more air, but as expected it's much louder. I typically leave it in Auto mode and rarely have to adjust it.The filter has done a good job reducing dust and everyday odors in the room. While no air purifier can eliminate every smell instantly, I've noticed the room feels fresher, and there's less dust settling on furniture over time. It's also very easy to clean.A few things to keep in mind: replacement filters aren't the cheapest, and this unit is best suited for bedrooms or other smaller spaces. If you're trying to clean the air in a large open living area, you'll probably want to step up to a larger model like the Core 400S or 600S.Overall, if you're looking for a reliable, easy-to-use smart air purifier for a bedroom or office, I'd recommend the Levoit 200S-P. It's quiet, simple to maintain, and has performed exactly as I hoped."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this for my living room and kitchen with an open concept of around 540 sq. Ft.  It took about 4 hours for the light to change from red to blue.  I can't really tell a difference because I'm home all the time, however my guests say it smells fresher.  I have 2 cats and a dog and their hair and dander is a nightmare! I've already cleaned off the front and the screen twice in two weeks, so that shows it working, but  I still have some dust and hair floating around just not quite as bad, however I did shave my long thick hair coated dog and that helped alot!From the reviews I expected more out of this, my allergies haven't changed I'm still congested and use meds for that, but I also have various food allergies.I put this unit in a high traffic area and center of living room and kitchen.  I've noticed my TV doesn't have near as much dust and hair accumulation on the screen.  For the price it's okay, it doesn't compare to the real expensive ones perhaps,  but it does help."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a very attractive and easy unit to use.  The filter is easily replaced, and the sleep mode is fantastic!  It is quiet at any speed but barely noticeable on Level 2.  WE can feel the difference in the freshness of the air in the home.  Less sneezing and coughing! :)"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a sleek shaped purifier that fits well in our hallway. We are using it on our top floor to help with the smokey weather we are experiencing outside that’s seeping inwards.In the first couple of days it has already helped with the air quality and reduce our allergies and also seems to be reducing the dander from our cat.It’s very quiet. I have to check that it’s on because it doesn’t sound like anything on the low setting."
    },
    {
        "review": "It arrived ahead of schedule, 5 days early. It came well packaged, with a manual in English. Very quiet, up to speed 2 you hear absolutely nothing, from 3 above, very comfortable sound. Control and pet mode via the app. The result and benefit, time will tell."
    },
    {
        "review": "I was waking up in the middle of my sleep because of my terrible allergy symptoms for the past few weeks (lots of sneezing, runny nose, watery eyes, itchy eyes/throat/ears) so I decided to get this for my bedroom. It has been a game changer!I started sneezing/watering/itching a LOT LESS since turning this on, and the air just feels a lot fresher now! I love it!The UX is great too! It's so convenient to be able to use your phone to control fan speed (you can choose 1 of 4 levels or do any % of max fan speed you want under the DIY mode), turn the interface lights on and off (great for keeping it dark at night to sleep), turn the purifier itself on/off, and keep track of what the air quality is like (there aren't numbers afaik but it gives you 4 levels of either very good, good, moderate, or bad and these show up as different colours of light on the ring around the power button of the machine as well), check how much filter life is left as a % (so far it seems to go down 1% per 3 days, which I guess should last about 300 days).As for noise, it is super quiet on levels 1 & 2. I can't even hear it from across the room! Levels 3 & 4 are definitely audible across the room, but not terribly bothersome. I sometimes like the white noise.I'd recommend it! (So far at least; I've only had this for 3 days so I'll update if anything happens)Edit: Just had the forest fire smoke drape our city with opaque yellowish-brown skies. The air purifier helped some during the day, but now the smell is seeping into my apartment. It’s a bit better in my bedroom where the air purifier is, but I can definitely smell that burning smell now.I will also note that the sensor says the air quality is “Very Good” though the graph has dipped a little. From what I remember reading, there are 2 types of air quality sensors (IR and laser) and the one this unit has is not as accurate. We had some of the worst air quality in the world for parts of the day and it’s saying it’s “Very Good” which is a huge stretch… All this to say, don’t trust what it says about the air quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "It arrived on the agreed date, at an excellent price, it fulfills all the functions mentioned, I had an allergy to placeerin since they were working with wood, the allergy slowly subsided in one day, I would definitely buy it again"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "This FULMINARE H13 True HEPA Air Purifier is a surprisingly effective little device for bedrooms, offices, and cozy living spaces. It’s small and lightweight, so it blends easily into a nightstand or shelf without feeling bulky or intrusive.Performance-wise, it does a solid job filtering out everyday irritants like dust, pet dander, and lingering odors. The H13 HEPA filtration gives it a reassuring “deep clean” feel for the air, especially in closed rooms where air can get stale fast.One of its standout qualities is how whisper-quiet it runs. In sleep mode, it fades into the background so well you’ll forget it’s on. The soft night light adds a calming glow that feels more like ambiance than appliance. 🌿✨"
