[
    {
        "review": "We moved into an incredibly dusty townhouse, I have terrible allergies, and we discovered our neighbors are chain smokers. We now have 3 Levoit air purifiers in our home: Vital 100 (non-smart version), Core Mini and Vital 200S.I initially bought the Vital 100 and put it in our bedroom because I have terrible allergies. It collected a ton of dust and helped a lot with the allergies. I thought I didn't need the smart version but in hindsight the availability of specialty filters and the remote control would be very helpful. It's relatively quiet although on high it's too noisy for me to sleep with. I absolutely love that you can turn the all the control lights off. We tried using this for the cigarette smell but it wasn't very effective except when the smell was very light. It did completely abolish cooking smells though. If I could go back in time I would have ordered the 100S instead but this one works fine.The smoke smell from the neighbors comes into our house through the laundry room which is a very small room. I bought the Core Mini to try to combat it. The Core Mini doesn't really do much to get rid of smells and was definitely overwhelmed by the smoke so now we move it around the house now when the pollen level is high. It works ok for dust and allergens but the range isn't great; you need to be right next to it to notice a difference. On low and medium speed it's barely audible and high is relatively quiet but overall the fan isn't very powerful. The lights on this one automatically turn off after a few seconds making it bedroom friendly. If I could do it again, I would have skipped this one and bought one of the larger ones sooner.Lastly, in an attempt to mitigate the smoke coming from next door, we got the big boi Vital 200S with the add on smoke specialty filter. So far it isn't able to remove the smell while they're smoking but it does cut down the severity and will clear it eventually provided the source stops for long enough. It's amazingly quiet on the lower speeds. It's pretty loud on the higher speeds but the fan moves a ton of air around. I'm disappointed that the auto mode doesn't detect the smoke smell but I can use the app to turn it to high speed as soon as I smell it. You don't have to use the app but it's really easy to set up and connect. The app allows you to set schedules which is really handy and as I touched on earlier, it works as a remote control. As with the others, you're able to turn the lights off completely so it's good for bedrooms. We've only had this running a few days but I'm pretty impressed with what it can do."
    },
    {
        "review": "I simply cannot say ENOUGH good things about this product! After 2 weeks of use the air feels lighter, I no longer wake up with a stuffy nose or junk in my lungs and I bought the pet specific air filters that are an added bonus. I LOVE the lighting features and that you can sync the device to my phone and set up schedules so it's quiet at night. The controls are SUPER easy to use and fool proof.Just don't forget to open the base when you get it and take the plastic packaging off around the air filter!!! I forgot to do this and wondered why there was no air flow coming out of the top till I Googled it. 😂😂😂"
    },
    {
        "review": "I use this in a room I use to have an Ionic air purifier, the old worked there was some dust near the unit, but the smell of Ozone was too much since i kept my door closed most of the day. the Levoit was a perfect replacement, no smell, lot less noise and my room felt refreshed when i open the door. I have the 330 model for over 2 years in the Livingroom and i happy with that one as well. the only down i don't like is the 300 can sense the air and adjust where the 200 can't, but you can program to go on or off multi times throughout the day, the night light is a nice touch for when it's in my sons room or i want to see enough light in a pitch black room. fits perfect in my bedroom, cleans the air, no dusty or ozone smell. very effective for the rom it is in."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this air purifier for my bedroom as my sleep can be disturbed by air quality pretty easily. I was highly skeptical of this product at first as the price point to me indicated that it might be cheap in terms of quality of the product but so far it has been pretty impressive. On even the lowest setting, it has substantially improved the air quality not just in the bedroom but in the adjoining room so we're looking at space of about 200-300 square feet or so. I would say I can breathe easier at night with it and my comfort level while sleeping has increased a bit.The air after it's been running for a bit smells and just seems fresher and I am considering getting a second one to see if it can handle a much larger area.Noise is pretty low on it's lowest \"normal\" setting and the night mode feature drops the noise to almost silent, but not quite. At it's lowest setting, there is an odd whine, for lack of better words that can just barely be heard. This whine was an annoyance at first but you get used to and can ignore it. It still works well on the lowest setting to keep the room fresh so it's a good deal.Setup was easy as can physically, however I cannot as yet speak to the application setup as I haven't gotten to that. I treat air purifiers as non-smart devices but I do plan to at least try to integrate it with Home Assistant and if that doesn't work I may try integration with Amazon Alexa. I'll update the review when that happens.Durability of the purifier long term is unknown, though the filters do seem very easy to replace and their price point does make them economical enough to justify getting a filter instead of replacing the entire air purifier.Summary: Good, powerful little air purifier that can sit on a dresser or nightstand, relatively quiet with some caveats. Long term durability is unknown but still was a good buy overall."
    },
    {
        "review": "I chose the Amazon box option mainly so I could check whether the item shipped safely and arrived without damage to the outer packaging. The Amazon box itself arrived in good condition, but the Core 200S-P’s box was damaged, likely because it had not been handled carefully during a previous shipment.Since I bought it in Used – Acceptable condition, I inspected the purifier carefully. I found no issues with the unit itself. It came with what appears to be a new filter, had no strange smell, and works perfectly, just like my other Core 300S-P, which I recently bought new.I also bought a second unit in Used – Good condition. The only thing I noticed was a black scuff mark on the bottom of the purifier, as shown in the pictures, but it does not look like actual damage. The box for that one also appeared to have been damaged during a previous shipment. From my experience buying used items on Amazon, that seems fairly common, and it is probably one reason the price is lower when the manufacturer’s box is damaged.I ran it for an hour on level 3, the highest fan speed and it seems to be working perfectly. Afterward, the room smelled cleaner and felt easier to breathe in. I also found no visual issues.After comparing it side by side with the Core 300S-P, I honestly think the Core 200S-P is a better fit for bedrooms, while the Core 300S-P is better suited for larger rooms. Overall, it was definitely a steal at $53.36 for both of the units and I’m very satisfied with this purchase. 🙏Update after 2 weeks: I’ve just check the filters it also surprising picks up more than just dust, it picks up tiny mosquito!!! 🦟 we have left the living room sliding door open because of the renovation so this is proof to be a life saving from these annoying little pest"
    },
    {
        "review": "Highly recommend it so far - have only used it the past week BUT it is during the worst air quality in the world time in Chicago from the Canadian and Minnesota wildfires.  It really seems to be working, helping.  Easy to put together - no actual assembly required.  Nice and small, very quiet (sound free on sleep), and you should totally download the recommended app.  I wasn't thinking I would, but so helpful and serves like a remote almost.  Already recommended to 2 friends and another who bought it already.  Good product so far!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This was my first time ever using an air purifier, so I was pretty skeptical even after reading all the good reviews. The first few days were honestly a little discouraging because my bedroom still smelled kind of funky. I live in an older house, and getting certain smells out of the rooms has been a big priority while I finish setting everything up.But after about a week, the difference became really noticeable. Now it’s actually refreshing to walk into my room. I’m really glad I didn’t give up on it early.I also share my bedroom with a Husky, and there’s no dog smell anymore — which is huge. The fan is pretty quiet, and even when I turn it up, the sound is kind of soothing. It actually reminds me of the ocean waves from my trip to Ormond, FL, which is a nice little bonus.The filters are easy to insert and remove (I haven’t had to replace mine yet, but I tested it out just to see), and the whole unit feels simple and user‑friendly.Overall, very happy with this purifier. It took a little time, but it absolutely did its job."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this purifier because I really wanted one that I could turn on from my phone while laying in bed, since I am completely blind in the dark due to my vision impairment, and I don't necessarily have anywhere to place this type of electronic near my bed that was the major deal breaker for me. This air purifier is about the size of a PS5, but a little more convenient due to the cylinidrical shape of it. The app set up is easy and it allows you to auto order a new filter through the app via a scheduled set up. I have mine set up for every 6 months and you can tell the difference between the 2 filters after those 6 months.... the app also will tell you the life on your filter left and will tell you the air quality/ pollen count outside of your home. All the modes do exactly as they say and the sleep mode is ultra quiet which is nice. I've been using this air purifier for almost 2 years now and it is still working great. You can immidetly tell when you take it out of the box that it is a good high quality purifier and not a purifier where they say its high quality and after a week it stops working...  My last purifier was lmof a lower quality and stopped working with-in a year, but also I paid $50 for that one and I didn't have a dog at that time.It is so nice to have a higher quality purifier that works exactly as it says on the ads. The app also includes other Levoit electronics you can add to your account so you have all your Lwvoit products in one spot on your phone which I think is so mice and easy. The app is also really easy to use and to set up everything on, it looks and feels very professional and easy which I really enjoy. I love opening up my app and seeing all my Levoit electronics in one spot, ready to turn on or off, or to change any mode it's on to something different. You can aslo set up a schedule of when you would like your devices to turn on and off and what mode to use whenbit does.The purifier has been so helpful with my allergies as it takes about 10 minutes for my severe allergy symptoms to begin subsiding a good amount after coming inside from walking the dog. To some 10 minutes may sound like a long time, but to someone with really really REALLY awful allergies 10 minutes is well worth the wait...Also, the air suction is powerful enough where I have to wipe I'm purifier down with a clean and dry paper towel to get some dog hair off of the sides where the air flows into the machine. It's also kept the infamous \"dog smell\" from settling in my room. I highly recommend this purifier it's great and if/when this one goes, I will definitly be purchasing another Levoit brand..."
    },
    {
        "review": "I don't know where to start, but in any case, I'm super satisfied. The device has a nice design and you can feel the quality. On the touch screen, there is everything you need. What I love is the fact that it is connected to the application. It's really super simple and complete without overdoing it. We can see in the photos that it is indicated when to change the filter (for example, it displays 100% when it is new); we can therefore monitor its state of wear as it progresses. In addition, just below, everything is planned:1. There is a “buy filter” link2. This link redirects you directly to Amazon3. The filter currently costs €25, which is not too expensive since you have to change it every 3 to 6 months. It's really well thought out. The instructions are in French, but I admit that we don't really need it because everything is explained step by step in the application. The device has 3 modes:1. Silent mode2. Medium mode3. Strong mode: useful for purifying a room quickly (for half an hour for example) before lowering the power. In strong mode, the fan is obviously quite loud, but that's for efficiency. In medium or silent mode, you hardly hear it anymore. There is even a night light mode (you can see it in one of my photos) which diffuses a little light at night. You can also deactivate all the lights if it is annoying, for example in a child's bedroom. For the moment, I am very satisfied and I recommend my purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "Our vet has this air purifier in each of their exam rooms, what a difference it makes.  I bought one for the laundry room as we have a new puppy.  You can sense the fresh air straight away.  Great purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "Just love it and cools the room when active. Integrated with Alexa and so far it's been working really well."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've made a complaint to amazon supoprt.If you haven't noticed it like my this product is not European, its American and 110 volts.No idea why they are listing it on European site without sufficient warning.Better tittle might beLevoit Vital 100 Air Purifiers (110 volt US)"
    },
    {
        "review": "The product arrived on time and in good condition. Although the manual comes in English, it is super easy to assemble and turn it on. Having the app on the cell phone makes it easier to control it and I was able to connect it with Alexa without any problem, in addition to the app notifying you of the life of the filter, so you can monitor it and change it when necessary. The purifier has worked very well for me, it has 3 levels, the highest is the loudest although it is not annoying, very similar to the noise generated by a fan, the sleep mode is wonderful, you practically cannot hear anything and you can program what time it turns off which I find very practical. When It arrived, I turned it on in the bedroom and an hour later I could already notice the difference in the air, I have allergies and the air felt fresher to breathe and I slept very comfortably without sneezing or coughing. I cleaned the filter with the vacuum cleaner and it was very easy, although it does not eliminate all the dust that accumulates, if it removes a large part of it, it undoubtedly helps it last and filter better for longer. Yes, I recommend it, it performs its function well and I do not consider the price to be excessive."
    }
]

