[
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this Levoit air purifier for a while now, and it’s made a noticeable difference in my home. It’s quiet, especially in Sleep Mode, and the air feels much fresher. It does a great job reducing dust, pet odors, and cooking smells. I also like how easy it is to use, and the Auto Mode adjusts the fan speed on its own. Overall, it’s reliable, effective, and definitely worth the investment for better indoor air quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been very impressed with this air purifier. It is quiet, easy to use, and noticeably improves the air quality in my home. I especially like that it has different fan speeds and an auto mode that adjusts based on the air quality. The setup was simple, and the app makes it convenient to monitor and control the purifier. Overall, it has been a great addition to my home, and I would definitely recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m very impressed with this product! It has made a noticeable difference in my allergic relief, especially during allergy season. The air freshness is amazing, and my home feels much cleaner and more comfortable. The appearance is sleek and modern, so it looks great in any room. I also love the sleep mode because it runs so quietly at night without disturbing my rest. Its portability makes it easy to move from room to room, and the overall durability gives me confidence that it will last for years. I highly recommend it to anyone looking for an effective and reliable air purifier!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This air purifier noticeably freshened the air within a day and helped reduce dust and cooking smells. It runs quietly, even at night, and the auto-sensing feature adjusts airflow instantly when needed. Filter changes are simple and easy. Overall, it’s an effective, quiet, and reliable purifier that makes our home feel cleaner and more comfortable."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have pets and since the pet hair is a main reason for me to have a filter in the first place, one feature I insist upon is a washable pre-filter.  This allows me to wash away trapped dust and pet hair and really extend the life of my HEPA filters.  It's also great to be able to literally see all the hair and dust being pulled from the air.  The app is actually fantastic and very easy to use.  Love that Alexa connects and helps me change up settings and that has been flawless.  The auto functions works beautifully, as I can watch the device change color and change settings according to air quality.  If I blow out a candle, spray perfumes or leave my bedroom door open I can see it work in real time.  There is still some dust that settles in my bedroom but overall the air smells so much better.  I live in brick ranch built in the 60's and a lot of the building materials, including tile and cabinets are original.  I also live in the hot and humid Deep South so that combo is not great in the summer.  This really gets rid of the damp and musty smells.  I have a ton of an allergies and this really helps me sleep at night. Very pleased and just bought a second one for another bedroom."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have had several air filters over the years and have always been slightly disappointed with them and unsure of whether or not they are truly helping. After doing a lot of house cleaning and dusting, I wanted something to help maintain cleaner air so I tried this.I can honestly say this is one of those rare semi life changing purchases. I immediately noticed a marked change in my indoor air quality as a long time allergy sufferer and being sensitive to smoke, pollen and other contaminants. The change was much more significant compared to other air filters I have tried.I keep mine on the medium setting and run it 24 hours a day. It's surprisingly quiet and the subtle noise doesn't bother me at all when reading or watching tv, I actually prefer it as a source of white noise. I can breathe and sleep so much better now and it also heavily reduces odors from cooking. It's so good that I bought another one for a separate room.I also like the extra features like pet mode, the air quality sensor, and smart device features. The air sensor is surprisingly accurate and changes if I dust or clean nearby or cook something a little smokey. I haven't tried the app and smart features yet but they're nice to have as an option.The filter is very easy to set up and I haven't had to replace it yet. Truly cannot recommend it enough."
    },
    {
        "review": "We got this air purifier after our daughter was diagnosed with dog allergies. We do have a golden doodle and while our daughter doesn't have strong allergic reactions to our doodle (she does to other shedding dogs) the allergist recommended we get one for her room. We put this purifier in our daughters room and leave the door closed at all times. While hard to truly measure its effectiveness, her room doesn't have dust settle on furniture like the rest of the house and her ceiling fan doesn't collect dust like others, or at least at a MUCH slower rate.Love the ability to lock the screen so she cant mess with the settings. The purifier runs very quiet and in sleep mode you can barely tell its on. Love that the lights on the display turn off when it's dark in the room. For the price I am very impressed with its performance. It is not too big but cant exactly be hidden easily. Fortunately it looks nice and is not too industrial looking. We've had it for almost a year now and have had no issues at all. The filters seem very high quality and although a little expensive, the the filters do last a while.Overall we have been very impressed with its cleaning ability, different mode settings and features, quietness, and would say its fairly inexpensive for all that. We just ordered the 200S to put in the main living area."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'll be honest, I wasn't sure how much of a difference an air purifier would actually make, but this one proved me wrong almost immediately. The build quality alone tells you this is a serious piece of kit — it feels solid and well-made, not like something that's going to fall apart after a few months of use.What really won me over, though, is that you can genuinely feel the difference in the air. It's hard to describe until you experience it yourself, but the room just feels cleaner and fresher after it's been running for a while.Setup was a breeze — no complicated instructions or frustrating app configuration. I had it up and running in minutes, and scheduling it to fit my routine was just as straightforward.One of my favorite things about this purifier is how quiet it is. Some units sound like a small jet engine no matter what mode they're on, but this one operates at a level where you can easily forget it's even there. No constant background hum disrupting conversations, sleep, or focus.The auto mode is a standout feature. It intelligently ramps up the fan speed when it detects a drop in air quality, then gradually winds itself back down once the air is clear again. It's the kind of smart, hands-off functionality that makes you wonder how you managed without it. You're not babysitting settings it just handles itself.Highly recommended for anyone looking for a reliable, quiet, and genuinely effective air purifier."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent, compatible with Alexa, and easy to use"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good product, it covers a large area, the anti-hair filter that it has is very useful, it is removable and washable, it keeps lint and dust. At night it is not very noisy, in times of heat it cools down and the air feels lighter. Its automatic mode that indicates the air quality is very functional, for example, after cooking it indicates poor air quality, after 10 minutes on its third speed it indicates good air quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very nice product , low noise level"
    },
    {
        "review": "We’ve been using this LEVOIT air purifier daily and the difference in our air quality is noticeable! It runs super quietly, even on higher settings, which makes it perfect for bedrooms, living rooms, and nurseries. Within the first day, I noticed less dust, fresher-smelling air, and fewer allergy symptoms.It’s very easy to set up, has multiple fan speeds, and the auto mode adjusts based on air quality which I love. The sleek design blends beautifully with home decor and doesn’t take up much space for how powerful it is. It also covers large rooms extremely well, which is a huge bonus.If you have pets, allergies, kids, or just want cleaner air in your home, this is 100% worth it. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Update to my previous comments:It's been 2 years since I purchased the Vital 100S and it has worked very well for me.Until ...I just purchased a replacement filter for the unit this month.  I considered buying the knockoff filters because they were significantly cheaper than the Levoit replacements.  The only reason I went with the Levoit branded replacement filter was because it looked like it included the washable pre filter.  I specifically wanted another pre filter as a backup in case something happened to the one that came with the unit.  They are not flimsy, but neither are they invincible!  What if I tear it, or lose it, or my dog eats it (which could absolutely happen!) ?The knockoff brands made it very clear in their product descriptions that the pre filter was NOT included with the replacement filter.  However, the product description for the Levoit replacement filter uses phrases like \"3 in 1\", \"washable pre filter\", and the pictures of the product show the pre filter and DO NOT specify that it isn't included.I am very disappointed with this order and Levoit's shoddy advertising.  And I want a spare pre filter, but it seems I can't find one for love nor money!I bought the Vital 100S.Like many reviewers of this product, I purchased it because the wildfire smoke had infiltrated my house.  I never ever thought that I would be \"that\" person - someone who needed their own atmosphere!  But the irritation in my nose and throat motivated me to buy this unit for my well-being.The reasons I chose this model are: the true HEPA, of course! Also the 3-stage filter. The CADR was good for the size of my rooms (I have open concept on the main floor, and a vaulted ceiling upstairs) the pre-filter is cleanable and I like the fact that I can also get specialized filters for Pet, Toxin and Smoke (in case things get really crazy!).  The reviews are excellent and the price is right.  I am seriously considering buying another of Levoit's units for the upstairs!I have not used any of the \"connected\" features so I cannot comment on those.The unit is easy to unpack and I was able to start using it immediately. It is very presentable; it's also light enough to be portable because I've been moving it from room to room (when the wind shifts sometimes the smoke comes into a different part of the house). It's super easy to use; I love the control panel, you just tap on it to turn it on, set the fan strength, and activate the timer. The first 2 fan settings are so quiet that I can barely hear that the unit is on. The third setting is a little louder but it IS moving a lot of air after all! I've only had it 2 weeks so haven't had to clean it or change the filter.One thing I didn't consider thoroughly was the placement of the unit. In order to work properly any air purifier needs to be kind of in the middle of things. Proper placement of an air purifier is between 3 and 5 feet off the ground, with about 3 feet of open space around it.  Luckily, the 100S fits well with my decor and is light enough to put on a table or my bookshelves. I was worried that it might vibrate a lot and eventually shake itself off the table but it's staying put quite well.So far, I am very satisfied with this purchase."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Okay not gonna lie I was a skeptic. When I turned it on the first time the number it showed was an 8. Which is almost close to perfect air quality. I’ve been running it every single day and it seems to work fine but I wasn’t sure how good it actually cleans the air. Well I just cooked and an olive oil smell was in my kitchen and it had created smoke. I looked at the air purifier and it was working hard and the number was up to 132!!!! I now have it running at three speed and it’s cleaning our air so fast! I’m a believer in the Mooka air purifier and will be buying a second one for my upstairs!! Love this thing and highly recommend!!! It’s also super quiet and easy to change and clean filters. 10/10"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this for our home and honestly noticed a difference faster than I expected. The air feels fresher and cleaner, especially in the bedroom. It’s surprisingly quiet, even at night, and doesn’t disturb sleep. I also like that it covers a larger area, so I don’t feel like I need multiple units running. Setup was simple and it’s been easy to use. Definitely happy with this purchase and would recommend it to anyone wanting to improve the air quality in their home."
    },
    {
        "review": "When my elderly cat (18 this summer! Cat tax included in review) was diagnosed with asthma, it meant that all three of us who live in my apartment (my husband and I plus cat) all have some sort of allergy or respiratory issues from different things. I've always had allergies to things like dust and pollen, and my husband had recently developed a cough and post nasal drip that the doctor could find no particular cause of.I happened to be browsing on Prime Day after looking into air purifiers and got this one for a very affordable 60 bucks. The reviews said it worked great just out of the package and setup was easy, and they were right. No assembly, nothing to fuss with. Just remove the plastic from the filter, pop it back in and plug it in.The difference was noticeable very quickly. Husband has basically stopped coughing and his post nasal drip has reduced significantly. I also noticed he isn't snoring anywhere near as loudly as he was before. My own allergy symptoms have alleviated; my sinuses used to feel stuffy which made it harder to fall asleep, but that's basically solved. My own post nasal drip has also noticeably improved. Even my cat's asthma noises have improved. I'm sort of shocked to encounter a product that actually noticeably solves a problem.Shortly after buying it, I had a small fire in my oven. Everything was okay, but the smoke was obviously a problem. I decided to put the air purifier on the counter to see what the number went up to- 130! But about an hour later, the number on the panel read about 10 or 12, and the normal range for my apartment is between 5-17.It has a sleep setting, but we keep it on 1 during the night because it's so quiet. I like to keep it on 2 during the day because it's still just light background humming.One thing I thought was nice is that there's a QR code on the side of it to link you to the correct filters to buy when you need to replace them. However, out of all the things that could actually use an app, it doesn't have one. It could be nice to have a really simple one that records the PM number so you could have an idea of the air quality patterns in your home. At the same time, it's refreshing that it doesn't have one lolMy apartment is 1,300 square feet so technically this little guy should be making some difference on the whole thing, but it might be better to have it in a more central location for that; I like it in the bedroom though, since it's made such a difference in our symptoms that were impacting our sleep, and my cat mostly stays in the bedroom so it just makes sense for us.10/10, really happy with it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I think it’s working well but I wouldn’t say optimal. Not too loud so that’s a plus. Easy to use. The lock button is a plus. I don’t smell the neighbors cigarettes anymore but I do still smell the pets. My old one used to eliminate both so that sucks."
    },
