        "review": "This machine automatically senses changes in air quality and adjusts the fan accordingly. Tried it in various rooms where our air quality varied between 8 and 20 and the fan stayed on low, however it turned to full and the red light came on when the wok started to smoke! (I can’t recall what number it registered this to be as I was impressed at the light and fan speed!) Not tried this overnight on sleep mode as the air quality has been good, though the low fan speed isn’t obtrusive so can’t imagine it disturbing sleep. I can imagine this will be great for the damp weather, new furniture smell removal cleaning and dusting days and also spring pollens.The carbon filter pieces had space between them so I googled if that was normal and apparently it is, as small molecules bounce around before getting trapped. I have bought the same model again for a family member with allergies and asthma, after buying two smaller models and finding fault with both."
