[
    {
        "review": "I wish I had bought these years ago!  I have so many allergies, my allergist MD said I had aced the skin prick test; also he said he'd hadn't had a patient like me for a long while.  I'm allergic to everything outside all through the year, cats, dogs, and and dust. I started custom allergy shots, yes, plural b/c I get one in each arm at each visit.  They couldn't fit all my allergen medication into one vial.  I also take OTC, Rx allergy medication by mouth, nose, and eyedrops.  I still suffer with frontal sinus headache due to my kids going in and out the front door several times per day.  They bring in all kinds of pollen with them.I have ThearU cold masks to alleviate frontal sinus headache pain via cryotherapy, but those only provided very temporary relief.  I enrolled in Botox savings program b/c I am considering getting Botox for my headaches.  Yes, taking OTC pain meds also only provides temporary relief and I don't like putting that metabolizing strain on my liver and kidneys, not to mention the damage risk to my gut lining.  I have a Levoit air purifier in my bedroom and I've noticed that really works to clean the air so well, the air in there smells different if I turn it on several house before bedtime.I recently thought to add air purifiers to the living room to capture those pollen spores at the source.  Levoit air purfiers are expensive, so I shopped for alternatives.I found Airtok and liked they were made in America and had a 2 pack purchase option.  I really liked their large room air purifier which can turn on automatically when it detects 'bad' air.  But I opted for this 2 pack option b/c I wanted to put them in different areas within the living room.  One is by the front door, and the other is in the opposite corner.  They've been on for about 5 hours so far.The low fan setting is so very quiet, I can't hear it well.  The medium fan setting produces a sound low enough I don't need to adjust the TV sound.  Both settings are doing such a fantastic job, I've not had to take any OTC pain medication or use my gel masks b/c I haven't developed a headache!  My daughter has commented twice now she loves the smell in the living room.  I didn't use the scent pads and told her both times, that's clean air you're smelling!Now I am considering ordering two more to put them in one in each kid room, and maybe two more for the sunroom and basement.  Since they have a steady-on setting, I'm wondering if I can plug the power cord into an Alexa plug.  Just think of setting a routine to turn on and off the machines based on which rooms are being utilized!Set up of these Airtok air purifiers was super simple.  The power cord is inside the machine so you need to twist off the bottom to get to it.  Go ahead and buy the 2 pack bundle with refill filters like I did.  You won't regret it!Update several months later: I'm back to buy more Airtok air purifiers for the kitchen and sun-room and I put them in family gift idea list to gift these for Christmas."
    },
    {
        "review": "To be honest, I don’t think I would have bought these at the original price. But when they were on sale for half off, I ordered immediately because we have very old dogs who are beginning to have frequent accidents on the already very old carpet that we can’t afford to replace at this time. Every time I walked into the house, I’d have to open all the windows because of the dog smell. I was literally going to lose my mind about it. These have saved my sanity. They’re pretty quiet, but not silent. I love the sound of a fan though so it doesn’t bother me. The child lock keeps my 1 year old from messing with the buttons and it’s all pretty straight forward. The scent pads are an added bonus and they come with extras! Filters are easy to take in and out. The product itself if pretty small, but it does a good job in our living space. This was a 2 pack so I currently have both in the same room, but feel I could move one to another space! Now that i have them, I would pay full price for the 2 pack!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Mine are 4 yrs old! Still works great! Quiet, definitely clears the air when we cook food in the house like steak/burgers or seafood. One of mine is by the kitchen counter just by the air fryer. I just change the filter every now and then."
    },
    {
        "review": "One of those products that you set and forget until it's time to change the filter and you realize how much it was working the whole time. A couple times my apartment's power flickered from a storm, I didn't think to check if the air purifier was still on but in a day or two I could smell the difference.Even when the air intake part gets blocked by cat hair, there's a noticeable difference in smell of my small bathroom where I keep the litter box, let alone when the filter needs changed. The filter light comes on to let you know when it's time, but it doesn't seem to notify you too early to get you to buy more; the filter is bright blue and you can tell exactly when it's really fully clogged vs the one not yet due for a switch out.The noise level is okay for me; the low and medium speed settings are quiet but smell-wise I only really notice a difference if it's left on high. But even that is still quieter than, say, a window fan.Deducting a star because I don't think the low and medium settings do much but also because the light is too bright. If you turn on the \"night light\" in the middle of the night, the blue light is definitely too much. But even if you turn it off, the little light bulb button is still too bright and casts a blue glow in my bedroom that I actively try to reduce with blackout curtains in the city.I don't regret buying it at all, especially for my cat's litter box. Just some stuff to consider if you're sensitive."
    },
