[
    {
        "review": "I’ve been very impressed with this air purifier. The design is modern and compact, making it easy to place in any room without taking up too much space. It runs very quietly, even at higher speeds, which makes it perfect for bedrooms or workspaces. In terms of allergic relief, I did notice an improvement in air freshness, especially with dust and general indoor air quality, which makes it helpful for everyday comfort. Regarding value for money, it offers a solid balance between features, performance, and design. You get smart functionality and reliable performance without feeling overpriced. The weight is also well-balanced—light enough to move around easily, but sturdy enough to feel stable and well-built. One of my favorite features is the app control. It’s convenient to monitor air quality and adjust settings remotely, and the interface is simple and user-friendly. I also noticed that it improves air freshness fairly quickly, especially in smaller to medium-sized rooms. The build quality feels solid, and the fabric exterior gives it a premium look compared to typical plastic units. If I had to suggest an improvement, it would be slightly stronger performance for larger areas and clearer filter replacement notifications. Overall, this is a well-designed and effective air purifier that combines performance, quiet operation, and smart functionality. I would definitely recommend it for everyday use."
    },
    {
        "review": "Okay so I’ve been using this air purifier for a little bit now and I’m actually really impressed with it.First off, it’s not ugly lol. Like it actually looks cute sitting in my space and doesn’t stick out like most air purifiers do. It blends in really nice which I love because I like my home to feel clean and put together.Now the main thing  it works. You can literally tell the difference in the air. Especially when I’m cooking or if the house just feels stuffy, it kicks on and clears everything out pretty fast. The air just feels fresher and lighter.It’s also super quiet. Like I can have it running at night and it doesn’t bother me at all. No loud humming or anything annoying, which is a huge plus for me.I also like that I can control it from my phone. Makes it easy to turn on, adjust settings, and check everything without getting up. That’s just convenient, especially when you’re busy.Only thing I will say  the filters aren’t the cheapest, so that’s something to keep in mind. And sometimes the app can be a little slow, but nothing crazy.Overall though, I feel like it’s worth it. If you want something that actually works, looks nice, and isn’t loud, this is a really good option.I’d definitely recommend it, especially if you have kids, pets, or just want cleaner air in your home."
    },
    {
        "review": "The SP3i was super easy to set up to run automatically, is quiet, filters very effectively and looks good doing it. Ours is set up on one end of a great room near to master and guest rooms. Seems to be doing an excellant job covering most of the entire first floor of roughly 2000 s.f. Everything you need to know magically appears of front edge of the top when you walk near the unit. Even more information shows in the excellent app including what useful percentage of your filter remains. I really value that this all connects via wi-fi so the app stays connected all the time. I am sick of bluetooth connections on devices that disconnect as soon as you move 10 ft away. We run a robot vac in the same area as t(e air filter. The amount of dust, etc being picked up now has been reduced by 2/3’s. This unit is proving to be well worth the cost. I will say the replacement filters are quite pricey justified by their seven layer construction and effectiveness. Beware cheap knock-offs - they are not the same, most having 3 layers."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this new Blueair purifier! I have a 3,000 sq. ft. home and already own three other air purifiers, so this is my fourth. I was curious to see what made this one different from the others, and I was able to test that pretty quickly.I painted my nails near the purifier while it was running on Auto mode. Almost immediately, the fan kicked up to high, and I could actually monitor the change in air quality through the Blueair app. It was really cool to see it respond so quickly. It also didn’t take very long for the air quality reading to return to “Excellent.”Now I’ve noticed the same thing when I’m cooking or even when I mop with a Lysol-based cleaner—the purifier automatically increases the fan speed. That gives me confidence that it’s actually detecting changes in the air rather than just running quietly in the background.So far, I’m really impressed with how responsive it is, and I’m enjoying being able to see the air quality changes right in the app."
    },
    {
        "review": "This purifier is a huge upgrade compared to my smaller Winix. It’s far quieter, pushes more air, is better built and feels durable, and controls dust and my allergies. When on speed 1 or 2 I can’t even tell it’s on, but on higher speeds it definitely makes its presence known.I don’t love the VOC sensor, only for the fact that it isn’t all that effective at removing VOCs and will make the purifier run at high speeds for hours. The standard filter only has a small amount of carbon (grams) compared to the kilograms of carbon in specialized gas removal purifiers like IQ Air or Austin Air. It is better than most due to the pelletized carbon instead of a standard carbon impregnated mesh, but don’t expect amazing VOC performance from this machine.I also love / hate the prefilter design. It makes the purifier look pretty and keeps the main filter clean. My main issue is that it is very elastic, and when removed all of the dust it captured usually gets flung right back into the air. My routine is to thoroughly vacuum it before I put it in the washer."
    },
    {
        "review": "I was pleasantly surprised by the size of the device and its sleek design it fits perfectly into my home interior. Setting it up and connecting to the mobile app was quick and easy, and all the necessary information is clearly displayed.It was interesting to check the air quality in different rooms. As expected, the air in the kitchen wasn’t ideal, but the device improved it საკმაოდ quickly. It runs very quietly, which is a big plus for everyday use. I also really like the light indicator that shows changes in air quality very convenient and easy to understand.The fan function is another great feature that I truly appreciate. Overall, I’m very satisfied with this purchase and would happily recommend it to others."
    },
