[
    {
        "review": "This compact air purifier has been an absolute lifesaver for my bedroom allergy flares. It is small enough to sit comfortably on a nightstand or in a tight corner, yet it keeps the air feeling noticeably crisp and clean all day long. Setting up the companion app over WiFi was painless, and it gives you a clear look at your actual indoor air quality in real time. The absolute best feature is the auto mode, which lets the built-in sensors monitor the room and kick up the fan speed automatically whenever it detects pet dander or dust floating around.When it comes to noise, it is practically silent on the lower night settings, meaning you can easily sleep right next to it without any annoying humming or clicking. While the marketing text claims it can handle up to a thousand square feet, it truly shines as a dedicated unit for a standard bedroom, office, or nursery where it can cycle the air constantly. The fabric pre-filter on the outside also does a fantastic job of catching heavy pet hair before it even reaches the main filter, making maintenance a breeze."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought the model 211i first as we have a fairly large house and we were disappointed.  I have had terrible allergies this spring so purchased the larger, well recommended unit and it basically did nothing to help.  The blue light was always on indicating clean air but it did nothing to get rid of pollen and odors.  It was basically a fan that moved air so we returned it.  This unit (which is the SP1i model) functions much better to remove smells and VOC's.  Our combined family room are roughly 700sq feet and we keep in the family room.  It senses food cooking odors from about 25 feet away and helps remove them.  I think this has a much more sensitive detector sensor and better filter; we are keeping it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this because of its great reviews online by Consumer Reports as well as others on youtube who have tried this product. This has an exceptionally high rating that I bought 2 for my family as well. It was very useful for us during the wildfire smoke. Also useful when someone outside our window or a passerby is smoking cigarettes. Also useful when cooking & the trapped air is wafting all over in the living room, bedroom & kitchen. Since it is very lightweight, you can easily carry it to the bedroom or near the kitchen area or living room to suck out all the bad smelling air or toxic air. Highly recommended. And because it has an app, you can check the smoke level in your phone. The filtration & filter replacement lasts a long time. Easy to replace filter, value for your money. Odor removal is quick after just a few minutes of it being on. Also perfect for those who have pets & dust allergies. Provides immediate relief when smoke if trapped inside your apartment or house or small area room. A must have in every part of the house."
    },
    {
        "review": "I picked this up mainly for pet dander and general dust in my bedroom, and it's made a noticeable difference. Within the first day or two, I could tell the air felt cleaner, and the auto mode does a good job of ramping up when it detects something and quieting down when the air's already clean, so I'm not manually adjusting settings all the time.The HEPASilent technology lives up to its name. Even on higher fan speeds, it's nowhere near as loud as other purifiers I've owned, and on the lower settings it's practically silent, which makes it easy to leave running overnight without it being disruptive.WiFi connectivity works well through the app, letting me check air quality readings and adjust settings remotely, which is a nice bonus if I want to kick it up a notch before getting home. Setup was straightforward and it paired with my WiFi with no real hiccups.Given the square footage rating, it feels appropriately sized for a bedroom or smaller room rather than something to rely on for whole-home coverage, and that tracks with how it's marketed. I keep it in my bedroom specifically and it handles that space with room to spare.My few hesitations keeping this at four stars: the filter replacement cost adds up over time, and the app occasionally lags or takes a moment to sync current air quality data. Neither is a dealbreaker, but worth knowing going in. Overall, a quiet, capable purifier that's earned its spot in my bedroom."
    },
    {
        "review": "Although it's a smallish unit, it held up to the recommendation I received. Our location has been in the middle of 18 mountain and grassland fires for the last month. As of 16 August 2026, the AQI fluctuated for the last month between \"Unhealthy for sensitive groups\" and \"Very unhealthy.\" My asthmatic wife couldn't go outdoors for at least two weeks. This unit purified the air in our living room, and we put it in the bedroom at night for better sleep. This product was recommended by my niece, who lives in the Rocky Mountains, which also experienced several mountain fires."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my second Blueair purifier.  After owning a larger unit and seeing for myself how dirty the filter gets, I completely trust in the  efficiency and reliability of Blueair products.  We recently went through exposure of intense smoke that caused red flag days.  We were very comfortable with the quality of air in the house thanks to Blueair.  This unit shows you, by easily seen colors, your current air quality.  And at night time, you can turn the light off so as not to disturb sleep.  This unit also connect to a phone with Bluetooth."
    },
    {
        "review": "The perfect air purifier for your bedrooms. I love that everything is controllable from your phone. You can customize all kinds of settings . It’s not loud or distracting. It looks modern so it fits in with any decor. You can set it to turn off and on when you want it to. The filter life is very long and best of all it detects when there are pollutants in the air."
    },
    {
        "review": "It's really nice to have, bigger than I expected, but that's even better. It works nicely, and I enjoy having a way to see the air quality on my phone. I used to always get a runny nose due to dust in my room whenever I cleaned, but this has helped me not get as many runny noses anymore. I can see very little, if any, dust in the air (like when you see it in the sunlight). I tested it by blowing out a match in front of it to see if it really detects stuff; it went to max fan speed, which makes me believe this is working. Speaking of fan speed, it's really cool and nice to feel; I honestly replaced my AC with this most of the time. The main reason I would not give it 5 stars would be the lights. I hate sleeping with any type of lights, and whenever I change it using the buttons, it sometimes leaves a light on even in night mode, which in turn I would need to fix by going on the app, which allows me to turn it off. Other than that, the air feels very fresh, and I can hardly smell anything; it feels clean and nice in the room I use it in. It does need to be connected to an outlet instead of battery, which makes it hard to put it in the middle of the area without a cable being in a way, but for it's price, i would say it's really good, the filters aren't too expensive and I would only need to replace them once every 6 months based on how much im using it."
    },
    {
        "review": "The purpose of this purchase was initially intended to purify the air in my room in winter, when it is very cold and the windows are sealed, or at certain periods of spring, when there is too much pollen in the air to be able to ventilate. I received this item perfectly protected and with packaging from the manufacturer which I found clever. Once received, I immediately put this air purifier into operation, in order to check if it was in working order. operation: Thanks to the instructions also redirected in French, starting up was easy. I am satisfied to have been able to read the explanations in my language (I am French speaking). By pressing the button on the top once, it is the silent mode for the night or rest; pressing twice is normal mode; pressing three times is full power mode. Observing this process: There is no button that seems to depress, so sometimes I brush the top and easily manage to change modes, sometimes you have to press harder. I haven't been able to figure out where the \"sensor\" is if there is one. This would be the only negative point I would have to point out. No remote control for this first price, it suits me perfectly for my room. This is sufficient for my use. Filtration result: I left the purifier running for about 1 or 2 hours (duration at random), then I returned to my room. It’s incredible how fresh I felt! I immediately felt the difference, to the point that I decided to use it again from now on (not just for the winter), I was so happy, delighted and impressed with the result. Use in silent mode: Although I am very sensitive to noise in general, I slept several nights with the air purifier operating in silent mode. And it went very well, to my great surprise. My breathing comfort has improved significantly thanks to this device. Other modes: Normal mode is bearable during the day, but perhaps not for many consecutive hours if the person remains in the room. Very good rapid efficiency. The full power mode is very noisy, so use it when it is temporary. Personally, I used it when I changed my sheets to wash them, while having aired before or after. If I use it, I close the bedroom door. On the other hand, although I am delighted with my purchase, I falsely believed that there was an air quality display with an indicator light. I got mixed up with the photos I looked at. So it would be desirable to indicate that there is no remote control, no connection with the telephone, no air quality display. This device suits me perfectly, except that I would perhaps have preferred to invest in the model just above which has the air quality indicator. Conclusion: I am very satisfied with my purchase, despite the difficulty I sometimes have knowing how to press the top correctly (I always succeed). Depending on our budget, we will possibly invest in a second model from this specialized brand, which would have a light indicating the air quality. I must nevertheless specify that I chose this for its \"skills\", and this model among the range according to the size of my room and the affordable price of Black Friday. In short, thank you to the brand for existing in Canada. Be very careful about the model comparisons. Finally, I would say that this model would be perfect in a bedroom, whether for a child or a baby or adults, or in a small room intended for teleworking. Happy shopping!"
    },
