[
    {
        "review": "My toddler and I both have severe allergies and asthma. To the point that over the past month we have both been having major issues with the pollen and smog in the air, even with being home most of the time! I ordered this one after doing A LOT of research, and I decided this was the best for the money. With a true HEPA filter that you replace once a year (opposed to once a month) it would save money in the long run. I chose this one for the den in our house and over the coming weeks we will be getting smaller ones for the bed rooms.This review for right now is 24 hours in to having it on in the house, and later I will come back and add to it.Set up was easy straight out of the box, and I put it out of traffic areas in the house. I was worried with where I put it there would be trouble for good air circulation, but it is doing great! In fact with it on high I noticed a tag on the other side of the room (directly across) was moving on one of the toys yesterday as I was cleaning. Then I cooked fish last night (our den has an open doorway to the kitchen), and I couldnt even smell it cooking!! I decided to test it this morning, and sat on the couch painting my nails. Even using nail polish remover I couldnt smell it!!! (which astounds me b/c I hate doing my nails simple b/c of the toxic fumes!!) As far as noise, its not that bad. On high, with the tv and with kids running around it is a little white noise and thats it. I sleep with the bed room doors open, and having a tower computer on in the den annoyed me, however on medium I couldn't even hear it in the den! It also moves a lot of air b/c even when the ac isnt blowing air, it feels like it is b/c of this tower! I am super excited at the thought of having better air quality in the house so we dont have as many issues, and I know it will take probably a good month for me to be able to judge that (and trust me I keep up with our flair ups b/c my son sees a specialist so I can tell you if it will make  a difference or not). I also liked the UV light, since we have kids over to play all the time it makes perfect sense to have it to.Also anyone that has lung issues, make sure to avoid any purifier that has the ion part (where you turn it on for a fresh smell) it actually causes lung problems (if you have underlying problems). Oh and check out the reviews on walmart . com for this purifier, it has hundreds of reviews and most are five star (which is one of the reasons I went with this model even though not everyone loved it on here).Check back in August and I will add an update =)****************************UPDATE****************************** 12/2/2012Hi ALL! Sorry took me so long to come back and update =) Fortunately if you see below I did give a heads up three weeks in we still loved it. This unit is holding up well, and really does a good job! Since buying it (I guess going on six months ago now --WOW THAT WENT FAST!!) it helped with our asthma and allergies. Within the first month I stopped waking up with a stuffy nose, and it was taking particles out of the air so I wasn't seeing as much dust. I still would love to have them in each room, but that is on the back burner. Make sure you have enough for the sq footage of your room. We have since moved to a larger place, that has more sq footage in the den, and also two open doorways leading to other rooms. As such, this unit is doing really well for how much air it has availability to; when I should honestly probably should have one more in here. It isn't too loud, and I love the uv light. Within the first month of us having it we were exposed to someone (a visitor) that wound up having pneumonia. With the fact we have a higher risk of catching lung illnesses, I was really nervous. I think a big contributor to not catching it is because we had this unit running on high with the uv light. I highly recommend this unit, and I hope it helps! =)***********************************Update 6/26/13We just about hit the year mark! Still working great and going strong! Make sure you wipe down (inside and out) once a month (as the book says). Still going strong, and working well! =) Buy this one, and you wont regret it!***********************************Update 11/13/13Unit is still working great! We added a second one earlier this year, and pleased with both! =)***********************************Update 06/29/14Both units are still going strong with no issues. Still helping with our asthma and allergies."
    },
    {
        "review": "My dog got skunked at 3:45am, on 05/24/26, the Sunday morning of Memorial Day Weekend. I tried everything, for several days, around the clock, and nothing else, eliminated, the very, very, very, strong, indoor skunk odor, until this item arrived on Thursday, 05/28/26! Because it happened at 3:45am, and it was my first ever skunk experience, I learned the hard way, that I should not have let my dog back in my house, and especially not back on my bedroom floor. The house reeked unbearably! Especially, in my bedroom! That same day, I took my dog to get a skunk bath, I replaced his collar, harness, bed, etc, and I began trying to deskunk my house, especially my bedroom. My parents let me borrow their $300-$400 very big, tall, wide, heavy, Cuckoo, room air purifier, and I used that in my bedroom, around the clock, on high, as well as multiple fans, and my bedroom and my living room ceiling fans, (my bedroom is by my front door and enters from my living room), and I opened my front door and my (living room/kitchen/open concept) back door, and I placed bowls of vinegar around, etc, around the clock, for several days. Nothing was working! Especially, in my bedroom! The smell was literally making me sick! I couldn’t take it anymore! This all started at 3:45am on Sunday morning, then thankfully, this item arrived on Thursday. I immediately plugged this item in, and placed it a couple of feet inside the doorway of my bedroom, with my bedroom door open, blowing into my bedroom, elevated a few feet off of the floor, nothing blocking it, with its UV light on, and I left it running around the clock. The next day!, on Friday 05/30/26, I couldn’t smell the skunk odor in my bedroom, I couldn’t smell it when entering my bedroom where it was the strongest, I didn’t feel sick from the odor anymore, and my bedroom air finally smelled fresh again! It was amazing! And, such a huge relief! That was yesterday, today is now Saturday, 05/30/26, and I wanted to write this review, because this item, quickly eliminated, days old, very, very, very, strong, indoor skunk odor, it performed better than my parent’s $300-$400 very big Cuckoo room air purifier, and it actually does work! And, it has a comfortable sound, even on high, around the clock. And, it looks good. I am so glad that I purchased this item! (After reading other good reviews about it. Including, good skunk related reviews.) I would definitely recommend this item! For ANY indoor air purifying uses/needs! (Not just for very strong dog skunk indoor odor. But, if it can eliminate THAT, it can handle A LOT!) 5 Stars! Thanks for reading. Sorry this review was long, but I hope it was helpful."
    },
    {
        "review": "This air purifier has made a noticeable difference in the air quality of my office. It's quiet, easy to use, and does a great job reducing dust, odors, and allergens. The HEPA filtration provides peace of mind, and the unit is compact enough to fit nicely in a bedroom, office, or living area. Setup was simple, and it runs efficiently without being disruptive. Great quality and excellent value. Great for a smaller space."
    },
    {
        "review": "So far, so good. I never thought I would buy an air purifier, but my seasonal allergies now require it.  This unit running in a 20x15 foot room.  It is not quite as quiet as I would have liked, but it is no louder than my warm mist humidifier. This is the only air purifier in the house so it really is doing \"extra\" duty because if I shut the room door, the room gets too cold.  Other than the first day and when I get home from work, this unit is running on the lowest of 3 settings. Here is what I like and dislike about this air purifier:Likes:Does a really good job of removing the dust and pollens that I am allergic toWhen using the UV, it seems to take out the molds that I am allergic to (keep in mind this is not measured by anything other than my nose)The unit is stable even on carpet with a medium carpet pad.Doesn't take up a lot of space.Easy to get at the filters (haven't tried to get to the UV light)Everything is replaceable so I should be able to keep this for a good long time.Time to \"sense\" a noticeable difference in the 20x15' room - about 15 minI even notice a slight difference in other rooms of the house, this is much more than I expectedDislikes:The obnoxious blue light when the UV is on. I do understand and appreciate the safety factor that the light provides, however, I would be happy with a dot indicator next to the power switch.Settings 2 and 3 are likely to be too loud for most people to sleep with. Luckily, they really are not likely to be needed during sleeping hours.Overall, I like this unit and would consider getting another one for the rest of my house if my allergies get worse. I would recommend that you run the unit on high only when you are not in the room or are not trying to sleep. Yesterday I experimented with turning the unit off when I left for work and turned it on when I came home. Using the 1 setting, the air was better in an hour (that's when I went in the room). The blue UV indicator light does make a good nightlight if you like them. I will also add that where I live, we are still getting snow on a regular basis so my windows are not open and are covered with plastic to keep down the cold drafts. Pollens are not really in the air, but dust from road sand/salt is bad. My furnace is Gerry-rigged into the air ducts so the furnace filter is nearly useless. (I am working on a fix for that). My house was built in 1892 so I cannot complain too much.I would recommend this air purifier. It provides better than expected results and is a good value for the money. I will update this review as time goes on."
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered two of these because I suspect I am allergic to something in my house. The first unit just arrived today, so I pulled it out of the box and plugged it in. It has a simple dial to control the level of air flow and a button for the AV light, so the operation is extremely simple.I put this one in my Office and turned on the AV light since it won't bother me in the Office anyways. Almost instantly the air smelled and felt much fresher. I do notice a slight plastic smell like others have mentioned but I expect that will fade away within just a day or so. The plastic smell is common to all new electronics (most just don't blow air across it) and typically fades quickly once the item is in regular use. This smell is not very strong so it really doesn't bother me much, I can easily stand the plastic smell for the otherwise much fresher feeling air.One of the things that made me decide to try out these air purifiers is that I have been having a lot of problems with common allergy symptoms such as congestion, runny nose, sore throat, etc... After only having the purifier in the room for a few minutes I am already starting to feel better. My nose isn't running at all, and the congestion appears to be fading, and my throat while still a little sore isn't quite as bad. I just got the purifier so I'll try to update this later after I have had it a while, but first impressions are positive.As for airflow, I am just using the lowest setting right now and it seems to be moving quite a bit of air through, and it's really very quiet (about as loud as a laptop running but not doing anything). I doubt I will ever have to worry about the high setting at all.Pro:- Clean air- UV light- Easy to use- Starts working instantly- No assembly- light weight, so easy to move aroundCon:- Cost, though if it works as well as it seems to be, it should be well worth the cost- Bright lights (bad for bedroom use, but does have an option to turn it off).Update 3/20/2014:I ended up purchasing 3 of these to try and address some health problems (allergies). Almost immediately I noticed a positive effect in the air around me (I had it very close and pointed towards me). After several days I was still noticing improvements in the air quality and my allergy symptoms while not gone were significantly better. This ultimately prompted me to hire someone to come out and clean my AC vents and install an \"AirscrubberPlus\" in my AC unit. It hasn't even been 24 hours since the airscrubber has been installed and once again I am seeing improvements in air quality and symptoms. I expect at this current rate my symptoms will be all gone within the next week or so as the air continues to improve.The air purifiers were a great help in determining what was going on an in helping to alleviate symptoms at a relatively cheap price point. With just the air purifiers I went from being constantly and severely congested to having very mild congestion. My throat is continuing to heal, as is my skin. I rarely cough now while I was coughing constantly before. The rashes on my skin from the allergic reaction are nearly gone, and my skin feels much smoother and better. These purifiers are a great step and testing and diagnosing the problem, and if you only have mild allergies it will likely resolve them. Just keep in mind this helps pull junk out of the air, but doesn't prevent it from getting there in the first place. If you have severe problems like I did I would suggest picking up one or two of these Germguardian purifiers and see if that helps. If it helps but you are still having some problems you could then look into the \"AirscrubberPlus\" which seems to be working great for me.I have literally spent years working with Doctors trying to figure out what's been going on with me (Had no idea I was allergic to anything). I am glad to finally have an answer and one that is so easily resolved. I have spent significantly more over the past years in medical bills trying to figure out what was going on than these things cost. They are well worth the cost even if you just suspect you might be having problems. Even with my Airscrubber running I am still running all three of these. The air is great, it smells fresh and clean, and just feels lighter and better."
    },
    {
        "review": "You don't realize how smelly or unclean your home smells until you setup and run a good HEPA filter air purifier. Throw in the UV light and you have a really neutral almost sterilized smelling home. I enjoy that personally. It will drastically reduce allergy issues if you have them. It has helped me a lot. Even on low with the light off it will collect a lot of air pollutants to prevent you from breathing them in. Its whisper quiet on low, tolerable on medium and I personally don't run it on high unless I'm gone. It isn't that bad but I am sensitive to sounds. Its pretty much ready to run out the box. Read over the instructions and read the instructions written on the unit. I absolutely love they did that. Don't need to dig out the manual later for things.Tips for use: 1. The UV light does generate heat. I would not recommend it in the summer if you have a temperature unstable room/house. 2. Vacuum off the black mesh of the filter ever week or two. 3. The air comes out from the side of the front mesh, try to place this away from a wall or object and have the fresh air shooting towards the middle or most open area of the room. 4. They have multiple filter types for different uses like pets. Read up on these and buy those replacements."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased this about 4 months ago, and I have to say, it has changed my life! I have two large dogs and allergies. Though my dogs don't shed much, they still have dander and they used to send me into middle of the night asthmatic fits. I wasn't sleeping a full night through without a double dose of allergy medicine and an inhaler (and even then it was iffy)...Until I got the GermGuardian. Upon first use there was a little of that \"new plastic smell,\" but it went away after about 36 hours of continuously running it. The first night I used it, I took my allergy medicine, but did not have to use the inhaler. Did not wake up once! The second week after using it, I noticed that there was less dust in our bedroom, and I had been able to take my allergy medicine less and less (now maybe once a week if that). In fact, I haven't touched my inhaler in over two months!I am going to buy a second (larger unit) for our upstairs living area. I take the smaller one upstairs while I'm cooking if I am making something that is really smelly (like fried fish or bacon) and run it while I cook. It really helps to minimize the amount of lingering odors. It would be nice to not have to move it around all the time!The best part though...In this yucky cold and flu season, I am pretty sure the GermGuardian kept me from getting full-blown sick! I started to feel a sore throat and stuffy, but it never broke out into a full cold.I have recommended this item to four people who ordered it, and all of them said that they are noticing a huge difference in the air quality in their home.***ONE THING TO NOTE*** You have to rinse the thinner filter off about every two weeks (and be careful, it can tear easily). I don't recommend vacuuming it (I tore it up, and it didn't seem to get all the crud out). I usually just rinse it out in the tub with cool water and let it air dry for about 5-10 minutes. It will help prolong the Hepa filter in it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought two of the air purifiers for my large combination living dining room area. There is a lot I like about the units. On low, they are very quiet. They are a bit louder than a box fan when turned on high. They have helped my sinuses and greatly reduced the need for dusting. They have a UV C light that can be turned on to help sanitize the air. I usually only run the UV when there is a lot of pollution or someone is sick.  They look nice. The replacement HEPA filters are less expensive than many other brands. Overall I am happy with the units.They do have a two issues that bug me. They blow the air out of the front of the unit at an angle. It makes it a bit trickier to aim the air flow, but it’s a minor issue. My other concern is the carbon pre-filter is pretty thin. If you notice in my picture, the filter isn’t uniformly dense and you can easily see my fingers through it. My bedroom air purifier has a filter that is far denser and is of a uniform density. This will lower the lifespan of the actual HEPA filter. I might try to find a generic pre-filters that are a thicker and better quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "It is a good product, it cleans the environment well, the problem is that it is a little noisy, but overall good"
    },
    {
        "review": "Doesn't workNow having to pay for postage"
    },
    {
        "review": "Effective product for cleaning medium spaces"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "This small, quiet and efficient air purifier is ideal for our needs. It fits neatly into any room, is unobtrusive, and is simple to operate and maintain. The build quality and overall aesthetics is top notch. The cost of replacement filters is reasonable and can be done in less than a minute... about every six to eight months. We noticed that the unit quickly removed any smoke and cooking odors from the area while running. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great so far. Very easy to use and very effective for a moderately sized row house. Within 15 minutes on the highest setting I could feel the difference in the air quality. I put it in different rooms daily. It's light enough to carry from room to room. I keep it on a low setting at night. It's quiet and a powerhouse. I'm really happy with my purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "I only just got this yesterday and used it last night for the first time but I feel compelled to write a quick review already. This thing is a game. changer. Ever since moving to Texas, I suffer from terrible seasonal allergies. I never have in my life until now (turns out I'm allergic to a handful of trees that are native around here. Fun.) Some years are worse than others but this year is baaad. For the past few weeks my mornings have had me waking up congested and unable to breathe, blowing wads of snot out of my nose (sorry!), and with a itchy/scratchy sore throat. First thing I do is take an allergy pill and wait in misery until it finally seems to kick in around mid morning. (I've had a terrible time finding meds that work too. It just sucks.) I don't know why I never thought to get an air purifier. I guess when I thought of air purifiers I'd always think of the fancy Dyson ones that cost hundreds of dollars. I mean, puh-lease. Not happening. Then I found this little guy. Had great reviews, was the perfect little size for our master bedroom (216sqft), and reasonably priced with reasonably priced replacement filters. In a plee of desperation I talked my husband into us trying it. It got in yesterday (quicker than expected, yay!). I immediately unboxed it upon getting home from work and plugged it in. It says you only need to run it for about 15-20 minutes on high to cycle the room but I set that little baby on high with a two hour timer and let it run. When it was time for bed, I set the 6 hour timer on sleep mode. The sleep mode is great. It's a lot more quiet than I expected. I still expected to be able to hear a little white noise from it (which doesn't bother me at all) but unless I lift my head off the pillow and really listen, I can only just baaarely hear it. And I have it on my side of the bed about 3 feet away. Our home air system is louder than it on sleep mode. If you enjoy white noise, you could probably just run it on low and be fine. It has a button to turn off the indicator lights at night too so you don't have bright lights keeping you awake if that's a problem for you. Anyway, I woke up this morning with NO allergy symptoms. None. No congestion, absolutely clear nasal passages, and NO sore throat at all! I'm blown away. I'll try to come back and revise this review if my opinion changes but after the first night and the relief I was FINALLY able to feel from my allergies this morning I absolutely rate this thing 5 stars. Worth every penny!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought one for my mom and one for my sister in law. Good thing I bought it for my sister in law because a couple months later the devastating wildfire in the Palisades of Los Angeles happened. So the entire LA county was full of smoke. Hopefully it helped but I'm not entirely sure how well it cleans the air because the amount of air that gets pushed out the top is not as forceful as my own air filters at home. My decades old Hunter air purifier has a ton more air flow it's almost like a high power fan. But I think it is able to move so much air because it doesn't have a pre-filter like all the new air purifiers use. It just uses replaceable HEPA filters and I know it works because I see all the dust it catches in the filter before I have to replace it.As for the Levoit it has a pre-filter which catches most of the dust and dirt but you never know how much actually gets through to the actual HEPA filter.I recommend the Levoit for smaller bedrooms, it's too small to do anything in a large room. At least it's fairly quiet on the lowest and middle setting."
    },
    {
        "review": "Edit to original review: it’s been several months at this point and I have two in our small farmhouse. They work amazing, best purchase we’ve made.So far: it’s perfect, surpassed all expectations, ALL.Backstory: we’re living in a house from the late 1800s, that has been dormant for about ten years until we moved in a couple years ago. We have five pets, four cats which are strictly indoor and use an automatic litter box (Popur S7 which does great for the smell, it can only do so much though) and one fat, lazy, stinky pitbull. The house is musky, it’s old, it had way too much mold in the detached basement when we moved in. And the pets? They stink bad too, this is coming from someone who is very particular about the house smelling good. The litter box is horrible, the dog is gross, the house is old.I went searching for an air purifier, I’ve been wanting the SHARK never change, but couldn’t break down and buy it for $300. Didn’t try it out, can’t say if it’s good or not.While I was looking at reviews, I found the shark had only 5,000 reviews on Amazon, and it was at 4.3 stars. Okay, that’s not too bad. But this Levoit one had over 100,000 reviews and 4.8 stars. That’s nuts in comparison. I done a lot of looking on Reddit and found that the shark wasn’t even mentioned in the majority of good quality reviews, so I disregarded it.This specific one happened to be in budget and also has amazing reviews.We received it last night and set it up this morning, yep this morning, in our cat’s litter box room which is also unfortunately our closet. That room is the worst room of the house in my opinion. It’s been running for about 6 hours and I already notice a huge impact. It’s easier to breath, the air doesn’t feel so heavy, and the litter box is nonexistent, even right after they use it. Hubby sprayed cologne on himself and not 20 seconds later I walked in and it was gone, already sucked away. I put a box fan on it to help circulation and have it on 3.I’m buying another. Maybe two more. If I remember I’ll come back and review again when it gets a little later in the month. We’re leaving for vacation next Monday, so I’m curious how it will hold up against the cats stagnant litter box, which usually stinks pretty bad when we get home after a week.TLDR; Amazing for pet odor, amazing for muskiness. Perfect and worth every penny."
    },
    {
        "review": "We have 2 in our house and looking to purchase a 3rd. Love these things! Ours run all the time and after a couple of years are still going strong! I've recommended them to quite a few people. I can't attest to any personal allergy relief since my immediate family doesn't really suffer from much (maybe due to the purifiers) but I do feel a peace of mind having them in our home, especially with pets! Does a great job to trap dust and debris. I am always very surprised to find how much these things pick up when I check/change the filter. I also appreciate the white noise that it gives off. We do run ours on the 3 setting most days and it provides a nice background noise, which is a personal preference for my family. There are 2 other lower settings which are much much quieter. The purifier is easy to use and easy to maintain (filters can be a pricey). I will actually clean the filter a few times before purchasing new and have found that works great for us and saves an extra buck. We have two white ones and find that they look nice and blend in well with the rooms they are placed in. One of the purifiers is in a space between the living room and kitchen area (most traffic and use) and the other is near our home office and entry. I feel that they do a good job for the space size. Would definitely recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love the Levoit Air Purifier! It is very quiet all of the time, but if you use the night time sleep mode, you can just barely hear it at all. The fan has three speeds as well as the sleep mode. You can set the sleep mode for up to 8 hours, the best I remember.  I do use sleep mode but not with the timer. You can turn off the display panel and I do that at night because I prefer a totally dark room. I run it all day on low and so far, a week out from getting it and setting it up, there are no signs of anything that needs to be cleaned from the outside as I've seen in other reviews. I don't have any pets, just nasty carpet.  I call it nasty, because all carpet is nasty to me.  I dislike carpet so much! I don't have a choice, though.  I think the filter is supposed to last around six months, so we shall see. I bought a replacement filter when I bought the purifier and several filters for the humidifier, as well.  It looks like I may have to change the Humidifier filter once a week as a week out, it is starting to turn brownish-yellow around the top of it.  I don't smoke and do try to keep an extremely clean place, so not sure what the discoloration is.  I'm the only one who has ever lived here. I use distilled water but also bought the demineralization kit and extra filters for the humidifier in case I run out of distilled water and have to use tap water.  I clean the humidifier every day. It's not hard to do once you do it.  I love the modern look and it is built very well. It's really not hard to use at all. I believe it is super effective combined with my also Levoit Humidifier. I have them on opposite sides of my small bedroom as I couldn't put my humidifier under the smoke alarm. My skin feels much softer and cleaner using the both of them.  I could instantly tell a difference in how well I could breathe using the them.  As before purchasing them, I couldn't breathe out of my nose at all.  The humidity is brutal here.  I have been able to get the humidity down to 58, which is something the local meteorologist said couldn't happen in these heatwave temperatures!  Ha! I only use GENUINE LEVOIT filters and they're a bit more costly, but I prefer to use the real deal and have less problems/headaches. It can be a bit catchy to find them on Amazon and the generic ones keep popping up; however, I went straight to the Levoit store to get the genuine ones. Blessed to be able to somewhat better control my Asthma and all-season Allergies with the help of these two awesome products! Thank you, Amazon and Levoit! Sorry for combining reviews but I need to do a copy and paste for the humidifier as it will save me time doing it this way."
    },
    {
        "review": "Amazing! I bought this to handle dust, pet dander, and pet odor. I’ve had it for 6 months already and it has been so effective at reducing the amount of dust in the home. (See the attached photo from when I just swapped out the filter at 6 months. Crazy how much it’s picking up even when I vacuum twice a week).It’s not a perfect solution for pet odor. You definitely need to stack this as a solution with regular pet bedding cleaning and opening windows occasionally but overall it helps with baseline smells.It’s relatively quiet on the second highest setting. The highest setting is as loud as a white noise machine on a medium setting (so if you have a baby like I do this could be a two in one air purifier and sound machine).Overall I would definitely recommend to make keeping your home clean a bit easier! I bought two of them - one for my home office where my dog sits in there all day with me and one for the master bedroom. I’m not sure how it would work in much larger spaces but it works well in medium-sized bedrooms."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been really happy with the Levoit air purifier. It's quiet, easy to use, and has noticeably improved the air quality in my room. It does a great job reducing dust and odors, and the sleep mode is almost silent, making it perfect for overnight use. Overall, it's a reliable and effective air purifier that's well worth the investment."
