[
    {
        "review": "My new favorite. Easy to use menu. Stainless steel pot. Cooking times are perfect. I cook for a lot of family and the 8 quart can handle it.  You can literally cook two different dishes, like beans and then the chicken for dinner one after another in about 1.5 hours and feed a lot of people.  Well built, easy to use, easy to clean and the steam release works well.  There is still some noise, but its a lot quieter than my old one."
    },
    {
        "review": "This has made cooking so effortless. On the days that I forget to take something out or things that would take hours, now take minutes. Highly recommended for anyone. It's really quiet & easy to use."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been using pressure cookers for years, and did not want to give up to the new tachnology. Being older and after falling asleep on my pressure cooker(and burning it up), I ordered this. I've only used it once, but the results were great. I love the stainless pot, it's easy to clean and transfers no taste. It was a great replacement for my pressure cookers, as now I don't worry of burnung down the house and killing everyone inside."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m relatively new to using the Instant Pot, but so far I love it. It makes cooking beans so much easier. It’s super functional, especially during times when you forget to lay out meat to thaw earlier in the day and feel pressed on timing. You can stick dry beans and frozen meat right in for cooking instead of having to wait hours to soak or thaw. I will say I wouldn’t rely completely on it being the “faster” option though simply because it does take a significant amount of time to depressurize, especially when it comes to food like soups where there’s a large quantity of liquid. I have a household of 4 and it’s great for us, though sometimes I do wish it had more room, but during my research I learned that the bigger Instant Pots take even more time to come to pressure and to depressurize so I just went with the 6 quart option and I’m satisfied with it. It is hard to remove the smells off of the inner ring when cleaning so definitely follow the instructions for using one inner ring for sweets and the other for savory foods (it does come with 2 rings). I’m not the best cook, but this allows me to cook way more things that I otherwise wouldn’t even attempt on my own because this kind of makes it a foolproof process."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased this large instant pot because we like to make bone broth and others students and soups and so I bought the biggest one I could find. Thinking that instant pot would be easy to use was a huge mistake. I cannot get past the installing the lid to perform a test run. This is a poorly designed system. You need to fiddle with this large red O-ring and get it to into the lid somehow I've done this about 15 times now and I'm able to get it in there so that when you turn the lid upside down the rings stays, but I can't get the lid to seal on the pot. The lid is impossible to push down by myself to lock and then trying to turn with a rubber, O-ring is not working at all. I think this is a huge design flaw, and this is not easy to use. I should just be able to open and close and not have to fiddle with this O-ring. I can't even get beyond the Test. I called the product support line. The one 800 customer service number listed here and they want me to send email photos of the product when it's brand new out of the box and there's no one that could talk me through tips and tricks of getting the top on. The customer support person hung up on me after putting me on hold and never call me back. They probably have too many complaints on this product. I would give this zero stars andreturn it if I could, but I think it's past the window so I guess this is going to be a donation because who has time to fiddle with this thing I've already spent hours trying to just steam water on the test. It's impossible. I am very experienced at using scientific instruments as a chemist, working in a lab and I figured an Instant pot in your kitchen should be something that ANYONE can do and I don't see how people are using this if I can't get it to work unless there's something defective with my unit."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this 8 quart instant pot for making Dr. William Davis very famousL-reuteri yogurt or any kind of yogurtThis will do it right because got a built in temperature adjustments & adjustment for how long you wanna ferment you're yogurtEvery moment i make a Skyr, Greek or l-reuteri they all comes perfect with kate agave inulin just follow Dr. William DavisCalled ( Super gut ) & this instant pot will make it perfect for you. Its a 5 star for me....!!!😊"
    },
    {
        "review": "This item broke right after the warranty expired"
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought this on my sister' recommendation. At 77 years old and a widower I am learning the art of cooking. Needed something simple to operate and this is the perfect."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love this Instant Pot! The 4-quart size is perfect for small families or meal prep, and it doesn’t take up much counter space. It heats up quickly, cooks food evenly, and the 7-in-1 functions make it incredibly versatile. The controls are simple to use, and cleanup is fast thanks to the nonstick inner pot. It’s a stylish, reliable appliance that has made cooking much easier. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I like the shape of this one and the death of this one much better than my old 3 quart instant pot let me explain. The old 3 quart mini instant pot was taller and smaller around. So if you’re a person that had a six or an 8 quart instant pot you had to re-buy all of your accessories. And I am in process of downsizing. I gave away my big six and my eight cord instant pots in favor of just having one smaller one and I chose the Rio. It’s is big around as the six and 8 quarts, but it’s not nearly as deep so it’s not as deep as the other instant pot mini design which I don’t think is available anymore I’m not sure this one is bigger around so it’s easier to get a chicken in there a whole chicken And maybe a little bit of carrot and vegetables. Don’t go over the line inside, but it’s much easier at least with your liquid. It works OK see if your chicken wing is sticking up or the very top of the breast, but it doesn’t work for the liquid to go up any higher than the line in there so be sure and note that because that will be a difference, but it holds 4 quarts in total so you should be fine but so far everything that I have made in it. I have been happy with and I like the ease of being able to put a small roast or a whole chicken in there without stuffing it up on its side or something like that I like to put it in the correct way so that it comes out easier. This is the second one of these Rios that I bought. I gave the first one away because someone came and wished they had one and they were in a situation that I think it could’ve been quite helpful so I gave them my first one and now I got one of these brand new beautiful white ones just very pretty."
    },
    {
        "review": "I honestly didn’t expect to love this Instant Pot as much as I do. It has made cooking so much easier and faster for my family. The wide design is perfect because I can cook larger meals without everything feeling crowded. I’ve made rice, soups, stews, and even yogurt, and everything comes out delicious every time.The controls are simple to use, it heats up quickly, and cleanup is super easy. If you’re looking for a versatile, high-quality multicooker that saves time and delivers great results, this is definitely worth it. I highly recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love this Instant Pot! The 4-quart size is perfect for one or two people. It doesn't take up much space on my countertop, but it's still big enough to cook a full meal.Before this one, I used a 6-quart Instant Pot to make bone broth. It worked great, but I actually prefer this smaller size. Now I can make fresh, smaller batches two or three times a week instead of one big batch. For some reason, it just feels so much better, and I enjoy having freshly made broth more often.It's very easy to use, and I love how versatile it is. I've already used the pressure cooker, sauté, and slow cook functions, and everything has turned out great. The stainless steel inner pot is also very easy to clean, which is a big plus.It also looks really nice on the counter. The Sea Salt color is simple and modern, and the compact size makes it easy to store or move around if needed.If you're looking for an Instant Pot that doesn't take over your kitchen but still does everything you need, I highly recommend this one. It has been a fantastic purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am so happy with my Instant Pot RIO Mini 7-in-1. It has quickly become one of my favorite kitchen appliances.The 4-quart size is perfect for small families, couples, or meal prep. I love how versatile it is—it works as a pressure cooker, slow cooker, rice cooker, steamer, sauté pan, yogurt maker, and food warmer all in one.Everything I’ve cooked has turned out great, from rice and beans to soups and tender meats. It saves me so much time, and cleanup is incredibly easy. The controls are simple to use, even for someone new to pressure cooking.If you’re looking for a compact, reliable, and multifunctional cooker, I highly recommend this one. It has made cooking faster, easier, and more enjoyable.Pros:✔️ Perfect size for everyday use✔️ Easy to operate✔️ Cooks food quickly and evenly✔️ Multiple cooking functions✔️ Easy to cleanRating: 5/5 Stars – Highly Recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Perfect size, just a bit bulkier than my earlier Instapot. This one is wider, while the earlier one was taller with same capacity so it looked sleek. My kitchen has limited space guess that’s y it hurts.But works beautifully & good quality of steel bowl."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve had this Instant Pot for over 6 months now and finally came back to leave a review. I honestly use it a lot more than I expected! The 4QT size is perfect for me and my roommate, big enough to make a few servings but doesn’t take up too much space in the kitchen.I’ve made chicken soup, beef stew, rice, and a bunch of other things in it, and everything has turned out really well. It’s especially nice for soups and stews because I can just put everything in and let it cook without having to watch the stove. Super convenient when I’m busy or just don’t feel like cooking too much lol.Really happy with it after using it for months. Definitely one of my most useful kitchen purchases!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm single & new to pressure cooking, so have a lot to learn. Have used it 3 times so far and am really pleased with it. Things cook so fast!! Really like that you can saute in it and go right into pressure cooking mode. Haven't tried slow cooker or steam mode yet, but am looking forward to it. Probably won't use the yogurt (it's just me & I don't eat enough of it to bother) or rice (most online recommendations are to just use pressure mode & time for type of rice) modes. Hard boiled eggs are fast, easy and the shells just fall off! It's the perfect size for 1 or 2 person households. Highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased the Instant Pot recently, and it has genuinely improved my daily cooking routine. The multi-function options are very well-designed — pressure cooking, sautéing, slow cooking, and steaming all work flawlessly.Rice, biryani, dal, soups, and even boiled vegetables are cooked perfectly with consistent results. The stainless-steel inner pot is sturdy and easy to clean, unlike non-stick pots that wear out quickly.I also appreciate the safety features: lid lock, pressure release valve, and auto temperature control. The appliance feels premium, user-friendly, and energy-efficient.Overall, the Instant Pot is a reliable, time-saving kitchen appliance, especially for busy households. Totally worth the purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "It is very pretty and functional I loved it"
    },
    {
        "review": "Love it. Made a yummy slow cook roast"
    },
    {
        "review": "Amazing product, smaller and quicker."
    }
]

