[
    {
        "review": "This pressure cooker has become one of my favorite kitchen appliances. It’s very easy to use, even with all 12 functions — the control panel is simple to understand and the presets take the guesswork out of cooking. Food cooks fast and comes out tender every time, whether I’m making rice, soups, or meat dishes. Cleanup is quick since the inner pot is nonstick and dishwasher safe. It’s also compact enough to store easily but still has a good capacity for family meals. Overall, great value for how much it can do."
    },
    {
        "review": "so far so good.  Honestly bought this one becuase my power quivk  pot ressure Release Valve fell off and i cant find.  Placed order for the replacement only to be told on back order. So i found this one, and I am honestly impressed with it.  I am not sure which one I like better.  This one is  easy to use, the size is great there are two of us in the house unless son comes over for dinner.  Thi one  is  practical, and it helps make meals faster while saving time in the kitchen. The quality feels good and it works as described. It arrived well packaged and in perfect condition. It has become a addition to my kitchen and I would recommend it.”"
    },
    {
        "review": "While this is a pretty standard pressure cooker for this price point, I chose this one because most don't have a sous vide function. Overall I am happy with it. I have a higher end brand at home, but purchased this during an extended stay with family and it's been perfect in that context. So far I have not noticed a big difference between this model and the name brand. In at least one respect, this model is better. The non-stick pot seems far more durable than the  name brand. I haven't been careful with this pot, and in a few weeks of heavy use (like once a day), there's no discoloration or dinging through the non-stick coating.As noted, it has a sous vide function. Don't sleep on this, getting pre-marinated meat at the market and popping it in the water bath without even opening the packaging is incredibly nice; the meat turns out great, it's incredibly forgiving, and there's zero clean-up. It's particularly choice for dinner parties where everyone hangs out beforehand and you want to be able to serve hot food as soon as everyone sits down. Only down side compared to a standalone sous vide is that you're limited to the area of the pot (though the pot is big so it fits most jobs), and the time to heat the water is long compared to the standalone.A few minor quibbles: the yogurt function is not great.. There is no built-in boil function, so that must be done independently. I had been very happy with the name brand version, as there is very little scalding, which is the big down side of doing it stove-top. You can use the saute function to boil in this model, but you have to babysit it more. The non-stick pot does a pretty good job of avoiding scalding but I don't trust it enough to walk away like you can with other models. Given no boil feature, the Comfee basically holds the milk to the yogurt temperature. That means you have to have a thermometer to test the temp yourself prior to adding the cultures, or risk killing them. Other models self-regulate and let you know when you can add the cultures. You also cannot easily add time if you check the yogurt and it's still too runny. A minor issue, but a surprising one. I'll still use this to make yogurt, but I'm guessing the sous vide function is a better way to do the post-boiling steps.Second, the manual is pretty worthless. The model works like most pressure cookers, but the buttons are not quite  consistent with other brands (\"Level\" is not the best choice of description). So, I wouldn't give this model to, e.g., my mother who's never used a pressure cooker before, as it would likely be too confusing. I'm a frequent user of other models and have been for years, and I even found it a little less clear than I'd like. On top of this, unlike name brands, there is no real quick start guide or recipe book. Not an issue for me, but might be for some.Third, the pressure valve is a little subtle and a little spitty(?) It always takes me a second to feel out which way is sealed and which is open, as the markings are faint and the rise between the two is subtle. Fancier models either make this really clear, or automatically seal when you close the lid. The valve on this feels very old school. And because the release is manual (turning the valve by hand rather than sliding a button, e.g.), it requires more care to quick release the pressure without burning yourself. The release spigot tends to spit a little, so I find I need to be very careful. On other models, I would trust my pre-teen kid to be able to use it without any worry, but for this model, I'd be worried they'd hurt themselves from carelessness.Finally, the choice of included extras is a little unusual: a rice cup (3/4 cup, as you'd get with a rice cooker), a rice paddle, a deep serving spoon, and a trivet. I didn't notice markings inside the bowl that show how much water you add per rice cup serving, so I'm not entirely sure why the rice cup. The rice paddle is an unexpected positive, though I suspect most people who are frequent rice eaters probably already have one that came with a rice cooker. Still, perhaps a good thing for college students or others who have limited space for small kitchen appliances who may actually use this as a rice cooker. I do like the included spoon, as I keep it in the pot when not in use and thus always have it for serving directly from the cooker. The fact that it's right there is a good way to never use metal on the non-stick surface.All that said, the durability of the pot is a much bigger deal than the minor negatives, all of which can be worked around. At this price point, the features and build seem on par with more expensive models, other than the throwback valve."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am very happy with this pressure cooker. It is easy to use, the size is practical, and it helps make meals faster while saving time in the kitchen. The quality feels good and it works as described. It arrived well packaged and in perfect condition. It has become a very useful addition to my kitchen and I would recommend it.”"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am a divorced male. I am having fun cooking. This pressure cooker is amazing for the price. Easy to use and colorful display. \"Cooking is an art\" just like a hobby. I have learned to make different foods."
    },
    {
        "review": "Seems to be a good appliance. A how to guide would be cool though. Tried looking at recipes on the website but very few were available. I am new to pressure cooking and it's been very difficult without looking at another product line to get information on times and procedures etc."
    },
    {
        "review": "This product is great for the price, prepares food quickly, buys it for a gift from mom and was perfect"
    },
    {
        "review": "Is perfect, have timer, good size and easy to clean"
    },
    {
        "review": "Efficient electric pressure cooker"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Had a All in One Ninja that finally gave out.  Tried this brand and no looking back.  Great for pressure cooking, roasting, and air frying. Do have to change lids but even that was fast, convenient and easy.  Quieter then the Ninja which surprised me. No leakage or odor issues even after use. Stainless steel inner pot make cleaning easy.  Its settings are very simple, pick cooking feature, set temp and time and wait till done.  Have cook lamb leg, lamb chops, ribs, ribeye, etc all in it and always left food cook as desired and each was always tender.  My Go To"
    },
    {
        "review": "After using a while I can say that I do love this appliance, I wanted one for a long time but didn't have space, I bought this one for it's air fryer capabilities. It airfrys OK, not as good as a standard air fryer but it does the job. I have not used the slow cooker function so I can't speak to that. I would not recommend purchasing this model for the air fryer honestly, just get a regular instant pot...I also love that I bought the bigger size even though it is massive! I like to prep a lot at once."
    },
    {
        "review": "I received this instapot/air fryer 8 qt. It is massive but I needed something this size.I used it the first day I got it.  I cooked 1 pot spaghetti in it. Three spaghetti turned out great.  I forgot to season the meat, because I was so excited about getting it in.  It cut my cut time in half.The only thing was coming the hamburger meat with the airfryer.  It cooked the meat but it browned it to much. Next time I will try cooking it on another setting.I haven't found anything that I don't like about it yet.  The size is great for my size family, it cools great for the first time using it.  I will try other settings to see how it works with the dehydrator, the pressure cooker, and the other settings.  I will update on those and how i like them."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a fantastic all purpose cooking product! My son threw it, and it still works five years later!I can make a meal from frozen in less than a half an hour, and it's delicious using the pressure cooker.I have also used the saute abd steam functions. I will be trying the sous vide tomorrow.I can't say enough on its durability!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This Instant Pot is honestly one of the best things I’ve ever received. I love that I can make almost anything in just one pot—it saves so much time and effort. The size is pretty big, but for me that’s actually a plus since I needed something spacious for cooking larger meals.Every now and then, one of the functions seems to malfunction slightly, but it’s not a deal-breaker and doesn’t happen often. Overall, the performance and convenience make up for it.The best part? I got this on an amazing deal from Amazon, which makes it even more worth it. For the price and versatility, this is a great purchase. Definitely recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I was always pretty anti-kitchen gadgets. The InstantPot seemed like just another thing that did stuff I could already do on my stove or oven. Boy, was I wrong.I honestly am in disbelief how much I love using this thing. It is so versatile that I use it more than anything else in my kitchen, except maybe the sink.The reasons why? Well, for starters it’s super easy to clean. Instead of making a mess with multiple pans and pots and lids with food stuff splattering everywhere, the InstantPot is one thing that’s fully contained. When the timer ends I take out the food, clean the pot, and wipe down the lid and little “gutter” and that’s it. Two, it’s so FAST! Now, granted some things will feel like they take the same or similar amount of time when pressure cooking because the machine has to build pressure. BUT, the difference is that I can set this and LEAVE! When it’s ready it beeps and I can choose to keep the food warm or have it stop cooking when the timer is done.What really sold me on finally purchasing this is the air fryer attachment. I’ve been wanting an air fryer so this was much cheaper than buying everything separately. I will say that while I do love the air fryer it’s probably not the best on the market. When using a two-tiered basket, whatever is in the top portion *will* be more cooked than the bottom. This is a problem I will try to fix by simply removing the top portion when it’s cooked and letting the bottom cook longer until it’s done. Not ideal, but for delicious air fried food ans the convenience of having these capabilities from one machine at this price, I’ll make do.I recommend purchasing an InstantPot cookbook to accompany this. It will help acquaint you to how this machine can be used, even if the cookbook is more oriented towards one of the models without the air fryer.What do I use this for? So far I’ve made vegan chana masala (yum!), vegan banana bread (yum!), air fried Brussels sprouts (yum!), truffle fries (you get the idea). I’ve also used this to steam food to make dog food for my pup with allergies. One of my favorite things to use this for is dry goods!! I will dump a whole bag of dry beans or quinoa or whatever in the pot, add spices, water, set it, and it’s done to perfection so quickly! I’ll then can everything and freeze it so I have beans and quinoa on hand all the time whenever I need them for a meal! It’s the best! Not to mention the pressure cooker seems to really INFUSE whatever you’re cooking with the spices you choose. The beans I’ve made with this I’ve eaten plain they were so so tasty!I live with roommates but this has been the best purchase ever. I’m lucky to have the room to store it, but it’s also great because they can cook on the stove or in the oven if they want, and I have everything I need right in this InstantPot so no one has to wait on anyone to clear out before they can do their own thing.Things I wish it did differently:- I wish the display showed seconds. Minor inconvenience but the display in general makes it feel cheap.- I wish the display showed what setting it was on and what action it was currently doing. For example, a small icon for “pressure cooking” so you can remember that you chose the correct setting. Or a little icon that showed it was building pressure so you don’t think you didn’t hit “start” or something before waking away. Also, something that showed the current temperature inside instead of what you set it to so you know how things are cooking or heating up/cooling down.- A persistant beep every minute or so when food is finished cooking."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great product. I love this product. It works perfect this is a great brand."
    },
    {
        "review": "Grabbed this on black friday promo as it saved on counter space combining instant pot and airfrier. Haven’t trued the dehydrator, but both of its primary functions work well. Makes better rice than American rice cookers, but so so compared to a Zojirushi. Thanksgiving was easier with this as it saved over space and made air fried potato skins the MVP casserole topping and brussel sprouts crisp. Cleaning the air fry lid might be difficult one day, but didn’t seem to need much the first few weeks of repeated use. Also has slow cooker capability. Importantly, the bucket is stainless steel, so no teflon flakes to give you cancer when it inevitably starts flaking off. The air fry basket may have a teflon coating though, so be careful with washing it and poking contents during mid cycle turns.The interface is clunky, but better than having bluetooth and an app that stops working after the latest ios release and makes the thing stop working altogether after an unwanted or failed firmware update pushed out to better steal your personal info and sell it to advertisers. PSA: “smart” speakers or fridges or tvs are not smart to buy, particularly if they have no “dumb” or disconnected capabilities. If you do buy a smart device and keep it airgapped (offline) don’t let it ever connect as devices denied updates for a time may brick themselves when first connected years later because they attempt to jump through too many updates simultaneously. This killed a grandparent’s walmart tv in good working order after being plugged into ethernet for the first time post relocation move as the manufacturer had never considered a user going from firmware v 1.1 to 4.1 in one jump rather than 1 to 2 to 3 to 4.  (Steps off soapbox).Yeah, this thing is worth it despite breaking some of Alton Brown’s kitchen device rules. Replaced my crock pot, rice cooker, lack of dehydrator, and lack of airfrier. Don’t make popcorn in it unless testing your smoke alarm or trying to get guests out of your house. Shouldn’t have to say this, but don’t dishwasher the electric parts like the frier lid."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this for quick weeknight meals, and it cooks everything evenly. The app recipes are helpful, and having so many cooking functions in one appliance saves both time and counter space."
    },
    {
        "review": "Updated 12/29/24 - My Instant Pot timed venting wish has finally come true, so I just changed my rating to five stars. They added a new app option when timed venting is selected, so now you can choose the amount of time you want to vent the pot. It takes the guessing game out of using the timed venting feature. It's the addition I have been hoping for ever since they added timed venting to the app.Updated 9/27/24: They just added a new notification feature to the app and I really like it. You get a push status notification when the pressure cooker starts preheating, then moves to the cooking cycle, then goes into venting mode and when it completes the venting cycle. It's particularly helpful to get notified when it goes into the venting process in case you want to precisely time the venting based on what you are cooking. It's a helpful enhancement.Original review - I have an older model 6 QT Instant Pot Pro and I wanted this new one for its ability to connect to wifi, so I can use the app to control it. I especially like that the app has an extra venting option that is not available on the panel of the Instant Pot itself. It's a \"Timed\" option (see photo) that I actually discovered by accident when I was programming a cooking cycle.  It's not explained anywhere in the documentation or even in the app, but it's very helpful when doing grains where I want it to natural release for a few minutes and then quickly finish the release without manual intervention. This is where the \"Timed\" option comes in. It seems to kick in about five to seven minutes after natural release starts. It varies, maybe based on how full the pot is, but since there's no documentation, it's just a guess on my part. It works great because I can be anywhere in the house and not have to rush to my kitchen to manually change the venting to quick release. I really love being able to monitor the progress from my iPhone and see when it has finished whatever cycle I've chosen.The cooking pot itself is different than my older model. It has two handles on it so it makes lifting the hot pot out of the unit so easy. I also like that it automatically seals itself when you lock the lid. No more manually turning a small knob from venting to sealing. That makes it foolproof. It cooks the same way as my older model, but these new options make it my preferred pot. It doesn't have as many preprogrammed settings as my older model, but I never really used those anyway. I like to use the standard pressure cook option and choose the cooking times and the pressure and venting levels myself.I took one star off because \"Timed Venting\" is not a feature on the unit and it's not explained in any documentation, but it's offered as a feature in the app.  I think they need to point that out somewhere and not leave it up to consumers to find it by accident or have to guess to see how it works."
    },
    {
        "review": "Our original InstantPot just \"bit the dust.\" We LOVED having it and it produced many, many wonderful memories meals for us.While we mourned the passing of our \"Old Faithful\" InstantPot, I decided to start researching other electric pressure cookers and again, we came back to InstantPot and wanted to see what options they had. After reading all of the reviews and articles on this particular model, I told my wife 'PLEASE, PLEASE get me this one for Christmas!\" She said, you can go ahead and order it but you're not allowed to open it until Christmas! Like anyone, I said YES!!!!I opened it and then downloaded the app being that it is Bluetooth compatible. I cannot tell you enough, what a pleasant surprise it was, to see just how easy it was to set up and connect via our home WiFi. I can now use the app to set the time, the release time, etc. It's amazingly friendly to use and works great. One thing I will tell you is that if you, like me, use the Saute' mode, to first brown meat, you can NOT start hte InstantPot in this mode via the app. You must physically hit the start button in order to have the Saute' mode come on. Yes, you can set it up in the app but cannot physically start the InstantPot in this particular mode. I know I\"m repating myself but I want to make sure that everyone understands this. To me, it's a safety feature and I can appreciate why it's done this way. The last thing you want to do is to accidently have your InstantPot start in this mode while you're away or remote.PROS: Excellent quality, every time I turn it on, it immediately conects to the WiFi and can be accessed via the appCONS: None noted at the time of this review."
    },
    {
        "review": "There are a ton of youtube videos, showing you not only how to use it but how to make one pot dinners.It's easy to use, wifi is easy to set up which afterwards connects whether you are using the app or not, to show remaining cooking time. I only have basic cooking skills, so I prefer to watch the youtube videos for recipes than the app for now.Food prep always takes the longest, but once you have everything ready, put the food in, close the lid, set the time and wait for it to finish.When you set a time according to a recipe, that is the actual Pressure Cooking time. The unit has to preheat before Pressure Cooking time begins, and that's several minutes depending on the model. Then the unit has to vent the pressure (choice of Natural, Pulse, or Quick Vent.) Be careful with Quick Vent as it may make some meats tougher than if you simply waited for the Natural vent process.If you enable push notifications, it will tell you when preheating has ended and cooking has begun, and of course when cooking has ended and venting has begun (you'll likely hear the venting process from the next room.Everything but the base is dishwasher safe on the top rack, BUT, you should use a milder soap like when washing by hand, not the regular somewhat harsh dishwasher soap. The stainless steel pot didn't come quite as clean as it should have, so a little scrubbing in the sink made it bright again. You could always wash it with your regular dishwasher load (but not the other parts (lid, sealing ring, some small vent parts.)I'm pleased with my purchase and have planned a whole week of cooking meals in it.I'm currently using a simple recipe of chicken, onions, honey, soy sauce, and garlic. Smells good."
    },
    {
        "review": "What’s the point of having this fancy model if I can’t download and use the app with it?! Apparently I’m not the only one. There appears to be an issue with connectivity and iPhone 15ProMax. I was planning on cooking up a storm over the weekend but will have to wait until next week to speak with customer service. I will revise my review if the issue gets resolved. If not, this is sadly being returned. Lots of nice upgrade features from my very old instant pot so I will be sad if I have to return it.Note: I tried to get app on my husband’s different model iPhone. FYI I live in NY, hardly an out of the way place. Photo below shows what I received when I scanned QR code in user manual to get the app.Update: Figured I'd try one more time today before contacting customer service.  IT ALL WORKED FINE!  I have absolutely no idea what the problem was before but apparently it's fixed.  I changed my rating from 1 star to 5.  I'm sitting at my computer monitoring the progress of my steel cut oats as I write this.  App is amazing!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my second instant pot. My IP Ultra model recently died so I had to upgrade. Here are several important differences from previous models:1) The inner pot has two hand holders - this is great because the previous models would swirl around when stirring. This new version prevents that from happening.2) The cord is not removable - not a huge deal, but wondering why they would make this change. The cord is located in the back left corner. So plugging into an outlet on the back right made for a strange bend in the cord. Wondering why they can't simply place the cord in the back middle. Not a deal breaker for me, but you should be aware of it.3) Steam valve: this works a bit differently than other models. No way to manually vent or release steam. It has to be done through the control panel. It is possible to change the setting mid-stream, but there is a delay of a few seconds once you input on the control panel.4) Older IP accessories may not work - I used to do Pot-in-Pot cooking with a 2 level PIP on top of a trivet. This worked fine in my Instant Pot Ultra. But the first time I tried it in my IP Pro Plus, the pin got stuck, and the lid locked closed. I couldn't open it because the pin needed room to clear. I managed to figure a way out to open it by turning the pot upside down. But this new IP seems to have a slightly lower clearance. So you'll have to use a shorter trivet, or a shorter PIP. Otherwise your lid may get stuck in locked mode.The bluetooth/wireless feature seems nice, but I tend to use the pot while I'm at home anyway. So I'm not sure how helpful it will be over time. But you do have the ability to turn on the IP while you're away from home. It involves downloading an app and connecting your IP to the wifi. The phone app gives notifications when the pre-heating is done, so thats a nice feature.The other main reason I bought this was because of the pressure canning. You can fit up to 4 quart size mason jars to can food. This is really nice. Because of its higher temperature/pressure abilities, this IP can theoretically cook food faster vs older models. I haven't tried it out yet.They also have a feature called \"Nutriboost\". This is simply a feature where the IP lets out steam periodically. Food in the inner pot then gets agitated. If this is done periodically throughout, then the food gets stirred. Its good for things like risotto and dhals where you want a smooth consistency. Its a nice feature but the name is a little misleading -- nothing about this boosts nutrition. It is simply a fancy way to stir your food while pressure cooking."
    },
    {
        "review": "UPDATE: Received replacement and it's the WRONG (older model with fewer features) in the box! This is insanity.Our previous Instapot died 3 days ago, and we needed another before Thanksgiving. The new one clearly arrived in a VERY used condition. Looks like someone cooked a few meals in it, then used it as a bowling ball. Shame on the manufacturer store for trying to pass this off as new. Returning immediately.Update 2: The replacement pot was in the correct box, but had a different Instant Pot in it. The ouside of the box very clearly says Instant Pot, and the device inside also is an instant pot, the same model as our old one but not the upgraded version we bought.Contacted Instant Pot directly to see what can be done about getting the WRONG item in the RIGHT box.Their incredibly lame and disappointing response is \"We don't sell that\"I can find the exact same model we ordered on their website. The one they \"don't sell\"Final update: Contacted Amazon and explained the situation. They immediately refunded our money (thank you). We ordered again without much hope. To our surprise, the package that arrived today was the correct pot in the correct box finallyBuyer beware, the device itself is fantastic but if your box comes with tape all over it you probably didn't get what you ordered. I am leaving this at 1 star because Instant Pot customer servicw was absolutley abyssmal and refused to even try to correct the situation. I would buy from a local appliance store vs. online because of this...getting what we ordered has been a lot of uneccesary drama.The pot itself can be reviewed now:The set in handles that keep the pot from spinning around while you sautee are fantastic. They fit firmly in place and make lifting the pot out easy.The liner pot is MUCH higher quality than the regular instant pots. The disc bottom is thicker than the original pots, and fully 3 ply clad, and it shows. There is no convex in the center of the bottom so you can keep food where you want it.The steam release is variable and no touch. The 3 setting options are great and require much less attention/timer setting. It is also MUCH quieter than previous models.The Keep Warm setting can now be used as a reheat setting, with a high, medium, low and custom temp.The Nutriboost setting is useful for gently shaking the pot while cooking to help blend better and keep food from sticking to the bottom initially.The buld seems very sturdy, very pleased over all with the additional features and functions of this pot. Would recommend, but suggest buying in person to avoid getting scammed."
    },
    {
        "review": "I had an old Instant Pot duo for two years and I loved using it, I ended up getting this one because of the canning feature on it and I’m absolutely obsessed! The app works amazing with it it cans my beans beautifully genuinely love this Instant Pot! I think my friends are getting tired of hearing me. Talk about Instant Pot cooking. I’m keeping my other Instant Pot too so I can have two on hand :-)"
    },
    {
        "review": "The best of all. Much faster than the previous ones. Pressurize is blown."
    },
    {
        "review": "Instant Pot Pro Plus Exceeds Expectations:I was initially hesitant to upgrade my old pressure cooker to the new Instant Pot Pro Plus, especially after reading a concerning review about its Wi-Fi connectivity and the company's financial troubles. However, after some research and a prompt response from Instant Brands' customer care, I decided to take the plunge when the price dropped again.Upon receiving the Instant Pot Pro Plus, I was delighted to find that my worries were unfounded. The Wi-Fi connectivity worked flawlessly after a bit of patience during the setup process, and the automatic venting and improved inner pot are significant improvements.Despite concerns raised about the company's financial situation and app issues in the June 17, 2023 review, I have not encountered any problems. Prior to purchase, I sent an email concerning the app issues and their rapid reply satisfied me that Instant Brands has addressed previous issues, and I am confident in they will support this product moving forward.It's worth noting that Instant Brands was purchased by affiliates of Centre Lane Partners in November 2023, which has likely contributed to the company's stability and product improvements.In conclusion, the Instant Pot Pro Plus has greatly impressed me with its performance and features. Don't let past concerns deter you—this appliance is worth every penny. (I did notice the price went up again after I ordered mine.) I am completely satisfied with my purchase and would highly recommend it to anyone in the market for a versatile and reliable pressure cooker."
    },
    {
        "review": "Everything about this is wonderful. The Wi-Fi app connectivity, the size, the quietness, the look and the results.."
    },
    {
        "review": "It looks like it's a good pot. But I can't say that I checked it because it arrived damaged and I returned it."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "After an incredible 12-year run with my first Oral-B Pro 1000, I finally bought it again!The battery on my original brush finally bit the dust, and toward the end, it would only stay charged enough to get me through 24 hours of teeth brushing (if I was lucky) before dying. However, I loved the performance so much over the last decade that replacing it with the exact same model was an absolute no-brainer.Here is why this brush is a classic:Hygienist Approved: My dental hygienist once told me that it really doesn't matter how fancy or expensive an electric toothbrush is—any solid electric toothbrush is far superior to a manual brush. This model gives you that elite, professional clean without making you pay for unnecessary, over-hyped tech features.The One Minor Con: If I have to name one downside, it is the noise. Even brand new out of the box, it does sound a bit like it might be powered by hamsters while it is working. But just because it doesn't sound whisper-quiet doesn't negate the fact that it is a remarkably solid, heavy-duty toothbrush.A Note on the Color: The color is fun, but the listing is a bit misleading. I thought I would be getting a mint green, but instead, it is definitely a powder blue. I much prefer green to blue, but eh, whatever—it still cleans my teeth perfectly!If you want a proven, durable electric toothbrush that will last you for years to come without draining your wallet, this is the one to get. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Let me start this review by saying that when I was younger, much to my parent's dismay, I neglected to brush my teeth. I would brush them but not as often and as thoroughly as a child should. This was partly due to my very bad gag reflex and partly due to the fact that it felt painful (?). Anyway, I've had yellow teeth my whole life (I'm 29) because of it. I never got braces (thanks again gag reflex) but my parents tried everything to get me to have better oral hygiene and to have a more aesthetically pleasing smile. Now that I'm well into adulthood, my smile being so yellow, and also very crowded, was starting to bother me. I knew I had to give in and fix one or the other. (To be clear if you have crooked teeth don't feel like you have to change yourself just for society - after 29 years, I can say that I truly wanted to change the yellowness purely for myself). I've gotten healthier in almost all other aspects of my life. I decided to make the plunge and buy this in hopes it would help get my teeth cleaner and help reduce plaque buildup. Not just for aesthetics, but for actual oral hygiene.So, I've used it twice a day for 3 days so far and my brother commented on how \"white\" my teeth look yesterday evening. That felt very good to hear, not gonna lie. I think this toothbrush is amazing for the price. I love how tiny the head of the brush is. It fits into my small, overcrowded mouth perfectly. I was worried that it would take forever to brush my teeth since I wasn't doing the work, the toothbrush was. However, it takes about 2 minutes and 30 seconds or 3 minutes if you're extra thorough. It allots 30 seconds to each section of your mouth, it will do a variation in the vibration to let you know when the 30 seconds is up and to move to the next portion of your mouth. It doesn't automatically shut off after 3 minutes (that I know of) if you want to go back and do another section of your mouth, which is nice. As for the pressure sensor on the toothbrush, mine does not work. It doesn't indicate any color or anything. It just appears to be a normal electric toothbrush. I may have gotten a \"bad\" toothbrush since it's not working, but to be honest, I truly just wanted something that would do a deep clean and this toothbrush does that. However, all the other reviews mention the sensor working so if that's something you're looking for, I would still highly recommend this toothbrush. I think mine might just be a dud in that department. The charging took several hours to be full on the first day. I keep it on the charger to ensure that it is always fully charged. If you don't have your charger with you and you need to rely on it without it, I'm told the battery lasts up to a week. Which, is very impressive for a $50 toothbrush. Amazon says that it has Bluetooth connectivity but I do not see any indication of that on the boxes or in the manual. My parents bought me an electric toothbrush when I was little, but I was too young to appreciate it. Now that I'm older, I think this is a great option for any person of any age. I do recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have used the Oral-B electric toothbrushes for many years.  I’ve been told I have a small mouth and the small round head of this toothbrush is perfect for me.  It makes every brushing like going to the hygienist—smooth clean teeth.  It has a timer for a total of 2 minutes, with a change every 30 seconds to move you through the front and back of both sides of your mouth.  I wouldn’t use any other toothbrush."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is the most powerful electric toothbrush I have ever used! I ordered this toothbrush to replace a manual one that I had. My dentist recommended an electric one so I picked this one up. This is amazing! My teeth have never felt so cleanWhen you first get it, it will come with no charge, so make sure you charge it. In the box, it includes the toothbrush and a charger. You don’t get any extra heads so make sure that you order some. When you do use it though, you will love how clean your teeth get! My teeth have never felt so clean! I use it every day. It is waterproof, so you can take it in the shower, which is perfect for me since my mornings are rushed. It is enjoyable to use and to hold, it’s terrific!One thing I really enjoy about it is the two minute timer. It keeps me accountable to actually brush my teeth for a long enough time, and it doesn’t allow me to brush for a longer time than I have to. It pauses every thirty seconds, so you can brush each quadrant of your teeth for thirty seconds, so you can give one section of your teeth the attention it deserves.With the pros out of the way, I do want to talk about a few cons. There are way too many settings to use. I know that it’s nice to have many options to choose from so we can pick what we want, but you don’t need three different ways to brush your teeth. Most of the time I just click the on button and don’t bother with the other settings and turn it off when I’m done. The other settings aren’t even that different. You can see that in my included  videoThe battery life is also not the best. Some people have reported getting a week or two’s worth of battery, but I’m finding I have to charge mine every five days, which isn’t a dealbreaker, but I travel a lot, so it’s not ideal.Speaking of not ideal, they use a proprietary charger which really makes this toothbrush not travel friendly. You need to take so many chargers with you for your phone and laptop. Those might have the same charger, like USB-C, but this doesn’t. So, you need to take this charger separately.Another thing is that you need to really keep the toothbrush, charger, and any surface it touches, clean and dry. Otherwise, wherever you put this, bacteria will start to build up. If you don’t clean your charger every other day, bacteria will start to build up and it’s gross. The included picture doesn’t do it justice, and that’s just on my sink.Despite my complaints, I really enjoy this toothbrush. It’s relatively inexpensive compared to other electric toothbrushes, it has lasted me a long time, and it’s powerful. I do recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great, lightweight electric toothbrush with several different replacement heads to choose from.  Lower upfront cost to purchase the toothbrush than other brands or models within the Oral-B family.  Recharges fast and is easy to take on trips too.  Only issue is with the price of replacement heads - that is where they get you.  Just do your research as the brush heads need replacing every few months and it adds up."
    },
    {
        "review": "Absolutely phenomenal. People weren’t lying when they said it feels like you just came from the dentist. I don’t know how it does it, but if you brush the same way you brush with a manual toothbrush, alongside the intense vibration, it feels like it removes 100% of plaque, especially the plaque that’s hard to get behind each tooth. Also, at first, the vibration may feel a little intense, but you’ll get used to it. But if it’s too strong, just press the button and it will go to a slower mode. I highly recommend the strongest mode for the most effectiveness. But hands down, this is the best toothbrush I’ve ever got in my life. I will say, because the brush is small, I usually apply the toothpaste on my finger and place it in my mouth manually, then brush. But that’s my personal preference. I just prefer more toothpaste. And it sits well on the charging pad. I honestly have no complaints."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this brush and wish I had gotten one years ago! After learning from my hygienist how to use it correctly, this brush made brushing so much easier than a regular toothbrush and I can feel that the cleaning is so much more thorough. Love it. Well worth the ~$50 cost."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this. Power runs about 5 uses for me. Good buy, only thing worth noting is that the new heads are like 15$ a pop which is expensive in the long haul."
    },
    {
        "review": "One of my best purchases.I used to clean my teeth with a manual toothbrush, thinking that if I spent enough time and diligence, it would provide the same level of cleaning as an electric toothbrush.I was wrong.After my very first cleaning with this device, I felt a level of clean teeth only experienced when I leave the dentist's office after a cleaning. And it wasn't just a subjective feeling. When I returned for my 6 month cleaning the next time, there was barely any tartar or plaque build up - all had been removed by this toothbrush. I also noticed that my level of bad breath and tonsil rocks declined significantly. Turns out a manual cleaning is nowhere near as good as this machine. I have purchased this toothbrush for familty and friends, telling them it has changed my life. I wish I had this device as a child!The toothbrush comes with interchangebale heads, so that you can pick the one that works best for you - sensitive teeth, hard brush, whatever. Oral-B makes these products available, but you can also purchase no-name brands as well. It does create quite a bit of vibration in your head that I found a little scary at first. However, despite having sensitive teeth and gums, the toothbrush never harmed them. The toothbrush ahs a pressure sensor that stops once you put it too tightly against your teeth to prevent this.There is supposed to be 3 levels of speed for the brush. Mine doesn't seem to have them - has shown in the video. It's not that I don't know how to operate it - the toothbrush I purchased for my family (in white instead of pink) had those features, as advertized. In the end, I don't feel that having those 3 levels are important, except perhaps to get used to the sensation of vibration in the initial phases of use.The toothbrush comes with a plug and charger. It seems t o keep its charge for 4-5 days (I only use this toothbrush once a day for 4 min). Then the little light at the bottom of the toothbrush turns from green to red, alerting me that it is time to charge it (so I can usually travel without the toothbrush charge if it is for a trip that is less than a week). The charge itself happens very quickly - it seems to be charged within 20 min.I highly recommend this spinning toothbrush. It has changed my mouth's health!"
    },
    {
