    },
    {
        "review": "Electrical toothbrushes come in two types, Sonic and Rotating-Oscating . The Sonic type vibrates at incredibly high speeds (up to 40,000 strokes per minute). The rapid vibration creates dynamic fluid action that drives water between teeth, which is the basis of the technique for cleaning teeth. The number of vibrations per minute must be high to do the job correctly.The Coslus which is sold as a sonic vibration type does not publish the vibration rate. I found it to be low compared with major brand sonic vibration brushes. The rest of the features are just bells and whistles. I can only be sure to clean my teeth fully by treating it like a non-electrical toothbrush and brushing for a full 5 minutes.In addition, it makes a high-pitched loud noise, which is great if you have a hangover."
    },
