[
    {
        "review": "My family and I have been using Oral-B electric toothbrushes for many years. So expecting the great level of quality performance I ordered this one. I was not disappointed. This Oral-B IO is exceptional and arrived fully charged. Also, it did a great job cleaning my teeth leaving my mouth feeling fresh. There is only one small caveat there is only one brush head included and my old Oral-B brush heads do not fit the new toothbrush. There are several reviews that mention the single included brush head is stiff. I’ve not had the same experience. Perhaps I received a different brush head."
    },
    {
        "review": "⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐I’ve been using this electric toothbrush for close to a year now, and I absolutely love it. Before this, I was using a regular manual toothbrush, and I truly had no idea what I was missing. The difference is enormous — this toothbrush cleans my teeth so much better and leaves my mouth feeling like I just left the dentist.One of the things that really convinced me it was working was my six-month dental appointment. My hygienist actually commented on how clean my teeth looked compared to previous visits. I hadn’t changed anything else in my routine except for switching to this toothbrush, so that alone made me a believer.It’s rechargeable, which is incredibly convenient, and the battery lasts a long time before needing to be plugged in again. The design is sleek — I have the white one, and it looks great on my bathroom counter. It also offers multiple brushing speeds, which I didn’t think I needed until I tried them. Being able to choose the intensity makes brushing feel more personalized and comfortable.The best part is how effortless it is to use. I don’t feel like I’m doing much of the work anymore — the toothbrush does it for me. My teeth feel cleaner with far less effort, and once you experience that, it’s hard to go back to anything else.Final Rating: 5 Stars — Amazing performance, noticeable results, and a must-have upgrade from a regular toothbrush."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a great electric toothbrush, rechargeable, very quiet, with a soft brush"
    },
    {
        "review": "Easy to use and great for beginners. My teeth have definitely been getting whiter from the settings. Would recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I really enjoy my Oral-B it works great and cleans better then the standard old school toothbrush. The only thing I would like to see it have instead a smooth finish where you hold it a rough finish so it don't slip out of your hand. I guess it's ok like it is but for me personally if it had a serrated type grip it wouldn't slip out of my hand. I would recommend product it works great."
    },
    {
        "review": "It is nice and working but the only problem i have is the charger, i cant use it here in the philippines since we are using 220v power and the charger is only for US use 110-130v. Seller should have put all the neccessary description especially the power voltage since they are selling it globally. Other than that everything is good. Shipping only takes 7 days for this one and the peach/pink one is 9 days. Ordered both separately."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great! Different gauges are kind of annoying because you have to click through the three settings to turn off but good product overall"
    },
    {
        "review": "Been a Sonicare user for 10-15 years and decided I wanted to try the Oral B. I didn't want to spend a lot, so I found this one and ordered it.Things I like:Love circular motion of the brush instead of the up an down movement of the Sonicare.Love that it has a sensor to alert you if you are brushing too hard. Such a simple feature and hopefully it shows on my next dental visit.Battery seems to last a long time between charges. I am going on two weeks without charging which is great for travel.Like that the handle stays cleaner compared to my older Sonicare because of how it is designed. Toothpaste and water run down it and does not have a place to collect.Things I don't like:The brush had by design traps water whereas the Sonicare brush design seems to drain water better. I rinse my toothbrush and then lay it brush side down on a towel to let it dry before standing it up on the counter or charger. If not, I worry about it not drying fully and things growing.I hate that it doesn't have an auto shut off. It does vibrate every 30 seconds but it doesn't shut off. First time I used it I probably brushed for 3.5 minutes before I realized it wasn't going to turn off.Overall the quality doesn't seem as nice. Maybe this would be different if I had spent more money on a higher end model, but because this something I was just buying to try, I didn't want to spend a lot. If I was completely sold on this brush, I would upgrade for sure.I really am torn between the two brands of brushes. Now if someone would make one that has the best of both. :)"
    },
    {
        "review": "I finally updated my old Oral B Pro electric toothbrush that I have used for 10+ years when it was on sale during Prime days.  I figured why switch if it wasn’t broken.  But I had noticed the charging was not what it used to be and the outer plastic felt like it was getting loose.I was shocked at how much cleaner my teeth felt with the Oral B Pro i02.  I’m not sure that it is the brush, it might be the more expensive Oral B replacement brush heads. Either way you don’t need to buy the more expensive Oral B i09 with so many modes.  The more reasonably priced i02 is all you need.I may return the Waterpik flosser my hygienist recommended for easier flossing of my back teeth.  I bought it for a great price during Prime days too.  I haven’t opened the box yet. My new electric Oral B i02 toothbrush works so well, I think the waterpik is an extra step that maybe is no longer needed."
    },
