[
    {
        "review": "I had been using a different electric toothbrush for many years however it was no longer effective. Love this brush and my teeth feel so clean. The App guides your brushing and I like the fact it is so easy to clean. I chose the IO #5 and don’t feel the need for the more expensive versions."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is great, especially for the price point. It's a fantastic value. If you just want a basic oral, this is the one. It's just like the big guy, perfectly soft bristles, it's not vibration so much as just buzzing and it shouldn't bother your hands. Looks great on the counter. It has a nice group of settings, there's no \"AI\" brushing but I had it on my last one and it wasn't much use. Durability is yet to be determined although it looks like the same as my other one. It's rechargeable and so far I made it a, week without recharging, so I'd rate it's portability as an A+, you get a travel case with it too. Very pleased with this purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "So, I'm a long-time user of Sonicare, which means I've gone through a number of them that always tend to break right at warranty expiry. Though I usually find them on sale, they are not cheap, nor are the brushes, and for the price they are still so prone to breaking down and various issues. So, when my current one started to have an issue (turning on randomly on its own, startling all around), I started shopping for a replacement. This Oral B brush went on sale, so I decided to check it out - maybe return if it wasn't all that great in comparison. At first, I was a little confused, because I thought these brushes mainly worked by rotation, but they are both that and sonication. I don't know if the vibration speed matches to Sonicare, but it doesn't seem critical. One immediate thing I noticed was the light ring which instantly lets you know if you are pressing too hard or not enough. As somebody with gum issues, this is appreciated. Next thing, do set up and try out the app. I was skeptical, but it really does a good job of figuring out what part of your mouth you are brushing, apparently by some kind of bluetooth-based sonar and something in the brush that can tell if it's facing up or down. It's not to the level of knowing which tooth, but it maps the front and two sides of both the top and bottom of your mouth, which is still pretty detailed. Rather than just using some kind of timer, it tracks that you spend the proper amount of time in each of the 6 regions. Your coverage within each region is then up to you. Sure, there are some times when it is a bit off, but I find that that tends to happen if I turn my head. So if you keep your head still, it seems to work more accurately. Not too hard to do. Besides the main brush tracking, you can set specific goals, and it will add recommendations for other steps like tongue brushing and flossing. I started a program for plaque removal. So now, instead of brushing or not kind of mindlessly in the shower one a day, I have started brushing twice a day, with more intention, and it's even slightly fun. And so far, my teeth feel smoother and cleaner. I also get less gum bleed, perhaps due to avoiding pressing too hard. I think this is still a bit pricey at full price, but maybe in this case it could be worth it for the improvement in your teeth and gum health. On sale, I can definitely recommend.  Will it last long term? We'll see."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the Oral-B iO5 and it’s honestly a huge upgrade from a regular toothbrush.The cleaning power is excellent—my teeth feel noticeably smoother and cleaner after every use. The micro-vibrations combined with the round brush head really make a difference, removing more plaque than a manual brush.What I really like is the smart pressure sensor and guided brushing. It helps you avoid brushing too hard and improves your technique over time, which is great for gum health.It’s also very easy to use, with multiple modes depending on your needs (sensitive, whitening, daily clean, etc.), and the overall design feels premium and comfortable.Overall, this is a high-quality electric toothbrush that delivers a professional-level clean at home—definitely worth it if you want to upgrade your oral care routine."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love my toothbrush. The bristles are very good, it has just enough power. I will say however, my only complaint is the battery does not seem to last that long! Other than that I have no complaints"
    },
    {
        "review": "This has quickly become a favorite for our entire family. Everyone has used it, and it's been a great purchase from day one. The quality is better than we expected, and it's easy to use, making it something we reach for regularly.What I appreciate most is that it has held up well with multiple people using it. It does exactly what it's supposed to do, and we haven't had any issues with it so far.If you're considering buying one, I wouldn't hesitate to recommend it. It's been a great value for our family, and we'd definitely purchase it again."
    },
    {
        "review": "I had a different brand before this one and that one was my first electric toothbrush. One thing I didn’t like about it was the size of the brush head. It was too narrow and since it was a vibration device only, the head material being plastic was very uncomfortable to use and the vibration of the head material against my teeth was annoying if you didn’t hold it just right. The size of the head was very small and narrow so it seemed to take a long time to get the job done. After receiving and using this device, what a difference it made. Very easy to use and cleaned extremely well. The brush head size was perfect and comfortable and even though there is some vibration, it was very comfortable and easy to get used to and wasn’t annoying. As far as cleaning goes, this device was exceptional and did a fantastic job on the first try, the rotation of the heads really seem to help clean. The APP mapping of the brushing worked great and let me know where I needed to brush and for how long. It’s not a cheap brush but so far seems to be well worth the expense. It came with three brush heads and I used the ultimate clean one only so far and did a great job. The brush heads may seem expensive but if the system does what it’s supposed to do then I’m all in. So far I’m very pleased with my purchase and delivery was received overnight so delivery was quick as usual from Amazon."
    },
    {
        "review": "To be clear, the cleaning power gets five stars.However, this is the messiest toothbrush I've ever used. The brush heads have two holes in the back, and you might think you could _hold_ it a certain way to keep toothpaste and spit from getting everywhere. You would be wrong.If you've never had a smart electric toothbrush, the ideas here are very cool and mostly useful, but be prepared to have a LOT more cleanup when done than simply rinsing the head under the sink and wiping your mouth. Pay close attention, or you'll have stains on your shirt. Toothpaste WILL be on your chin, your hand, and dribbling down your arm, unless you keep your elbow raised for the duration!I love the ideas and how well it cleans my teeth, but for the reasons mentioned above, I can't really recommend this to people I actually like."
    },
    {
        "review": "My roommate was raving about this toothbrush that he bought for himself a month ago. He knows I try to take good care of my teeth, and encouraged me to consider getting one, I’ve been using a manual toothbrush for my entire adult life. I had a ver basic electric toothbrush when I was a teenager, but it was not great, so I  was skeptical, as I thought I did a pretty great job caring for my teeth with a manual one, but OH MY GOD was I wrong!I took a leap of faith and bought the io 5 with three different heads. I got it on sale.Well, very first time I used it, I felt like I had gone to the dentist to get my teeth cleaned and polished. My teeth feel sooooo good. I am currently also using the app, which is sorta fun, it maps out and tracks where you have brushed and how long, and the pressure guide is very helpful!  It also tracks flossing, tongue cleaning and mouth wash rinsing, and you get trophies for completing a full mouth cleaning routine.  It’s really helped me to commit to consistent oral care.If you don’t have benefits to get dental cleanings, I genuinely and honestly strongly suggest that you get this toothbrush. I honestly don’t think I’ll ever need to go get a dental cleaning done now that I have this tooth brush.  Also, if you don’t have dental benefits, it is very much in your best interest to get this toothbrush, as dental repair is very expensive and having this brush is likely going to greatly reduce your risk of serious tooth problems.Also, I learned that it has a dual oscillating plus micro vibrations, which is why it cleans so well.I will undoubtedly buy another one of these when the time comes, maybe even level up and get the top of the line.Have only had it for a few days, so I can’t speak for its longevity or durability yet, but if it craps out, I’ll update my review.Seriously, do yourself a favour and get this toothbrush."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m really disappointed with this purchase. I bought this Oral-B toothbrush from Amazon less than a year ago, and it completely stopped working after just 11 months of normal use.For a product from a well-known brand like Oral-B, I expected much better durability and quality. It was working fine at first, but suddenly it just stopped turning on, and there was no visible damage or misuse on my end.This feels like poor value for money, especially considering the price point. I also expected it to last well beyond a year, so having it fail this quickly is frustrating.I wouldn’t recommend this product based on my experience."
    },
    {
        "review": "As someone who values a sparkling smile, I was eager to try out this cutting-edge device, and let me tell you, it did not disappoint.From the moment I started using it, I could feel the difference. The advanced technology behind this toothbrush delivers results like no other. Within just one week, it's clinically proven to provide 100% cleaner teeth and healthier gums compared to a regular manual toothbrush – an impressive feat by any standard.What sets this toothbrush apart is its Smart Display, which offers real-time personalized coaching. Paired with the accompanying app powered by Artificial Intelligence, it guides you through each brushing session, ensuring every surface of your teeth receives the attention it deserves. It's like having a personal dental assistant right in your bathroom.But the benefits don't stop there. The built-in 2-minute timer with quadrant intervals ensures that you're brushing for the recommended duration and covering all areas of your mouth evenly. Plus, the pressure sensor alerts you if you're applying too much force, safeguarding your gums and enamel from potential damage.In terms of convenience, this toothbrush excels. The rechargeable battery lasts impressively long – I've found myself needing to charge it only once a month, if not less frequently. And with the included travel case, maintaining your oral hygiene routine on the go has never been easier. Whether you're jetting off on a vacation or simply heading to the office, your dental health remains a top priority.Of course, like any product, there are a few areas for improvement. While the toothbrush does alert you when the battery is low with a flashing red light, a battery indication meter would provide even greater peace of mind. Additionally, addressing the maintenance of the brush head to prevent bacteria buildup would be a welcome addition to the product's features.Overall, the Oral-B Power iO Series 5 Limited Electric Toothbrush has exceeded my expectations in every way. It's effective, user-friendly, and backed by the trusted Oral-B brand. If you're ready to take your dental routine to the next level, look no further – this toothbrush is a game-changer."
    },
    {
        "review": "Omg I love this!The brush handle did come with some dust on it but I cleaned it with a wet towel and looks brand new.I love how gamified my brushing routine has become. I love the light that shows the pressure. If it's a green light it means the pressure is perfect and if it's red, that means you are brushing too hard.There's also an app that can show you exactly how much your teeth have been cleaned. I didn use it a couple times and it was fun because I could mark if I've flossed, used mouthwash, etc. but I prefer not using the app just using the brush because it vibrates after 30 seconds and I know it's time to change the quarter and then I brush exactly for two minutes and after two minutes, the lights are of different colours showing that I have brushed the right amount and I really love that.My mouth feels super clean now!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Works well"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "What started as having just one of these in our household has turned into the whole family using these Sonicare toothbrushes.  Having considered all the various models this particular one proved perfect for our use case.  We have 5 of these in our household.  We do have the white and black models and either are based on preference but over time I tend to think that even though the black (this model) might show residue easier that also makes it easier to see and clean and it's possible the white could discolor over time.The travel case is a nice feature to have.  Have not traveled with it as of yet to see how functional and how much room it may consume if trying to travel light but it's there.  The is not enough room to also store the charger in the case but will hold the handle and the brush (separated from the handle) in the included durable travel case.  It does come with two additional brushes which is nice.  The charging base is a standard two prong plug.  Be cautious as some models seem to have a USB charging base that would require an additional purchase of a charger to charge in a standard outlet.This model has three settings with lighting for each.  The bottom of the two buttons easily move through each setting with each press.  There is a low battery indicator as well.Brushing with this is amazing.  It's much more effective than a standard toothbrush or any standard electric toothbrush used over time.  Even the kids notice how much cleaner their teeth seem after a use.  Brushing harder is not good on teeth as any dentist has told me over time so this brush helps regulate how you brush.  You don't have to brush with the Sonicare.  The Sonicare does the brushing.  You can simply slowly guide the brush over your teeth and let the Sonicare do its job.  If the brush is pressed too hard against the teeth the Sonicare vibrations will halt as a sign you are trying to brush too hard.Overall this device is highly recommended and it's even better if you watch for a good deal that does or had occurred periodically."
    },
    {
        "review": "It took me awhile before I figured out how to not spray the mirror but this tooth cleaning tool is fabulous and I recommend it ASAP. My dentist was so impressed he ordered them for the office to sell. It charges but I never leave it off the charger. You can message your gums, clean as well as remove particles in your teeth. Fabulous. The brushes get accustom but once you do it’s easy peasy. Teeth are white and very clean."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have had better service from this unit than previous Philips Sonicare models, so I'm a happy fellow.  Charging is easy; just place the unit onto the charging pin on the platform. Material is sturdy and quite waterproof and it is a good weight for sturdy application without fatigue.  I've tried to wear the battery down for travel and couldn't do so over a couple of days continuous discharging and still going strong.  It's especially good for gum care along with tooth cleaning. I also like the 2-minute operating length with beeps every 30 seconds."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am a lifelong manual medium bristles toothbrush user.  Over the years, I have seen electric toothbrushes in my friend's and family's bathrooms and never thought I would ever want to use one.After doing some research, I decided to buy this electric toothbrush.  At first, I was not sure if the small brush head would do as good of a job as my standard size manual toothbrush.  It took me two days and four brushings to get use to it.  The small brush head did a better job at cleaning my teeth.  I can not believe how clean my teeth feel after brushing 2 minutes with this toothbrush.  Even my gumline has felt cleaner after brushing with this thing multiple times for a week.  With my manual toothbrush, there were times I could feel that my gumline was not as clean as it should be.  Never once did I irritate my gums while brushing like I did with my manual toothbrush many of times.  The electric toothbrush pressure sensor prevented me from doing that to my gums.The 2-minute timer for the clean mode is good for me.  After brushing teeth, I switch the intensity to the gum care mode to clean my gums.  I like how the brush head replacement reminder and pressure sensor can be deactivated if you do not like those features.  My traveling case struggles to stay closed.  I may have to buy a different one for traveling with this electric toothbrush.I am impressed with it and wished that I would have bought one of these years ago.1-24-26I'm not impressed with the charger.  If I use the toothbrush until the battery indicator starts to flash auburn color LED, it takes more than eight hours to fully charge the battery.  There is not enough counter space for me to keep the toothbrush docked on the charger.  My  Philips Norelco All-in-One Series 9000 Trimmer, Wahl Pro Series Detail Trimmer, and Wahl Lithium Ion Pro Rechargeable Cordless Hair Clippers all charge faster than this thing.  Heck, a Dewalt 6Ah battery chargers faster than this toothbrush."
    },
    {
        "review": "After 3 years it's time for a new one.  It held the charge for weeks and  was reliable.  Eventually it started to wobble and the head doesn't get the same contact to clean as well.  I didn't realize how long I've had it.  Pretty good."
    },
    {
        "review": "This toothbrush is great, gets my teeth clean, easy to charge, etc but whats even better is Philips customer service. This model stopped working after about 6 months of use, and I reached out to customer service and they sent us a brand new -upgraded- model. WOW!"
    },
    {
        "review": "after trying this i could never go back to a normal toothbrush, actually life changing, the heads last a couple months easily, the battery lasts for long enough to not bother me, and its very comfortable to use, insane value for money, i got it for 55$"
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased a Philips Sonicare toothbrush expecting it to last much longer than six months. Unfortunately, after only a few months of use, it started becoming noticeably louder and the cleaning performance seemed to gradually get worse.I contacted Phillips customer support directly through their website. They sent me a new upgraded version at no charge under warranty. It was a quick and easy process.I did learn that this model has been discontinued, likely due to product faults, but given they honor their 2 year warranty with an upgraded model, I was very pleased.5 stars for Phillips - I just can’t recommend this particular model of sonicare"
    },
    {
        "review": "excellent product"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this toothbrush because my old model that’s no longer made had quietly become my go‑to—and I’m thrilled this one kept all the features I loved and then added a few extras.It came highly recommended by my dentist, and I’ve been using it steadily since. It gives that same clean, confident feeling and upgrades things like pressure sensing and smarter modes.Pros:Pressure sensor alerts you if you’re brushing too hard, love this for protecting my gums.Three cleaning modes (Clean / White / Gum Care), gives flexibility depending on what my mouth needs.BrushSync tech: the handle knows when the brush head needs replacing, so you’re not guessing.Travel case included, long battery life, solid extras.Cons:It’s a bit more expensive than my previous toothbrush, but honestly, worth it for the functionality.If you absolutely cannot stand any kind of tech beep or smart reminder, the extra features might feel like “too much.”I’m still waiting to see how long the rechargeable battery lasts compared to the old model.Final Thoughts:If you’re upgrading from a standard electric brush or your model is now discontinued (like mine), this one hits the spot. It keeps the trusted parts I loved and adds smart features I didn’t know I needed. Would absolutely recommend for anyone serious about brushing right."
