[
    {
        "review": "GREAT & SUPER effective toothbrush, had one of theirs prior for 4 yrs but, the button gets stuck & hard to turn on/off. Amazing price & long battery life, in addition great for travel as light weight"
    },
    {
        "review": "I originally bought this toothbrush a year and a half ago. It's a great toothbrush. Small, powerful, and the battery lasts long. It even comes with a great travel case and extra brush heads. Unfortunately, roughly 1.5 weeks ago the battery stopped charging. I contacted support and they sent me a replacement under the warranty. Wonderful support! Will buy from Bitvae again!"
    },
    {
        "review": "So I've waited about a month since I putchased this toothbrush to give you an honest review. The toothbrush works really well, you can see and feel that the majority of what you're getting are the toothbrush heads. I've been using the type with blue and white brissles and it's held up well. When I've finished brushing (usually 2 cycles) my teeth feel clean and my mouth refreshed. The fact it comes with 8 brush heads, a little traveling case and 2 tooth brush head protectors is value in itself. Now, I liked how the toothbrush head clicks and locks into place, so you know it's not going to fall off. The handle is fairly easy to hold but nothing spectacular about that. The motor and the handle portion feel a bit cheap, again going back to the quality of the brush heads being the best part, this part doesn't live up to the remainder of the brush. Additionally all the heads and the extras you get are great, BUT to charge you have to use the supplied charger, why not a universal type USB-C that everyone is using nowadays. Secondly I feel slightly uncomfortable that the charging port does not have a cap on it, so the toothbrush handle ends with a flat, blunt edge where you use the adapter to charge. And if you're like me, I brush my teeth in the shower in the morning, so I know it's being exposed to water and toothpaste ECT. That is the only reason for the 4 stars and not 5. -No universal charger port, no cover to the charging port and handle is fairly inexpensive feeling, however it is a good toothBRUSH and for the price you pay it is worth the investment. I feel if they fix those few things they'd be right up there with Phillips and other well known toothbrush makers. 4 out of 5 with potential to be a solid 5 with some fine tooning."
    },
    {
        "review": "Item is as described. I got the peach pink color and I would just call it pink. It’s pretty. It arrived charged. Thorough user manual.  I love that it is quiet; my old one was clanking loudly. I love that it is well regarded by the industry experts for a price that is very reasonable. I’ve only had it a few days; so far so good."
    },
    {
        "review": "First, there are two types of electric toothbrushes.  True electric and ultrasonic.True electric toothbrushes have heads that spin, etc.  They provide spin or rotation to the bristles needed to brush your teeth so all you have to do is move the brush across your teeth.  If this is what you want, then skip this set.Then there are ultrasonic toothbrushes, like this one.  These toothbrushes have heads that just vibrate.  There is no spin or rotation to push the bristles between and around your teeth.  You still need to physically run the brush back and forth, in a circular motion, etc, for them to work.With that clarified, this brush works great.  The head a nice size - not too big, not too small.  The bristles are firm but not scratch off your enamel hard - as long as you don't use too much pressure.  The head has longer bristles on either side that reach between your teeth and along your gum lines.The toothbrush stops vibrating for a moment every 30 seconds and then turns off at 2 minutes.  This allows you to time your brushing by quadrant (upper left, upper right, lower left, lower right).  This makes it easy for those non-morning folks who suddenly realize they've been brushing one tooth for 5 minutes (you'll understand if this is you).The vibrations take a bit of getting used to - in some modes they can tickle your gums.  Each mode is supposed to be for a specific use:  White, Clean, Soft, Polish, Gum Care.  The modes appear to simply change the amount of vibration - white being the strongest and gum care being the weakest.  I would suggest just finding the mode you are most comfortable with and staying with that.Yes, you DO need to put the brush in your mouth BEFORE you turn it on.  Just like you put the lid on the blender before turning it on.  If you don't, then there WILL be a mess.  This is not a failing of the toothbrush, it is simply the nature of the beast.I like that it comes with 8 heads.  I've had other electric toothbrushes only to find after 3-6 months that I couldn't get replacement heads for them anymore.  At this price point ($20 as of this review), if I can't get replacement heads after going through the 8 included, then I've still spent less than if I was buying standard toothbrushes.The heads do fit snugly and securely.  The more you switch them out, the weaker that connection will be, and a head could come out during brushing due to the vibrations.  I recommend you buy separate toothbrushes for each member of the family rather than trying to share and switch heads out daily.The toothbrush holder is simple but effective.  It keeps the head protected while allowing it to air dry and it holds the toothbrush for convenient access.  I attached the cover to a textured high gloss wall next to the sink and it has stayed in place without issue.  The cover opens with just a light pull on the toothbrush so there is no fighting to get your toothbrush out.Overall, I highly recommend this toothbrush if you are looking for an ultrasonic (vibrating not spinning or rotating) toothbrush."
    },
    {
        "review": "The Bitvae Electric Toothbrush is easy to travel with its slim, non-bulky design and travel case. You can use the adhesive strip to attach the case to the bathroom wall if you don't plan on using it to travel much. The vibration takes a little getting used to if you've never used a sonic toothbrush but my teeth feel so much cleaner than when I use a regular brush. Hold the bristles to your teeth at a 45° angle for 5 seconds for each side of each tooth. DO NOT brush back and forth or in circles like you would with a regular toothbrush. Just hold it in place for 5 seconds and let the vibration do the work! I love the various modes that are easy to switch between depending on what you want to do. It is a solid product with a long lasting charge and an unbeatable price!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I've had mine for almost 3 years, zero issues.  My wife's \"expensive\" toothbrush broke down, so I ordered another Bitvae electric toothbrush for hers.  It is an incredible performer and bargain."
    },
    {
        "review": "Pros: charges quickly; seems to do a good job cleaning teeth.  The vibrations take a bit of getting used to, but teeth are clean and gums are not injured.  Nick package with extra heads, instructions, a case and a holder.  Great for travel as it is extremely light and has a case.Cons: Dedicated cord.  Now I have to keep track of a different cord.2 Minute Timer: exactly 26 seconds.  Not even close.Brush head shed a bristle on 3rd use.  I'm taking an extra.Loud.  Like wake my roomie loud.No data yet: how long it holds a charge.  Ask me after my 3 week trip."
    },
    {
        "review": "Poor product, doesn't clean the teeth properly, vibrations not strong enough.For this price u can get a much better wel knownBrand sonic toothbrush , don't waste ur money with this"
    },
    {
        "review": "It is really difficult to attach and remove the caps, children cannot do it without help. If I had not thrown away the box, I would have returned it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent qualityWorth for moneyBattery amazing"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great product. Light and not heavy to use. Sonic boom teeth brushing! Thank you seller and courier!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Good quality"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I recently upgraded from my old Oral-B Pro 100 to the Oral-B iO Series 3, and I can definitely tell the difference. The brushing experience feels much smoother and quieter, and my teeth feel noticeably cleaner after each use.One of my favorite improvements is the pressure sensor. It helps me avoid brushing too hard, which is something my old toothbrush didn't have. I also like the different cleaning modes they're simple to switch between and let me choose what feels best.The brush head glides comfortably over my teeth, and the handle feels solid and well-made. Battery life has also been great so far, lasting several days before needing a recharge.If you're still using an older Oral-B model like the Pro 100 and have been thinking about upgrading, I think the iO Series 3 is well worth it. It feels like a much more refined brushing experience, and I'm really happy with the purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "What a bargain!! This is replacing our old power toothbrush and upgrading to something much better. The cleaning modes are delightful, and the recharge time is efficient. Keeping the brush assembly in the holder and protected from the elements with the plastic case is such a great idea. The quality of this Oral-B toothbrush is second to none, as expected. The power and vibration of the brush is something we'll have to get used to, but that's a given considering our old one is well over 10 years old. 2 thumbs up on this product."
    },
    {
        "review": "Really like this toothbrush. Holds a charge well and I really like the brush heads they seem to clean very well. Has a 2 minute timer and lights that help you to know if you are applying the correct amount of pressure. I'm pleased with it and happy I bought it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the Oral-B iO Series 3 for a few weeks now, and the difference compared to a standard electric or manual toothbrush is night and day. It leaves your teeth feeling amazingly smooth, like you just stepped out of a dental cleaning.​What makes it great:​Unreal Cleaning Power: The round micro-vibrating brush head gets into every spot with zero effort. My teeth have never felt cleaner or fresher.​Smart Pressure Sensor: This is probably the best feature. The light indicator shows green when you're using the right amount of pressure, red if you're pressing too hard, and white if you're too soft. It takes all the guesswork out of brushing and protects your gums.​Built-in Timer & Modes: The built-in 2-minute timer pulses every 30 seconds to let you know when to switch quadrants, making it super easy to ensure a complete clean every single time.​Solid Battery Life: Holds a charge really well for daily morning and night use, and the charging base takes up very little counter space.​If you’re thinking about upgrading your oral care routine, this toothbrush is worth every penny. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I always forget to write reviews after I buy stuff on Amazon. I should try to do it more because it is helpful when you find a review that is real.So, I bought this toothbrush to replace another brand that I bought about a year and a half ago. The old toothbrush just wasn't doing a good job at cleaning my teeth. I have always had problems with cavities and plaque build-up. The only sure-fire way of getting all of the plaque for me was to use Plax prior to brushing. Still, I find myself in the dentist's office every six months with a hygienist jack-hammering my mouth with water pick to get my teeth clean. It's embarrassing and it makes me feel anxious about my gum health. I saw the Oral-B iO Series 3 here on Amazon and it was discounted. According to Oral-B it is really good at getting rid of plaque. I took the manufacturer at their word, and bought it. Holy crap, ya'll! This thing is amazing!The iO3 has a round brush head similar to the polishing tool your dental hygienist uses. I've used cheaper Oral-B electric toothbrushes that also have round heads, but they weren't as robust as the brush head on the iO3. The bristles aren't hard, but they are dense and arranged in a way that they can hug your teeth while brushing. You can get that brush on every surface of each tooth (except directly between the teeth, of course). The motorized handle has a pressure sensor that changes color based on how hard or soft you are pressing. If you get it just right, it lights up green.The iO3 also helps you time your brushing so that you the recommended two minutes. It pulses when it's time to change to a different quadrant. It doesn't automatically shut off when the two minutes are up, however. That's fine with me as I will just continue brushing other parts of my mouth like my tongue and the roof of my palette when I'm done with my teeth.There are supposedly three types of brushing settings to choose from, but I have only used the default cleaning setting. The other two setting are supposed to be for sensitive teeth and whitening. The default works just fine for me.The build is solid and feels good in my hands. I like that the handle comes with two brush heads, a travel case, and case for the brush heads. I like to take my brush head off and put it in the case after I'm finished just because I'm paranoid about having a toothbrush exposed in the bathroom. It's nice to have the option to shield it from germs.So, TLDR, this is a great electric toothbrush. My teeth haven't felt this clean since the last time I went to the dentist. Oral-B did a fantastic job of designing a product that makes brushing easy and will almost certainly result in you having a positive visit at the dentist, and may help reverse gum issues and prevent cavities. I definitely recommend you buy this product if you are in the market for an electric toothbrush."
    },
    {
        "review": "I previously owned the Oral-B Pro 1000, and while it did a good job cleaning my teeth, this model is definitely an upgrade.The pressure sensor is one of my favorite features. When I press too hard, the light changes color, making it easy to know when to ease up. It's a simple feature, but very useful.It's also noticeably quieter and smoother than the Pro 1000, and the battery life is much better. Overall, brushing just feels more comfortable and enjoyable with this model.I'm very happy with this upgrade and would definitely recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is by far the best toothbrush I have ever used! The dentist told me several years ago to buy an electric toothbrush so I bought the cheap oral B ones from walmart and forced myself to use that several times a week. Thinking that was better then just using my regular manual one. My husband bought this in black about a month ago and liked it and it was on sale so I decided to jump and get it as well. I've been using it for a week now and my mouth still feels as clean as it did the day I came home from the dentist with a cleaning.  It was a little strong on the vibrations at first but after the week of using it consistently it no longer bothers me. Its not loud at all and I love the 30 second interval vibrations it gives you so you know to move on to the next quadrant in your mouth. Over all the best thing I've bought all year. Would recommend it to everyone."
    },
    {
        "review": "UPDATE: product was covered by warranty. Turned out not to be the battery but the handle which Oral-B replaced. So far so good. Customer service was helpful and responded in a timely manner.Worked great for 8 months, now it won’t charge. Trying to get product support without much success, they close support via chat and phone call at 3:00. I’m still at work till 5:00. Bought replacement heads I hope I can still return. Kept it clean and yet it is still dead. Probably won’t buy again unless since this product should last at least a year. Sad, I like the toothbrush. Will update if resolved."
    },
    {
        "review": "Within than less than a year ; not functioning ; tried to seek help but didnt get help afterwards. Ex n not worth to invest. Is there anyone can help to rectify ?"
    },
    {
        "review": "leaps and bounds above Pro 2 2000 in comfort, including quieter lot less mechanical sound. pressure sensor works great to maintain optimal pressure. lets see how does the new movement affect cleaning."
    },
    {
        "review": "This Oral B iO really is an improvement from my old electric brush and gives a better cleaning compared to my old one.It leaves your teeth with the feeling that you have after having your teeth cleaned by your dentist, so highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "Easy to use. Holds charge for a long time before needing to be recharged. The dentist is always pleased with the condition of my teeth and gums. Bought one for my daughter and she loves it too."
    },
    {
        "review": "After two months of use, I can say, this is the best electric toothbrush I have used. When I saw this new type of brush, however, I initially wondered if it wasn't another way of attracting consumers, but no. The cleaning system seems very different to me from what I used before, including from Oral B. FOR:- The vibration/rotation system of the brush is simply very well thought out. It's very gentle to use, it also seems very precise and the result is really good. - The light which lets you know if you're pressing too much on the brush is very visible, it's quite simple to adapt the pressure exerted. - I also like the vibration speed. CONS: - A little expensive. In the long term, if the toothbrush remains as reliable as ever, this could compensate for its price. Conclusion: We love the Oral B iO brush! Hoping it lasts several years."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I have always used the Arm & Hammer Spin-Brush, and now that it is no longer available, had to find a replacement. I specifically wanted one that used batteries, so I don't have to fuss with a charger when on a trip.I was frankly concerned that there were no two-battery units like the Spin Brush, worried that a one-battery unit would not be as aggressive as I would like. And when I first used this one, it seemed less forceful, so my concern remained.Over a few days I realized that this brush vibrates a a much higher rate than the old two-battery Spin Brush, so it seemed to be doing its job just as well as my old device. In fact, it finally occurred to me that the whole idea of an electric toothbrush was to increase the brushing action rate compared to manually brushing; therefore faster is better, offsetting any lack of aggressive power.I have come to believe that this brush is every bit as good as my old one, even with only one battery.One thing I should mention though, is after several weeks I failed to notice it was moving slower. Just as an experiment I put in a new battery and voila! It began spinning at a much higher rate - I hadn't noticed it slowing down, and will now pay attention as it may need a battery every two to three weeks. That's not a problem as my old Spin Brush needed two batteries over 4 to 5 weeks, so it's basically a \"break-even\" on battery usage.It's been over a month since I got this brush, and in fact ordered several because they are very well priced on Amazon; I waited to review it honestly and can now say I am comfortable with the lighter touch and faster speed as a better solution to power toothbrushing.I hope this doesn't get discontinued in a couple of years now that I find it so useful!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great quality, works great, easy to hold!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This was reasonably priced. Works great and is a wonderful option for people like me who change toothbrushes often.."
    },
    {
        "review": "Powerful enough to make me feel like my teeth are clean. The battery life is good. It is durable and ergonomic."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using this style of electric brush for years.  I liked them and I'm very happy with this one.The ones I was using before were various generations of Walmarts version, their Equate brand.  But it got hard to ever find them in the stores.I recently gave up and I bought the Oral B, which seems to function identically.  It is also easy to find the replacement heads."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this tooth brush. It took me a minute to figure out how to change the heads but now it’s easy. Great replacement for my spinning that was discontinued."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great dual action brush. Found it great to use when dealing with Parkinson’s. Just turn it on and let it do the work. One brush lasts me for about year. Replacement heads are also available through Amazon. Easy to replace them. Comes with battery, but I found the best and strongest to use is the Energizer Lithium."
    },
    {
        "review": "Mixed feelings on this one. I've been using it for quite a few years now. I like how it works, when it works. It's just that the brush heads and the brush itself wears out a lot quicker than I like. I generally have to change the heads once a month or so. What happens is while that the bristles themselves aren't really worn down at that point, the head itself loses its back and forth rotation. It might \"appear\" to be still be turning, but check it in the mirror when there is pressure on it, i.e. against your teeth and gums, or test it against your fingernail, and you'll see when it's no longer effective. At that point, it's just basically vibrating in your mouth without cleaning anything. Folks who use this regularly should check for this. It took me a while to realize that after a month or so, I was merely pretending to brush my teeth but not really cleaning anything. Also, once the head wears, the seam/gap between the main piece and the rotating brush part loosens and widens quite a bit and pinches the insides of your mouth.The brush itself tends to wear out after about 4 to 5 months, where once again it still \"appears\" to be working, but if you check carefully, you'll find that even if you put a new head in there, the rotating properties diminish greatly. I think the inner mechanism simply wears out by then, and no longer connects and moves the brush head as well. Yes, once again, let's all thank corporate America for \"Planned Obsolescence\".I used to use Sonic Care. The $125 model I bought was good, but no longer held a charge after 2 years. How convenient for Sonic Care. Then I tried their battery operated $40 model, which worked OK but had a really stupidly designed battery cap which allowed water to flow into the compartment. Wow, that's TITANICALLY STUPID!!! Anyway, found this and works OK ... and have been using it since. However, not without the stated reservations. If one were to change the brush and brush heads as often as necessary (which I do), it's not really all that cheap to use. It's actually pretty expensive to use. About 10 to 12 heads and 2 or 3 brushes a year. Do the math. If I find a better alternative, I'll switch without too much nostalgia, ha ha.Note: I do want to state that my brushing routine is probably a lot more thorough and longer than most (about 5 minutes per session), so others may get a longer \"effective life\" than I get. But still, can't imagine their recommendation of changing the heads every 3 months being adequate. Folks who use this really should monitor the \"TRUE effective life\" of their brushes and heads, otherwise you might \"think\" you're brushing your teeth, but might actually be doing nothing to effectively \"clean\" them.Hope this is helpful.Cheers"
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like this brush, especially because it is battery operated: practical and easy to use on a daily basis."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent product, very difficult to find the sameModel. I would recommend it anyday, if available make sure to buy it with some extra brush heads."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great Brush. No charging, no wires, just a AA battery."
    },
    {
        "review": "AVE PERSO LA FIDUCIA DI TROVARLO, MA NAVIGANDO SU AMAZON RITROVATO IL PRODOTTO DA ME CERCATO, ARRIVATO IN TEMPO."
    },
    {
        "review": "I use the same toothbrush for years now"
    }
