[
    {
        "review": "I am beyond impressed with this toothbrush! I’ve been using it for a while now, and the battery life is absolutely mind-blowing—the claim of up to 180 days is no joke, as I haven't had to recharge it once since the initial charge. It's incredibly convenient, especially if you hate dealing with charging bases taking up counter space or traveling with extra cords.With 42,000 VPM, it delivers a powerful, deep clean that leaves my teeth feeling like I just left the dentist’s chair every single day. What really sets it apart, though, is the customization. Having 5 different modes and 3 intensity levels means anyone can find their perfect setting. It’s gentle enough for sensitive areas and braces but powerful enough to tackle plaque easily.On top of the stellar performance, it comes with 8 replacement brush heads, which easily covers a couple of years of use right out of the box. The sleek black design looks great on the bathroom counter, too. If you’re looking for a high-quality, long-lasting sonic toothbrush without the premium price tag, this is absolutely the one to get. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m extremely impressed with this electric toothbrush! The combination of 5 cleaning modes and 3 intensity levels makes it easy to customize the brushing experience, especially for those with sensitive teeth or braces. I was worried that an electric toothbrush might be too harsh, but the adjustable intensity settings allow for a gentle yet effective clean.The different modes are great for everyday cleaning, gum care, whitening, and sensitive areas.One of the best features is the inclusion of 8 replacement brush heads, which provides excellent value and means you won't need to purchase extras anytime soon. The brush heads are soft, durable, and reach difficult areas with ease.After using it for a week, my teeth feel noticeably cleaner, and my gums seem healthier. The battery life is impressive, and the toothbrush is lightweight and comfortable to hold.Overall, this is a fantastic electric toothbrush that offers premium features at a great value. I highly recommend it for anyone with sensitive teeth, braces, or anyone looking to upgrade their oral care routine."
    },
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love this rechargeable electric toothbrush! It provides powerful vibrations that leave my teeth feeling incredibly clean after every use. The battery lasts a long time, and being waterproof makes it perfect for everyday use. I also love that it comes with several replacement brush heads, which makes it an even better value. It’s easy to use, comfortable to hold, and has become one of my favorite purchases. I highly recommend it to anyone looking for an affordable, high-quality electric toothbrush."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've purchased three 7MAGIC hair dryers before, and they've never disappointed me. This electric toothbrush continues that positive experience. It feels well made, delivers powerful cleaning, and offers excellent value for the price.The sonic vibration is strong yet comfortable, and I like having multiple brushing modes and intensity levels to choose from. The long battery life is a huge plus, and including eight brush heads means I won't need replacements for a long time.Overall, this is a good-quality toothbrush with great performance and thoughtful features. Based on my experience with other 7MAGIC products, this brand continues to impress. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I was skeptical because of the price but I ordered another one for my partner right after I brushed my teeth with it the first time. I got smooth clean teeth the very first brushing with this toothbrush! It felt like I just left the dentist. It has multiple settings. My partner loves his. This is the best toothbrush I have ever had. I like this one better than the $60 one I had a few years ago."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using an inexpensive battery powered toothbrush for the last few years.  A friend suggested this 7Magic Sonic Electric Toothbrush.  I’m so happy to upgrade!  The battery powered one was becoming difficult to find replacement heads and would often break when trying to change the battery.  This 7Magic Electric toothbrush is hands down the best toothbrush I’ve ever owned.  My teeth feel cleaner.  The charge lasts a long time.  I love the 3 different speeds and cleaning options from Sensitive, gum care, polish, whitening to cleaning!  I’ve been pleasantly surprised by the overall quality!!When it arrived, there was already a full charge, ready to use right away. The extra brush heads are also a huge bonus, I now don’t need to worry about trying to find a replacement any time soon.For the price, I think this toothbrush is a great value.  I would absolutely recommend it to anyone looking for an affordable and reliable electric toothbrush."
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered this toothbrush in pink for myself, and I really like it especially that it comes with 8 replacement heads. Also, the charger for the toothbrush is a regular newer Apple iPhone cord which makes taking it with you and charging it very convenient. My husband liked my toothbrush, so I told him I’d order one for him in the black color for our anniversary. It just arrived and we were sent the navy blue color. Not the color I chose or paid for, but he doesn’t want to waste the time for me to exchange it for the black one. Nor do I feel like making the drive to drop it off and then wait for the new one to arrive either. Hoping that going forward they check which color was selected before just adding one to peoples orders. Overall, we are enjoying the toothbrushes! Would have been perfect if it had a travel container to store it in order to keep it from breaking when traveling since the brush heads extender parts are extremely thin."
    },
    {
        "review": "Before I started using this electric toothbrush, I always felt like my teeth weren't completely clean, especially in those hard-to-reach areas. Even after brushing, I could still feel plaque along my gum line.After switching to this toothbrush, I noticed a difference almost immediately. My teeth feel much smoother after every use, and my mouth feels cleaner throughout the day. I also love that it does most of the work for me, so I don't have to worry about brushing too hard or missing certain spots.The battery lasts a long time, it's comfortable to hold, and the different cleaning modes are a great bonus. Overall, this has really improved my daily oral care routine, and I honestly don't think I'd go back to a regular toothbrush. If you're thinking about upgrading, I definitely recommend giving this one a try."
    },
    {
        "review": "Purchased to replace my old electric toothbrush and I must say I was pleasantly surprised. Cleaning is truly effective: the sonic vibrations are powerful but at the same time delicate on the gums, and after just a few uses you can perceive a sensation of smoother and cleaner teeth. The different modes of use and intensity levels are very convenient, allowing you to personalize the experience according to your needs. The integrated timer which helps to respect the times recommended by the dentist is also highly appreciated. The real gem, however, is the charging via USB Type-C. Finally no bulky bases or proprietary cables: I can recharge it with the same smartphone charger, very convenient especially when travelling. The battery life also seems excellent and allows you to forget about charging for a long time. Good build quality, elegant design and silent during use. Considering the price, it is a purchase that I would make again without hesitation. Advised!"
    },
    {
        "review": "My favorite for €20: I bought this 40,000 VPM sonic electric toothbrush for around twenty euros and I am literally won over. For this price, I didn't expect such quality. It's by far the best health investment I've made this year! The feeling of absolute cleanliness: What amazed me the most was the impression of having ultra-clean teeth after each brushing, as if I had just come from a scaling at the dentist. The 40,000 vibrations per minute really disintegrate dental plaque spectacularly. My teeth are smooth and perfectly cleaned. Versatility and customization: 5 brushing modes: Whitening, cleaning, sensitive, polishing and gum massage - enough to adapt to all needs 3 adjustable intensities: Perfect for alternating according to the sensitivity of my gums IPX7 waterproof: I can use it in the shower without any problem Exceptional battery life: The battery is truly impressive. It easily lasts a full month with two daily brushings. Some high-end brushes advertise 3 months, and even if I don't quite reach the 90 days advertised, one month of autonomy is already exceptional for this price. Accessories included: The box comes with several replacement brush heads, which represents a real saving in the long term. No need to immediately buy brush heads again. Why I recommend 200%: For €20, you get sonic technology comparable to €100-200 models. The difference in feeling of cleanliness with a manual brush is just phenomenal. My gums are healthier and my teeth are significantly whiter. My verdict: If you are still hesitant about going electric, go for this model. The quality/price ratio is unbeatable and your dentist will thank you during your next visit! If this review was useful to you, do not hesitate to click on the \"Helpful\" button below, it helps me a lot!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The electric toothbrush has surprised me very positively. Cleaning is very effective and you can see the difference from the first uses: cleaner teeth and a fresh mouth feeling for longer. It has many modes and intensity levels, which allows you to easily adapt it according to the sensitivity of your gums. The pressure sensor is a great success, especially so as not to press too hard, and the timer helps to respect the recommended brushing time. It includes several replacement heads, which is very practical, and the battery lasts a long time on a single charge. In addition, it is comfortable to handle and the design is elegant and discreet. In general, it is a very complete, powerful brush with good value for money. Totally recommended for daily use."
    },
    {
        "review": "I was looking for an electronic toothbrush with a reasonable price/performance ratio. And first of all, I wasn't disappointed. As always with Amazon, the delivery was very quick. The toothbrush is black and, to my delight, very light. It offers many good settings. What I like best is that the intensity can be selected in three levels. The individual programs are also very good. The toothbrush comes with various replacement brushes. A charging cable and a practical wall bracket are also included in the scope of delivery. Another big plus is the quiet volume of the toothbrush during use. You don't feel like you're using a sledgehammer like you do with some other electronic toothbrushes. I've been using them for a while now and I have to say I don't want to miss them anymore. My gums are also doing much better and I can always use the different programs that are most convenient. The programs are very easy to set. One button is for intensity and the other for selecting the program. The last program used remains the same. My children were able to try it out thanks to the additional heads included in the delivery and they now have their own because they are as excited as I am. And the battery lasts really long. Here the price/performance is more than okay! And I don't want to give it away anymore."
    },
    {
        "review": "Used in tandem with my regular electric brush-"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Take in mind when you read most electric toothbrush reviews, they are coming from manual so OF COURSE YOUR TEETH FEEL AMAZING AND CLEAN, but what about when you’re coming from a really good electric toothbrush (Phillips Sonicare and another cheaper one that both felt like improvements after manual) and there are so many choices without a clear understanding what makes one $79 while another is over $200?  I started to go a little crazy trying to figure it out.  I asked one dentist to suggest and she said either oral b or sonicare (she doesn’t sell them at the office) while another said oral b (he did sell them) so that was not really helpful.  When pressed my dentist who doesn’t sell them prefers oral b and she likes the smaller head.  I GET THAT NOW!  It’s like I’m polishing each tooth and wrapping the head around the tooth almost and I LOVE THAT!  I think the Phillips isn’t getting in between near as well.  The thing about either brand is that there is such a wide price range that I couldn’t tell the real $100 difference other than maybe an app and possibly more cleaning modes but that’s about it.  I decided to go with oral b to try this round more precise head and went to their website to take the quiz to see what was best for me and this is where I landed.  I wanted to stay under $100 (and you can on Black Friday and other big sales but I missed it and paid $119 which isn’t terrible if it’s significantly better than my last electric).  I just used it for the first time and MY TEETH FEEL AMAZING , in fact my whole mouth feels so clean.  I’m someone who buys a firmer bristle head (NOT HARD but I need to feel scrubbed if makes sense).  I think sometimes I may be hard on my gums trying to really scrub my teeth but the happy medium is in this oral b brush head! I’m just not clear which one it is as it came with 2 and says one is ultimate clean and the other is gentle care.  I’m assuming it’s ultimate but it’s soft but really dense and just scrubs but it’s gentle on the gums.  Love it.  Very satisfied.  It’s not loud at all and it’s got a great light sensor that indicates when you’re at the perfect pressure.  I actually found it quite helpful and it’s clearly visible even if you’re not looking in the mirror.  I’m kind of excited about the app because after a long lifetime of heat checkups, something has gone wrong and I’m facing some pretty big restorative dental work so perhaps I’ve been slacking I don’t know But I’m trying to be very diligent and that’s part of the reason for the new purchase.  I also felt like my old one wasn’t getting me as clean as it used it so it could be I needed something more aggressive.  This is really perfect and considering the price tags you can easily go up to on the big name models, I think this really is the sweet spot for an electric toothbrush ESPECIALLY IF YOU’RE NOT COMING FROM MANUAL. If you’re coming from manual, any real electric toothbrush will be so impressive but I needed to be impressed after exclusively using electric.  This is it. I’ve got no doubt about the battery life.. they are all that way.. the travel case is a great touch and it’s nice. Nothing like having your electric toothbrush go off in your closed suitcase when you’re all packed.  lol.  I was always able to get off brand replacement heads for my sonicare that were great at a fraction of the price.  I’ll be interested to see if I can get a real match to this one otherwise it may be worth it to stick brand name.  Here’s to your dental health and perfect check ups."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is truly an amazing toothbrush.  I find this does a much better job of cleaning my teeth and removing plaque.  The features are pretty cool-it's the little things, right?  You can change the colors of light (where the pressure sensor is) with multiple options.  It has a magnetic charger at the base.  The case has a charger feature which is a great feature-it comes with a cord and a power adapter-you can't even get that for $1300 cell phones anymore.  It even has an interactive display-yes I like the smiley face when I'm done.  I haven't tried the app yet, I've been brushing for a long time without one but I'll give it a shot because I do enjoy technology. This is quieter than my first Oral B but still sounds like a small drone in my head, still fairly quiet. The bristles are comfortable.  Battery life is pretty good so far. Best part? I got it for a great deal when it was on sale last week. This is light years better than their competitor (rhymes with monic air) which I purchased for a lot more and wish I had returned when I had the chance. I hate it so much I'm willing to give a $200 toothbrush away.  It may not be the newest in the iO line but I'm really impressed so far.  Time will tell on how durable it is but I'm going to stay with the Oral Be family."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using this for a month, I normally only brush once a day because of my rushed schedule.  I have noticed a whiter smile and cleaner feeling teeth.  My son loves this, every night I brush my teeth with this using the app and at the same time he copies the directions with his normal toothbrush.  It takes us 2 min 20 seconds to get a perfect clean score and at 10yrs old he is ok with that.  The app shows you when to change sections of your teeth and how much pressure to use with customizable colors.  its a little spendy but worth it for the clean feeling .  It lasts about 6 brushes per charge and can charge in or out of the case.  The app is easy to use and even with out the app the brush communicates to you through color about how much pressure to use."
    },
    {
        "review": "This toothbrush turned out to be a great purchase. I spent a lot of time comparing models, reading reviews, and trying to stay within a reasonable price range, and the Oral-B iO Deep Clean with Protect checked all the right boxes.It feels well-designed and comfortable to use, and the clean is noticeably better than a standard electric toothbrush without being harsh on my gums. The brushing experience feels controlled and thorough rather than aggressive, which I really appreciate.Setup was easy, charging is straightforward, and overall it feels like a quality product that delivers exactly what it promises. I’m very happy with this purchase and would recommend it to anyone looking for an effective, reliable electric toothbrush without going overboard on cost."
    },
    {
        "review": "Wow. This Oral B is a big improvement over the one I replaced. It’s whisper quiet in comparison, and I really like the pressure sensor light (green if good pressure, red if too much pressure, white if too little pressure). I also like that I can set the brush mode (speed) to “sensitive”, which is what I use exclusively with a sensitive brush head. My older Oral B only oscillated. This newer one both oscillates and micro-vibrates.My old Oral B was about 10-12 yrs old. It still worked perfectly. Buying sensitive brushes had become fairly inexpensive. I’m pretty sure it would have kept on working at least another 5 yrs. However, my hygienist repeatedly told me: “You’re not doing this, you’re not doing that, blah blah blah.” Tiresome. Sometimes the brush would strike under the gum line around a crown and cause lingering pain.I learned about the new Oral B with the pressure sensor and decided to buy one. Here was the surprising thing to me: I wasn’t brushing hard enough, at least according to the pressure sensor. The first time I used it, I was repeatedly in the white zone (too little pressure).Also, here’s the thing that really did it for me, I didn’t really know how to brush correctly. I found a video on YouTube (“Tips On How To Brush with an Oral B Electric Toothbrush” by Murmann Dental Health) that explained and demonstrated exactly how to brush using an Oral B with pressure sensor. That was very illuminating. I highly recommend that or a similar video. The thing that stood out from the video was that our teeth are rounded, so we need to wrap the brush around each individual tooth .I’ve been following what I learned in the video. So far, the brush hasn’t caused pain under the gum line. The IO sensitive brush along with the “sensitive” setting on the device have been a more comfortable brushing experience for me. I’m consistently in the green zone. Hopefully, it all makes a difference at my next dental appointment.I was sorry to see my old Oral B go as it was still useful, but sometimes useful doesn’t mean effective or appropriate for teeth & gum challenges. It can still be useful for other purposes.I have never used the app, so no comment there.The travel case is very nice and will come in handy. The only thing I don’t like about it is it doesn’t include storage for what seems to be a proprietary charger. The charger is two-pin, and I guess it’s supposedly safer to use in wet environments; you may need to include it in your travel bag depending on your travel time.5 stars from me."
    },
    {
        "review": "My original Oral-B electric toothbrush died partway through brushing so I replaced it. I thought I was getting basically the same version and for the most part it is the same. This is a Smart version which is new. I liked using the app to set it up the way I like it but there’s no way I’m going to try to keep track of whether I brush each area of my mouth adequately. Otherwise it works well and as expected. I don’t find it to be any noisier than my last one but it did cost quite a bit more."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought my first oral b in 2016, what would be the equivalent of this model back then. I’ve thoroughly enjoyed it, and used it religiously all these years and it’s still going strong but the rubber face is starting to degrade so I figured I’d upgrade. I was NOT expecting the technology to have advanced so much, it is MUCH more powerful than the old style, with much less vibration and noise. It feels like I’m achieving the same clean in half the time with this one, and the new brush head style doesn’t have that stupid hole that dribbles toothpaste slobber all over your face like the old one. The screen is an added “cool factor” but doesn’t really offer a life changing upgrade aside from being able to see the battery percentage. The new charging dock design is nice, makes it easier to wipe clean without the little peg in the middle. All in all, this is a very nice upgrade and well worth the price. Here’s to the next 10 years of compliments from my dentist!"
