[
    {
        "review": "I purchased the Philips Sonicare DiamondClean 9000 Electric Toothbrush as a 2-pack (black and white) and have been very happy with the overall quality and performance. Having two handles in one package is extremely convenient—for example, one for home and one for travel, or one for myself and one for a partner—without needing to buy a second set separately. The build quality feels solid, and both brushes look sleek and modern, with a premium finish that matches the price point.In terms of brushing performance, the sonic cleaning is excellent. My teeth feel noticeably smoother and cleaner compared to a standard manual toothbrush, and the different modes make it easy to tailor the experience to daily cleaning, gum care, or more intensive polishing. The pressure sensor and timing guidance are genuinely useful; they help prevent brushing too hard and encourage you to cover the full mouth evenly, which is a nice touch for long-term gum and enamel health.The app connectivity is a bonus, especially if you like data and feedback. It can help reinforce better brushing habits and highlight areas you might be missing, though it does add a layer of complexity—Bluetooth pairing and checking the phone during brushing isn’t for everyone. Battery life has been good so far, but you do need to stay on top of charging both handles, especially if you’re traveling frequently or using multiple modes.Overall, this dual-handle DiamondClean 9000 set is a great choice if you want top-tier cleaning performance, smart features, and a premium look, and you value having two brushes in one package. The cost is on the higher side, but if oral health and convenience are priorities, it’s a strong investment."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love my Sonicare! Gave the black one to my son. Price was fantastic and the settings are great. The charger cup is super cute and the rechargeable case is a must! The speed and vibration are unmatched without clunky noise and the “deep clean” setting is perfect for the evening brush. The whitening setting is great for morning to set my smile for success. Quality is always expected from Sonicare."
    },
    {
        "review": "I needed a new toothbrush, and was very happy to find this set.  I got it during Amazon prime day and it was much cheaper than I have seen it in stores.  I had the same diamond clean, but the last version of it.  This one definitely vibrates with more intensity.  It cleans really well.  The quality is great.  I had the glass with my last toothbrush and the glass can still fit on top of this charger or you can use it with the plastic charger.  I have been using it with the plastic charger instead of the glass. It seems more compact that way.  It charges with no issues and it has an app that connects to the toothbrushes and it tells you how long that you’ve been brushing each day and how many times a day that you’re brushing and it gives you goals.  I really like that new feature.  It’s makes it fun to be able to see how long I’ve been brushing my teeth."
    },
    {
        "review": "Okay, if you are reading this and the price is higher than $199, WAIT.  It goes down to $199 fairly regularly-- at least it did 2-3 times this year (including prime day), and did last year for Black Friday sales.I LOVE my sonicare.  You will have to pry it out of my cold, dead, hands.  It makes brushing so much easier, and I like the light when you are brushing too hard, which I've heard dentists say is a pretty bad thing.The battery life is great-- a solid 2-3 weeks out of one charge.  I love that I can charge it, go on a week's vacation, and not worry about bringing the charger.  I just throw a cover on the brush head and toss in my carry-on (note: since it is a rechargeable battery, please put it in your carry-on).  The cover for the brush head is useless, so use something else when putting it in luggage.It has 4-5 different modes-- whitening, gum sensitivity, deep cleaning, etc.  I like the whitening one, which is 2 min 40 seconds.  It buzzes every 20 seconds to get you to move on to the next section.  You can choose from strong, medium, or mild vibration.  And the strong one is STRONG.  I feel my head buzz when I use it, lol, so I normally stick to the medium.My teeth feel so much cleaner when using this, and I love the discipline it gives me.  However, I have seen this vary in price from $199-399.  Please don't buy it when it's at its high price.  You can get a much better deal!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the Philips Sonicare DiamondClean electric toothbrush and I’m really impressed with the results. My teeth feel much cleaner and smoother after every use compared to a manual toothbrush.It has a very comfortable brushing experience with gentle but effective vibrations, so it doesn’t feel harsh on gums. I also like the different brushing modes, especially the sensitive and whitening options.The battery lasts a long time, and the charging glass/travel case is actually very convenient and looks nice on the counter.The only downside is that replacement brush heads are a bit expensive, but overall the performance makes it worth it.Overall, this is a high-quality toothbrush that really improves daily oral care. I would definitely recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Read other reviews. Bought the unit “on sale” which seems to be a red flag. The “on sale” units might be past the “sell by date” for the battery. Mine came and would not charge, would not turn on, and was a brick.Buyer beware - battery shelf-life is suspect.Glad it happened before the return period expired. Other commenters mentioned that it happened after the return period ended."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using this toothbrush for a month now and it seems to be a legit sonicare. I was skeptical after reading some of the comments. The power and function buttons do not have the soft rubber like cover older models do. Not sure why not but it does not affect the operations.I like that the new travel case is also a charger so its one and done you do not have to pack a million things. I have had this for a month th and charged it once. I use it 2 to 3 times a day. Great battery life compared to old models. I like that it does not have a hole on the bottom to charge it. It sits in its dock. Makes it easier to clean in my opinion.Size is the same and the functions are comparable.  It does have an extra function my old model did not. Works just as good if not better. Its a great value for the 2 that you get."
