[
    {
        "review": "I've long used Sonicare toothbrushes and since I get good reviews from the dentist, I trust them to keep my teeth fresh and clean.  I'm replacing a \"fancier\" model of toothbrush, but this one has all I need as I always used the regular setting and never paid attention to the brush head replacement warning anyway, replacing my brush head when it seemed worn.  It has the same quality of buzz I remember from when my old Sonicare was new (it had in the last month or so seemed clunky, that's why I replaced it.) It's actually easier to use since it has fewer buttons, so I'm not accidentally pushing a button and changing a setting as often.  The only thing I don't like is the brush head that came with it, but I replaced it with the Diamond Clean head that I'm used to and it's now basically all the same, just a better price.  The brush seems well made and the usual quality of Sonicare products, I'll update if it dies sooner than normal.  Overall, I like it.  I won't discourage you from buying one of the more expensive models if you want the additional settings, but this has all I really need.  So I'll stick with it and making sure to floss to keep my dentist happy."
    },
    {
        "review": "If a woodchuck could brush their toothes with a Sonic Electric Toothbrush? All the toothes.Sidenote: as a small human I once asked for a teethbrush since brushing one tooth at a time with my toothbrush was taking too long. Yeah.  Smart kid.Anywho. Grow up with a dental care glow up. Rechargable. Pink. And powerful. This will get ya pearly whites white and ya gums blissfully stimulated. Almost from the dentist minty fresh feels.Not loud. I've had toothbrushes that sounded like an airport fly over. No, it's too early/late I am getting up or going to bed. Shush.Good bristle firmness. I would say medium. The baby bear level of tooth scrubbing goodness.Charges quickly. Holds a charge while traveling of course it promptly goes back on the charger at home. Cuz I know me. A charger makes it harder to walk away and leave it somewhere.Also value for the monies. A good solid brush that is so far from a quickie run it until the batteries die number."
    },
    {
        "review": "My manual toothbrush wore out, so I upgraded to this entry-level Sonicare. It doesn't have all the fancy buttons of the high-end models, but it leaves my teeth feeling professionally clean just like after a dentist visit!What I Like:• Simple design: It has fewer buttons, so I do not change settings by accident.• Classic power: It has the strong, familiar buzz of a new Sonicare.• Great value: It does everything I need without paying for extra features I never used.• Charger: Includes a USB car charger. (USB wall adapter block not included; plugs into any standard USB port).Things to point out:• Brush head swap: You do get a brush head included in the box however there are different brush head options that you can purchase separately at the store.• Build quality: It feels well-made, like other Sonicare products.If you want extra settings, you can buy an expensive Philips Sonicare model. But if you just want a great clean, this simple sonicare toothbrush is all you need!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I finally switched from a regular toothbrush and I can definitely tell the difference. My teeth feel noticeably cleaner and smoother after brushing, especially around the gum line. I really like the pressure sensor because apparently I was brushing harder than I needed to. The timer is helpful too and keeps me from rushing through brushing in the morning. Battery life has been great so far and I like the simple white design. Easy to use and does exactly what I wanted!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This product is exactly as you would expect with a Sonicare chargable tooth brush, well made and out performs rivals.  Replacement heads to be purchased separately."
    },
    {
        "review": "This Phillips sonic care electric tooth brush has a very small head, I think it is a kids size brush head. If that is the case, it is great for kids however if it is for adults, it feels too small. It is a very basic electric tooth brush, no bells and whistles. It comes with an electric charger stand, see attached photos.It is easy to use, sits comfortable in your hand however when it starts to get wet it gets a little slippery. The vibration sensation can start to be little much after a couple of minutes. It is a good basic electric tooth brush, the price is decent for what you get. I found my one lasted about 1 hour of use before it needed a recharge. This tooth brush I think, works better for when you have to travel and space is a consideration."
    }
]

