    {
        "review": "☆Seller kindly gave a retund, but didnt need to! I was so moved that she simply wanted to make things right, that i gladly would have changed my reflection from that message alone! I love a seller that just wants to make their customers happy, and thats what this seller is all about ♡. But this review made her chuckle so I'll keep it up lol. ☆I don't even know where to begin when it comes to what needs to be said about this mid-sized Sedan- I mean toothbrush. Even on the lowest setting, this thing has enough horsepower to cut clean through your tongue like a scalpel sharpened by Dexter himself.  I'm exaggerating but not by much.It does come with a lot of replacement brush heads which is great for the price, so after I gained enough feeling back in my mouth, I popped on a replacment head and asked my parents (with a garbled half-numbed mouth) to try to survive a full tooth cleaning to see if I was just sensitive to vibrations. Neither of them lasted longer than 15 seconds. They both couldn't stop laughing because they found themselves yelling their responses because they still heard and felt the vibrations long after they turned off the device.Listen, if you dont turn on the device, its amazing lol. Its built with good materials, has a lot of replacement heads and the included stand and travel container was so cute! I wanted to love this toothbrush but it is not usable. Im wondering if I got a defective item because there is no way everyone giving positive reviews was using this in their mouths.Maybe to power wash their driveway, remove graffiti from brick, or to lift a few shades from some old dentures, but NOT for teeth cleaning. And im just gonna say what we are all thinking-WHO THE HECK IS SIMEN M. AND WHY SHOULD WE CARE THAT HE RECOMMENDS THIS PRODUCT? (see image) The generic actors in white lab coats cracked me up. I could almost see the Getty images watermark.This product is so insane that I didnt even return it. I keep it in my cabinet as a threat to any of my nieces/nephews who use bad language in this house. We dont need to wash their mouth out with soap when all I have to say is \"go brush your teeth\" to instill the fear of God in anyone. 😆"
