        "review": "Pros: good hardware, SSD running the OS is very fast. Runs games better and smoother than my Xbox one. Light and durable case.Cons: writing this about a month in. This is a laptop for setting on a desk and plugged in at all times. Too hot to game in your lap and the power supply could boil an egg. The power receptacle into the laptop feels fragile and could wiggle and start to break if you aren't careful, and probably is not an easy fix if you can't charge your battery anymore. Windows 10 is full of bloatware and self advertising for Microsoft and takes some settings surfing to disable apps and widgets that you cannot uninstall. After 2 weeks I sat the laptop down to use the bathroom and when I came back there was a huge crack in the LCD screen. No big deal I thought I watched a video to replace it myself and ordered \"omen replacement LCD 15.6\" for 60 dollars. When I pulled the case and battery I started to realise why this is so cheap. I DO NOT recommend replacing or doing any work on them yourself, I bet when you send yours in for repair they just throw it in the garbage and send you a new one. The Screen was unnecessarily high bond taped to the case and crumpled as I peeled it off. Once I got rid of the tape and the now ball of screen I saw that what I bought isn't the same screen at all and doesn't even fit inside the case. After some hard googling I finally found the screen I need and it's $150 dollars. If you buy this I highly recommend getting the warranty and just send it in, probably a rule for laptops in general"
