        "review": "Update: I've had the Chromebook about three months. It has started to turn itself off for no apparent reason. The screen will also flash black sometimes while I am using it. Either it is possessed, it's been hacked, or there is something wrong with it. I'm guessing the third option is correct. I also ffind that the keys are very sensitive and will also type double or triple letters as you are typing. The double \"f\" in the word \"find\" in that last sentence is an example. Some keys do it more than others. Original review: Overall, I like this Chromebook. The screen and the keyboard are both decent-sizes. I do think the colors are much more muted on this device than on any other I've owned in this decade. It's not a deal breaker, but definitely noticeable. I also miss the touchscreen of my last Chromebook so when this one has lived it's life, I'll probably go back to one with a touchscreen. It's battery life seems fine. I often sit cross-legged and find that there are sharp edges on bits on the shell of this Chromebook that are painful when they come into direct contact with my skin. The price was right, it works well, and didn't require much setup, so overall, it's not bad."
