    {
        "review": "I bought this for my husband for Father's Day.  He was overdue for an upgraded chromebook.  After researching and comparing, I chose this device.  I ordered it on June 3rd, it arrived June 9th and I set it up today, June 11th.  I was feeling good about this purchase, and was pleased with my decision, until I tried to access the camera, one of the features that attracted me, it was an included app.  I could Not get the \"Mirror Preview\" to turn off.  I didn't want selfies, I wanted pictures.  I spent nearly 1 1/2 hours online with support, with no resolution.  As it turns out, my Issue falls under the category of SOFTWARE, NOT HARDWARE, which conveniently is NOT covered by WARRANTY or INSURANCE.  I am sorry, but I am having difficulty accepting that rationale due to the fact that item purchased and described ( camera) was not 100% operational, but was, rather, defective due to the fact that it did accommodate all of my required parameters for choosing this device.  But ultimately, and herein lies the real kicker:  I can have this issue addressed and possibly fixed by \"purchasing\" a \"service upgrade\" entitling me to 1(one) 30 day Single Incident - Lenova Live Assistant - Set-up.  Part #5WS1J63373.  Oh, but that's not all, I get this for a mere $69.00, with an ISSUE DATE of June11 and an EXPIRATION DATE of June 25th.  What does this even mean?  I either have to accept or decline (or just let it go).  Will this option be availabe later?  Will it cost me more?  Welcome to the life of a consumer.  I just tell myself:  The fact that it makes no sense, makes all the sense in today's world.  So far, I love this device, itself"
