    {
        "review": "Small but so POWERFUL!  Has great sound and easy to use! Hooks right up to my phone and was able to control it through that. Has small suction type under the speaker and it was able to stick to the table and not worry about it falling over. Had it since the beginning of the summer and have not had to charge it as of yet! Great loud sound as well! If you really wanted it loud, you can increase volume on the speaker and then on the phone as well!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "For those of you who might have the same question as I had before purchasing this: How is the max volume? Is it loud enough?  YES! YES! It will easily fill a 10 FT by 10 FT room. And sound is clear and bass is good for its size!  Back in 2008-2009, I used the Soundmatters foxL that was like $250. Since then, these little portable speakers evolved, price went down, but performance went up.  I don’t have much need for portable speaker these days so last one I used was JBL Flip5. And JBL really shines on Bass. I can tell you that perhaps clarity of this PulseSound is on par or even better than JBL. However, the Bass is below JBL Flip5. But here is the catch, this PulseSound costs way less than JBL. I am very satisfied with this product and highly recommend it."
