[
    {
        "review": "I am absolutely blown away by the Soundcore Boom 2. If you are looking for the perfect outdoor speaker, this is it.​Sound Quality & Bass: The sound profile is incredibly crisp, but the star of the show is the \"BassUp\" feature. For a speaker this size, the bass hits remarkably deep without distorting the mids or highs. It easily fills a large backyard or noisy beach area.​Design & Portability: The built-in handle makes it super easy to grab and go. It feels rugged, well-built, and durable enough to handle drops or outdoor elements. The synced LED lights on the side are a fun touch for evening hangouts.​Battery Life & Waterproofing: The battery life is phenomenal—it easily lasts through a full weekend trip on a single charge. Plus, the IPX7 waterproof rating gives me total peace of mind by the pool. It even floats if it accidentally drops in the water!​App Integration: I highly recommend downloading the Soundcore app. The customizable EQ lets you fine-tune the sound exactly to your liking, which elevates the experience even further.​Bottom Line: Anker has outdone themselves. It offers premium, booming sound at a fraction of the price of its competitors. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Anker Soundcore Boom 2 is a serious contender in the portable speaker game. It’s super well-built with premium materials and packs a punch with loud, crisp sound and surprisingly deep bass. Bluetooth pairing is seamless and instant, and despite all that power, it’s remarkably lightweight and easy to carry around. Since it’s waterproof, you can take it anywhere without stressing whether you're by the pool, beach or at a party with friends.Plus, the battery life holds up for hours even with the extra bass button cranked, and the Soundcore app is a huge bonus in my opinion, letting you tune your audio with a customizable EQ, tweak the LED light show, and keep the speaker running smoothly with firmware updates. Love it and recommended to y'all."
    },
    {
        "review": "This portable bluetooth speaker is AMAZING!! It fit in my carryon backpack and was perfect for a trip to the beach! So easy to use and it a a cool LED light show on each end of the speaker.  Held a charge for my whole vacation! Plenty of powerful bass and strong mids and highs! I want to get another one as you can link tgem up in party mode!!Its not Bose, but it’s REALLY close!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Makes hanging in the backyard so much more fun. Bass definitely hits rights and the way it pairs with my galaxy s25 ultra is lovely. A match made in heaven. Its easy the operate, if you can't figure it out return it and buy some paper cups and strings. Batteries last long and the build quality is a1."
    },
    {
        "review": "Wow! I just ordered this for $85 and I’m blown away. This sounds better than any of the smaller Bose speakers I’ve had over the years. It has plenty of base and I can’t imagine most people ever needing anything louder. I think it looks nice, and the lights are sort of cool, although I don’t imagine I’ll use them much. The fact it’s fairly small and waterproof only adds to the value. I also just saw you can pair two speakers together to get stereo sound with separate right and left channels! Most people may not care about this but for me having portable stereo sound would be amazing. l just ordered a second one and I’ll update after I try it. No matter what happens, this is a steal at $85 and probably still a bargain at regular price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought this as audio and some lights for my golf cart.  Its pretty nice.  Not as loud as I wanted, but thats just me. Its plenty loud though.  Bass boost works well.  Lights are cool.  Battery is definitely good.  Sat outside overnight in a light rain and it wasnt an issue.  Well built."
    },
    {
        "review": "I work as a grill cook, which means I’m in a very noisy environment. So I need a speaker that is very loud. And I can say this speaker gets very loud for its size, but is never harsh on the ears, like some other speakers which leave an almost ringing in your ears after a high note. And it does not distort at max volume which is a plus for me.I used to have a 50w Rave Neo from soundcore, until recently when I sold it to a coworker who was in need of a good speaker. I had it for nearly 5 years. When I had it, I was constantly getting compliments on how impressive that speaker sounded. So I decided to buy another speaker from Anker since it’s quality I can trust.Comparing to the 50w Rave Neo, both with bass boost, and boom 2 out of box sound profile. The boom 2 gets louder than the rave Neo, however gets a little “muddier” at high volumes, while the rave Neo keeps a fuller sound. Probably due to the fact the boom 2 is missing a full range driver, and only has tweeters and a racetrack “subwoofer”. However does not matter in my use case. The battery life seems the same, after 3 hours of use at high volumes with bass on, I only used 40% of the battery on the boom 2, while I also used 40% of the rave Neo. Portability goes to the Boom 2. It is only the length of a ruler, height of 3/4 of a ruler, and is fairly slim. so it fits on any standard sized table easily, it also weighs less than half what the rave Neo weighs. The rave Neo felt like a workout carrying it work, while the boom 2 is easily carried by one finger. I also give appearances to the boom 2. The metal grill on the boom 2 feels very rugged and is much superior to the metal grill on the rave Neo. Both plastics feel the same as well, however it does seem the boom 2 is more vulnerable to scuffs and marks as I already have a scuff on the boom 2 with only 3 hours of use, while I have never gotten a scuff on the rave Neo. The LIGHTSHOW. The boom 2 is amazing to watch as it lights up and moves the radiators to the music. Very nice touch since I never really enjoyed the lights on the rave Neo. The rave Neo was also impressive, but the diffusion on the boom 2 looks very premium. Charging. Both charge with an input of usb type c. However, with the rave Neo, you had to use a usb type A charging block, which was super annoying because I have been trying to get away from usb type a, and micro usb. Type c charging blocks and cords are worlds superior. And the boom 2 can charge from any type c charging block.Sound. The boom 2 is loud. It is not audiophile quality. But if you plan on sticking it in the corner of the room or on the outside of a basketball court, you might not feel or hear every instrument or every vocal chord in a singers throat, but I guarantee you will be satisfied with the volume of music you are receiving from this speaker, which does sound very pleasant at least, which is what this speaker is meant to do. Get loud, so you can listen to music while you are doing other activities. I highly recommend higher end soundcore speakers, can’t go wrong."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m very happy with the volume and fullness of the sound coming from this little box. I bought this for outside on the patio and around the pool. I had been using a Bose Flex, which was great for indoor near-field listening, but a little weak for outside. This Boom 2 gets plenty loud enough to reach the pool half way across the yard at a comfortable listening level, and it can easily get loud enough to annoy the neighbors. Music is full and clear - the bass won’t rattle the furniture, which I never expected from a box this size, but there’s plenty of it for casual listening and small outdoor gatherings, for which this guy is perfect. Bluetooth connection to my iPhone is flawless; once it’s paired, you just need to turn it on and it automatically connects. The Soundcore app is easy enough to use if you need it, which I usually don’t. I just turn it on and start the music on my phone, and the party is on. USB-C charging is convenient, because almost every gadget I have uses it now, so there are plenty of charging points around the house."
