    {
        "review": "For those of you who might have the same question as I had before purchasing this: How is the max volume? Is it loud enough?  YES! YES! It will easily fill a 10 FT by 10 FT room. And sound is clear and bass is good for its size!  Back in 2008-2009, I used the Soundmatters foxL that was like $250. Since then, these little portable speakers evolved, price went down, but performance went up.  I don’t have much need for portable speaker these days so last one I used was JBL Flip5. And JBL really shines on Bass. I can tell you that perhaps clarity of this PulseSound is on par or even better than JBL. However, the Bass is below JBL Flip5. But here is the catch, this PulseSound costs way less than JBL. I am very satisfied with this product and highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great little speaker for the price and size. Very easy to use. Very good sound quality. Easy functionality, compact to go anywhere. Compatibility was easy to connect."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "was having a hard time choosing between this, and Oontz angle 3 Pro, and a Doss Soundbox Pro. Im looking for something primarily for the house to be used in a bedroom/office. EVERY SINGLE ONE WAS A WINNER and I wouldnt hesitate to choose any of the 3. Sound quality was very very....VERY comparable with each one and pretty much a wash (explained below). I dont like letting my batteries drain so I cant vouch for battery life on each one, but im not worried. Below is why I would choose each model, hopefully it helps you. Also if it matters, I listened to Radiohead-The National Anthem and Skrillex-Rumble to test the speakers.--Why I chose the Doss Soundbox Pro: I hate to admit it but the price....and I actually chose this one over the Tribit and Oontz after my sound tests. The sound was on par with the other 2 (similar wattage to the Oontz) and I liked this one just a hair more than the Oontz because it was a little crisper sounding where the Oontz was a little fuller...if that makes sense. So with the sound being the same, the fact that I could ALSO pair multiple Doss speakers for a multi speaker set up just like the Oontz (this is a great feature for when entertaining guests/having a small party/get-together), and considering I'd primarily be using this in a bedroom (where the powerbank wouldnt come in as handy like the Oontz has).....I had to choose this one. I didnt realize it was the cheapest until I had finished testing all 3 and went back to the invoice. This is the best bang for your buck speaker of the 3 and im big on value....but dont mind spending either if the value is there.--Why I would choose this speaker (Tribit Stormbox Micro 2):This one is the most travel friendly. Its the smallest and has a strap across the backside of it so you can easily attach it to a backpack, bike, UTV/ATV or any type of bar....the straps so tight to the body of the speaker that you can even put it on something as small as a car antenna and itd hold securely. Since the strap is snug to the body it stays secured. They dont list the wattage and this had the lowest wattage of the bunch at 10w compared to the other 2 at 20w/21w each.....but it was without a doubt equally as loud as the other two with trebles and bass being on par with the other two. Id really like to see how loud and clean a tribit with higher wattage sounds if this 10w speaker matched the higher wattage speakers I compared it to in my test.--Why I would choose the Oontz Angle 3 Pro instead: This one was the biggest and beefiest which I am a fan off....but I dont want you to think its a brick. its still plenty light where it wont feel like a burden lugging it around. This one also has a ocean/boat theme color pattern which is sweet and almost swayed me since i will be using this on my boat too. The other thing that almost swayed me was that the speaker can be used as a powerbank!!! So this ones sound is just as good as the other but the standout features are the looks, and the fact that it can be used as a powerbank which can come in very handy. Its not included but they have a bracket mount that clamps on to stuff.......not sure how it would hold up to movement and things like that but there is that option out there. These can also be paired with other Oontz speakers for a multi speaker set up.--Why I would choose the Doss Soundbox Pro: I hate to admit it but the price....and I actually chose this one over the Tribit and Oontz after my sound tests. The sound was on par with the other 2 (similar wattage to the Oontz) and I liked this one just a hair more than the Oontz because it was a little crisper sounding where the Oontz was a little fuller...if that makes sense. So with the sound being the same, the fact that I could ALSO pair multiple Doss speakers for a multi speaker set up just like the Oontz (this is a great feature for when entertaining guests/having a small party/get-together), and considering I'd primarily be using this in a bedroom (where the powerbank wouldnt come in as handy like the Oontz has).....I had to choose this one. I didnt realize it was the cheapest until I had finished testing all 3 and went back to the invoice. This is the best bang for your buck speaker of the 3 and im big on value....but dont mind spending either if the value is there."
    },
    {
        "review": "The DOSS SoundBox Pro Bluetooth Speaker exceeded my expectations. The sound quality is excellent, with clear vocals, deep bass, and impressive volume for its size. Bluetooth connectivity is quick and stable while the colorful light effects add a fun touch to the listening experience. Overall, this speaker offers outstanding performance at a reasonable price."
    },
    {
        "review": "For my cell phone. 👍 sound is great, setup easy with directions. Packaged perfectly."
    },
    {
        "review": "The only reason I didn't give five stars is because the battery life is shorter than my needs most times. Otherwise, this is a great item for the price. A bit contradictoral."
    },
    {
        "review": "Kick ass. Great little speaker. Great sound and bass. Gets loud if u want. I paid 22 beans. Long battery"
    },
    {
        "review": "I just looked up my previous order because I needed a new charger, and realized I have had this speaker for FOUR years. I have never had a single problem with it! I use it daily and it’s worked perfectly- such a good buy."
    },
    {
        "review": "In the world of  Bluetooth speakers, this one struck me as a tad pricey, but not overly so. I am hoping for quality of build to let this thing last many years, and we'll see how that works. Meantime, the sound is nice. I use it mostly to listen to podcasts (including podcasts with music) and to stream stuff from Amazon music and Pandora, and the sound quality is OK for me for those purposes. I haven't used the bass emphasis button, finding I don't need that for what I listen to. The lighting feature is amusing, but I keep it off to lengthen battery life. The speakers provide a stereo sound, but I can't really discern a stereo result. Which is OK, I wasn't really expecting much in those regards, considering the speakers are so close to one another. The unit pairs with my iPhone extremely quickly. Haven't had it long enough to assess battery life (which can be a function of volume, use of lighting effects, use of the bass effect, and perhaps the phase of the moon). Overall, it meets my expectations fully and feels like it is well made."
    },
    {
        "review": "This speaker is great. So far the battery life is superb and it gets very loud! I use this speaker in conjunction with a NUX Mighty Plug for guitar on the go. As expected with such a small speaker box the bass isn't extremely powerful but it sounds very crisp and full range if placed in the corner of a room with solid walls. I had a problem with the unit powering itself off at first until I realized it wasn't a low battery but an 'auto-off' feature when not playing anything. Searching this on the web, I didn't find anything on either their website or manual regarding an 'auto-off' feature for this model. Some suggested that DOSS has a firmware update available that disabled it. I spoke through email with a very nice person named Lizzie with their Customer Care team. Lizzie explained that units with the Version ID of VS3582 do not require any firmware updates to enable or disable this feature. If yours is a VS3582 then all you need to do in order to enable/disable the 'auto-off' feature is a button combo of Mode+Power and you'll see if flash red twice for off, green twice for on. Hold the bass button to cycle through lighting options (low, high, off).So far this little speaker has impressed me with what I intended to do with it and all my expectations are met. I am considering a 2nd one for stereo play!Hopefully Lizzie gets a raise soon"
    },
    {
        "review": "PACKAGING: The SoundBox Pro from DOSS is not only protected by a simple bag, there is also a plastic mold tailored to the speaker in the box. Otherwise there are very good instructions for use (also in German), a USB A to Micro USB cable and a 3.5mm jack - jack connection cable. DESIGN: The speaker is rubberized all around, you might suspect leather on the short sides, but it is the rubber coating with a leather pattern. The keys are easy to reach and have a clearly noticeable pressure point. Small LEDs provide additional information. On the back behind the rubber cover there are Micro USB, 3.5mm jack and a Micro SD card port. At the front, a grille protects the two active and passive speakers. There is a plastic frame all around that is illuminated by LEDs, very stylish. FUNCTION: In terms of sound, the SoundBox Pro should not be underestimated. The volume is decent and the sound distorts minimally at max setting. The bass comes across well for such a small box, it can be compared to a kick bass so it's crisp. You get a long rumble if the speaker is placed on a surface that can vibrate a little, e.g. a wooden table. You can still change a lot using the equalizer settings on your cell phone. Stereo pairing is a great function that worked flawlessly for me. I couldn't detect any delays and there is no echo effect. The lighting effects are nice, especially at a garden party. These are best seen at night. For me, this is a function that certainly has a great effect in some situations (e.g. quiet music in the evening on the sofa with pulsating LEDs). CONCLUSION: I don't want to be without the speakers. If I bought two, there was a discount during the promotional period. It definitely makes sense to go for it here and create a great soundscape through stereo pairing. If Bluetooth isn't the right choice, you can also connect directly to a 3.5mm blade (always connect to the master for stereo pairing) or alternatively songs on Micro SD."
    },
    {
        "review": "Paired with Amazon Echo in the bathroom You can listen to Amazon Music in the bath.You can also give commands to the Echo from inside the bath.Turn off the lights in the bathroom for a relaxing bath time.Perhaps because the LEDs on the speaker are reverberating in the bath, the sound is very good.I really liked it.The main unit is dark green with a matte texture.At the time of posting the review, it was 8,299 yen including tax, plus a 1,200 yen off coupon."
    },
    {
        "review": "It’s a powerful yet small soundboxe! It shuts down on his own when the music player stops which is great to save the batterie ! I love hie the lights flashes with the music it’s very soothing! I love this product !"
    },
    {
        "review": "Although it was small, it had good sound and was more than worth the price. I can use it anywhere as long as I charge it, so I listen to Amazon Music while cleaning or cooking."
    },
    {
        "review": "It's not what I expect, it's very quiet"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Great portable Bluetooth speaker with clear sound and good volume for its size. The battery life is impressive and easily lasts through a full day of regular use. Bluetooth connection is quick and stable, and the compact design makes it easy to carry around. Overall, a convenient and reliable speaker for everyday use."
    },
    {
        "review": "For a $20 speaker this thing is pretty awesome!!Sound is great! Very loud to be a smaller speaker. Connected very quickly and easily done! Can change the lights to either go along with the sound of the music or just a slow roll through the colors. You can also turn the light off if you’d like!My favorite thing about this product is if you have 2 of the same ones you can connect them together and put one on each side of the house!!  I’ve been playing it for about 3 hours now and it has only used 1 dot of battery on half charge out the box. All in all pretty great budget friendly speaker!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m a group fitness instructor at a busy gym, and I teach high-energy classes like HIIT and bootcamp. My speaker is on for about four hours straight every morning, and it needs to handle a room full of wireless interference: Apple Watches, wireless earbuds, fitness trackers, even other small Bluetooth speakers. The X2 cuts through all of that like it’s nothing. I leave my phone at the front of the studio, then walk to the back row to check squat form, grab weights by the windows, step outside to get water. The music never skips, never stutters, never drops. Not once in over 30 classes. The sound quality matters too. I need the beat to be crisp so my class can follow along, and the bass needs to punch through without getting muddy. The X2 delivers. My students can hear every count clearly even at the back of the room. And the IPX7 waterproofing has been a lifesaver: sweat, spilled water bottles, even a rogue splash from someone’s hydro flask. Just wipe and go. For any fitness instructor or personal trainer working in a busy wireless environment, the X2’s Bluetooth is a workhorse. It doesn’t get overwhelmed. And the sound and waterproofing make it perfect for the gym. Class after class, it just delivers without any drama."
    },
    {
        "review": "I do livestreams on Twitch and YouTube ,mostly gaming, sometimes just chatting with my audience. I like to use a Bluetooth speaker for background music and sound alerts so I don’t have to wear headphones for four hours straight. The X2 has been perfect. I’ve done over 20 streams with it, each 3-4 hours long, and the Bluetooth has never dropped once. It connects to my streaming PC in about two seconds every time. No noticeable audio delay either. But here’s something I didn’t expect , the RGB lights are actually great for streams. I placed it behind the monitor, and viewers keep commenting on how cool the setup looks. It adds a little something to the visual without being distracting. I’ve also spilled energy drink on it twice during late-night streams, and the IPX7 waterproofing meant I just wiped it off and kept going. No damage. Battery easily lasts through my longest streams. For any streamer, podcaster, or content creator who needs reliable wireless audio, the X2 is a hidden gem."
    },
    {
        "review": "Surprisingly good sound quality considering the pint sized speaker. Unfortunately the size really limits the size of the battery you can get inside so the battery life is pretty terrible. In my case thats not a big deal because I am usually using them indoors and plugged in all the time. but if you are looking for a portable battery powered solution this might not be your answer because I generally get less than an hour or run time out of a full charge. Even when the battery is still showing 2 of 4 bars of battery and you should theoretically still have 50% battery life...I find by this point the bluetooth struggles to stay connected and I either have to plug it in or constantly reconnect the bluetooth. I am giving 4 stars because it suits my needs and the sound quality os good for the price and size. but if I were using this as my primary portable speaker I would probably give it 3 stars or possibly even less."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this little unit to replace my other bluetooth speaker I got years ago after the battery couldn't hold a charge anymore. But the one I had didn't exist anymore.This one works decently. It's sound quality is decent. It has pretty good volume and clarity, but is a little lacking in bass in the genres I listen to. (Rock, Metal, Alternative) It's hard to describe, because the bass is still audible, but it just is as full to be perfect. But for it's small size and price, I think it's still decent.The bluetooth has worked flawlessly so far, and the LED light is cool. It has two modes where it's just on, or it tries to react and animate to music, which is cool for more rhythmic songs. Or you can just turn it off. I would have liked to have been able to just change the color to a single color, but it's forced to be rainbow. Just a small feature I would have preferred, but that doesn't affect it functionally.I mainly use this in the bathroom while I shower. And that hasn't been an issue. I haven't gotten too much water on it, but it seems fine in that area.Overall I really like this unit, and still give it five starts, even if it could have some minor improvements."
    },
    {
        "review": "I had a complicated issue with an older TV needing a Bluetooth transmitter. I chose the DUDGSIS Portable Bluetooth Speaker for its reliability in Bluetooth connection and its small size. After sorting out the TV and Bluetooth Transmitter, I was rewarded for my choice in DUDGSIS because it connected immediately. I was further rewarded in finding that it has a great sound and good volume (especially for a smaller unit). This is a great unit and a solution for use of a remote speaker that is simple to set up and works the first time. Lastly, it’s a great price for what you are getting."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great little Bluetooth speaker. Sounds great for the size. Obviously don't expect subwoofer level bass, but it pushes it out pretty good. Love the light on the top. You can turn it off and change the style by pressing the power button quickly. It's also waterproof so it's great for outdoors, near pools, the beach, the shower, etc.Connects fast to my phone and haven't had any issue with the Bluetooth connection. Go for it if you're looking for a compact little speaker that sounds good."
    },
    {
        "review": "Wow! I’m genuinely impressed by both this speaker and the level of customer support I received. Easily a 5-star experience.My first unit unfortunately arrived with a defect. Right out of the box, it paired successfully with my devices, but within seconds of playback, the audio would begin skipping, produce static interference, and occasionally cut out completely before reconnecting. The speaker also became noticeably warm during use. After troubleshooting with multiple devices and confirming the issue wasn’t related to Bluetooth compatibility, I contacted Dudgsis support.Their response was prompt, professional, and solution-oriented. The support representative was incredibly understanding and efficient. There was no back-and-forth or unnecessary delays; they immediately arranged for a replacement unit and shipped it directly to me. The entire process was smooth and hassle-free. The replacement arrived just in time for my weekend gathering, and I’m grateful for how quickly they resolved the issue. Now that I’ve had the opportunity to use the replacement speaker, I can confidently say it performs exactly as expected.Pros: Excellent build quality with a sleek, modern design and attractive color finish. Compact and highly portable without feeling cheap or flimsy. The buttons provide good tactile feedback and are responsive without requiring excessive force. Bluetooth pairing is fast and seamless. My devices detect the speaker almost instantly, and the connection remains stable during use. The audio performance is impressive for a speaker of this size. The sound signature is well-balanced, vocals come through clearly, and the bass response is surprisingly powerful without overwhelming the mids. Even at maximum volume, the speaker maintains good clarity with minimal distortion. The RGB lighting effects are a nice touch and sync well with the music, adding to the overall experience. Battery life has been excellent so far. It charges quickly and provides hours of playback on a single charge. For such a compact speaker, the output and soundstage feel much larger than expected and easily compete with some larger portable speakers I’ve used.Cons: None so far.Overall, I’m extremely impressed with both the product and the company behind it. The replacement unit has exceeded my expectations, and the customer support experience gave me confidence in the brand. If you’re looking for a compact Bluetooth speaker with strong audio performance, solid battery life, and responsive customer service, this one is well worth considering.I look forward to using it for a long time, and hopefully it continues performing this well for years to come."
    },
    {
        "review": "I wasn't expecting much from a speaker this small — but the X2 surprised me right out of the box. After using it for over a week, here's the honest breakdown.Pros:Sound quality is genuinely impressive for the size. Clean vocals, balanced mids, and bass that actually exists (thank you, passive radiator).Gets plenty loud — I usually keep it around 60-70% and that fills the room.Battery lasts days. Charged it once when I got it, still going strong.Bluetooth 5.3 is rock solid. No drops, even when I leave my phone in another room.Lights are fun — colors cycle through at night and add a nice vibe without being tacky.Cons:The charging indicator stays on solid white when full — not a big deal, but if you want complete darkness, it's something to note.Bass definitely shows up more at higher volumes; at very low volume, it's less present (pretty standard for small speakers).Used it in the bathroom while showering, in the backyard while gardening, and on the patio for a small hangout. Handled everything. For $24, this thing is a steal. If you want portable sound that actually delivers, grab one."
    },
    {
        "review": "The speaker connects to my phone quickly via Bluetooth and stays connected from indoors to outdoors without cutting out, which is really nice.The speaker feels solid in hand, not cheap at all. Sound quality is excellent, and the volume is impressive for its size. I was worried a smaller speaker wouldn't be loud enough, but it fills the entire room easily.What surprised me most is the battery. One morning around 8 a.m. I had it playing at half volume while working in the yard and moving in and out of the house. It was still playing when I finally sat down to rest in the evening. Easily got 10 to 12 hours out of it. The next day I tested it at full volume while cleaning the garage, and it still lasted a solid 4 hours. For such a small speaker, that's really impressive.Charging is quick too, it takes about three hours to full. The USB C port is a nice plus no more fiddling with old mini USB like some other speakers still use.Overall, for this price, getting such a great little speaker is a steal. If you want something that plays all day without worrying about battery, this one's worth considering."
    },
    {
        "review": "The build quality is solid. Sound is amazing especially for the price. I had an issue, which i usually just tolerate or return, but reached out to the seller. They were very responsive and provided a solution that was great. As a budget bluetooth speaker, especially considering the customer service, it would have been an easy 5 stars. But with the tws specification, new Bluetooth chip listing etc, id expect it to live up to its features. Sadly it doesnt, ive tried many times, tws doesnt play sound, had an issue with static with the first one, so i surmise its a chip issue. Nonetheless, its good for what it is, great even, but dont expect seamless operation for all features. If you just want an affordable bluetooth speaker with great sound, solid bass, definitely consider this."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’d originally planned to buy a larger speaker, thinking it would have more power and features, but after reading a lot of negative reviews, I eventually decided to go for a smaller model. This one has received good reviews and is reasonably priced, so I thought I’d give it a go. I’ve been using it for a month or two now and I’m quite happy with it.It's a bit smaller than I expected, but honestly the size works out perfectly. Doesn't take up any space at all. Compact and lightweight, but the sound and volume hold up just as well as some larger Bluetooth speakers I've owned before. It's not heavy either. I can carry it in my hand without it feeling like a bother, or even clip it onto my bag if I want. Super convenient. Even when I toss it in my backpack it barely takes up any room, which means I can fit more stuff in there now.Sound quality is really good and battery life is solid too. In the car, I only need to turn it up a bit over halfway to hear clearly over the road noise. Around the house it fills up a room easily. For such a small speaker, the sound is clear, the bass is decent, and nothing sounds tinny or weak.Plus it's really light. Heading out to work or to the park, I just toss it in my bag and barely notice it's there.If you're looking for something portable and easy to carry around, this one's worth a try. 5 stars for size, sound, and value."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Speaker is amazing! Pairs good with 2 of them i keep attached to scooter! Came 1 day early and works great!Small stupid stuff could be better rubber letters rub off easy with hot temps and the rope hanging thing could be stronger i wouldn't trust hanging and swinging from a bike or scooter. But the sound quality is awesome with 2 of them!To bad batterys not bigger or upgradable! It kinda dies fast if using it loud on Android. Funny even with the thing plugged in the power will drop and shut off if leaving volume to high. I leave about 40 60% volume will keep it 100% charged up. Still sounds great at those volumes.I use 2 of them on my scooter and they shake the ground and chair even a bit its awesome! I'd get 4 of them if i could just cause how much i use it anymore with hands free calling and stuff works great haven't had any issues with either one i have.The black one i have took a spill. Someone tryed taking it off scooter and it cracked a bit they were unsuccessful but when i was rolling it fell eventually going 25mph cause plastic hanging ring and my black one fell good and you would not be able to tell it fell honestly! This blue one I got a mount for so it won't fall now. I have a feeling it will last a long time from the quality of them and taking care of them. In a case if you can when not in use will definitely help."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is absolutely a good speaker, especially with the price $35. It is easy to connect, it sounds really good and deep bass as well. The size is good as well. The weight is good but seems light. Battery life seems to go lower depending on how loud you use and how long you use it. Usually other speakers with 60w are $60-$100. This is actually great deal. Getting two of these gives you an increase of 120w which I havent tried maybe later. I'd say I keep this, and to continue to use it, indoor and outdoor, which I'll soon try outdoor. In theory, this Monster speaker brings loud sound and big bass."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really liked this speaker. The sound is loud and clear, with good bass, and it connects to Bluetooth very quickly. I’ve used it both indoors and outdoors, and it works great. The battery lasts a long time, and the design feels sturdy. For the price, I think it offers excellent quality. I would definitely buy it again and recommend it if you’re looking for a speaker with good volume that’s easy to carry around."
    },
    {
        "review": "Pro:Adequate volume for working outside in a 30 ft radius.Sounds good enough for streaming music, which met my requirement, my hearing could be better, so should be good enough for most folks.  I like the sound.I like the sound level of my phone can change the speaker level.  Be aware when changing the sound level using the speaker it will change the level of sound set on your phone.State of speaker power level is indicated on the Bluetooth connection for Android.CONS:The buttons on  the rubber side strip are black on black, making the symbols dofficult to see in dim light.  I am planning on highlighting the raised symbols with some white paint, as this is probably my biggest device complaint.  I have yet to try music from a memory card.Device arrived uncharged, it took several hours to fully charge.I know I read several complaints on battery life, which I did not experience any issues, listened for several hours at less than half volume, but have yet to get to the 4 hour mark of others.  I tend to charge it back up after each use.  So I can not fully address battery longevity issue.If you are looking for Rock concert loud, this might not be your first choice, but plenty loud, I'd guess around 120db, but just a guess.At the price point, it is far better than others I have used in music fidelity.  It sounds a bit base if listening to books or podcasts, not objectionable, but noticeable,Overall I would buy it again as it meets my needs."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very nice looking speaker not to big, not to small.  Wish power cord was longer.  Nice sound.  A lot deeper and loader than my SONY speaker.  Connected very easily and quickly via Bluetooth to my Amazon smart speaker.  Great value for purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am thoroughly impressed with the Monster S620! For a portable outdoor speaker, the 60W output delivers incredibly powerful, rich sound with deep bass and clear highs that don't distort even at higher volumes.The Bluetooth 5.4 connection is rock-solid and pairs instantly with my devices. Its IPX8 waterproof rating gives me total peace of mind using it poolside or outdoors without worrying about splashes or rain. The built-in mic is also a great touch for taking quick calls hands-free. If you're looking for a rugged, high-performing wireless speaker for home or travel, this one is an absolute home run. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Monster S620 bluetooth speaker is easy to pair, has a hreat sound quality and is very durable. Used out doors this past weekend and it stood up to heat, moisture and being dropped more than once. Sounds like a much bigger speaker. Easy to control the volumn. Perfect for at home, indoor or outdoor use and on the go, great size to pack in a tote and take camping or to the beach. Would highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought one Moster S620 and it sound crisp, clear and deep base.  I ordered a 2nd and paired the 2 together for great sounding true stereo 2 channel sound.  You will not be disappointed.  At $39.99 you can buy 2 and it's still less than one JBL and sounds every bit as good.  I also read the CEO of Monster was one of the co-founders of Beats.  You can't go wrong."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Bought this speaker for my beach trip. Wasn’t worried about water or sand with this speaker. It has a very clean sound, can get pretty loud for its size. Bass is okay, but expected for speaker of this size. The build quality is great, very portable, battery lasted the entire day at the beach and night. Never had a connection problem with Bluetooth either. Overall a great speaker for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have had mine for 5yrs and still jams. I bought this one for my daughter because she always took mine. Small and packs a lot of sound. Small to take anywhere. It always is a fast connection. Good price for the the quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great speaker.  I have tried several brands of these bt speakers; Tribit, Soundcore, Harmon Kardon, Bose, B&O and a few others. None compare to this for the qualities I want in a bluetooth speaker. I see it as a personal speaker for listening to music privately and for podcasts. I have a nice stereo system for serious listening, but it's not always convenient to do that. What I found was that there is a lot of sound profile manipulation by the producers of these products favoring bass output, because that's what a large portion of the buying public thinks is \"good sound\", with the resulting side effects on the rest of the profile.. The Wonderboom might tweak it a little, but not even close to overdone. The sound quality is really solid, including the mids and  trebles. Clear and full; undistorted. Bass is solid, but balanced. Clearly present but not obnoxious.  That's number one. It is light, and it is the easiest to use of the bunch. The 360 degree sound is a real plus and does fill the room. It is well protected against dust and moisture, and it floats if you drop it in the lake. It is very nicely shaped, easy to pick up, hold, carry , pack. Use it anywhere. It also has zero over compensating frills, like apps and equalizers, which are a total waste of time on something that you just want to work and not have to fuss over. This one does just that, and it has better sound quality than all the others tested, except the Luna 2 and B&O a1, but, at lower volumes it is pretty much indistinguishible.. I've sent one to my son and one to my daughter, who took it to the lake house last weekend and said it was a real hit on the dock and the boat with over  a dozen people in the group, whom she said were universally complimentary.  It does have two adjustments. The basic mode is \"standard'. Push the button once and it gives you an \"outdoor boost\"; again and you get \"podcast mode\", which I found not to be necessary, but it does help if there is ambient noise, like, say, a shower. I also tried it in stereo with another unit and it's great.  I don't really need that function, but I just might hang onto the second one and do the stereo anyway.  These these little guys are affordable enough that you can get two for less than a competitive single unit will cost and you can bet that they'll sound better. Great product. Well conceived, well designed and well executed.  A truly great product."
    },
    {
        "review": "Ultimate Ears Wonderboom Speaker 4 is an amazing little speaker.  This is our second one (only because we lost the first).  Sound quality is top notch and it’s easy to use and so portable.  It’s lighter and smaller and less expensive than then the big name brand pill versions. Love the fun color choices too.  We bought it because of its floating feature so we can take in on our Duffy boat. But it’s a great speaker for the pool, at the pickleball courts or just enjoying music in our backyard.  Holds a charge all day."
    },
    {
        "review": "This speaker is nice and loud while maintaining quality sound.  It doesn't sound like it is struggling at high volumes and doesn't get distorted.  It is water proof which is nice.  We take it on the paddleboard and it has a nice hook for a carabiner to keep it attached.  Had no issues pairing with multiple devices and the large Plus/Minus indicators for volume don't leave you fumbling to find the adjustment"
    },
    {
        "review": "This speaker is bass heavy and I don't know if I hate or loved it. Great for certain music bad for others that doesn't need the additional bass. No way to adjust bass since there are no app for this speaker. The speaker sounds great and it gets plenty loud.Pro:-Setting it up is easy. Out of the box it's in pair mode. Easy pair on the android device.-Great built quality. It is sturdy and well built.Con:-No app to fine tune sound setting-start up and power off noise is loud. No way to adjust that.What more can I say. It sounds great compared to other speakers in this category and price range. Basic, no frill, no overly complicated speaker. It gets to the point. Great speaker when it's on sale. Still great even at the non-sale price."
    },
    {
        "review": "This speaker could have been great.  I still use it, but I wouldn't buy it again and wouldn't recommend it to others, for two reasons.The primary reason is the volume of the voice that speaks when the sound mode is changed.  To others it may be a minor thing and not at all a dealbreaker, but it has not yet ceased to be very jarring to me.When in the shower, I use this speaker to listen to audiobooks, so every time I turn it on, I switch to \"Podcast Mode\".  I suppose because it is waterproof, it only has sealed buttons that must be repeatedly pressed to cycle through options, rather than switches that one can \"set and forget\".  I wish the speaker had memory for the last configuration used, because without that or toggle switches, this means that every time I turn it on I have to press the button on the bottom of the speaker twice so that it cycles to my preferred sound mode setting.Which in turn means that every. single. time. it shouts out \"OUTDOOR BOOST!\", \"PODCAST MODE!\"Because no matter how low the volume is turned down, the sound mode is completely independent and has one volume level:  SHOUTING.  Okay... maybe it's not truly shouting, but it's very loud and cannot be altered.  As I said, it's quite jarring.The secondary reason I'd hesitate to recommend it to others is that I've noticed the sound cuts out every once in a while.  This is with the paired source only a foot or two away, and I've never had the sound cut out like this with any other bluetooth speaker, so it seems like the issue is with this speaker itself.It's too bad, because if it wasn't for those two complaints, I could really love this speaker.It's waterproof, which obviously was a big selling point for me and my \"I don't want to waste listening time with such mundane things like a shower\" attitude.It's compact and has a small sturdy loop at the top which makes it easy to carry around and hang--you guessed it--in the shower (from a sturdy in-shower towel rack, using an S-hook).  It's not a cheap lightweight speaker, so I wouldn't trust a suction-cupped device to hold it.And despite its small size, it is easily loud enough, with no distortion, to hear clearly over noisy things like the shower or running fans.I wish I could give it another half-star, because listing all these positive qualities almost makes me think three stars is not enough.  But I wish the review that led me to buying this speaker had warned how loud that sound-mode announcer voice is, and with that and the sound cut-outs, I just can't give it four."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent sound quality. Rich base and the higher end is not at all tinny as some of these smaller speakers can be. It's very portable and makes an excellent patio/deck speaker for parties, etc. My only complaint is that this is a speaker that is exclusively blue tooth. You cannot add any corded attachments - older iPods, CD players, etc. I do understand that this stuff is being phased out, but while it's still around, having the capability would have been nice."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love it! Works great even in the hot tub!!Good sound, good durability, good volume, good battery life!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Best investment ever. Loud and waterproof"
    },
    {
        "review": "Easy to hook up to this device Bluetooth wise.Great sound. I use this in a large room during a group circuit session and the volume is fantastic."
    },
    {
        "review": "This product is good  for just small room sound"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a great speaker. It gives out really good sound. I find if you want more bass to put it in front of a wall or something like that.Haven’t used outdoor boost mode or podcast mode yet so can’t comment on that!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I really like this speaker.  It’s very small/compact but has a very nice, high quality, clear sound.  The Bluetooth connection is SUPER easy to use; I just downloaded the app and it connected immediately - no repeated set up attempts and no fuss!  And the Bluetooth connection doesn't drop - even when switching back and forth between multiple phones/devices which is somewhat rare with these kinds of speakers.  It has a strap with a \"buckle\" so you can strap it on to almost anything and it's also waterproof which gives me peace of mind since I'm using it in the bathroom to listen to while showering etc.  It plays a LONG time on a charge but you can also keep it plugged in all the time with the easy to use USB-C port.  It's not the loudest speaker in the world but given it's very compact size, I really wouldn't expect it to be and I'd prefer crisp sound over booming volume.  I would NOT recommend this you are trying to find a speaker for a large room or to hear throughout multiple rooms but for smaller areas (like a deck/patio, a smaller bedroom, or a bathroom which is where I am using it), it's an incredible deal.  I got it on sale during prime days but depending on the color and when you buy, I've seen it at or near the same low price since.  I'm definitely happy with this purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Nice little speaker.  You're not filling a large room with sound with this little guy, but in a small space it's a great choice.  I'm not an audiophile so I'm not going to try to describe the sound in any detail, but I'll say it's pleasant, full sound, and the battery life seems excellent."
    },
    {
        "review": "Quality made personal speaker, Bluetooth connects w/o complaint.  Not particularly loud.  Works fine on my desktop and headboard.  Battery life seems good, but have not timed."
    },
    {
        "review": "Tested it side by side with rhe ULT 1. Item is good, but the ULT 1 is louder / has more bass. I would still recommend to someone on a limited budget, but they're getting what they pay for. I tested next to a busy road. Noticeably quieter than the ULT 1, but you can still hear it. Bass is definitely weaker than the ULT 1. All that being said, it is impressive for a small speaker. You can see the size difference in the photo. Definitely great for indoors, suitable for personal listening (right next to you) outside. You'll lose the sound 25-50 feet away from you outside though. Its a good deal under $40, I grabbed it for $33. Not worth it over $50. I picked the ULT 1 up for $78, just to compare. Ended up returning this one because I don't need both. Also, you can customize EQ on the ULT 1, but not this one. Sound is very clear, great for a small speaker, but max loudness is comparable to a phone on max volume rather than a portable speaker. Worth it if you want a speaker that is tiny and cheap, but if you're looking for great bass without the cord / bulkiness - consider the ULT 1. Btw, ULT 1 is a good deal under $100, don't pay over that for that one. But its legit worth it, if you're willing to pay about double the price of this one. Sound improvement isn't double exactly, but the bass and overall loudness are definitely noticeable. Final note - form factor, design, size, and build quality are great on both. You could feel comfortable using either inside or outside and both are light. 4 stars here instead of 5 because of the bass limitation and lack of EQ - keep in mind the bass is better than every other speaker at this price point (under $50), just can't compete with others under $100."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love the sound. This little Bluetooth speaker cost me a little more than half a Benjamin and turns my smartphone into a respectable sound system. Plus, it’s compact, portable, battery powered (for approximately six to eight hours at high volumes w/quick recharge using the newest standardized rechargeable/data connection that has a small, rounded-rectangular “pill”-shaped reversible plug), waterproof, and incredibly drop-resistant.  When I drop it, instead of worrying I tell myself, \"Relax, it's a Sony, it will be fine,\" and it always is. This is actually my second one. I dropped the first speaker many dozens of times over the past four years (easily 50+) and it continued to play flawlessly.What finally pushed me to replace it wasn’t normal wear and tear. During a cross-town move from Brooklyn to Manhattan, I carelessly packed it in an open box. A sudden stop from the moving van bounced it out of the unsecured box, and a heavy table ended up resting on top of it. Amazingly, it wasn’t crushed or dented. The only issue was a slight decline in sound quality at higher volumes — the bass was no longer as clean.Considering what it survived, I was thrilled to find another one just like it for sale on Amazon. Because it’s affordable and so durable, I kept the original as a backup and bought a new one."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great sound and battery life.  Fits in almost all cup holders and perfect for a golf cart!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This little speaker has big sound...solid base!  Easily pairs to iphone and also to a windows laptop.  The microphone works good when using it for a conference speaker. People on the on the other side of the call said it sounded clear and not distorted. This will come in handy when I travel vs. my bigger speaker I normally carry with me when I travel."
    },
    {
        "review": "The SRS-XB100 is a lightweight, highly portable speaker. The sound quality is excellent, especially for such a small unit. Highs are crisp and clean, mids are solid and clear, and lows are punchy and robust. The interface is easy to use, although the stereo pairing function can be a little finicky. But where this small speaker really falls short is the volume.For several years I've used two similar, slightly larger speakers from a different brand: one in my bathroom and one in my kitchen, pairing them both together for outdoor listening. When it was time to replace them I ordered two of the SRS-XB100 and tried the same approach. But I found that a single speaker was barely loud enough to be heard over the shower, and that I needed to pair them together to hear music clearly while cooking. I wouldn't even try to use them for outdoor activities.In short, if you want a small speaker for use at moderate volumes in a sterile listening environment, this is an excellent choice. But if you enjoy music at higher volumes while participating in other activities you should look elsewhere."
    },
    {
        "review": "Diamond for Music Lovers!!I was looking for a Bluetooth speaker mainly for personal use and for home. My main priority was good music quality and decent audio and bass. And Song's SRS-XB100 fulfilled my requirements perfectly.Pros :-1. Best sound , audio and vocal clarity you will find in this price range.2. Very good battery life3.Dust and Water ResistanceCons:-Though I don't have any cons as per my usage and expectations, but it may sound less loud and audio won't feel like blasting in the room and outdoors.I bought it at ₹2999 from The Independence Day sale.Who should buy it?Music lovers, especially and professionals looking for a small, handy and portable and easy to use bluetooth speakerSomeone looking for quality of music rather than loudness, bass or that party vibe.Please avoid buying it if you are looking for that loud bass that boosts up the atmosphere, though it's bass is also very good, you won't be disappointed, but still don't consider it as a hard party speaker.Ideal for music lovers looking for usage at home and personal use."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great purchase! Little box with great sound quality and good bass. I thought it was better than Alexa. Discreet when connecting."
    },
    {
        "review": "Over delivered on quality for the price. Great little speaker to carry around. The clarity of the bass is what sets it aside for me. Listening to jazz I can clearly hear beautiful double bass lines without distortion - Great product"
    },
    {
        "review": "Sound like I love my sony I like my sony this model srs xb100b extra bass portable wireless speaker good"
    },
    {
        "review": "This speaker is small but it works very well, it pairs easily and quickly, it has good volume, the audio quality is very good even though it only has one driver, the bass has good punch without distorting, the mids are heard quite well and the trebles are controlled. You can set a room or a living room, even a meeting of less than 10 people. If you want to host a party in an outdoor area, if you must look for other alternatives, for personal use, whether in an outdoor or indoor area, it is perfect. I use it to listen to music and podcasts from my desk and wow the speaker is a 10. NOTE for Audiophiles: In this type of speakers the audio is heard somewhat compressed, there is more gain in the Bass and even though it is controlled and does not distort, it gets a lot into the other frequencies, the mids are regular and the highs are rounded. Be careful, it is not a defect, it is a characteristic of this type of commercial Bluetooth speakers, no matter the brand, size or even price, these are focused on a different musical enjoyment. If you are looking for Hi-End in audio there is a whole world of studio monitors, DACs. Amps that you can investigate that will give you another musical experience. Greetings from MTY México."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love these JBL speakers! At this point I have several of them because I honestly started collecting the different colors. They all look so cute and stylish, and the color options are beautiful in person. ✨Besides the design, the sound quality is surprisingly good for such a compact speaker. The audio is clear, loud, and perfect for everyday use whether you’re at home, outside, traveling, or hanging out with friends.Another thing I really like is how portable they are. They’re small enough to fit easily into a bag or backpack, and the built-in loop at the top makes it super convenient to clip or hang them almost anywhere. It’s one of those little details that makes them even more practical.The battery life also lasts a long time, which is something I really appreciate because I don’t feel like I constantly need to recharge them. Plus, being waterproof makes them even better for taking outdoors, to the pool, beach, trips, or just daily use without worrying too much.Overall, these are such fun, practical, and reliable speakers. Great sound, beautiful colors, excellent portability, and very convenient for everyday life. Definitely a great purchase and one of my favorite portable speakers! 🔊✨"
    },
    {
        "review": "Picked this up mainly for something small I could clip onto a bag or keep around without taking up space, and it honestly hits way harder than expected.For the size, the sound is surprisingly full. It gets pretty loud and has decent bass, not like a big speaker obviously, but way better than most ultra-portables I’ve tried. Perfect for outside, travel, or just having something on in the background.Battery life has been solid too. I’ve been using it on and off and it easily lasts through the day without needing to recharge.The clip design is actually useful, not just a gimmick. I’ve had it on a backpack and even clipped around the house and it holds securely.Only thing is you have to keep expectations realistic, it’s not going to replace a full-size speaker or fill a large room. At higher volumes it can start to lose a little clarity.Overall, for what it’s meant to be, this thing is hard to beat. Great little speaker."
    },
    {
        "review": "Ok, wow! I was expecting a lightweight, cloudy sounding speaker, but what I got was a sturdy, great sounding, LOUD speaker. I like that you can choose sound \"types/options\", or take control of the graphic equalizer yourself for a more specific sound/vibe. The clip is not heavy or clunky to use, but is very solid. The controls are on the side of the speaker in a small groove so they are a bit tucked away from accidental pushes. There is on, Bluetooth, and a multi speaker function, which is great if you want to link serveral JBL speakers together at once. The speaker itself was super fast and easy to Bluetooth to my phone, and the second I turned my music on, I was hooked!  I love the pink/mint colors (pics don't do it justice!), and the large volume and play button on the front. The rubber \"bumpers\" on the back are great safety and anti movement/vibration prevention. The ONKY thing I wish they would change is to give the speaker a flat base so it sits on tables/counters/etc. Overall, I absolutely love this speaker! I cannot comment on charge life, but if charges fast. The cord is only about 8-10\" long, so don't expect a lot of wiggle room if you intend on keeping it plugged into charge while in use. Overall, I am very happy indeed! I HIGHLY suggest getting the JBL app and registering your speaker! It makes controls and commands so easy! It took less than a minute to download from Play store."
    },
    {
        "review": "This looks so much better in person. It is a beautiful speaker. The sound is fantastic and it is very loud.10 out of 10 I would recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "The JBL Clip 5 is nice portable speaker. It Weighs under a pound with an integrated carabiner,  you can take it anywhere easily. The build quality is rugged can handle drops and rough outdoor conditions. With an IP67 rating, it’s both waterproof and dustproof — ready for outdoor activities like pool parties, hikes, or rainy days without worry.I was pleasantry surprised with it sound quality for its size. Don’t let the size fool you. Its Bass performance is solid and very good for a speaker of this size. At maximum volume, distortion can creep in, but for most casual listening levels this isn’t an issue.It offer a good Battery life around 10 hours of continuous playtime on a single charge. Bluetooth 5.1 ensures a stable connection with good range, and pairing is quick and hassle-free. There’s no auxiliary input or app support, but for a speaker this size that’s expected.It is perfect for travelers, campers, commuters, or anyone who wants reliable sound on the go.  It absolutely excels as a portable companion.Pros• Excellent portability with built-in clip• Rugged, waterproof design• Strong sound for its size• Long battery lifeCons• Slight distortion at top volumes• No aux input or app customizationOverall: A fantastic choice if you want a rugged, portable speaker that sounds great and goes anywhere you do. We picked for our recent beach trip and throughly enjoyed it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this thing!  It's easy to use, convenient and cute.  For some reason, when I'm working around the house, I don't really like wearing my AirPods.  But this is handy and I can take it all over with me when I'm focusing on a room.  Excellent sound quality in a small package.Easy to charge, hang up and connect to my devices.  When I turn the speaker on, it automatically connects to my phone or tablet.I did put an AirTag on it yesterday.  Since I carry it all over the house, I had \"lost\" it temporarily.  This should make it easier to find.I think it would be great to have at an event or gathering if you need a portable speaker."
    },
    {
        "review": "Sound wise it's great, bass is there while not as punchy as the bigger speakers. For it's size, it does great sound, probably better for more speaking audio than music but I was happy with it until I noticed the thing dies after a hour or so. I would charge it over night. Use the next day and it would last a hour or 2 and then disconnect and found out it was dead. I waited for it to go on sale because I wanted a smaller speaker than the flip with good audio.Small and easy to clip on you or a backpack or for me, on a belt at work. But while I found it a good deal, the short battery life is no where near the 12 hour life. It did a update and not sure if that has anything to do with it but not getting anything past 2 hours on battery life.Update: Bluetooth turned out to be the issue. After a few resets it finally works again but does sometimes stutter to stream from phone to speaker. Not the end of the world but slightly annoying when jamming and then it cuts out"
    },
    {
        "review": "The JBL Clip 5 is a great speaker! I’ve had mine for over a year now, and it has held up wonderfully—it’s still going strong. The sound quality is amazing, and the battery life has been very reliable. I even recommend downloading the JBL app to access additional features like software updates, customizable EQ settings, and more.All in all, the JBL Clip 5 is the best value for your money when it comes to a portable speaker. You can always count on JBL for great sound and quality products!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Amazing speaker! And it was a nice surprise that the seller packed a nice gift with it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great music box, great sound"
    },
    {
        "review": "Outstanding"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "The JBL Boombox 3 delivers powerful sound with deep, rich bass that you can actually feel. Whether indoors or outside, the volume gets seriously loud without losing clarity. Music sounds crisp, balanced, and energetic across different genres.The battery life is impressive and easily lasts through long listening sessions or outdoor gatherings. I also like the solid build quality. It feels durable, premium, and easy to carry despite the size. The Bluetooth connection has been stable with no issues pairing devices.Overall, this speaker is worth it if you want strong bass, clear sound, and enough power to fill a room or backyard with music."
    },
    {
        "review": "Super expensive but sounds great! I don't regret buying it at all. But it is way more expensive than it needs to be. Battery life lasts about 3 hours when cranked up all the way. The best thing is that you can continue to use it while it is plugged in. It is waterproof and does float. Anytime it gets dirty i just rinse it off. But beware it will continue to drain water out of it for hours so don't set it on a surface that it will ruin after you get it wet. Sound quality is very good. Bass is strong and it is very loud. If I am in the garage with the doors closed you can here it in the street so don't under estimate it. Also you have to use the app to set it up which was kinda of dumb but it does allow you to tweak the sound which was a very nice feature. you will notice though it lags a bit when connecting when you turn it on and when it disconnects when you shut it off which is no big deal but definitely can be improved upon. Over all for a portable speaker system there isn't really anything out there that can touch this for sound quality, durability or how loud it can go while still have clarity. This is probably why JBL charges a serious premium for it. You will also notice it does have some weight to it so it is not something you would want to carry around all day. I also notice it does improve the sound a bit if you leave it plugged in while using it is you are going to listen to it real loud. If you buy it, you wont regret it. I sure don't. I use it very frequently to the dismay of my neighbors"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great Speaker.  Almost as good as a component stereo system.  Great sound.  The JBL excels outdoors.  It just sounds great.I also purchased a Sonos Move 2 and had them at the same time and compared the two.  I switched back and forth between them, comparing the same song.The Sonos is going back but it is a nice speaker.  Not as balanced.  Best at low volume levels.In general the Sonos sounds like it has a lot of digital signal processing DSP / EQ.  I also didn't want a microphone listening to me all the time like the Sonos.The JBL is large and heavy but I think that is a small price for such good sound.I used Apple lossless CD burns via bluetooth for my comparisons."
    },
    {
        "review": "Nice sound quality. It gives loud noises or music sound around my work. Great Bluetooth connection and easy to use. And you can also play it portability anywhere you want for a long time. And it might be the distortion of JBL  boombox 2 or 4. Just because of the sound and the bass."
    },
    {
        "review": "10/10 for sound quality. This was an impulsive purchase. But it was well worth . Now the price point isn’t for everyone.  15lbs isn’t heavy.. but I wouldn’t set on a table or on top of anything that can’t handle the weight or vibration from all the bass. This boombox isn’t a regular speaker. This has a lot more power compared to a regular JBL speaker.  Also great is you wanna make your neighbors or roommates hate you. lol"
    },
    {
        "review": "I finally bit the bullet and bought this Boombox 3. I own three other Bluetooth speakers. This one just sounds the best. It has tight sound and a booming bass. I work in a factory where the ambient noise reaches 89 decibels at times. This speaker soars above it all. Yes, I know about hearing loss, and I’m not going to get into it here. At first I thought about getting the Boombox 4, but I like the sound better with this model.4/17/26I finally brought this speaker to work. At full volume I got about fours of use, and now I’m down to 10% battery. I’m actually disappointed."
    },
    {
        "review": "This speaker is amazing!Long story, but I bought it on accident, I didn't think I'd ever be okay paying this much for a speaker, but I can't go back.I listen to music all day every day. I have a few different speakers & headphones...JBL Charge 4JBL Vibe BeamApple earbuds (pro & regular)Some other brands of speakers that are less notable, the list goes on...There's something lacking in each one, mostly the volume and bass quality. For working out I dance, and I like my music LOUD. This speaker is IT. It's the only (non-club/concert) speaker I've ever though, wow - that's too loud, I should turn it down. The first time I turned it on I was blown away.It's pretty big and heavy, but I guess that just comes with the huge amount of sound it produces. I feel like the battery life is okay. I really only use it in the house so I don't need it to last very long. It charges relatively fast and I haven't had any issues with connectivity. Super user friendly. It's seriously the best (home) speaker I've ever heard. I'd say it's definitely worth the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "I would like to recommend this JBL speaker because it offers excellent sound quality, powerful bass, long battery life, and a durable design. It has met my expectations, and I believe it is a great option for anyone looking for a reliable, high-quality audio device."
    },
    {
        "review": "J'ai reçu mon JBL BOOMBOX3 ,ET LA PRISE POUR SECTEUR NEST PAS CONFORME EN FRANCE,IL ME FAUT UNE PRISE ADAPTÉ POUR LES PRISES FRANÇAISES, COMMENT SOLUTIONNER CE PROBLÈME"
    },
    {
        "review": "This speaker is incredible.Being an audiophile, I know a good sound when I hear one and the Boombox 3 is fantastic. Warm bass with clear and detailed midrange and sweet top notes. Really easy to connect to your smartphone, you’ll be playing music before you know it. Having existing JBL devices, it was important for me to have the Partylink feature that you don’t get on the more expensive Boombox 3 WiFi (big mistake JBL).This really is everything you’ll need for any outside party….amazing indoors too.Buy with confidence. Highly recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "The JBL Boombox 3 exceeded all my expectations. From the moment I turned it on, I was blown away by the sound quality. The bass is absolutely incredible, deep, powerful, and unlike anything I've heard from a portable speaker before.The build quality feels premium and durable, and the speaker looks as good as it sounds. It gets impressively loud while still maintaining clear audio, making it perfect for parties, outdoor gatherings, or simply enjoying music at home.The long battery life is another huge plus, and the waterproof design adds extra peace of mind when using it outdoors.Overall, this is a fantastic product and one of the best Bluetooth speakers I've ever owned. If I had the budget, I'd buy it again without hesitation. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "excellent"
    }
