[
    {
        "review": "I have wanted these Henckels knives for a long time and finally got the opportunity during a Prime Day sale.I can't say enough good things about these knives. They are sharp so be careful! Compared to the dull knives I used before, there is no comparison. These knives easily slice through everything I use them for, mostly meat and veggies. This set contains every type of knife I need, including scissors and a sharpener.I will not allow these beautiful knives to sit in soapy water or the dishwasher, therefore I can't speak to how well they will hold up over time to rusting. I am relying exclusively on the well-regarded reputation of the manufacturer.Overall, I gave these knives 5-stars because of the quality, sharpness, and ease of handling. They are sturdy and I am not concerned about rusting or degrading of the metal. This is an excellent set for the price and I'm very pleased!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm pretty sure that this set I just bought is the fourth set in my lifetime. No question of which is the best set and it's the Henckels.  My, what a beautiful set of knives, with one for every need in the kitchen or at dinner. The steel is high quality and the blades are thin, a combination which is ideal for ease of use. What strikes you is the hefty handle and the slender blade, providing a great balance in the hand. And, of course, they come razor sharp and also an excellent sharpener is provided with the set. I don't think there is a competing set of knives on the market which can compare."
    },
    {
        "review": "bought these knives to prep dinner. I wasn’t expecting to enter a committed relationship.The first time I used the chef’s knife, it slid through a tomato so effortlessly that I had to look around to make sure nobody saw me smiling. The sharpness is downright scandalous. Carrots? Paper-thin. Steak? Like butter. My old knives watched from the drawer in shame.The balance is incredible, the grip feels just right in your hand, and every slice is so smooth it should probably come with a warning label. Cooking has become dangerously enjoyable. I now volunteer to chop everything. “Need onions diced?” Say less.My spouse is starting to get jealous because I’ve been spending an awful lot of quality time with this knife block. Honestly, I haven’t felt this much excitement in the kitchen in years.If you’ve never whispered, “Oh… wow,” after slicing a bell pepper, you’re about to.Five stars. Sharp enough to cut vegetables… and dangerously close to stealing my heart. ❤️🔪"
    },
    {
        "review": "I've had this knife set for over a year now. I have no cons to it at all. I use the honing rod probably every other time I use the big chef knives, and they're still as sharp and beautiful as the first day I got them. Every single knife is sturdy and feels solid. I hand wash all the sharp blades, but I do run the serrated ones through my dishwasher sometimes because I'm lazy 😅. I like that the prep knives lay on their sides in the block, I think that protects the blades better. The steak knives fit in vertically, but I just put them in upside down so they don't rest on the cutting edge. I don't like how close the honing rod is to the bread knife right below it, but that's not too big of a deal.The knives and block look beautiful on my counter, and everything seems to be great quality. I am glad I bought this and am considering buying one for my daughter."
