        "review": "I bought the three piece set to keep at the fire station i work at because the shared knives are awful and abused by people that think a ceramic plate or stainless counter top are appropriate cutting surfaces. I caught them on sale and honestly couldn't be happier. The set was packaged in foam cut so nothing shifts during transport, they really took the time to pack them well.  They're shaving sharp right out of the box and after your first few cuts with them, if you're not at least a little nervous around their edges, you're not paying attention. I caught my fingernail the other day. It didn't just shave my nail like my good set at home would... it cut through my nail and actually nicked the skin underneath.. it cut through the nail!!! So my decision is made, I'm going to buy the set with the roll for our new house, as well as a few more knives from their other collections because I cannot imagine they wouldn't be just as amazing. I've cut meat, veggies and chopped roasts, loins and pork butts, so I'm not being gentle with them, and I can still shave with them. I haven't seen any sign of rust yet. I think they're beautiful, love the rustic design and can't tell you how great they perform in the kitchen.  10 out of 10 you need these(or another set from this manufacturer of this style isn't your cup of tea). They have sales pretty regularly. Though, even at full price you're getting knives that cut waaaay above their price range. The only problem I've had is that a coworker managed to drop the non cleaver directly into its tip and bent it.. then he decided to grind it flat.. I spent some time re-profiling the tip and keeping it cool to not ruin the temper and haven't had any complications with the tip edge at all. It's good steel"
