[
    {
        "review": "I read through plenty of reviews and looked at a bunch of different knife sets. I watched review videos and other videos to learn about knife blocks as I have wanted one for quite some time. This block and set is gorgeous. It looks INCREDIBLE on my kitchen counter and the knives are sharp. Very sharp. I easily sliced through several sheets of paper with a couple of different included knives. It chopped up some garlic, onion, and broccoli with ease. I used the included shears to cut things my normal scissors couldn't even touch with ease. The knives look and feel like I'm working with top of the line equipment. They are balanced and feel great in the hand. I've only had them for a couple of weeks but have followed the advice I've seen online to immediately hand wash and/or wipe them with a towel and they have kept their shine and sharpness perfectly without any rust spots. I got these on sale for Black Friday so I got an incredible deal but even if you can't get these for cheaper they are exceptional for the cost."
    },
    {
        "review": "Perfect knives very sharp and stylish just what I was looking for. Be very careful they are extremely sharp but they cut so easily. My knife shopping is over these are the solution to my old tired dull knives"
    },
    {
        "review": "I waited a few months before I wrote a review, and with that said, the wife & I are VERY pleased. They look really nice, and the fact the holding block is more angled, they're easy to get in & out of the block if your cabinets are a bit lower like ours. At 1st I didn't like that their weight seemed a bit light to the feel. But when you're cutting a bunch of something (like a bunch of cheese for crackers for snacks for a family of 5 with 3 teenagers), you'll be thankful they're lighter. We don't have a dishwasher, so we already hand was & dry them, and so far no rust or deglazing, & the literally look like they did when we got them. OH.... And they're SHARP AS HELL! I'll warn you right now, some point you WILL get cut, so don't say I didn't warn you.... Honestly is you're looking to replace your older set, & not \"break the bank\", then this set is what you're looking for. My ONLY wish is that the steak knives could have some serrations on them, but they're sharp enough that it 90% of the time doesn't matter. Just don't cook your steak super well done like a psychopath, and you'll be great."
    },
    {
        "review": "Razor sharp!  I bought this set to replace a 10 y/o set of Chicago Cutlery blades because i lost a few.What a difference!  These blades are perfectly balanced and just \"feel good\"!  They are SHARP!  Effortlessly slice a tomato, and glide thru a steak like a light saber!  HIGHLY RECOMMEND!!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I did a lot of research on knife sets. This one came to me with five stars. I’m adding to that. At this time, I love them, they’re very solid and seem to be well made and professionally designed. They are very sharp, as the company people comment. I will stay in touch if anything goes wrong with them or have anything I want to share with you about the knives."
    },
    {
        "review": "After owning several medium priced knife sets in my lifetime, I found this one to be exceptional. The knives come razor sharp and all one piece.  There are no seams no rivets, just completely one piece knives with no crevices or anything to collect dirt or bacteria in.  They are well balanced and feel good in your hand and slice through meat like butter.I was originally surprised that the wood block that hold the knives had unlined slots that the knives go into. However, upon investigation I found out that this is actually the preferred method to store knives.  Wooden blocks that have inserts in them for the knife blades can cause more problems than they're worth and actually a well sanded, smooth, pure wood slot is better, according several artificial Intelligence applications that I asked about this.  Just be aware that you can't leave them laying around when you're done nor can you put them in a dishwasher. When you're finished using them, you've got to wash them with soap and water and dry them before putting it away.For the price. I think you're getting a great deal on these knives and I highly recommend them.tkeeg"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this set to replace another block of knives that I have had for seven or eight years. In general, I like this set. All the knives arrived hyper-sharp; I have already cut myself two times. They are so sharp that it's almost like you can get cut just thinking about them. That's a good thing. However, I don't like how much of a footprint they take up on my counter. My last set, which you can see in the picture, takes up a much smaller amount of space. This new set juts out and makes itself known like it has self-esteem problems or something. (Overcompensate much?) Also, I really, REALLY dislike how the scissors are located in the middle of the block. How is that a good idea?! The knife underneath it is almost guaranteed to at some point slice into the rubber handles of the scissors. Not a great design. Am I going to keep it? Of course. The construction in general is good, the knives are sharp, and I like the style. I just wish it didn't take up so much space And I wish the layout were a bit different. I will be sure to check this with the next knife block set that I buy. (If you have discerning eyes, you will have noticed that the knives on the bottom row are put into the block upside down. That is a pro tip that I pass along to you: The sharp edge of the knife never comes into contact with the block itself, which keeps the knives sharper over time. You are welcome.) Four stars instead of five because the block takes too much space, when it really doesn't need to, and those darn scissors are right smack in the middle where it is incredibly inconvenient."
    },
    {
        "review": "I almost want to take away a star for all of the times I've cut myself 🤣  these things are so sharp! Heed all warnings from every review stating it! I won't let my 12 y/o use them due to concern for his finger safety but these knives are great! Super sharp right out of the box and honestly put my old Ninja never dulls to absolute shame.  I purchased these because the thin blades of the Ninja were ridiculously dull and pieces started snapping off of the blade (could have put my eye out!) and my only regret is not buying safety gloves. My elder son was slicing an avocado and I went running in what felt like slow mo screaming no because he was cupping it in has hand and anyone of these knives could slice right through the skin and the fruit in one swipe. Other than that, they feel great in hand,  sturdy, and hopefully they kept up the good work."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I received this camera today and am very excited to use it, so this might be a rushed review! LOVE the camera!It has great beginner friendly modes and is very simple to use and get the feel of. I will say that if you have never used any form of ‘professional’ camera, the different modes and buttons may confuse you for a bit, but once you get adjusted it’s very simple!The lens is nice and allows ample zoom to allow close ups!However, if you are looking for zoom quality from ample distance, you’re going to need another lens. I ordered a telephoto lens, so I’ll see how that works out.In terms of pricing, the camera is amazing quality, though I did end up finding bundle kits that come with a bit more for the same price. If you’re looking for quality pieces only, then this is definitely the right pick!The camera is fairly lightweight in itself, with lenses it will obviously get heavier, but not bulky and very easy to handle with the grip.All the different modes and settings allow for a variety of pictures! I’m more focused on nature pictures, but this does great for people and animals.The camera has GREAT picture quality and refined details. I’m able to magnify into my photos and see crystal clear details you can’t see with the naked eye.I do hiking occasionally, so this camera is going to be great for it! Very excited to see how it does as we plan on going to upstate NY for a hiking expedition and visiting multiple spots.I’ll update further on its performance if needed!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this camera as a cheap way to take good pictures and the pictures and better than expected. I recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "As someone who wanted to level up from phone photography but wasn’t quite ready to dive into $2,000 camera bodies, the Canon EOS Rebel T7 was the perfect bridge — and it has exceeded expectations.⸻Image QualityThe 24.1 MP sensor captures crisp, clean images in both daylight and low light. You’ll instantly notice the difference in depth, clarity, and color accuracy compared to any smartphone. Whether you’re shooting portraits, street scenes, or nature — it delivers professional-looking results.⸻Ease of UseThis is where the T7 shines. The controls are intuitive, even for someone brand new to DSLRs. The built-in Feature Guide explains settings in real-time, helping you learn as you shoot. It’s like a camera and teacher in one.⸻ConnectivityBuilt-in Wi-Fi is a huge plus. I can snap a photo and send it to my phone instantly for social media or editing. The Canon Camera Connect app works smoothly with iOS and Android.⸻Build & Features• Lightweight but solid — feels durable without being bulky• Interchangeable lenses give you room to grow (the included 18–55mm lens is a great start)• 3 FPS continuous shooting — not blazing fast, but great for beginners shooting action• Full HD 1080p video recording — smooth, with decent autofocus⸻Who It’s ForIf you’re a beginner who wants a real DSLR experience without feeling overwhelmed — this is your camera. It’s also a great backup for experienced shooters who want something reliable, portable, and affordable.⸻Final VerdictThe Canon EOS Rebel T7 is proof that entry-level doesn’t mean low quality. It’s a fantastic intro into the world of serious photography, and once you start using it, you’ll wonder why you waited. Sharp photos, simple learning curve, and real Canon reliability."
    },
    {
        "review": "Although it was an open box [not taped shut] and the battery was in a plastic bag[ no protective cap] and no paperwork whatsoever included ,for a supposedly new camera , i,m keeping it as it has enabled me to take 110 good quality pictures so far! Easy to use if you like or you can be creative with it! Download the manual from the internet! reminds me of my canon AE1 but much more capable!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this camera has many features that are not found in this price range"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Canon EOS Rebel T7 is a fantastic choice for beginners who want a simple, affordable, and reliable DSLR for photography. It offers great image quality and ease of use, though it’s not the best for video-heavy users."
    },
    {
        "review": "The photos with this camera are fantastic! A great camera easy to use.  An exceptional camera. My daughter and granddaughter love it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great camera for a beginner!  I love it and would definitely recommend buying if you're just now starting off"
    },
    {
        "review": "In my case, R100 came, the seller was super accessible and attentive, he provided all possible support for what happened. The product was sent quickly and delivery also came ahead of schedule, everything in order, with manual, invoice and well packaged. Original product, camera is light and compact with a rubberized finish, it has its own built-in flash and you can also add another one if you prefer, battery and charger, it comes with a Canon strap, it even appears to be resistant, the rest are working perfectly too. For the charger, I recommend having an adapter to be able to charge it. Note: the card shown in the photos is not included with the product, it was a separate purchase. Overall, I loved the product and service, super reliable store, I highly recommend it. Thanks!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I liked it a lot, I am not a professional photographer, but it was worth it, the camera has good focus, records very well, has a lens that focuses automatically, takes good photographs. Of course, you have to buy the cable to share the photos to your computer, but you can find it in electronics stores"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Canon Rebel T7 camera offers a compelling entry-level experience for photography enthusiasts. Its 24.1-megapixel APS-C CMOS sensor delivers crisp and vibrant images, while the DIGIC 4+ image processor ensures swift performance.The camera's autofocus system performs admirably, especially in well-lit conditions, providing quick and accurate focus on subjects. Its beginner-friendly features, such as Scene Intelligent Auto mode, make it accessible for those new to DSLR photography.The T7's ergonomic design and lightweight build enhance portability without compromising on durability. The 3-inch LCD screen is clear and bright, facilitating easy composition and review of shots.While the camera lacks advanced features like 4K video recording, its Full HD video capabilities produce decent results. Battery life is commendable, allowing for extended shooting sessions without constant recharging.In conclusion, the Canon Rebel T7 is an excellent choice for entry-level photographers seeking a reliable and user-friendly DSLR camera with solid image quality and performance."
    },
    {
        "review": "great camera for the price"
    },
    {
        "review": "The camera does everything it promises. Excellent! And it arrived much earlier than expected."
