[
    {
        "review": "The product was delivered the next day and although not packaged super neatly, nothing was damaged. The camera itself and the lens come in separate, well packed boxes inside the outer box. No issues at all, though, the only thing I didn't receive was the book, which indicates that it would be digitally delivered but I haven't yet received the download link for that.As for the additional accessories being poor quality, they simply aren't poor quality. Are they Canon quality and do they look like Canon products, no. But the quality is good, some are Japanese, some are from Taiwan, both acceptable as far as quality goes, so I think there may be an assumption that because it's not quite as well presented or packaged that somehow its inferior. The lenses are strong and solid.You don't get what's in the photograph, that's an accurate statement. But you do get what's listed in the specs listed. I'm super excited to kick off my DSLR adventure after having previously owned a Dimage A2 (back when 8 MP was considered huge."
    },
    {
        "review": "This was a  great deal ! Thank you so much ! Everything working flawlessly ! Appreciate the great customer service !! If I could give it 10 stars I would !!! Thank you !!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Arrived in the two day delivery time frame.  Had a problem with the memory card.  Purchased a 32 GB that is recommended .  Seller is giving a small credit because of this.  Very prompt responses from seller and most helpful.  This is my third Canon camera.  First was a 35 mil and then a Rebel T1 digital around  17 years ago.  It still works but I wanted an upgrade.  Looking forward to all the beautiful pictures I will take.  This is a great bundle for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "As a life-long photographer,  this was my treat to myself in retirement.  Canon quality through and through.  Couldn't be more pleased."
    },
    {
        "review": "Still learning how to use it.  But glad I got it."
    },
    {
        "review": "This bundle has everything you need to capture your own professional photos!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great starter kit takes wonderful photos always more to get but this is got lens for most shots"
    },
    {
        "review": "If I could give this 0 stars, I absolutely would.I purchased this camera listed as new, not refurbished. When it arrived, I was initially very pleased. I’ve used Canon cameras most of my adult life, and this one seemed no different—great picture quality, easy to use, and the included accessories made it feel like a solid value.However, that positive impression didn’t last.After just three uses, the camera completely failed on the fourth shoot. I took one picture and the camera stopped functioning entirely. At first, I assumed it was a dead battery. After recharging, I tried again—nothing worked. The flash would fire, but the menu wouldn’t even come up. At that point, it was clear this was not user error—it was a defective unit.Then things became even more concerning.When I attempted to register the camera with Canon, the system indicated that the camera and one of the lenses had already been registered. That should never happen with a product sold as “new.” It strongly suggests this item may have been previously used or resold. About a week later, when we tried again, that warning mysteriously disappeared—which only adds to the suspicion.At this point, we contacted Amazon, since we were still within the return window. I simply wanted a replacement or refund for a clearly defective product. Because we no longer had the original packaging, we were told we had to deal directly with the third-party seller, Beach Camera.This is where the experience completely broke down.Despite receiving a defective camera that failed almost immediately, Beach Camera:Refused a straightforward exchange or refundOpened a vague “investigation” instead of resolving the issueAttempted to offer only $88 compensation for an $800+ broken cameraRequired me to pay return shippingCharged a 20% restocking fee—even though the product was defectiveCharging a restocking fee on a defective item is unacceptable. Passing the cost of their failure onto the customer is worse.Thankfully, Amazon ultimately stepped in to make things right, although I now have to cover costs upfront and wait for reimbursement. Without that support, this would have been a complete loss.Bottom line: Most vendors—and Amazon—stand behind what they sell. Beach Camera does not. They failed at every stage: selling a questionable “new” product, refusing to take responsibility for a defect, and attempting to penalize the customer for their own failure.I strongly recommend avoiding this vendor."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I am a seasoned photographer from long ago, I was hesitating for years getting into digital photography because there's no comparison to real film. This camera is absolutely shocking, you better have your belt buckle and your socks pulled up when you read the manual for this beast! This is definitely not for the newbie, you will be blown away instantly. The photos are pretty awesome I haven't printed any yet so I can't compare it to real film but I did take a picture of the moon with the lens that came with it and it blew my mind, nothing else to say, Nikon! PS, the picture is a picture of the image on the back of the camera not the actual picture, it is crystal clear I just don't have to have it on hand and this is one that I texted to someone because I was so excited at the moment it happened. I am not compensated in any way, and you can get it with PayPal in 4 payments, just FYI"
    },
    {
        "review": "The D7500 came out in 2017, is one of Nikons higher quality models from that time. Does not have latest tech compared to latest cameras or even phones. But for my needs, its almost perfect. Excellent viewfinder, awesome battery life (typical of dslr's, and one of the advantages over mirrorless cameras). So easy to get a great image. Fast accurate auto-focus. I prefer Program mode, but when in Auto mode, you can still get amazing, dependably  sharp lower noise photos. The lens (18-140mm) it comes with is awesome, great image quality at all focal lengths. I bought an older model, because it was new (hard to find this model new anymore), on deep discount (at least compared to price when released in 2017), and was the higher quality model I was looking for. Lens and camera body are weather resistant. Great movie quality, too.  I almost always use 4k, I'm ok with 30 fps., (though many newer models have 4K 60fps) movie image quality is clear, sharp, pleasing.It is certainly larger than a compact camera, but I can't afford one of the better compact models out now, and even many full frame cameras are  now smaller than the D7500. What with Tariffs and general inflation, good cameras are VERY expensive now. I must admit I am partial to Nikon, and I wanted a camera with a decent range telephoto lens. This camera tiks all the boxes important to me, I extremely happy with it. The lens is fairly compact for an 18-140mm configuration, is just an outstanding lens."
    },
    {
        "review": "This camera, although it would be considered “dated” by younger generations of photographers, is still very much a powerhouse and a must have for anyone wanting to take photos in a variety of situations! This is a step up from the previous DSLR I owned so there is a small learning curve for me as far as the features. I also consider it a step up from the z50 mirrorless I own. While mirrorless is lighter weight, there are situations where it just isn’t capable of doing what I need.The real test for this D7500 will be marching season during halftime shows, but as of so far, I’m impressed! The 18-140 lens is truly an excellent lens! It is able to zoom in and out as I need in all situations I’ve used it so far. Very fast auto focus and I love that I can easily switch to manual on the lens itself without fiddling with settings on the camera. This significantly lowers the risk of me missing a photo opportunity because I’m looking for a setting in the camera menu.Sturdy body. This does add weight to the camera but honestly I feel like that isn’t a bad thing. I started my photography journey with an SLR with no auto focus and black & white film in HS. I learned to develop the film and photos myself.The features and options on this camera are truly amazing and I still have a lot to learn about it, but so far I’m impressed! I’ve always been a Nikon girl and they continue to provide excellent photography cameras and lenses!*photo taken at my local Memorial Day ceremony. This pup was super fast and I took several photos in quick succession to get the one shown on the review here. The D7500 didn’t hesitate, focused quickly and I was able to take this picture. The owners were thrilled when I posted it on the local page as they had yet to get a good pic of their new pup :)"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very nice upgrade from my old Nikon Coolpix A900. High quality photos once you learn how to use manual mode. I like being able to control light with the shutter peed/F-stop. I have not used to flash yet because I use manual mode. Great combo with the lens (18-140mm). I have since bought a 70-300mm Nikor lens. It may be out-dated but, I LOVE ths camera. BIG upgrade for me. Nikon quality!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a great camera.  I got it in June 2025.  It's now Feb 2026 and I have had NO ISSUES with it at all.  If you're coming from an older Nikon, like I was, it'll take time getting used to the buttons/settings being in different locations (which is weird lol) but other than that, it's been a great camera.  You tube has some helpful videos on using this camera and learning that settings."
    },
    {
        "review": "Loved it but still learning its intricacies!"
    },
    {
        "review": "3 week update:  Have used this camera daily.  It is simple to learn, simple to use, a real joy for wildlife.  After 3 week the menus and controls are becoming more 2nd nature.  Because of all the features I expected that it would take longer to start feeling familiar.  Occasionally I have to go back to a reference to find what I am looking for, but really, this camera is an amazingly intuitive piece of technology even for a beginner.Your camera takes good pictures goes the joke. It is no joke with the D7500.I have used the Coolpx P900 for ~two years. I have never used a DSLR. The D7500 is my first. The pix with this review were taken on the first two days I owned it. These pix were shot on shutter preferred and manual.I had no idea a DSLR camera could be so amazing and forgiving.If I can do this, imagine what you can do if you have knowledge and experience.I carefully researched DSLRs before making this purchase. You will find that if you do this camera is highly rated. Let those reviews will guide your decision.I got this camera because I wanted a camera I could grow into, a camera that would work for wildlife and action, and a camera that was considered an excellent buy in professional reviews. I also chose Nikon because I was familiar with the layout and language because of my P900.For me it was a spectacular choice.  I highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "great camera.  still learning all the bells and whistles.  Replaced a much older Nikon I lost in a housefire.  I had my old camera down but now I am a novice with this one."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great semi-professional camera. A good start for intermediate profiles who want to take a little more photos other than in automatic mode."
    },
    {
        "review": "I was searching for the upgrade.  At first, I was thinking of a pricey Nikon mirrorless camera.  After doing more research, i decided to go with Nikon D7500 for upgrading my outdated and old school Nikon D90.  I decided to purchase this DSLR due to its price and all requirements that I am looking for are met, with tilting screen, 4K video recording, audio & video inputs, Wifi & Bluetooth capability and with 51 focus points which is good for shooting wildlife, portrait and landscape.  Also, all my lenses are with F-Mount.  With a big surprise, all the items (DSLR + Kit Lens) are all brand new and very well packed and secured.I strongly recommend the seller for the job well done.  You got my trust."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great for beginners to semi-pro photographers"
    },
    {
        "review": "Girlfriend is more than happy to have a nice camera in her hands. So handy that all photos can be directly transfered to your mobile phone."
