    {
        "review": "I've owned fancy coffee making machines with confusing displays at a high cost and will never go back. These simple Black+Decker coffee machines are perfect. They're also durable and don't have the malfunctioning problems like these \"fancy\" coffee machines that are over-designed with technological components that fail far too soon. I've seen these simple coffee machines last longer than the Keurig's and Cusinart machines in office spaces where multiple people have to operate the machine to make their coffee. The price is dirt cheap but you get an old school reliable coffee making machine that not only does the job perfectly every time, but is simple to operate and lasts. I not only highly recommend this product but also the Black+Decker coffee grinder as well. Imagine spending $200 on a Cuisinart coffee machine that doesn't even burr your coffee beans, but then you could buy this coffee machine and their coffee grinder and pay less than half the price and less hassle. I swear by this coffee machine and highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "STOP BUYING EXPENSIVE COFFEE POTS!!!  I was tired of spending $80+ once a year on a coffee pot that would only last a year and had special screws so that you couldn't get in and clean the water pipes inside that so easily clogged.  Just think of the crap your coffee water is being filtered through before making your coffee.  I'm so angry, those screws should be illegal.  This coffee pot is just a simple, manual machine that would make coffee fast.  Forget throwing so much money away so you can set a clock to have coffee for the morning.  You can pour the water and put the grinds in the night before then simply click it on in the morning or spend one minute doing it in the morning and have your coffee faster than you can finish your morning bathroom routine.  I'm angry at these companies that deliberately put those screws there to deliberately (uhum) screw you to get more money from you.So what if you spend a few days to get your perfect coffee flavour, you generally have to do that with any pot.  I did have to use a bit more coffee with this one because it pours so fast - or maybe it's simply because it's a 12 cup pot instead of the 10 cup I was using.  I also had x3 thermos coffee pots from the more expensive machines so I simply pour the coffee into one and voila !!  Hot coffee for the day without the burn.THANK YOU 'BLACK and DECKER' for this cost-saving \"Easy Pour, Non-Drip Carafe with Removable Filter Basket\" product.  I actually didn't check the type of screws on this one, yet - I'm still too angry about them, but I hope you think about normal ones if you're using those 'screwy' ones.  Give the consumer a chance to drink clean water by letting us clean those pipes inside.  I guarantee you'll increase sales on any of your coffee pots if you advertise that ability to always drink clean water with 'Black and Decker' products!"
