[
    {
        "review": "Inexpensive, but impressive. I purchased this unit after purchasing the Krups version (which is also nice). The Krups one did not have an auto-shutoff, but this one does. I sometimes forget to turn off the coffee and didn't want a possible fire risk with a dry pot situation. This Amazon Basics unit is no frills, does what it says, and has the auto-shutoff (yes, I tested it, and yes, it works).  The build quality is cheap, but works as intended. For under $20, I can't complain. The carafe is a 5-sup, but fill up my Yeti mug perfectly with 2 full cups - which is the perfect amount of coffee for me.  Brew time is relatively fast and carafe keeps it nice and hot.  Recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great coffee maker!  I'm the only one to drink coffee in our house and love this coffee makers small size though it would work well for a couple too. Easy to use and no leaks. Brews at the perfect temperature.  Decided to purchase this as reducing plastic waste from kcups and also reduce costs. This coffee machine performs very well and very happy with this purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "★★★★★ Perfect for one or two peopleI really like this little coffee maker! It's compact, brews quickly, and doesn't take up much counter space. The Pause & Serve feature is handy when I want a cup before the pot is finished, and the auto shutoff is a great safety feature for peace of mind. Because I always forget to shut off the Coffee potFor the price, it's an excellent value and makes a great cup of coffee. I definitely recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I started using this coffee maker on July 7, 2026, and I'm writing this review on July 14, 2026. Here are some things a potential buyer should know.Things I like:1. It makes good coffee.2. It has a small footprint on my counter.3. The automatic turn-off of the warmer after 2 hours.4. The ease of use.5. The coffee is nice and hot, and the warmer keeps it that way for 2 hours.Something you should know: Believe the reviewers who note that the five cups it claims to make are very small cups. My coffee cup holds a comfortable 10 ounces (300ml). If I fill the water up just short of the 4-cup line on this machine, it makes two of my 10 ounce cups. That's perfect for me, but it might not be right for you, unless you do use tiny cups.There is nothing that I strongly dislike about this coffee maker, but there is one thing that I find mildly annoying: It is so light that it slides on my counter when I open the bin to put in water and coffee or when I press the on-off switch. These simple tasks become two-hand operations--one hand to steady the machine, the other to do the task at hand. (I might try to find a way to remedy this.)This machine is not perfect, but for the price and for what I need, I am very satisfied with the purchase. If I have more to add after I've put more miles on it, I will update this review."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am very happy with this coffee machine. It is easy to use, heats up quickly, and makes delicious coffee every time. The design is modern and looks great on my kitchen counter. I also like that it is simple to clean and doesn’t take up too much space. The coffee comes out hot, flavorful, and smooth. For the price, the quality is amazing. I would definitely recommend this coffee maker to anyone who loves a good cup of coffee!"
    },
