[
    {
        "review": "I bought one a 3 years ago I cleaned it regularly. When I cleanedit this time  it won’t turn on after cleaning.  Doesn’t even light up. Talked to my friends they said that thought was crazy to expect more than 3 years. It worked great until that last cleaning. Did I do something wrong? Great coffee maker up till this so I did order another one it is on its way.  It I need coffee NOW.  LOL"
    },
    {
        "review": "⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Love the color and how easy it is to use!I just received my new Keurig, and I’m really happy with it so far! The dark green color is absolutely beautiful and looks even better in person. It fits perfectly on my coffee station without taking up too much space.Setup was quick and easy right out of the box. Within a few minutes, I had it ready to brew my first cup. I like that it has multiple cup-size options, and it fits my travel mug without any issues.The coffee brews quickly, is nice and hot, and the machine is much quieter than I expected. Overall, it feels well-made and is perfect for anyone who wants a simple, reliable coffee maker without a lot of extra buttons.If you’re looking for a compact Keurig that looks great and makes a good cup of coffee, I would definitely recommend this one!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This Keurig single-serve coffee maker has been great for everyday use, especially if you don’t want a large machine taking up counter space. I’ve had mine for over a year, use it every day, and it still works just as reliably as it did when I first got it.It brews incredibly quickly, usually in around 30 seconds or less, and it’s surprisingly quiet while running. I also love how small and lightweight it is. It’s easy to move around, pack up, or take somewhere else when needed, so portability is definitely one of its strongest features.I’ve had no issues using different pod options with it. It works with the regular coffee pods I buy, including Starbucks, as well as the reusable pod options I’ve tried. I like having the flexibility to use either prefilled pods or my own coffee without needing separate equipment.Pros:* Excellent space-saving design* Very quiet* Brews in around 30 seconds* Small and lightweight* Extremely portable* Works with multiple pod options* Compatible with reusable pods* Easy to use* Reliable for daily use* Still working great after more than a yearOverall: This has proven to be a really dependable little coffee maker. I use it every single day, it takes up barely any room, and I can have coffee ready incredibly quickly. After more than a year of regular use with no issues, I definitely think it’s a great value for the money."
    },
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love my new Keurig K-Express! From the moment I took it out of the box, it was incredibly easy to set up and start using. Within just a few minutes, I was enjoying my first cup of coffee.What impressed me most is how quickly it brews. Mornings are busy, and having a fresh, hot cup of coffee ready in about a minute is a game changer. The Strong Brew button is one of my favorite features because it gives my coffee a richer, bolder flavor without any extra effort.The compact design fits perfectly on my countertop without taking up a lot of space, and the removable water reservoir makes refilling simple. It has been reliable, easy to clean, and consistently brews a great cup every single time.If you're looking for an affordable, dependable single-serve coffee maker that delivers great-tasting coffee and is simple to use, I highly recommend the Keurig K-Express. It has exceeded my expectations, and I couldn't be happier with my purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "First, an introduction, this will take some going through, bear with me. First, I had refused for years to get a Keurig, as I did not feel the quality and richness of a good strong cup of coffee was possible. But I finally got tired of trying other methods of brewing, from using a regular single cup espresso maker, moka pot, pour over, French press... I finally opted for the ease of a Keurig mini-plus. Coffee was ...eh... I switched coffee brands, to what I feel has to be the best commercial brand. And the coffee was EXcellenT! About a year later, despite regular cleaning cycles, the thing just stopped working. I tried to take it apart, watched some youtube videos which just solidified the fact that the company made these non-serviceable. P.O.'d at this obvious tactic to sell more, I waited a few weeks, but went and got another one. Same deal a year later. Another one. This last one gave me signs before ending it's own life. I would have to run several cycles where nothing would come out... till finally something... drip... by drip... several hours later, the thing would start running again, only to stop again the next day or two. Finally, it just died.So I REFUSED to get another. These things are ridiculous, right? So I got a new French press. Coffee is great!! But... omg... what a pain cleaning that thing every.... single... time... I mean, really, it's no big deal. But, it CAn be. So I saw this thing on sale, I thought, well, it's HAlf the price of the other ones... and I def want something different this time. Cut to now....This thing has SEVERAL issues that I don't like. First of all, it is a thinner cheaper plastic, and has a cheap looking shine to it. Ok, I'm over it. The plastic... I mean, can't they make these things with glass reservoirs.... the plastic reservoir has screws on the inside of it. I don't care if they say it is food safe... Plastic is also considered food safe... but that doesn't mean it is.. those are just bureaucratic rhetoric lies. But I digress,...So this coffee maker has an adjustment for high altitude... is THAT what ruined my previous Keurigs? High altitude? Hmmm. Ok, so maybe that's a plus. It also has different sizes that you can choose -8,10, & 12 oz. With the mini-plus, you choose the size by the amount of water you pour in. That means that this one measures what it sucks in. Hmmm. The mini-plus had the controls on the top. Easy peasy. This one has the controls on the side. It also doesn't have rubber feet on the bottom. So when you try to push the buttons, the thing slides away from you. Impossible to push any buttons with one hand, you have to use two. Even with rubber feet, you have to use two hands. I'm not a paraplegic, but it's rather stupid to have to hold the thing to press a button or two, or three. Which is what you have to do. It's just really awkward because you really have to hold it in the back to keep it from moving when you press the button in front. And you have to do that without touching the reservoir, which will pop out if you tried that.But let's get to the coffee. So with the mini-plus, the first liquid out of the machine, was dark coffee. As it was finishing, the coffee would be a little more clear, but not pure water. With this machine, for the first few seconds, it is spewing out crystal clear WATER. I don't even know how that is possible. But this, it does. It also claims to be faster than the mini-cup. I hestitate to say \"brews faster\", because it doesn't brew, Keurigs simply spew water into and through the k-cup, it's a pressurized system, not a true brewing system. And it definitely IS faster. And that's a problem, as evidenced by the watery coffee that it spews out. Sure enough, the \"coffee\" tastes like water. This is the 8 oz brew, mind you, with the machine set to \"strong\". I first tried the 12oz, and ended up pouring it down the sink. The 8 oz wasn't much better. My next step is to switch out cups while it's pouring out the water at the beginning of the cycle and see if I can get a stronger \"brew\".All in all, it's convenient enough. But it will sit on my counter, mostly unused, for when I have those really lazy, sleepy, or sick days, when all I want to do is pop in a capsule, and deal with the rest of it... Very disappointed. Perhaps if you live in a low altitude area, the mini-plus would work for you. I really do recommend that one above this."
    },
    {
        "review": "I loved this keurig for my family. It was perfect for my dsuggter, who had just started drinking mainly decaf coffee. Bought in Oct 2025, and it just stopped working after I cleaned it with descaling solution in June 2026. I had previously cleaned it earlier in the year without any issues. Not sure what went wrong. Not sure if I will buy another one. It was a good thing while it lasted."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the Keurig K-Express for a while now, and I’m very happy with it. It’s compact, stylish, and fits perfectly on my kitchen counter. The Warm Stone color looks modern and elegant.The coffee brews quickly, and I love the Strong Brew option because it gives my coffee a richer, bolder flavor. The 42 oz water reservoir is convenient since I can make several cups before needing to refill it. It’s incredibly easy to use and clean, making it perfect for busy mornings. If you’re looking for a reliable single-serve coffee maker that delivers great coffee every time, this is an excellent choice. I would definitely recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this to replace my original Keurig. The old k50 or whatever it was. This thing takes up less space, looks more sleek, and works better than the original. It's faster, the coffee tastes better, it has the strong button. Also, I keep my coffee maker in my bedroom, and with the old one if you wanted it to be ready to make a quick cup of coffee it had to be turned on which meant that it had lights illuminated. I had to cover them with tape. This new one can go from being turned off to making a quick cup of coffee immediately. And after 5 minutes it automatically turns any illumination off. That means it doesn't make light in my bedroom at night. It's just a way way better version. It's quieter. I love it I'm so glad I got it. I will say that I got this brand new, and it was a really good deal, and I can see why because the manual includes an offer for discounted coffee that expired over two years ago. I'm guessing Keurig punched out a few too many of these models and they've been sitting in a warehouse for too many years. My advice is buy it now before it goes out of stock. It is an excellent coffee maker."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been unable to use the item as the power plug does not meet Australian standards in fact when Itried to use the appliance it blew the electrical fuse making it in workable. As I purchased this in good faith not knowing I could not use it I would like to request a refund of the purchase price please"
    },
    {
        "review": "Not UK compatible. This is a US machine and is 110V! Shame on Amazon for selling this here."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very bad product, I used it for less than six months and it no longer works"
    },
    {
        "review": "This product is advertised on an Australian site in Australian dollars but I can’t connect it to 240 power even though I’ve tried two different adapters.  I will try to ring keurigs number tomorrow to see if I can get any satisfaction."
    },
    {
        "review": "I should have read the reviews before I bought the Keurig coffee maker.  The plug is for the USA and not UK.  I am just hoping that I do not have to pay to return the product.I returned the item 9 days ago and no sign of my refund. I will be insisting on a refund to return the item as it cost me £35 to return with Parcel Force, that was the cheapest option."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Love this coffee maker. The price was great and so easy to use. Easy to clean and coffee taste great. Replaced a former maker of the same model. Brew time great."
    },
    {
        "review": "It works and does exactly what I need it to do.  Brew Coffee.  What a concept.  And you don't need a Training Class on how to use it and how many buttons to push and program it.  I like my Coffee Strong and Hot, so I use enough coffee and a little less water.  And you turn it ON or OFF.  Amazing!!!  It's almost like it was designed to do that or something.  Good Job Mr. Coffee."
    },
    {
        "review": "Easy to use. Doesn't have a bunch of gadgets you have to figure out. Just a regular coffee maker. I'm happy with my purchase.  No k cups, no descaling, just makes coffee the old fashion way."
    },
    {
        "review": "For the past ten years I have been using this 12-cup Mr Coffee model.  I never turn it off... use it 24/7.  They last from six months to just over a year.  I have bought about ten, five through Amazon.  It used to be the switch would fail (even though never turned it off), but I replaced switches and would generally get well over a year from them.  Then, two of the machines (over the years) developed internal leaks, and I could not find the leaks from the bottom, but they were leaking.  Two or three of the machines had heating coil failures.  The price has continued to increase over the years, so I bought a 12-cup Black and Decker this time.  I have owned it two days and I like it fine.  The carafes are interchangeable with the Mr Coffee ones (I have a lot of those), so that's nice.  I already ordered my second Black and Decker, because the price is great and I hate being without my daily coffee (hot tea actually).  I throw two larger tea bags where the coffee filter and grounds go and make tea most of the time.  For the second pitcher I throw one more tea bag on top and so, get two pitchers from three tea bags... the tea bags cost $3.25 for 24 bags, so I get 16 12-cup pitchers of nice strong tea for $3.25."
    },
    {
        "review": "So in my humble opinion, coffee pots shouldn't be as expensive as some of them are.  Pour water over the coffee grounds and into a pot with a heating element under it.  With that being said I have seen some coffee pots run in the Easley over $100 range. Now okay I understand if you want to have a clock involved so it can start your coffee for you, that's fine and I'm sure that'll cost a couple extra dollars, and if you want something really nice and prestigious looking because you care what your guests think about what you've spent on random items then yeah drop a hundred bucks on a nice one maybe it's stainless steel or something and has a good company logo on the front of it.Personally, I'm not that difficult. I get up in the morning I push the button on this thing and by the time I get out of the shower I've got a nice hot pot of coffee waiting for me and life is good. The only thing I wish this had and this is only because my previous pot did have this option is that if you don't turn this off it'll just stay on all day and you really don't want to cook that empty pot all day.  There is a light on the button so if you're leaving the house and the light is still on yeah you might want to shut this off. And honestly after a couple weeks I got into the habit of making sure I shut it off as I picked up the pot to pour my coffee so it hasn't really been an issue, it was only a problem for a week or two because like I said my previous pot automatically shut off so I got lazy and just let it do its thing.  So anyway, if you're just looking for something to make your coffee, and you don't really want to spend $50 or $100, I've had this for quite a while now and it works great. I do have well water which has a lot of extra minerals and crap in it so I do find myself doing a 50% vinegar solution which you pretty much need to do with any coffee pot from time to time but in my case a little more often... And other than that, I expect this thing's going to last me a few more years."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good coffee pot. All the others are iffy. Good for the price tho it’s gigher"
    },
    {
        "review": "So simple to use. I didn't want a programmable coffeemaker (don't need bells and whistles). Just a simple on/off switch. The coffeemaker is lightweight (don't need it to be heavy), and easy to move around the countertop. Pull away from the wall when making coffee, put back against the wall when done.  It's a space saver for me. Easy to clean. And it brews good coffee. And of course most of all, good coffee comes from great brands of coffee beans. Hey people: buy beans from a really good company, don't compromise or settle for less!!! Only downside of this coffeemaker is that the basket has a flat bottom instead of coned-shaped, but that is a minor issue I think with this coffeemaker, so I still rated it with 5 stars. Thank you Mr. Coffee."
    },
    {
        "review": "*** updated 1/16/2021***It’s been a few weeks.  I tried one more time but the flavor is still there.  Maybe it’ll go away but I had also purchased a pitcher that boils watet for tea and it’s great with a. French press we had that I forgot to use.  This product I declare as junk for me and regret the purchase thus rating it a one star.  I no longer have incentive to try again so it’s unlikely I’ll come back for another updated review.********I’m going to start this review off by talking about filters.  There are cone filters and then there are flimsy filters.  Until I went back to these flimsy filters, I never fully appreciated the cone filters and this will impact future machine purchases for me.Cone filters pack flat meaning storage is less invasive.  The hood their shape and are less likely to spill and the won’t collapse when transferring to compost or garbage. It’s a little thing but I appreciate it.So, the point of all this, is that mr coffee uses the flimsy filters.  Surprisingly there are a lot of machines that don’t use the cones, which is disappointing.First impressions:The plastic look and felt cheap.  I saw reviews that commented about the cheapness of this machine and shrugged it off.  Other machines are made of plastic after all.  This plastic looks and feels somehow cheaper.  I instantly had a negative association to it.The side windows which advertised visibility from both points was a selling point for me.  What was failed to be mentioned is that you can’t read the clear numbers when contrasted against a black background or steam.  I wrote the marks in with permanent marker to be able to see when filling.One feature I did like is that the spout moves out of the way and the lid snaps it back into place.  Simple and elegant engineering.  I would never clean these grounds out when hot though.  Recipe for spilt grounds and burns.The prepIt requires a washing and a single run to remove the plastic flavor, per instructions.  I ran 4 times after I washed and before the first use.  The plastic smell seemed gone.The usageThe first cup seemed fine.  Additional uses the plastic taste and smell crept in strongly.  I ran a cleanse through it four more times and it’s still there rendering expensive coffee undrinkable.My wife felt like the first coffee had a weird flavor, so maybe I didn’t notice the first time?  The fact we have flushed this so many times and the flavor persists is deeply concerning to me.  I’ve owned a few coffee machines and never had this issue persist for so long.  I’m going to keep trying and if something changes, I’ll update.  I’d like this to be a good machine for me, but it’s not.The water heats quickly!  This is a lot faster than my older coffee makers!The lighted switch is more subtle than I’d like.  It’s a dot vs the entire switch, but in the end my wife and I turn it off after the last cup and it’s not an issue as we both stay at home now.  There is no auto shut off.The drip stop works okay.  A few drips will come out if you pull early, but it does stop while you pour a cup.  A critical feature for my wife.The carafe pours well at an okay speed without dripping down the side.  Some will leak if overly full and you have to pour slooooowly to avoid spillage.  This seems better designed.This steams a lot and should not be under a cabinet when running.  It WILL damage the  cabinets.  It’s easy to pull out and push back in.The summary:Would I purchase again?  No.  Even if the flavor fixes itself, I have concerns about the cheapness of this machine and the plastic used and the health impact.  I couldn’t find anywhere that discussed if it was bpa free.  I hadn’t been concerned because sunbeam owns me coffee, but after seeing and feeling the cheapness of the plastic, and with the plastic taste still present, I’m concerned.It is cheap, the functionality seems good for just a weeks ownership, but the lack of drinkable coffee is an issue.  Even if that’s resolved, there’s concern in the back of my mind about the long term health impact of this machine.Hopefully this is helpful.  I’d recommend spending more money as I feel I wasted $28 and will be purchasing a new coffee maker, again."
    },
    {
        "review": "It works well, it's pretty."
    },
    {
        "review": "Until today working well"
    },
    {
        "review": "The coffee maker is not heating the coffee sufficiently. I've always liked this brand, but this machine isn't working properly."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent product. It complies with what it mentions, we have been looking for this brand in the city where we live and no one sells it so we decided to order it online and the whole family is happy with it. It arrived even earlier than expected."
    },
    {
        "review": "If it worked properly the coffee machine wouldn't be that bad. It is bulky, made of cheap plastic, unattractive, but it does the job for the most part. Condensation builds up on the underside of the cover which spills onto the counter every time you open it. There are no features, just an on and off switch, which you'd think is fine for the price but even other coffee makers at the same price have several features.That being said, the first one I got leaked from the bottom. Every time I made coffee there would be a pool of water on the counter. I asked for a replacement, which I got. This one worked for about a month and then the switch started coming loose, and then stopped working entirely. I asked reported the problem and they offered me yet another replacement, to which I was skeptical but accepted. Then after waiting for over a month I wrote back asking for a refund instead of a replacement, which they said they would do. Two more months went by without a refund so I ping them, now they're saying they want me to send in the last defective machine to get a refund.If you're looking for a cheap, straightforward coffee maker, get a different one. For $40 you expect something cheap and simple that will work, not to have to deal with awful customer service for months. Not only that but like I said, in the $40 price range there are better machines  out there. I should also mention that the customer service was directly from Mr. Coffee, not Amazon."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I bought this exact coffee maker about 3 months ago and I haven’t had any issues or problems with it so I decided to get a second one for my vacation home. The coffee maker is compact and looks nice on my counter. The instruction manual has straightforward step by step instructions for first time use and for normal coffee brewing. However, there are a couple of things in the instruction manual that I disagree with. First, it says “the appliance can be used by children 8 years old and above if they’ve been given supervision or instruction.” I can’t imagine letting my 8 year old grandson use my coffee maker or why I would want him to. Also, it says you should unplug and thoroughly clean all parts of the coffee maker daily. That’s probably a good thing to do but I have only been cleaning mine periodically. And for clarification, #3 under Normal Brewing says to use one level spoon of coffee for each cup. This should say one level Tablespoon for each cup of coffee. Other than those things I found the instruction manual to be helpful and clear.The coffee maker has all the common features found in coffee makers. It can be programmed to go on automatically at a specified time which is convenient for people who work or are in a hurry in the morning. We tried this function and it was easy to do, however, since we are retired we like to prepare the coffee the night before but then press the on/off button when we get up in the morning. The coffee maker has a pause and serve function so you can grab a cup of coffee before the brewing stops. It also has an automatic shut off that turns the coffee maker off two hours after it was turned on. I find this feature to be very important because I often forget to turn it off. There are two other features on this coffee pot that I really like. First, it has a button to make the coffee a little stronger. You just press the “strength” button and a little coffee bean symbol shows up under the time. This slows down the drip and gives the coffee a bolder flavor without making it bitter or too strong. The second thing that I really like is that this machine makes HOT coffee which is the way I like it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Been hearing the Jeffersons theme song in my head with this thing, because I feel like I'm Movin' On Up, To The East Side. I've been drinking instant, or pour over, or percolator, campfire, etc. And one cup at a time. This one is a tad pricey, but it pays for itself over time, compared to how I normally drink it, for sure. And it negates the need for filters, so you save on those. Definitely comes out cheaper in the long run, compared to instant. Tickled pink to be able to make 10 cups at a time and keep it hot, instead of one cup at a time, and having to reheat it. With this, I can just top it up and make it hot again. So luxurious and timesaving.Love the rich setting for making it stronger. Puts hair on your chest, like I need any more of that. LoL.Love that it stops dripping while you pour a cup! That feature is to die for, because sometimes you really need that first cup, and it's not done brewing, so you make a mess. Not now.Also great to have a digital clock to look at if I don't have my watch or phone, or it's quicker to look at the coffee maker.Built well, works well. Again, price is slightly stiff, but it also holds up its end of the bargain in performance and features. Have to call it a Win."
    },
    {
        "review": "Sometimes I want a whole pot of coffee and not just 1 cup so this works great for me.  It is very asthetic looking and goes very will with my Stainless Steel and Black Kitchen appliances.  I really like that this coffee maker is programmable and I can set the time that I want it to brew my coffee so that when I get up in the morning my coffee is waiting on me instead of me waiting on my coffee to brew.  This has a \"strength\" feature to it and I couldn't really tell much difference in taste but I already use a very dark - strong french roast to begin with.  The touch controls on this are very sensitive and just the slightest touch of the buttons will change the time or the programming so be careful with that.  I set it for 10 cups and I get 10 cups, not 8 or 9 cups but actually 10 cups so that is great.  The price really makes this a good value too.  I really like how well this coffee maker works."
    },
    {
        "review": "This coffeemaker is great.  I have (and LOVE) a french press, Nespresso and Keurig machines but sometimes you just want to brew a pot of coffee for company without a bunch of steps.I appreciate that the functions are so simple.  The “strong” feature is probably my favorite, as I appreciate strong black coffee.  This delivers a solid cup without any bitterness or burnt taste.  The mesh reusable filter is great, you may or may not feel the need to line it depending on the type of grounds you’re using.  But it’s nice to have that built in without a need to constantly go buy filters.The programmable functions are simple too.  I always try to test things first without reading the manual since let’s be real, that’s how I roll when I open an amazon package…and while I went back to review everything, it was very intuitive to use without doing any reading at all.This is a solid, basic machine that feels well built and has just the functions I need without a bunch of complicated options I don’t want.  Definitely worth the money in my opinion!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a no name brand 10 cup coffee maker, and it’s great. The price is so reasonable for all the useful features. It is very modern looking with black and stainless steel accents. The coffee pot is large enough for 10 cups of coffee, and has a pause and serve feature, which is great for people like me who have no patience when a pot of coffee is brewing and I need a cup asap. You can also program the coffee maker to set it up and have it turned on automatically, that is great for the mornings or if you are having a party and don’t want to think about setting up the coffee pot. One feature which was so unexpected was the adjustable brew strength, I never thought of that before, but I have to admit, I really appreciate having it. What a difference it makes with my brew. I am really impressed with this. It is perfect to keep as an extra, use in a vacation home or for everyday use. This coffee maker works really well, is a good compact size while brewing a full 10 cups, and is a reasonable price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Stay away!!! I ordered this machine because I have limited space. It made OK coffee but it broke within two months. Since the coffee pot is made and sold via a Chinese company, there is no customer service and I guess no warranty either. I went to their website but the contact information tab doesn’t display contact info. I went to the Amazon online store and again no contact information. Shame on Amazon for associating with such a vendor."
    },
    {
        "review": "This 10-cup programmable coffee maker is a solid option for everyday home or office use. I like the adjustable brew strength, which makes it easy to customize the coffee depending on my preference. The programmable timer is convenient for having coffee ready when needed, and the pause-and-serve feature is useful when you don’t want to wait for the entire pot to finish. The permanent filter is another nice touch since there’s no need to constantly buy paper filters.The stainless-steel design looks clean and fits nicely on the counter without taking up too much space. The glass carafe is easy to monitor, although it does require some care to avoid accidental damage.My main complaint is that some of the controls and settings take a little getting used to, and the carafe could be easier to pour without occasional dripping.Overall, it’s a capable and convenient coffee maker with useful features at a reasonable value."
    },
    {
        "review": "This coffee maker is really nice and easy to use. It comes with a reusable filter so no need to spend extra money on disposable filters. Another really nice feature is the adjustable brew strength that offers a personalized brew of either regular or strong. The look of the machine is nice and I like the buttonless/touch screen feature. This was a great price for such a nice drip coffee machine."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Arrived so quickly.  It arrived 2-3 hours after i ordered it which was great because my current coffee maker suddenly quit working that same morning.  It was a Mr. Coffee 12-cup that lasted for 13 years so I figured that i got my money's worth.  So I thought I would go with Mr. Coffee brand again.Anyway, this time I decided to try the 5-cup because I no longer need a 12-cup as I now live alone.  I've only had it for 3 days but so far I love it.  It works great.  I don't like warm coffee and this little coffee makes makes hot coffee, but not too hot to burn you.  It stays hot until you turn it off.  It is not programmable but that is not a feature that I'm crazy about anyway.  The handle on the carafe isn't too small, just the right size.  The carafe has a wide opening which makes it easy to clean and the glass carafe is just the same glass as a 12-cup, only smaller. The basket uses the 7\" filters which I was already using in my old unit so I didn't have to buy new ones.  I don't like the cone filters and I'm glad this one doesn't require them.  I especially like that it doesn't take up as much counter space because I have a small kitchen and don't have much counter space to spare.It doesn't brew as fast as a large coffee maker but that is no problem for me.  I turn it on when I get up, then go get dressed.  By the time i get back to the kitchen, it is finished.  It does have the pause feature if you are in a hurry.  So far, I'm very pleased with this little coffee maker and don't share any of the negative reviews.  I did run plain water through the unit before making my first pot of coffee to clean it through and through. There was no bad plastic smell, no smell of any kind, and no bad taste of any kind from my first brew of coffee as others have mentioned.  I don't grind my own coffee beans but I use Folgers pre-ground coffee, so i don't know anything about grinding your own beans and how this would be any different.  i know some people are really picky about that kind of stuff, but I am not.  I am more concerned about convenience.  If you like stronger coffee, just add more grounds or less water, or both as there is no adjustment on this unit to make the coffee stronger or weaker.As I have only had it for 3 days, I don't know anything about the lifespan of this unit, but so far, I am very pleased and loving the little coffee maker.  I will update the review if it doesn't last long.It is perfect for small kitchens, dorm rooms, etc., and is very light wright.  It looks just like a 12-cup coffee maker, only smaller, without lots of bells and whistles- just a basic coffee maker.  ( I've had 2 Keurigs in the past and neither one lasted more than a year- too expensive to keep replacing every year.  I won't buy anymore of those)  This little unit is perfect for me.  Glad I found it and hope it last a long time."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought a 5 cup mini brew coffee maker to use for travel a few years ago. I remember it produced a pretty good tasting coffee. I broke the carafe and wasn’t sure whether to replace it or not but I’m glad I did. Again this one works pretty well even though there’s no bells and whistles for this coffee maker. Makes as good a cup of coffee as my more expensive coffee maker."
    },
    {
        "review": "For a long time I've searched for Mr. Coffee's 4 cup coffee maker but all I've found here and on eBay is one that's not used. That one is at a ridiculous price when you add in a highway-robbery price for delivery. What would show up in my searches on Amazon was this 5 cup version. I had resisted buying it for about a year, but finally ordered it a few nights ago -- then promptly cancelled the order because some reviews made me think I wouldn't like it. Fast-forward to last night shortly before midnight. I decided to give this maker a chance to prove it was worth buying, so I hit the buy button. It was here, waiting for me when I woke up today.I love it. The design differences between this model and the 4 cup one were things I thought I would hate, but I don't. Really, I have only one quibble. The filters don't fit nicely in the filter holder, but that doesn't affect how they perform. Over time I may be disappointed if the pot's lid gets coffee stains on it. Cleaning this 5 cup model is easier than the 4 cup one is. That's because my hand fits more easily in the pot for drying it, thanks to the bigger size. I also like the finish on this model. It's mostly a matte white which will go with the matte white toaster oven I'll be receiving tomorrow.I also like the on/off switch that is on both models. I use an Echo smart plug that I can turn on via my voice as soon as I wake up: \"Alexa, turn on coffee.\" The switch is always in the on position but the plug is off until I tell Alexa to turn on the coffee. When the maker is on, I appreciate the fact there is not automatic shut off after a certain length of time, like there is with other coffee makers. When having two mugs of coffee, I often don't get around to drinking the second mug till an hour or more later. I want it to be hot when I'm ready for it. Reheating coffee in the microwave is not the same as having the pot on the heat. There's a scientific reason for this.Now about the coffee: it tastes great with both models. I think it takes the 5 cup model longer to make the coffee but it's really not an issue. I will never brew 5 cups. Most often, I will use the 2-cup setting with 3 scoops of coffee. I like it strong. Someone needs to let Mr. Coffee know they are lousy at measuring cup sizes. My mug (which looks bigger in the photo than it actually is) holds 11 ounces. The 2 cup setting delivers a little less than 11 ounces. I think Mr. Coffee uses the usual cup size other coffee makers do: just 6 ounces per cup (not the expected 8 ounces for those of us who use a regular measuring cup for our cooking needs). But the 2 cup setting gives me less than 12 ounces. It's closer to 10.5 ounces. I doubt I'll ever use more than the 4 cup setting which will give me two mugs of coffee.The pot is easier to pour from versus the 4 cup version. Getting the last little bit out of the 4 cup version is difficult, but super easy with the 5 cup version.It's obvious I love this 5 cup model. I hope Mr. Coffee won't stop making it in the future like they did with the 4 cup version. When I need a new coffee maker, I want this model to be here, ready and waiting for me to hit the buy button again.UPDATE: After using the coffee maker for a while I noticed the lid on the pot has a faint stain that I can't wash off. I expect it to get worse over time so I ordered the black version so I could use the black pot in my white coffee maker (see photo). I know it'll get stained too, but I won't be able to see it. Totally worth it. I'm adding two photos to show how it looks if you want to avoid the coffee stains. You can just use the black pot or you can adapt the white pot to accomplish the same thing. Just remove the just the white lid and snap the black lid into the white pot. Photos show what I mean, I hope. This white pot/black lid is what I'm happiest with."
    },
    {
        "review": "My mother loves the wide mouth cup. Much easier for her to clean thoroughly, the way she likes. It brews coffee quickly and she loves it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this for my elderly aunt who’s 87 and still lives alone. She doesn’t like newer technology with too many settings and options. She just wanted a simple small coffee pot that would make body for her each day and this one works great and is very affordable. The only thing is it uses the smaller coffee filters so you’ll need to get some of those. However if you have regular ones they’ll fit you just have to kinda smash them in or cut them. Amazon sells a big pack of the smaller filters for like $3 or less so it’s worth it if you just need a small simple coffee pot"
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been a Mr. Coffee user for 40 years. I love the 4 cup makers. This is the second time since Feb. 2025 that the coffee maker has stopped working. The first time 7 months into using it, it was replaced. So what to do this time. I am 10 months into using the replacement item. It makes great coffee and makes sense for a one-person user that's why I gave it 5 stars. BUT, it is a disaster in terms of longevity. What has happened to the quality of the product.  QUALITY of things has gone down with the coffee maker."
    },
    {
        "review": "Sitting here with my fresh brewed coffee from my new Mr. Coffee maker. Since I'm the only one in the family that likes coffee, this mini brewer is great for two cups. It's a simple machine that does not have all the frills like a 12 cup maker i.e. no timer, smaller carafe, small size, no automatic off heating plate. BUT for two quick cups of good brewed coffee, it's perfect."
    },
    {
        "review": "Finally, after FOUR unsuccessful attempts, I found something decent.For the last three months, I have ordered THREE 5-cup coffee makers for my small apt that did not work out.- The first I had to cancel b/c it was never shipped after 2 weeks.- Next one, the timer did not work!- Another one, the plug would not dislodge from the back of the unit's plastic housing - I tried pliers, etc but the damn thing was stuck INSIDE the small compartment and at risk of being completely ripped off if I kept trying.- And then the final one - the glass carafe was as THIN as a light bulb that it broke when trying to gently wash it!This Mr Coffee model is probably not the best for consumers expecting \"luxury\" quality for such a low price, but it brews, pours, and stays hot with no issue. AND the glass carafe is MUCH thicker and less \"delicate\" when handling it. The only star left off is that you need to be more careful of how you position the paper filter and the overhead spout that shoots water into it - If done the wrong way, the paper filter may fold at one side, thus leaving grinds on the bottom.STILL at this price, and for my needs, go with the old goat of MR COFFEE - just like mom used."
    },
    {
        "review": "I already knew the product and it met expectations"
    },
    {
        "review": "The latest update of my 5 star review I wrote 2 months ago is unfortunately down to 0 if I could give a zero star because the coffee maker just stopped working on the day when the so called return window closed! So basically the machine lasted for 2 months. On top of that a customer service agent on Amazon lied to me that I will receive a refund in 24 hours but I got no email stating that the refund was made so I wasted my time and money with the machine and the customer service agent. Avoid this seller!*******************************It is super simple, easy to operate reusable filter coffee maker that turned to be my best purchase! It makes up to 4 cups of coffee for less than 2 minutes and you just wash the filter under a rinsing water and ready you are for your next tasty cup of coffee! The only disadvantage is that the seller doesn't say you need to buy the reusable filter separately which was a bad aurptice for me expecting the filter to be included in my coffee maker purchase. This caused me to have my coffee maker unusable for 3 weeks at home while I was waiting for the filter to come by another seller. Once you have them joined, you can enjoy your coffee time."
    },
    {
        "review": "Simply perfect and the ideal size, I can take it on a trip without a problem."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great coffee maker just failed to mention its different voltage to UKNeeded to by a US To UK voltage converter hence 4 stars"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the Keurig K-Mini Mate for about three months now, and it has quickly become one of the most practical additions to my morning routine. Living in a condo with limited counter space, I was hesitant to buy a bulky coffee maker. The K-Mini Mate solved that problem instantly. It is remarkably compact—less than five inches wide—meaning it slips effortlessly into tight corners without cluttering the kitchen.Despite its small footprint, the machine delivers exactly what you need from an everyday single-serve brewer. The operation - EASY TO USE. You pour water into the rear reservoir, drop in your favorite K-Cup pod or one of those reusable pods - place your mug on the drip tray, and press the brew button. Within a couple of minutes, you have a fresh, piping hot cup of coffee ready to go. If you remove the drip tray at the bottom, it fits a full 7-inch travel mug with ease.In terms of performance, the temperature of the coffee is consistently hot, and the flavor extraction is great for a pod system. It brews relatively quietly compared to older Keurig models I have used in the past, which is a huge plus if you are waking up earlier than the rest of the household. I also appreciate the automatic off feature, which shuts the machine down 90 seconds after your last brew. It is a subtle touch, but it gives me peace of mind knowing I will not accidentally leave it running all day.Cleaning and maintenance are as straightforward as it gets. The removable drip tray catches any accidental overflow or drips and washes easily in the sink. Because you pour fresh water in for every single cup rather than keeping a large standing water tank, the water always tastes fresh, and there is less worry about stagnant water sitting in the reservoir overnight."
    },
    {
        "review": "I chose the glamping green because it’s for my camper. This thing is small and convenient. My husband is the only one that drinks coffee and occasionally a friend or two when they go with us This fits perfectly under the bench of my pop-up trailer and works well with my solar generator. I did put this in a case for storage and protection of the unit. Got a really good deal on it would highly recommend. It does come out really hot quickly. Easy to clean up as it does get a little messy from the splash off coffee"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this after our old single serve Keurig broke after many years.  I love the convenience of the size and how easy it is to use.  The old one had a little learning curve to it but this one is user friendly.  We use it when we travel since I drink tea or decaff coffee and my husband drinks caffeinated coffee.  We bring our own K-cups so we can both have what we prefer, and it doesn't take up much room in the baggage."
    },
    {
        "review": "We bought this to replace our dinosaur Keurig. We had the OG silver, bulky, heavy Keurig. It lasted us a lifetime then died a sudden death. We actually mourned! We have a camper now so I bought this new mini to be a space saver. I like it. I don’t love it yet but I like it. It’s small, lightweight and does the job. It splatters quite a bit, so we drape a lightweight kitchen rag over it while it brews. I’ve also noticed it doesn’t push out all the water every brew. After each brew we immediately remove the pod and toss it. Then randomly I open it later and find the pod area filled with water. Where does this water come from?? Tapping the brew button forces that water to be purged but I have to know why it’s there! It never seems like our cup of coffee is lacking a couple tablespoons so I just don’t know. Maybe a small bit is held back each brew until it creates enough to send it to the pod area. I’m perplexed. Also, if I brew plain water for tea after we have brewed coffee, I have to flush it out with 2 cycles of water or my tea is yucky, ashtray smelling tea. It really clings to that coffee smell!! That being said, love the size and weight, it brews really hot, pretty darn fast and the color is cute. So, 4 stars."
    },
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love this Keurig K-Mini coffee maker. I never thought I'd resort to such a small coffee maker but I am so happy I did. It is so compact and makes the coffee so quickly. I needed the counter space so I thought I'd give it a try and I am beyond happy I did. I love the Green color as well. As a senior citizen I find it so easy to use and with my old fingers ( ha ) it's just perfect."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this for travel and I have also put it on my coffee bar since it takes up so little space.Pros: Small size, quiet operation, and quick coffee!Cons: Cup height is limited so travel cups might not work; the My K-Cup filter insert is not included and only one Keurig brand model fits. That one model is: https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FN6NKZGT?ref=ppx_pop_mob_ap_share***This was so compact for travel (hate to use those dirty nasty ones in hotel rooms) that I was able to fit it and some k cups into a small/medium Vera Bradley tote bag.***I recommend this coffee maker for travel or home and it’s darn cute!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "It's convenient. Works perfectly. Right coffee temperature, is small and lightweight, but well made; sturdy material. Brews coffee fine. Shockingly quiet. Leaves a little splatter but it's easy to wipe. Really cute color!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very nice, I like it that it is small. It doesn’t take up a lot of space. And it works as good  the larger ones. Yes, I would buy it again and I love the green color. Heats up really fast."
