[
    {
        "review": "I really like the versatility of this Coffee Maker. Some mornings I want to brew a full pot, while other times I only need one cup, so having both options in one machine is extremely convenient. It also saves me from having two different coffee makers taking up counter space.The 12-cup glass carafe is a great size when making coffee for more than one or when I know I’ll want a second cup. For those times when I just want something quick, the single-serve side is exactly what I need. I also appreciate being able to make either hot or iced coffee depending on what I’m in the mood for.The coffee comes out nicely brewed and flavorful. The Auto Pause & Pour feature is another small convenience that I use more than I expected—it’s nice to be able to grab a cup before the entire pot has finished brewing.The controls are straightforward, and I like the clean black finish. Even though it offers two brewing options, the overall design is practical and doesn’t feel unnecessarily complicated.For me, the biggest selling point is simply choice: a full 12-cup pot when I need it, a single cup when I don’t, and the option for hot or iced coffee. ALSO - NO K-CUPS needed!  Just use your favorite coffee for a single cup. It’s a very practical everyday coffee maker and a good option for a household where everyone doesn’t necessarily drink coffee at the same time.  The only thing I do wish this machine had was the ability to use a K-cup instead of ground coffee for the single-serve.  But, this is not a deal-breaker since this machine offers so much more."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love the color, it goes with my kitchen machine. After cleaning I immediately tried out the single coffee maker and it works great. It is a bit on the slower side, than what I'm used to and I'm still experimenting with the amount of coffee, but I made a tasty cup of coffee and ice coffee. I love that I can program my morning coffee again. It is very easy to use.The only thing I wish was different, I would have liked to have a removable water tank. I have to pour the water from my water filter into a measuring cup and then pour it into the machine, otherwise I make a mess. Filters are easy to clean and I appreciate being able to change between mild, bold, and ice coffee.I just hope this machine will last longer than my last 3 machines!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Our Ninja coffee maker was great but dying.  Really tired of spending $125+ for this small appliance that only lasts two years or so….we’ve replaced a lot of coffee makers!I’d been looking at this unit but when the price notably dropped during Prime Days, that was it!  Still, I didn’t have high hopes for this inexpensive unit.  No clue about its lifespan (yet), but so far I LOVE IT!There are two downsides: it brews slooooooow on both sides, pot or cup.  The other is a common issue—aiming water in the lid opening is rough if there are cabinets overhead.  Even without cabinets the fill area is rather small and awkward (coming from a Ninja with a separate water tank).Upside is everything else is awesome!  Brews VERY hot….like a $600 coffee maker a coffee master would buy.  Coffee tastes excellent from extruding at 200+ degrees using the “bold” setting, and the warming pad keeps it very hot!  Ninja didn’t come close.  Controls are super easy to use, looks beautiful and more expensive than it is, carafe pours beautifully without the drips at the end, delay timer and “stop dispensing to grab a cup” features are perfect.If you’re in the market for a coffee maker and you don’t require flashy manufacturing labels or endless brewing options—this is the unit!!  Buy it!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this as a Christmas Present for my mom as she was in need of a new coffee machine.After researching I chose this one and I’m glad I did,it’s easy to use and set up,I like and she also likes the separate 2 way coffee maker,it’s easy to clean and it’s not a big hassle either which is great! It can brew quickly compared to other past coffee makers we’ve had,it stays hot.i also like the idea that you can put a travel mug on the tray on the other side while getting ready for work or just going out and needing a cup of coffee on the go.the tray is removable to give a bit more room to fit a slightly taller travel coffee mug.I do wish that the tray area had a bit more height and width to be a bit more versatile with different size coffee mugs as my moms one coffee mug is too tall and to wide but other than that I’d say it’s pretty compatible with something a bit smaller. I’d definitely recommend this machine! And will consider buying other products from this company"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this one to replace my single serve Keurig.I wanted all three options that this one provides.The timer is so nice so that I have coffee when I wake up in the coffee pot.It stays warm for a couple of hours and then turns off.  This makes me feel good about not burning the house down with my forgetfulness.You can brew 12 cups!The single serve side  causes some splashing and I’m not sure why but I just wipe off the maker  anyway.It’s made well.It comes with a reusable mesh pod like thing to make single serves.  I ordered a mesh basket that fits in this for the pot side also.I like them better than paper filters or plastic.The coffee isn’t brewed aa fast as a Keurig. On either side but that’s ok because it’s delicious and it works.The only thing I dislike is that the pot isn’t the easiest to wash.It’s very easy to use and set the timers and click too.I do recommend this coffee pot.  Ita nice."
    },
    {
        "review": "I don't love this coffee maker. The burner is way too hot so if coffee is brewed and in the pot on the burner for longer than 15-20 minutes, it's so hot it will burn me. I have to leave for work and take the lid off my coffee in the car before I can even drink it. Not ideal obviously. And when there's a cup or two left on the burner, it burns in the pot and smells and tastes like nasty gas station coffee, so it's undrinkable and wasted.Also, when you pour water in using the caraffe, it doesn't just drip, it gushes out no matter how slow/fast or what the pouring angle is.  I have to pour it into the machine with a towel on the counter. The single cup brewing is the part I like. I haven't tried iced coffee yet, but the instructions basically have you brewing normal coffee into a cup or the caraffe with ice in it. I guess the burner turns off for that part. It would be a really great machine without the overheating and dripping issues and now I've spend $100 buck on it and can't justify getting a new one so here we are."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love my coffee pot! Works great love the color. My coffee taste good. Love how I can make both a cup and a pot. Brew speed for a pot isn’t too bad and  cup take about 3-4 minutes but both are very hot. I did buy reusable filter to use with it. I also bought a metal measuring cup to pour water in single serve so it won’t go everywhere while filing it. I’ve been using for a few weeks and so far love the versatility of it. I am coming from a Nespresso pop plus, I just wanted regular coffee without buying pods. Love I don’t need them with the single serve side."
    },
    {
        "review": "Overall, I really like this coffee maker. It does have a couple of quirks though.One thing I didn't see talked about in any of the reviews I read before buying was that this has two separate water reservoirs. If you fill water from the opening at the front of the maker, you're filling the single cup portion first, and then the excess goes into the main tank for brewing a pot. I find this to be the easier place to fill it using, but that also means that you always have water in the reservoir for the single cup. I'm not a huge fan of that. It also means that if you decide you want a smaller single cup later, there's no way to remove any of the water that you've already put in. So, you're always going to get a full sized cup.The single cup function is great and really convenient though, and I find myself using it more often than I expected. The mesh filter is really handy but you will always end up with some really fine grinds on the bottom of the cup. This isn't a problem for me, but some people may feel sick if they drink this portion of the coffee.The iced coffee function is nice to have, but makes really weak coffee. Typically, to make iced coffee, you would leave the grinds soaking in cold water for several hours. So, this is a quick way to get room temperature coffee, but it's not great and melting ice will only further weaken it. Also, if the machine drips at all after you've taken the cup off, it falls into a small pool under the cup holder. It's nice that it's there, but would have been better if there was something you could remove to rinse out instead of just being part of the unit itself.I also wish that it was possible to adjust how long the hot plate stays on for. It doesn't go off for four hours, and that's just way too long to leave coffee sitting.The carafe is pretty decent. It doesn't stain easily, which is always nice. But it isn't great at getting all of the water out when pouring, even if turned completely upside down. Not a huge deal, but it's not what I'm used to. There also seems to be something about the way the brewer and carafe line up that always causes a few drops of coffee to fall from the machine after you've taken the carafe off, falling onto the hot plate. I find myself having to clean it off way more often than I should.Overall though, it's a very solid machine that does a good job making coffee. It's easy to use and although I have mixed feelings about all of the additional functions, they're nice to have in something around this price point. I'm happy with the purchase overall."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent coffee maker works very well, plus the feature of preparing a single cup is the best"
    },
    {
        "review": "A super coffee maker, it makes excellent coffee, there is no burnt taste, it uses all the powder due to the \"shower\" water distribution system. Reinforced, robust vase. I recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Carafe and K-cup duo coffee maker. Works well but you have to be careful when selecting the carafe or 1 cup!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Good purchase"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’ve been really happy with the Keurig K-Elite. It’s one of those appliances that does exactly what I need it to do without making my morning more complicated.It heats up quickly, is easy to use, and I really like having several cup-size options depending on how much coffee I want. The Strong Brew setting is probably my favorite feature because I prefer a bolder cup, and it actually makes a noticeable difference. The large water reservoir is another big plus since I’m not constantly having to refill it.I also appreciate that it gives you more control than a basic single-serve machine while still keeping everything convenient. The controls are straightforward, cleanup is easy, and it consistently makes a good cup of coffee.If you like the convenience of K-Cups but want a machine with a few more useful features than the basic models, the K-Elite is a solid choice. I use mine regularly and would definitely buy it again."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve always gotten keurig products from Costco, but I needed a new one because the other one I had for like 4 years broke down on me. The product never fails me and it’s seriously my go to product. The reservoir has enough water to do two rounds of coffee and it’s easy to use. Can’t go wrong with it"
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased this Keurig K-Elite for my daughter, but I have been using it too, so I’ve had a chance to try the main features myself. We purchased it recently, and it has already been a great buy. I have used Keurig machines for years, and this one has a couple of features that really make it stand out.What I like:• The iced coffee feature works really well• It makes better iced coffee than just brewing a regular K-cup over ice• The iced setting seems to get the strength and ratio right so it does not taste watered down• Works with regular K-cups for iced coffee• Hot water on demand is very useful• Great for tea, oatmeal, hot cocoa mixes, and other hot drinks• Easy to set up• Directions were easy to understand• Brews regular K-cups nicely too• I like the variety of cup sizes• The water reservoir size is convenient without making the machine too bulky• Feels quieter than other Keurigs I have used• Fits nicely on the countertopThings to be aware of:• It is quieter than some other Keurigs, but it is not completely silent• It still makes some normal brewing and heating sounds• If placing it under cabinets, remember the handle needs extra clearance when opened• I do recommend keeping up with descaling because I think it helps with both taste and machine longevity• We use our Keurigs heavily, and while none have lasted forever for us, we keep coming back to the brandOverall:This is a great Keurig, and the iced coffee and hot water features are what make it feel special. It is easy to use, brews well, and has features I would really miss now."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love the K-Elite Keurig coffee  I would say this is my third one after many years. They seem to last me about three years. This one is identical to the previous ones that I’ve owned, however there’s one function that I do not like. The power button will not stay on. I have read that this is a new function of the Keurig machines to save energy. It turns off after a short time of brewing, your 1st cup of coffee. When I go back for my 2nd cup, I have to restart the machine and wait for the water to heat. Otherwise, I love the Machine and have actually used the iced coffee which I never used on my previous machine."
    },
    {
        "review": "Keurig is always a good machine. I bought this K-Elite model to replace my old classic model with 48 ounce reservoir mainly because of the larger 75 ounce reservoir so I wouldn’t need to refill as often. However, I’m having to refill just as much as often as because when the water level decreases to near half way it’ll stop and say Add Water. At least on the old one it wouldn’t do that until it was nearly empty. It brews to 4 different sizes but the coffee is watered down too much if you select the larger sizes; so it defeats the purpose. I could have replaced the old with the same model and done just as well. The brewing is very good, fast, and great tasting coffee using the 6 and 8 oz sizes."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this and still working strong!! It has been great! Lots of coffee made in this house 🤗 Brew size selections are a good fit. The temp control and stronger options are great for two different coffee lovers! Brews quickly, easy to clean!! Should last a good while!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "First let me tell you I drink at least 8 cups of coffee a day and this Kuerig meets the demands.  Brew time is faster if it’s been working for awhile like two cups. This makes strong coffee and regular flavor. Husband likes strong.  It is not portable and the kcups can be from any where. It is a good size and really takes up very little space on my counter.I maintain mine based on manufacturer opinion.  I love it that much I don’t want to be without it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I received my Keurig K-Elite Single Serve K-Cup Pod Coffee Maker yesterday so I don't have a lot of use to review it by but I will say that having had several Keurig coffee makers in the past I like the look, feel and utility of this model.  I read several reviews prior to purchase that claimed the temperature of the brew was not as hot as was set in the machine.  I experienced the same and wanted to understand it better.  I have my machine set at 190 for the temperature.  I used a calibrated Thermapen ONE Thermometer, the one chefs use and rely on, and the temp of the coffee in my cup right after brewing completed was 158.  Then I measured the brew as it exits the machine but before it got into my cup and it was 187.  Turns out my ceramic cup was at room temperature and some of the heat from the brew was used up to heat my cup, which lowered the resultant temp of the coffee in my cup.  Bottom line:  my machine is very close to the temp I set for the brew.  If I preheat my cup the coffee in my cup will be very close to what I have my machine set to.  So I am happy and my coffee maker is performing as specified."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent quality, easy to use, wonderful to have your coffee or tea at the exact moment"
    },
    {
        "review": "Stopped working after 2 days warranty not covered outside US, eventhough sold by Amazon UK extended insurance also proving to be a totalnightmare!!Stay away! Amazon involvement is a total scam!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The best coffee maker"
    },
    {
        "review": "There are some nice features to this model that we enjoy.  We like the Strong button with a  10oz cup for a bolder brew.  The coffee seems to be hotter than our previous Keurig 2 model. There is an option to adjust the temperature of the water but we like it at the highest setting which is 192F.  Nice selection of cup options i.e..  I like a clear Hot Water Button as I often have tea in the afternoons.  The Elite is a nice looking unit and it is easy to use. A convenient feature is that you can program the start and auto off times.  So far I am pretty happy with this machine."
    },
    {
        "review": "The K-Elite Single Cup Coffee Maker is a stylish and practical addition to any kitchen or office. It looks great on the counter and brews hot and iced coffee, which is a nice bonus. The staff loves the smooth and flavourful coffee, and it's super easy to use—perfect for busy mornings. This machine has you covered whether you're after a strong, hot cup to start the day or a refreshing iced coffee in the afternoon. A great pick if you're looking for something convenient, reliable, and good-looking!"
