]

[
    {
        "review": "Buy this!! I love waking up to the smell of coffee, and this machine does it right everytime. It is also is so common sense to use that you could program it without reading the instructions. Added bonus: no k-cups needed! A single cup is easily brewed with the environmentally friendly reusable single basket. This is the one!"
    },
    {
        "review": "So, like you all ,I've been a coffeeholic for many years. Like you ,I've struggled to have a decent maker in my kitchen. I recently finished up with my Cuisinart mod#CHW-12. Had it for 5yrs. It got to point of no longer producing a well tasting cup. We did the Vinigar cleaning etc. So, i spent MANY hours searching online for a decent Maker. Problem was the abundance of poor reviews encompassing many manufacturers!  It's  now 2018 and we have trouble creating a Kit Coffee Brewer thats decent!  I did a switch and desired a maker that will produce a single cup as wife n i both have coffee at different times and mostly need the one 16oz cup. In searching for the 12cup Carafe / or single cup Maker ,my choices became limited. Read the reviews and pulled the trigger on this. It's only been 1wk now but i can honestly state that it is the BEST maker I've ever used! I ran a full 12cup Carafe first off, thn dumped. Then did same for the single cup side. ( full 14oz). Then ran 12cups clean water through for both. Then did the Coffee that I'll drink. No issues. Had to play round wth the exact amount of grounds for the single side so to get the outcome i desired. Has clock, easy to pre prog., and, the single side will turn off when done. The Carafe side will stay on (hot plate) for 2hrs after brewing complete. You can simply press On/Off button to turn off anytime. For those who have an over-spilling issue with the grounds within the gold filter basket?, you are using TOO MANY grounds!  The single side comes with a gold reusable filter which also encompasses two - Level markers. One is min and the other is Max. If you fill above the Max level, WELL, overflow of grounds will prob. occur. On the Amazon site you'll see the Reusable filter for the Carafe side in \" frequently ordered with\". I also ordered that as i don't like paper filters. It performs well. Water level for Carafe is helpful. It's towards the right rear, on the side. It's accurate. Brew time for 12 cups was good. I've learned to warm up my Mug when using single side as it is not as hot as Carafe as no hot plate for the Mug. I use single side to run water for tea as well.  What would make this model perfect? If it sounded out a tone when brewing is complete. It also has No charcoal filter as with my Cuisinart. No biggie as i always have used filtered water to begin with. Coffee is better when there's no Chlorine in the H2O! Filling either the Carafe or single side is easy and Max level markers are visible enough to get it right. Carafe pours very well and i like that the Carafe lid stays attached as u simply press thumb to open but it's not required to pour. Single side grounds chamber pulls out easily. Single side has a bottom (under mug/cup) that reverses to then become a elevator to bring cup higher if you'd like. I brewed a cup at lowest level without any spill or splatter. It drips slow enough that i don't believe i need to elevate my mug. This model also looks fantastic, Beautiful!  Has a \"Bold\" brew mode for both Carafe n Sing. The brewing is slower, so u gt a richer brew. Light on clock only on when unit is ON. Has seperate green light that indicates you are using \"Program\" mode. I don't use \"Pods\" but if i did the manual states that \"Senseo\" Pods will work. Note that unit will only brew one side at a time. It cannot brew both sides at once. Very pleased so far. If any issues I'll update here. P.s. if Manufacturer reads this, you may want to consider modifying so to have an end of brew audible tone! Jst a thought.  Update!; 1/5/18. Jst did 2 Lg mugs for me ( nine- 8oz cups), using Carafe of course. Wife then needed to do her single 14oz using of course the Single serv side. When throwing the slide switch over to Single, it turns off the Carafe side. So, yeah, hot plate under Carafe is still hot, but, it's now off. So, in future, wife does her single, first, then i do Carafe. UPDATE ; 1/22/18-  3wks now and NO ISSUES!  When removing coffee filled Carafe, absolutely no spilling onto hot plate. The spring loaded valve above, performing well. Reviewers having the Hot plate discoloration or burning may be turning unit on with a Hot plate thats dirty. I make sure plate is clean /dry before and after ea. use. I make sure bottom of Carafe is clean/ dry as well. Wife using single serve ea. day and says \" best cup of Coffee ever\"!  Update; 4/17/21.  NO issues, all still good.  UPDATE!!! - 10/10/21-  So, finally I'm now considering buying a new one of these as this one is intermittently not pumping enough water up and into Coffee basket. About 12× now in past 6mon's I've had to pour out Carafe into another cup, place Carafe back, then pour my Coffee,(that looks like Tea), into the grinds basket and do a Double Drip, sometimes twice to get color I wish. I got roughly 3.5 years out of this Maker. I guess that's good considering Everything's made in Cheapo China. If/when I buy a new one, I'll post back. Have a good Coffee!  UPDATE: 11/14/21. So, I purchased this exact model once again on 10/12/21. After 1 month, I can honestly state that it's a great difference between original and new. New machine brews perfectly as did the original one up until the 3yr mark. No issues to report with this New Maker( Same model as first one). Pictures here are of 2nd maker,(2021)."
    },
    {
        "review": "Delighted with this coffee maker! It arrived on time and in good condition. I had a very expensive coffee maker that quit working and thought I would save some money and try this Hamilton Beach version. SO glad I did!The set up was easy and that first morning I was very happy with my hot delicious, coffee!The single serve option is important to me and it works perfectly. I LOVE having a single cup of coffee without using a k-cup!Highly recommend this machine!"
    },
    {
        "review": "It's about what you'd expect for a mid-range Hamilton Beach coffee maker. Normal price of $80 feels a bit steep, but I think it's worth what I paid for it on prime day. It does what it says on the box/product listing and it works better than the dollar store coffeemakers you'd find in an economy hotel room. Looks to be of quality from afar, is somewhat cheap and plastic feeling when you actually use it. Just sturdy enough that I'm not concerned that I'll break it. Single serve and full carafe functions do not share a water tank, and you fill the single serve reservoir with exactly as much water as you want to brew into coffee. Pretty intuitive and I guess pretty standard for this type of coffeemaker. But if you are used to filling the tank once a week and brewing a set 6oz or 8oz this is not that. \"Brew Options\" button toggles between bold and regular brew strength.... And that's it. There's no way to set brew temperature, but the default temperature is fine. It brews a single serve in about 3 minutes or so. Faster than a drip coffeemaker of yesteryear but if you're expecting it to be as fast as a pod system you're looking in the wrong place. The thing that matters most though is how the coffee comes out, and I have to say it's worth the extra hassle of using loose ground coffee and filters as it's much better than pod-brewed coffee. The slower brew speed results in a better coffee. Much more cost effective than pods too. The reusable single serve filter is surprisingly easy to rinse out. For $50 it's not bad. I would not pay $80 for this. At a price point of $80 I expect to at least be able to choose a brew temperature, even if there are a few pre-sets instead of by-degree. If you can get this for under $60 and you are specifically looking for a coffeemaker that doesn't use pods, then I can recommend it. Otherwise at full price, I don't think it offers enough to differentiate it from other $60 coffeemakers to justify the extra $20. It does have a clock in it and the ability to set a time to automatically start brewing at a set time, which is a feature I really don't use, but for some maybe this will make the $80 asking price worth it as I am not sure if this feature is commonly available in cheaper options."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am so happy with this dual coffee machine! Just FYI it doesn’t use pods. The one cup feature has its own small basket which you use your own coffee. Coffee temperature is perfect. Is is very easy to use, and I have not had any leaks. It has helped to make more space in my small kitchen by combining the two features and has saved me some serious money not having to buy pods! I would definitely recommend this product."
    },
    {
        "review": "After struggling with fancier more expensive coffee makers it was nice to go back to a simple machine that just functions without leaking. My wife loves it and it’s great we don’t have to clean up the countertop after every use. Basic and reliable but that’s all we wanted."
    },
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love this coffee maker!!! I was looking for a maker that offered both, a carafe and single cup option without using KCups, and this one does. It has a convenient small gold filter that you fill with your own ground coffee. If you want the gold filter for the carafe side, you have to buy it separately. Otherwise, use paper non-cone filters.It also brews both sides at a nice high temperature. It’s easy to use and has all the standard options. I give it a solid, five-star thumbs up!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This the best coffee pot I've ever owned, seriously. I appreciate good coffee and regularly buy beans from a local roastery.  I am not a barista nor do I claim to be a coffee expert. I enjoy good coffee and a drip coffee maker is good enough for my daily habit.This maker can be used to brew single cups on one side or a full pot on the other side.  Typically, I am the only coffee drinker in my house.  Sometimes we have guests.  This coffee maker allows me to serve both situations easily.To use the single serve side, I fill the cup that I'm planning to use with the correct amount of tap water and add it to the single serve side of the maker.  This is accessed from the top under a small lid that flips up.  This side is designed to only hold enough water for a single serve amount of water.  I don't use manufactured pods as I prefer fresh grounds but this maker apparently can handle pods too.  I grind my beans or use pre-ground coffee and add that to the slide out tray on the single serve side just above the cup location.  There is a metallic mesh screen that holds the grounds on the single serve side and I find that I waste less coffee than when I try to make only 1 or 2 cups in a large pot.  The single serve side has a nested set of plastic circles that sits under a tall mug when not needed.  These little circular risers can be un-nested and stacked to allow a shorter cup to be closer to the dripping coffee (see photos).  This allows the maker to accommodate a variety of sizes of cups. The single serve side takes about  2 minutes to brew.  I think the coffee tastes great and I can control the strength of the brew based upon how many grounds I add.The full carafe side is much like any basic drip-coffee maker.  There’s a small reservoir that holds enough water to brew a full pot of coffee.  There’s a flip lid and a basket for coffee grounds.  You can use paper filters or buy a separate metallic, re-usable mesh filter that fits inside this basket.  I like these baskets as it’s less wasteful than using paper filters daily and I don’t have to remember to constantly purchase filters.  I’ve used the same mesh filter for over 7 years now.  It doesn’t filter as finely as paper filters do and the last sip of coffee contains a small amount of grit / sediment but this seems normal to me now.  If someone doesn’t like this idea than I would warn them not to drink the last sip.  It’s pretty easy to avoid.The coffee maker has a very obvious and easy to use manual switch that selects whether you are brewing a full pot or a single serve.  Only one side can be used at a time.  You simply move the switch to the left or right as the illustrations show to select which side you wish to utilize.I frequently use the timer feature.  Prior to work I have one 16 oz metal travel mug filled, warm and waiting for me when I wake up in the morning.The display is bright when you touch a button and dims to normal again after about 30 seconds so it doesn’t light up the kitchen at night like a beacon.  There is a single bright green LED light that indicates that the timer is set and ready to go.  Personally, I like this feature as it is an obvious acknowledgment that the timer is ready to go at the time that I programmed in.  Some might find this too bright but it’s hard to imagine it being a nuisance to most people.Other reviewers have indicated the their carafe broke instantly upon the first use.  I’ve used my carafe several times without issues.  I also noticed that a new pot is around $10 so if it does break down the road, I can probably replace it easily.  Some said that it tastes like plastic, I haven’t experienced this.  Some said that it leaks after 3 months – I’ll try to update this review later but so far so good – no leaks.  Others say it takes too long to brew.  I think it takes about as long to make coffee as every other coffeepot that I have owned and if you set it up the night before, you won’t have to wait for it.  It can be ready for you whenever you tell it to be ready.  I even read that some people were annoyed that they had to slide the coffee pot out from under a counter in order to add water to the top of the coffee maker.  I once added felt pads to the bottom of a coffee maker to make this process easier.  Without a dedicated water line and a commercial coffee apparatus, I’m not sure how the manufacturer would avoid this overly burdensome task.  You have to add water somehow; that’s how coffee works.I have not had any negative issues at all with this coffee maker and I’ve been using it daily for over 1 month.  It’s easy to use, it’s easy to program and I like that I can make a full pot or single cup depending on my needs.  I definitely recommend this unit."
    },
    {
        "review": "It is a good coffee maker, it performs its functions and is easy to clean."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am so amazed the versality of this Hamilton Beach coffee maker of Single and full pot brew. The product output is awesome! Good brewed coffee every single morning is a heavens gift!"
    },
    {
        "review": "It works perfect, the scheduling option helps a lot in my busy mornings as does the option to only prepare a portion when needed."
    },
    {
        "review": "・Function: With the automatic drip 2-way mechanism, you can choose whether to make a large amount of coffee in the pot or make one cup.The only thing worth noting is these two functions, and the rest is no different from a regular coffee maker.When you press the coffee brewing button, it makes just the amount of water you put in the jug, so if you pour too much, it will overflow.The temperature of the coffee itself is piping hot, so I think it's good for people who don't like hot coffee. However, it was a negative product for me, who bought it expecting an auto-drip function with a timer. This is something that can be said about all overseas products, but the timer is definitely off, and it's off by hours, not minutes, so I have to make adjustments every half day for about 2 to 3 hours (Is it possible?) I wanted to wake up in the morning and find coffee poured into a mug...but my long-awaited dream didn't come true...There are very few coffee makers that pour coffee into a mug, so it was a big shock as I had high expectations."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I am so happy to do a review about this coffee pot. I’m gonna tell you everything I love about it. I love the fact that it has a carafe. I love the fact that it has a button you can press to make it stronger. I have to say this is the best cup of coffee I’ve ever made in my own home. It is absolutely delicious and I don’t use anything but Folgers nothing special. If you get this, you will not have a problem. You will not have a bad cup of coffee. When I first got it, it did some leaking. I went to the troubleshooting. It told me how to fix it. Well now it’s perfect. I also like the fact that there is a Customer Service phone number that you could call if the troubleshooting doesn’t work out. So many companies nowadays want you to text and they don’t want to talk to you. Well, I feel like I should be able to talk to them if I bought the product. This company feels like I do because of that I appreciate them. The coffee pot is very large and it also is very high. It does not fit under my cabinets, which is a problem. Well, it fits under my cabinet. I just can’t open the top. So I solved it by buying a round apparatus that has wheels on the bottom that people use for plants. I’ve set it on that and now I can roll it back to the wall and forward when I wanna fill it problem solved. The price is very reasonable. I think I mentioned that that’s also very important in this day and age. You will not be unhappy with this coffee pot, with the carafe that keeps it warm for quite a while. Follow the instructions to put hot water in it first let the pot warm-up. I also don’t dump the water out. I put the hot water in the coffee maker and it makes the coffee hotter. It is just steaming. This is a great product if you’re looking for great coffee this is the one to buy and remember it may leak when you first get it, don’t worry about it. Just follow the instructions. Make sure the ball is hitting the pot and it’ll be fine. Best coffee I’ve ever had in my house."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve had this coffee maker for several years now and I’m very satisfied.  It has a 12 cup brew capacity which is plenty for us.  It also fits well with our kitchen decor with the black on stainless steel color.  I line that it keeps the coffee hot in an insulated carafe rather than a hot plate so the coffee never burns.  It has been very reliable so far.  Also, the process to set the delayed start is very easy so we set up the coffee maker at night and have coffee ready for us when we make our way to the kitchen."
    },
    {
        "review": "5 weeks and works fantastic.  Nice to wake up to 6 mugs of piping hot coffee, that stays nice and hot (even with adding creamer) for about 4hrs and warm thereafter, so it doesn't go to waste...I like it hot.  Had to buy new paper filters, but no problem with collapsing and getting grounds in the coffee.  The ability to pull out the carafe while coffee is brewing is nice when forgetting to auto button at night.  It is a great replacement for one where that didn't function properly. So glad we got it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this coffee maker to replace our Cuisinart coffee maker that gave up the ghost after many years of service. I wasn’t sure about my choice to go with the Black & Decker because it was quite a bet cheaper than a new Cuisinart but I have to say it’s been great and I don’t regret my choice at all. My biggest gripe with the Cuisinart was how small the opening on the carafe was that made it difficult to clean. The Black & Decker has a large opening making cleaning a breeze. It also has a better pour spout than the Cuisinart. The only downside is that the carafe doesn’t keep the coffee hot as long as it predecessor did but that’s rarely a problem in our household. The programming display is also a little Hard to read with my old eyes. I doubt it would be a problem for younger users. All in all it makes a great cup of coffee in under 10 minutes and I often use the scheduling feature so I wake up with that first cup waiting for me in the mornings."
    },
    {
        "review": "This thing is an A+ for us. This is the same one that we have at out winter home and have had it for years. I makes great coffee and keeps it hot for hours. I am not sure if it is induction or what but there are no hot surfaces and if you turn it back on it heats the coffee in the thermos. The on thing I would change on it is make the display darker so you can read it. You need a magnifying glass to read am or pm. Still doesn't stop me from buying it again. My older one is a little noisier than the new one. I really have to listen to make sure it is brewing. I love the appearance and you can see the water level, holds a little over 6 cups of water. Looks exactly like my 15 year old one, if it ain't broke don't fix it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've had this coffee maker now for about 3 weeks. I don't love it, but I don't hate it. I'm also not 100% sure if I would recommend it either. Here's why. PLEASE READ ENTIRE REVIEW FOR IMPORTANT INFO.Before purchasing this, I read lots of the reviews, and watched all of the video reviews before I decided on this one. Because everyone seemed happy with theirs, I went ahead and bought it. It was pricier than others, but I always go by the old saying, \"you get what you pay for\". It shipped very quickly and arrived the next day. When I got mine, I went through the setup procedure and I was ready to enjoy my first pot of coffee. The first thing I noticed was the lid was very loose, and I knew it was supposed to \"lock\" into place. After all, that's how the coffee is supposed to stay hot, in the carafe, and not on a warming plate, right? Even the description states:• 4 LAYER VACUUM SEALED THERMAL CARAFE: keeps coffee hot for up to two hours with the 4-layer vacuum sealed thermal carafe.On mine, I quickly discovered that there was a plastic seal missing from the carafe lid, which supposedly makes the carafe air tight. I reached out to Black+Decker and they quickly sent me a replacement lid (thank you Black+Decker). Finally, after getting the new lid I would be able to enjoy nice hot coffee. And I did...sort of. After using it for a few weeks now, I've noticed that the first cup of coffee that comes out is piping hot. By the time I get my second cup (maybe 45 minutes later) the coffee is what I would describe as \"very warm\", not hot. By the time I get to my 3rd cup, (don't judge) the coffee in the carafe is just lukewarm, (hello Mr. Microwave). I think I expected it to remain closer to hot much longer. BUT, while writing this review, I noticed in the product description it says:• IMPORTANT PRO TIP: To help coffee stay at brewed temperature, warm the carafe by filling with hot tap water and then discarding before brewing.So, I tried that this morning, and, it did help somewhat to keep the coffee in the carafe hotter, longer. I'm going to keep doing this and experiment to get the best results. My feeling on this is that it's just an extra step in the morning I wouldn't have to do with a traditional coffee maker with a glass carafe. One thing I do like is that the carafe does stay cool to the touch on the outside and also the no-drip spout feature.What I used to like about my old coffee maker is being able to use the glass carafe to measure the water and pour it right into the reservoir. With this carafe, there's no way to do that so I have to use a measuring cup. This is a minor inconvenience though.One other feature I wish this coffee maker had is that the clock display does not illuminate when power button is pushed (see picture) or while brewing coffee. It seems like a very dim display.Bottom line, typically if I don't like something I buy, I return it. However, I'm not going to return this simply because I don't want to go through the hassle of packing it all up and returning it, and I still get my coffee every morning."
    },
    {
        "review": "I had a coffee maker from another well-known brand that was more expensive. The power button developed a mind of its own, so I replaced within the warranty window and the replacement developed the same issue a year later. I decided to go with this brand for the price and simplicity. The power button is on the side instead of the top where condensation may have caused the issue on my other machine. In general, it's simple, but REALLY well made with a smart design. I'm hoping this lasts us forever. We're a fan of the carafe style because I wake up much earlier than my partner. The coffee stays fresh, hot, and doesn't burn. It's perfect!One note - It doesn't come with a filter basket, so be sure to purchase one!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the BLACK+DECKER 12 Cup Thermal Programmable Coffeemaker for a while now, and I’m thrilled with how it’s transformed my morning routine and even my camping adventures.This is a pretty and sleek, black-and-silver machine, that features a stainless steel thermal carafe with a four-layer vacuum seal, keeps my coffee hot for EASILY up to two hours while staying cool to the touch.Its Vortex Technology, programmable brewing options, and user-friendly digital controls make it a standout in my kitchen. Priced between $50 and $100, it delivers premium features like a brew strength selector, a fresh brew timer, and a no-drip spout at a budget-friendly cost, making it an absolute gem for coffee lovers like me who value quality and convenience.The coffee this machine brews is consistently delicious, thanks to the Vortex Technology, which evenly saturates the grounds for rich, full-bodied flavor. Whether I’m craving a bold morning kick or a smoother cup, the brew strength selector lets me customize each pot perfectly. I love how the machine reaches the ideal brewing temperature of 195° to 205°F, as noted by reviewers, ensuring every sip is packed with flavor. The LCD display’s fresh brew timer is a thoughtful touch, showing me exactly how long it’s been since my coffee was brewed—up to 120 minutes—so I know it’s still at its peak. One morning, I brewed a pot at 7 a.m., and by 10 a.m., it was still piping hot, which is a game-changer for my busy days.The programmable features make my life so much easier. I can set the 24-hour auto-brew timer the night before, and waking up to the aroma of fresh coffee is pure bliss. The digital controls are intuitive, with large, clearly marked buttons for setting brew strength, batch size (including a 1-4 cup option for smaller batches), and the timer. I’ve found the 1-4 cup setting perfect for when I’m brewing just for myself without sacrificing flavor. The Auto Clean system is another lifesaver, alerting me when it’s time to run a cleaning cycle with vinegar, keeping the machine in top shape with minimal effort. One user mentioned, “Set it up the night before, and you wake up to that smell of freshly brewed coffee,” which perfectly sums up my experience.For camping, this coffeemaker is a dream. Its compact size (9 x 7.75 x 14.25 inches) fits easily in my RV, and the thermal carafe is a godsend for keeping coffee hot during chilly mornings by the campfire. I’ve taken it on weekend trips, and the no-drip Perfect Pour spout means I can pour coffee into my mug without spilling a drop, even on uneven campsite tables. The carafe’s wide mouth makes it easy to clean with a damp towel, and the removable, dishwasher-safe brew basket simplifies cleanup after muddy outdoor adventures. I once brewed a full 12-cup pot (each cup is about 5 ounces) for a group of friends at a campsite, and everyone was amazed at how hot and fresh it stayed for hours.Maintenance is a breeze, which I appreciate as someone with a packed schedule.The washable brew basket is compatible with reusable filters like the GOLDTONE, saving me money on paper filters and making cleanup quick. The carafe’s wide opening allows me to wipe it down easily, and the machine’s Auto Shutoff feature gives me peace of mind, turning off automatically after brewing. I also love the durability of the stainless steel carafe—it’s sturdy, and the vacuum seal ensures it keeps my coffee at 154°F or hotter for hours,The only minor downside is the LCD screen isn’t backlit but that is no big deal.I love this pot and its features and functions."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love it! No burner and no fear of it shorting out and causing a fire because it was left on! Keeps 12 cups hot and we can choose to may as many cups as we need"
    },
    {
        "review": "Meets everything expected. It has good capacity, prepares coffee quickly, the temperature is good, the jug keeps the coffee hot for the necessary time, it only heats the water when brewing and does not burn the coffee. It turns off as soon as the coffee is finished, so there is no risk of overheating. It does not have a filter, it requires paper filters."
    },
