[
    {
        "review": "This was actually the second one of these I have purchased, because I was happy with the first one, and wanted to be able to rotate them.It is really quite simple.  It is a 64oz wide mouthed mason jar.  It just happens to also come with the removable filter screen column/cone that you put inside of it, and the well made handle/pour spout.  You can also put the white plastic lids that you can buy for wide mouthed mason jars on it, if you want.  So, you don’t have to use it for cold brewing coffee.  You can put any kind of drink in it, and just use the pour spout handle cover.  Or, you could just use the mason jar with a regular wide mouth lid, and store anything you want in it.  The glass is as thick as you would expect from a mason jar.  It’s nice that they include the cleaning brush, although I am not sure how useful that really is.  I have not had any difficulty cleaning it, with just a regular dish cloth or sponge.  I can just fit my hand through the wide mouth opening."
    },
    {
        "review": "This cold brew maker combines simplicity, durability, and practicality. The 64‑oz mason jar design feels sturdy, and the stainless steel filter is well‑made — fine enough to keep grounds out of the brew while still allowing a smooth, rich extraction. The airtight lid and leak‑proof seal are a big plus, especially if you like to shake your brew or store it on its side in the fridge.The pour spout and handle make it much easier to use than standard mason‑jar brewers, and the large capacity means you can make enough cold brew to last several days. It also works well for tea or infused lemonade, just like the listing mentions. Cleanup is straightforward, and the filter rinses out without much effort.Overall, it’s a reliable, easy‑to‑use cold brew system that delivers consistently good results. Great value if you want a big batch brewer that doesn’t fuss or leak."
    },
    {
        "review": "Cold brew at home!Arrived on time, as described, in new condition, not damaged despite being shipped in a thin box, original product marketing, with label stuck to it. No tape on openings, and yet it made it on one piece! WahooI have used it one week now and I have saved $6 already. Good quality materials, able to reuse over and over.Good appearance for the price.Easy to use and clean. Metal mesh is good quality. No sharp parts."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this cold brew pitcher because I finally did the math and realized my daily \"little coffee treat\" was turning into a full-blown financial commitment.This thing is ridiculously easy to use. Just add coffee grounds to the filter, pour in water, stick it in the fridge, and let it do its thing. The next morning, you've got smooth, delicious cold brew waiting for you with almost zero effort. Cleanup is simple, the filter works great, and I've never had issues with coffee grounds ending up in my drink.The best part? The money I've saved. Instead of spending $6–$8 every day at a coffee shop, I can make multiple servings at home for a fraction of the cost. With how expensive everything is these days, every dollar matters. Groceries cost a fortune, gas isn't cheap, and somehow a quick coffee run can turn into a $10 outing before you know it.My new motto is:\"If I can make it at home, I'm making it at home.\"This pitcher has become part of my daily routine and honestly feels like one of the smartest purchases I've made. The coffee shop may miss me, but my bank account definitely doesn't."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been really happy with this cold brew maker. It makes smooth, flavorful cold brew, and the large capacity is perfect because I don't have to make a new batch every day. The glass feels sturdy, and the filter does a good job keeping the grounds out of the coffee.My only complaint is that the lid can be pretty difficult to remove, especially when it's on tightly after brewing. It's not a dealbreaker, but it can be a little frustrating.Overall, it's a great value for the price, works exactly as advertised, and I'd definitely recommend it to anyone looking for an affordable cold brew maker."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is so great. Works perfectly, is easy to clean and fits perfectly in my fridge. I love the look of it and am so happy it’s glass and not plastic!! Easy to use and so sturdy."
    },
    {
        "review": "Obsessed! I love how heavy duty the coffee sleeve is because it prevents coffee grounds from traveling through to the pitcher of coffee the gets consumed. It makes a good strong pitcher of cold brew that stay fresh in the fridge for up to a week. It may stay fresh longer, but mine usually lasts about a week. It is very easy to use and also easy to clean. Look super cute in my fridge as well."
    },
    {
        "review": "Do NOT use with hot water!Appears to be a well designed product and was able to get a replacement when glass jar cracked during the first use. Although primarily designed to make cold brewing multiple servings more convenient I had some expensive loose leaf specialty tea samplers that I hadn’t used due hassle of messing with an individual diffuser each time. Lost all my tea from that batch🥲Since Mason jars were originally designed for canning fresh foods after heating them to a boil and there were no indications on the instructions that these mason jars were not compatible with hot water I tried my first batch with the expensive specialty tea and warmed water. Glass immediately cracked before I finished filling. Will stick to just cold brewing only."
