[
    {
        "review": "This coffee pot is so great! I wasn't expecting much, but it has impressed me. I bought this for one purpose. My husband was having a high risk, complicated surgery, and I was going to be living in the hospital with him during the time he was in there. I like MY coffee, and I want my own coffee even away from home. It dawned on me that I couldn't take my huge, double sided multi-use coffee pot with me. I started looking for something other than a keurig, and I found THIS!I read reviews. I figured for $22, it's worth a shot.This thing is awesome! It comes with a cup and lid, and a little coffee scoop (i still used my own. The one that came with it is smaller than mine.) It has one button. If you hit the button while it's not plugged in, it still sets it to start. As soon as you plug it in, it will start. It's important to read the instructions that come with it and follow them. It takes about 3 minutes to brew the cup. It takes a little practice to figure out how much water to use to leave room for sugar/ creamer, but it brews great coffee. I am not sorry I bought this, and I've even sent the link to friends who also love their coffee. I've only had it for about a month now, but I even use it at home in lieu of my $120 coffee pot. I even had a few nurses comment on it and say what a good idea to bring a small coffee pot to provide those small comforts of home. Job well done, Elite Gourmet!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I received this about a week ago and it has been PERFECT. When I first received it, I fell in love with the color (as it is my favorite) and size. It was nicely packaged and in perfect condition. I ran the first cycle through with just water and wiped it down like the manual said. I only made one cup each day using the tumbler included I used cold bottled water and poured it in the tumbler leaving space for creamer. Because I wanted to make sure I have the right amount after fully brewed.*Today I went to make a cup as usual since ive had it.. And noticed the water I was pouring in was coming out of the bottom fast but not all of it. It was about 2 inches or so less of water that I initially poured into the Tumbler that was leaked out. I wiped it up and continue to press the blue power button. And it brewed fine (minus the amount leaked in the beginning) without any more leakage. I will make another cup later on today and do a update.* Tumbler is very nice to have and keeps coffee hot/warm for a hour+ ...As long as you keep the lid locked after you sip. Easy to clean, I like the reusable filter it comes with. I just dump the used grounds in a plastic sack and toss it. Rinse filter quickly and dry fast. Long as you don't use super fine grounds then the filter is perfect!.**All in all I LOVE this and recommend for occasional coffee drinkers. Especially with limited space and no need for full size.... I'm just waiting to see if it leaks again later today when I update!****Another update: I have had this for a while now. I usually only make one cup per day. I clean it right after I am done and I make sure it is unplugged. This is a great machine for someone who is maybe just a single coffee drinker in the home or if it's just two people. It has not leaked since that one first time. Which I do think now the only reason there was water was because it dripped from the cup and I didn't notice. So I think this actually didn't leak on me as I thought. I'm still using it everyday and it is wonderful.***Well OVER 1 YEAR UPDATE***So this little single coffee maker is the best!!! I use to almost everyday, once a day. And it is still working just as good as when I first got it. I love this thing and definitely definitely recommend!!! Just make sure to always unplug it when you're done and don't make a bunch of cups back to back. At least I wouldn't recommend that. But if you are on the fence of ordering this and you only have one coffee drinker in the house, this is the perfect one!!! ✨☕"
    },
    {
        "review": "This cute little personal single serve coffee pot is exactly what my mother-in-law needed and I’ve made sure that she got one. It comes with its own mug. The brew time was very quick and the coffee tasted just perfect. No need for filters as it has its own little basket that is washable. But we decided to purchase the coffee pads, the little round coffee pads look like coffee and a teabag. Couldn’t find them in the store so I purchased them on Amazon. I told her not to fill up the water too high in the mug before she poured it in because she’s gonna be putting her creamer in it. She’s 80 years old so sometimes you have to remind her of things. But all in all, it’s a great little coffee pot and I’m glad I purchased it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this single serve drip coffee maker.  It is easy to use and clean.  There is a slight issue, liquid is accumulating INSIDE the coffee tumbler that came with coffee maker see attached video.  I have no idea how it gets inside and it doesn’t seem to drip out.  Other than that I am very happy with this purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "This coffee maker has been a game changer for coffee at work. Gone are the days of relying on mediocre office coffee that was always somehow empty when I wanted a cup.This product is easy to use and brews a great 14oz cup of black coffee in less than 90 seconds. The reusable filter is easy to clean with a quick rinse. I opted for optional paper filters instead and all I have to do is simply dump the puck of used coffee. The LARATH brand basket coffee filters here on Amazon fit perfect. 14oz of water + ~4 tbsp of ground coffee is all you need. This is equivalent to one large cup of black coffee or 2 medium cups if you split it and add milk. Overall the machine is relatively quiet and will not disturb others around you. The insulated cup is poor at keeping heat but if you plan on finishing your coffee in less than an hour than it's a non-issue.I'd highly recommend this cheap little machine for (Large) single cup drinkers and those seeking a more convenient black coffee experience at your work desk. Hopefully it lasts me a long time, but for the price, I won't be upset if it's done in a couple years and that's okay."
