        "review": "I paid $100. Owned for 7 months. There is no water reservoir like the Ninja or Keurig where you can select your cup size , rather it just brews out however much water you pour in. Same with k cup side, you add water for each cup and it pumps out all of it every brew.Drip stop doesn't work. Still drips onto burner. Carafe lid drips while pouring. Messy.7 months later, it won't brew the last 2 cups of water in tank.Its takes over an hour to brew a 10 cup pot. An hour and a half later, it's still struggling to spit out the last 2 cups. descaled it. Still takes a half hour to brew 4 cups. Continues gurgling like it's struggling. I'm just going back to my ninja and keurig."
