        "review": "I really like the chair, but theres something about it that i hate, but ill mention that last.Its super easy to build, the lumbar support was a little to big for me, so i had to replace it, and just move the vibrating deivce into my new one. It was kinda pricey, which makes the thing i hate about it even worse, but for a good quality chair, with all the lumbar support and decent recline, the price should be expect. especially since it comes with a foot rest as well, and the vibratitng lumbar suppor. The foot rest, at least for me does not extened far enough for my feet to feel comfortbale using it, I still use it but it hjust feels a little awkward and end up having to adjust my feet.multiple times.so overall the chair is pretty good, especially when compared to others in a similar price range.Theres is only one thing that i hate aboutt his chair, and thats the fact that its so noisy. The metal is constantly clinging whenever i move around, and the material will constantly squeak, when ever you try to recline. The fact that the chair costed over $100, and is no noisy honestly upsets me so much.Have youb ever had a old matteress and any time you moved a little, it would make so much noise? Thats how i feel whenever i make any type of movement on this chair.I dont know, if all chairs will be like that, i sure hope not, and if its truely not supposed to be that noisy even though i just bought it about a month ago(it was making the noises even on the first day). If its truely not suppposed be doing that i sure hope the company reads this and contacts me about replacing the chair for one that doesnnt make so many annoying noises over any movement.if all chairs are like that, then i think theres a serioous design flaw, and should be looked into and fixed asap.Other than that, its a good chair and if those small noises dont bug you then i would recommend  buying this chair over any available in a similar price.I hope my review helps someone out there to decide to purchase or even not to purchase this chair."
    },
    {
        "review": "(Note - I was going to buy another one for daughter, it went up to $159.99 in 2-3 days! Might still get it but this chair is awesome especially for sale price from few days ago)For less than $100 this chair is awesome. I’ve seen reviews stating it took an hour or even longer to assemble…no. I am not a handyman whatsoever and it took me about 30 minutes to completely assemble. Maybe 45 minutes unboxing and separating pieces to make sure I had everything. Easiest chair I have ever put together. Instructions are clear and very simple.As for the chair overall; it is not a $500 gaming chair with top of the line materials. If you pay >$90 for a gaming chair (this chair) do not expect it to withstand years of abuse. If you are careful around it, it should last plenty of time. If you game 10 hours a day and constantly adjust the seat roughly, it will probably last a couple years. For my 11 year old it is perfect. He isn’t allowed to game 10 hours a day so it should last longer than 2 years. If it lasts 2 years I will have gotten more than enough value for what I paid. I’m 6ft tall and overweight and it is comfortable for me. My son sat in it and he loves it. My 17 year old daughter sat in it and now she wants one. Why not! Reclining ability is good. It does not lay down completely flat but more than enough. Foot rest is simple and not bad if you are not 6.5ft or taller. The chair has a very comfortable firmness and isn’t too firm either. It fits my 5ft and change 11 year old and my 5.5ft 17 year old. And my heavy 6ft never mind how old.For the price, this chair is a great buy."
