    },
    {
        "review": "This is my third gaming chair in the past few years and is my favorite of the three. It looks fantastic and sleek in my office space. I was drawn to the creme color and couldn't be happier with it in person. In fact, it matches even better than I anticipated. I have a smokey grey desk and shelf system which it fits well with and also looks good with my hard wood floor.Before I jump to more pros, I will point out the cons first that caused me to knock a star off of my review. The condition was not perfect. The flange was cracked as you can see from the picture and on one side of the seat there was a little dimple and the other side kind of wrinkled, but very minimal and not a deal breaker. The cracked flange is not a big deal because they usually end up cracking anyways and it doesn't have any effect on the mechanics of the chair.Now onto some more pros.*Comfortable! It is a good size, big enough for a big 245ln 6'0\" guy like myself but somehow manages to stay slim in your space as well.*High Quality material - even when I was putting it together it was evident that every piece was solid and good quality. This contributes to the comfortability of the chair.*Easy to set up - if you have put any chair together in the past it does nothing unique to complicate it, but I found the tools to be well built and organized.*Footrest - much better than the last chair that I bought. The last one tended to swivel to the left when I tried to kick my feet up. This one feels much more stable so far.*Speaker system - I saved the best for last. I am pleasantly surprised at the quality of the blue tooth speakers. It wasn't difficult to set up, but you do have to download the app to initiate it. I like to listen to YouTube or podcasts while I am playing certain games, such as Microsoft Flight Simulator or City Skylines. I love how I have the sound of the game in front of me, while having the sound of my videos behind me. It balances the sound between the two sources very well so that they do not conflict with each other too much. I would usually have to turn my game down in order to hear my podcasts. I haven't figured out if I can pair with my PC though. I don't think that I can.I have only had it for a couple of days, so longevity is still a question. But it was well packaged with clear instructions and the packet is actually quite sleek."
    },
