[
    {
        "review": "I’m not sure what more you can ask for out of a chair at this price. Easy to assemble, looks pretty good, easy to operate, cushion, lumbar, and neck support are all really good and better than I was expecting. I love the foot rest and the ability to set the exact recline with ease. I’m 5’10” 170 lbs and this chair is very comfortable and foot rest is perfect. For larger people this chair may not be perfect, but it would likely get the job done. If you want something that looks fancy, this isn’t your chair. It looks nice and it’s sturdy, but not fancy. All parts are heavy black plastic. Are there better chairs out there. Yep. Do they cost 3x to 10x more? Yep. I’d say you get 90% of the chair for half the price of name brand “budget” gaming chair options. I’d be surprised if anyone who bought this chair didn’t rate it 8 out of 10 or higher."
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair is a lot nicer than I had anticipated after reading some reviews.  It was packed extremely well and the directions and assembly was super simple!  They pack all the hardware in an easy access package that's labeled for every step in the assembly process.  They also give you the tool, an Allen wrench, that works on each bolt and screw.The chair is well designed and comfortable.  The seat is firm and thick!  Don't get me wrong, it's not hard by no means.  It has great cushion.  It's just well built.  Should last for years.It's sturdy!  It's not a cheap chair.  I bought the textile version at an incredible price and that's great marketing because after putting this baby together, I'd have no hesitations about buying another in the faux leather because I now know the quality is really they from this manufacturer.  Highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair has been a fantastic purchase! I thought I would have to get a super expensive chair to get the comfort and support I wanted but this one was very reasonably priced and I got it on sale too. It's extremely versatile and very comfortable even for all day gaming. The lumbar pillow is the perfect firmness. The seat width is such a breath of fresh air. I can change how I'm sitting regularly and comfortably with plenty of room. All of its movement is smooth, i.e hinges, support column, wheels. My favourite feature so far is locking the recline in the exact angle I want with a quick push of a lever. It was easy to put together (though it took a bit of hand strength for some spots, like the last screws on the sides, so it may not be very easy for anyone with dexterity concerns.)It's almost completely noise-free and what noises it does make are quiet. The fabric is holding up well so far (2 months at the time of review). As a seamstress, I had concerns since the faux suede types usually aren't, but it's doing well. And the temperature regulates great. No overheating or sweating. The only thing struggling occasionally are the zippers on the neck and lumbar pillows. Sometimes they slip open since the fabric is so tight over the inserts, but they can be closed again and the zippers aren't technically broken yet. The footrest is a nice addition but doesn't extend far enough out to fully stretch my legs out. An extender that collapses into the main bars for the footrest would be needed since the bars are exactly the depth of the seat when put away. It they were longer they would stick out the back underneath the seat.All-in-all, a fantastic purchase that my weary body is appreciating when I'm at my computer. I'll try to remember to update this on the durability in a few months!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is actually a pretty solid chair. Was easy to put together, I’d say it took me about 35-40ish mins to put it together. I like the color, was a bit lighter than I expected tho. The material is very soft and comfortable, I like how it feels and everything. The seat padding is pretty firm, but not uncomfortable, could be a tad softer tho. I might need to break it in more. It reclines well and the leg/foot rest is solid and sturdy. The neck rest pillow works well, but I do wish the lumbar pillow was a tad thicker and actually strapped to the chair. My only gripe is the left arm rest wiggles a bit, that’s it. Over all happy with my purchase, would get again in a different color just to have or would give one as a gift."
    },
    {
        "review": "Really happy with this gaming chair. The lumbar and neck support are fantastic—I can sit for hours working and gaming without my back aching. The build quality feels very solid and sturdy. I also really like the fabric; it’s soft, breathable, and much more comfortable than leather/PU leather, especially for long sessions. Definitely recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered this chair on August 6th, and after a little over two weeks of regular use, I absolutely love it. It is much more comfortable than my previous chair, which I had been using for years, and I can sit in it for long periods without feeling uncomfortable. I also haven't noticed any degradation in the cushioning, materials, or overall comfort so far, which is a great sign.The only downside I had was the assembly. There wasn't really a clear manual included with the chair, so figuring out exactly how everything was supposed to go together was a little confusing. I had to rely on YouTube videos to figure out some of the assembly, and finding a useful video was a bit of a hassle. Once I figured everything out though, the chair went together fine.Overall, I am very happy with the chair. It has been a major comfort upgrade from my previous chair and after a little over two weeks of use, it still feels just as good as when I first put it together."
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair looks great. I bought it because it had pocket spring construction and the seat wasn't your typical \"chunk of foam on a piece of plywood\"...and it was red. I hate it. It creaks and wobbles every time you move in it. It took me a solid hour to get one of the arm rest bolts threaded, then the next day, the arm fell off. It's back on, but I have no faith that it will not say goodbye again. The fabric is so slippery that after you sit in it for 15 or 20 minutes, you start to slide forward, out of the chair. Microfiber. Yuck. Warning: Do *not* try to lean back when the chair is in the upright position or you'll end up sitting on the floor (after the seat scrapes your back on the way down.) The headrest is in the right position and is quite comfortable. The lumbar cushion is uncomfortable and, if you do give it a try, it helps in pushing you out of the chair. Sitting on it doesn't help. If you decide to recline, make sure you have a friend there to take a video...so you can post it in the 'funny videos' area of YouTube. It reclines, but the spring isn't adjustable and has so little tension on it that you may end up somewhere you don't want to be. (e.g., the floor)I don't know who this chair was made for but it certainly wasn't me. Maybe it was you. I'm not a gamer. I just wanted a decent (and fairly comfortable) chair for my desk. Maybe if I was a 16 year old gamer I'd be ecstatic. But I'm not. While I'm at it, how does that tubby guy in the picture get his hugeness on that seat and cross his legs? I'm probably half his size and fairly flexible and I can't do that. I tried. Didn't work. I can easily get one leg up on the foot rest though - two if you cross them.Finally, on top of all of this, the pneumatic cylinder seems to lose air on a random basis.As much as I thought I would like this chair I do not. In fact, as much as I hate to say it, this is probably one of the worst chairs that has ever been introduced to my rear end...and back...and arms. I have been in old, wooden office chairs devoid of all padding and/or adjustment that were more comfortable.Even though it says \"FREE RETURNS\", I would return this chair in a heartbeat - except that I'd have to disassemble it and get it back in the box in a satisfactory manner. You should buy this chair, but only if you want a nice-looking, fabric covered chair that you will never enjoy sitting in. For me, it's just money wasted."
    },
    {
        "review": "I didn’t think this chair would be as comfortable as it is. I’ve bought a few gaming chairs this year looking for a good one under $200 and this was the one! Nice feel and super easy to put together! Love it and bought the light purple one as well 😌"
    },
    {
        "review": "Super comfortable, but you have to get used to the chair for a week to find it comfortable. This is because of the pillows. At the beginning you think “how uncomfortable are the cushions”, but your body first has to get used to the new sitting position and then you just say “BABA!”. The gaming chair offers a lot of little extras, e.g. the adjustable backrests or the front footrest, which can be extended. ASSEMBLY: The whole thing took me almost an hour, but you have to keep in mind that I had never assembled any chair before and was a bit shocked by the instructions at first, but it turned out that the instructions were easy to understand. You can compare it with an Ikea assembly plan. CONCLUSION: My conclusion is that I can definitely recommend this chair because it offers many extras and is comfortable (once you get used to the shape of a gaming chair). Nevertheless, the price of this chair is of course a lot of money, but I would say it's worth it, because you'll definitely keep this chair for a few years and the company is world-famous for its good gaming chairs."
    },
    {
        "review": "its a very good very comfortable chair in + the fabric and very good quality very comfortable for long gaming sessions another + the chair and high very easy to assemble all the tools its in sight nothing to complain about very good chair very happy for the price it doesn't get any better."
    },
    {
        "review": "Superb armchair that exudes quality.Assembly in 15 minutes and without tools other than the one provided.Stable and very comfortable"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I sit at my desk for 10+ hours a day, and my old chair left me with constant lower back pain. This one is a complete game changer. The adjustable lumbar support actually stays where I put it, and the recline function from 90° to 135° lets me shift positions throughout the day. The mesh back keeps me cool, and the seat cushion is firm but comfortable. Assembly was straightforward and the casters roll quietly on my hardwood floors. For the price, I honestly didn't expect this level of quality. Highly recommend for anyone who spends long hours at a desk."
    },
    {
        "review": "My last two chairs started squeaking within a month. This one is built differently. The metal base feels heavy and durable, and the casters roll smoothly with zero noise – even on my tile floor. The recline mechanism works like a charm, and the chair stays locked at whatever angle I set. The seat is wide enough for comfortable sitting, and the foam hasn't flattened out after weeks of daily use. Assembly was quick and the instructions were clear. I've recommended this to a few friends already. Solid chair for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm 6'3 and most chairs feel like they were designed for someone much shorter. The headrest on this one actually reaches my neck, and the lumbar support hits the right spot on my lower back. The seat height goes up high enough for my long legs, and the recline function is smooth and secure. The mesh back is a lifesaver in warmer weather. Assembly was easy and the chair feels solid underneath me – no wobbling even at full recline. If you're over 6 feet, give this one a serious look."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’m really impressed with this chair. Assembly was a breeze because the instructions were clear, and I had it put together in no time. Right out of the box, you can tell the hardware has some serious weight to it since nothing feels cheap or flimsy. Once assembled, it feels super sturdy with great weight support. Best of all, there’s zero creaking or squeaking when you shift around or lean back. The pull-out footrest is the real game-changer, though. Being able to kick back and take a quick nap in the office is insanely comfortable. Totally worth it!"
