    {
        "review": "After spending 8+ hours a day at my desk, I finally upgraded to the CAPOT ergonomic mesh chair—and the difference is night and day. It’s not just a chair, it’s an adjustable support system designed for serious desk work.✅ ProsComfort: The seat cushion is firm yet breathable, and the mesh back keeps me cool even during long sessions. Lumbar support is adjustable and actually targets the lower back instead of just being decorative.Durability: Frame and components feel solid—no wobble or flex after assembly. Rated for 400 lbs, and it absolutely feels like it could handle that without strain.Weight: Despite its heavy-duty rating, it’s surprisingly lightweight when rolling or repositioning thanks to the smooth PU wheels.Custom Fit: Between the 3D headrest, 4D flip-up armrests, and 3-level tilt lock, I was able to dial in the perfect seated position. Great for switching between typing, video calls, and relaxed browsing.Color: The matte black finish with subtle texture gives it a professional and understated look—perfect for a clean setup.Ear/Head Support: The headrest cradles comfortably behind the neck and base of the head, reducing fatigue without forcing posture.Low noise level.❌ ConsArmrest Adjustments Take Getting Used To: Lots of movement axes, which is great—just not intuitive at first.Assembly Takes Time: While everything is labeled and packed well, it took me a solid 40 minutes with careful attention.📝 Final ThoughtsThe CAPOT chair nails what most office chairs miss: true adjustability without feeling gimmicky. If you’re someone who switches between focused work and laid-back browsing, this chair adapts right along with you. It’s now a core part of my productivity setup, and I’d confidently try other CAPOT ergonomic products moving forward."
