[
    {
        "review": "Took a while to put together, but it was worth it. It’s a very comfortable chair and as advertised it seems to be exceptional quality so far very pleased."
    },
    {
        "review": "This office chair looked nice in the listing photos, but it’s even better in person.I ordered this for my home office space which previously had an armchair that my kids broke by tipping in it.  I love the light gray color of this one, since my desk is gray wood, and I love that it is a leather-type material that can be wiped down, since I have messy kids. It has a nice, stylish sleek look to it that elevates my office space.The chair was easy to assemble, but it does come with some assembly needed.  It took about a half hour to get it assembled. My twelve year old did it though, so it might take an experienced adult less time.The chair is just as comfortable as you would hope for it to be.  It has decent cushioning, and the lumbar pump works impressively well. The material is soft and doesn’t stick to your skin or make noise when you move.This chair is adjustable in height.  For reference, I am 5’6”, and at max height my heels are about 3” off the ground.  In the middle setting, my heels just touch the ground, with a couple more inches to drop.As far as width, I would say it’s standard for a full-sized office chair.  I am about average in size, but I do think it’s more accommodating for larger adults than many others, due to the fact that the sides are mostly open, and the arms easily lift up.  It’s also a pretty deep seat bottom and tall seat back.  The build is also very sturdy.I couldn’t ask for a better office chair.  I’m super happy with the overall quality, features, and design of this chair.  I can’t imagine that it would disappoint anyone who bought it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I don't have much experience putting furniture together. This was probably the most challenging piece I've assembled so far. The two armrests were by far the hardest part. Start to finish, it took me about an hour to put the thing together.First, the instruction manual also has a typo worth knowing about. One step lists screw (11) as M6 x 25 mm, while the parts legend and the screw bag both show M6 x 30 mm. This happened right in the middle of the hardest part. I spent a while convinced I had the wrong screws before realizing it was just an error in the booklet. At least the parts are labeled, with FRONT printed on the seat plate, so orientation wasn't a guess. Still, the typo cost me a lot of wasted time.  Not worth deducting a star in the review, but a real annoyance.Once it's together, though, the chair is really comfortable. I like office chairs with soft arm support. These armrests stay comfortable through long stretches of sitting. The headrest pillow is a nice touch and gives good support when I lean back.My favorite feature is the inflatable lumbar support. With a pronounced lower back curve, I find pumping up the lumbar makes a real difference. A separate back cushion isn't something I've needed.The faux leather feels pleasant to the touch. There wasn't any chemical smell when I started using it. Because it's a leather-style surface, it breathes less than a mesh chair. Where I live it gets hot and humid, so that's definitely a tradeoff. Anyone who sweats a lot might want a different material.The wheels roll smoothly across wood floors without sticking or catching. Moving it around my workspace is pretty easy.Overall, the assembly could be smoother or better documented, but the comfort, the adjustable lumbar, and how easily it rolls make this a solid office chair... once it's put together."
    },
    {
        "review": "The Mr. Picky I live with is loving this chair after rejecting many others. It is super comfortable and looks and feels like quality furniture. It is high enough to support his frame of six feet and support his neck which was a problem with other chairs we tried. It was very easy to put together and only took me 40 minutes. I just have a few notes to make it easier for you. There is a QR code to scan for a video or the chair comes with an instruction booklet in the bag with the seat of the chair. I showed in a picture that you may have to move the arm piece a little to see all four holes that will attach the arm to the back and seat cushions. The instructions talk about 25 and 30 mm screws in the instructions book where you attach the arm but there are only 30 mm screws included and only these are needed. One tip not mentioned is you need to lean the back piece on something like the box to make it easy to attach the arm and then the seat cushion also to the arm. These are all minor and I hope will save you time when you put together this chair.I think it is well worth the cost (and even more) and it is so comfortable to sit on. The wheels were able to easily glide on my low pile carpet. It is an added bonus that the arms lift up to push the chair closer to your desk if needed. It looks good in any office or even a living room."
