[
    {
        "review": "I purchased the violet version of this chair, and I've been very happy with it. Assembly was straightforward and didn't take long. The chair is comfortable for long hours at my desk, whether I'm working, studying, or gaming.I especially like the adjustable lumbar support, which provides good lower back support and helps me stay comfortable during extended sessions. The mesh back keeps me cooler, and the violet color looks beautiful in my setup.For the price, this chair offers excellent value. It's sturdy, comfortable, and looks great. I would definitely recommend it to anyone looking for an affordable ergonomic office chair.You could also make it a bit more personal:⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Perfect for Long Streaming SessionsAs someone who spends a lot of time at my desk streaming, studying, and working, I needed a chair that was both comfortable and supportive. This chair has been a great purchase. The lumbar support helps reduce back strain during long sessions, and the mesh back keeps me from getting too warm.The violet color is gorgeous and fits perfectly with my gaming setup. Assembly was easy, and the chair feels sturdy and well-made. Overall, I'm very pleased with this purchase and would recommend it to anyone looking for a comfortable office or gaming chair."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is an excellent desk chair, especially for long hours at the computer, but i have to confess that it's taken a little time to get used to it only because this chair and my old faux leather desk chair (also sold on amazon and pictured below for reference) are at totally different ends of the spectrum. The new VIOLET mesh computer chair is extremely comfortable even after spending most of my days and nights sitting in it since i spend many, many hours daily working, communicating and gaming on my desktop computer. the chair may appear to be lightweight; however, it's got a decent amount of weight to it because of the high quality materials used to make it, especially the solid metal parts that make up the strong and stable base.In my opinion, the ability to adjust the arm rests, seat height and lumbar support proved to be a godsend, which i was not expecting, because it all enhances the versatility and functionality of the chair. Being able to change the chair to recline a bit is probably very useful for many, but I prefer a sturdy, stiff, upright chair back, so i adjusted it accordingly at a set in place 90-degree angle. The lumbar support is especially helpful to maintain proper posture and spinal alignment, yet again there was a small issue in that i generally sit with a slight forward lean or, as stated earlier, with my shoulders directly over my hips. in order to have full back support, you must lean back slightly, and that's an awkward position for me in any chair.the arm rests can be moved down at your sides or in an upright position as if there were no arm rests at all. and i have found myself switching back and forth between the two depending on what i am doing and how much movement i require in the chair. they can also be moved forward and backward a short distance, which i did find a little bothersome when the arm rests were down and i bumped them when i happened to move my arm(s) a little. they do not lock in place, but i'm positive that this is just another little concern that i can easily get used to since the old chair's arm rests were not adjustable at all.did i mention that it's PURPLE!?! not the only reason, but definitely one of the main reasons, that i purchased this chair over every other chair i looked at. and there were a lot of them under consideration. it comes in several different colors, including the traditional, brown, white and black, among others, which i really liked a lot since my room of course has a purple theme going on, and this fashionably attractive and functional chair fits in perfectly with the decor and further brightens up the space!i am so happy with this purchase even though it took me 3 hours and not 15-20 minutes to assemble. and that was all on me because (1) i am really slow and methodical when i'm doing new things, taking care with every step to do it right, and (2) i am not handy in the least and can barely hammer in a nail these days. as advertised, all tools, primarily the allen wrench, are included. no parts were missing, and nothing was damaged upon delivery. and, best of all, i can say that i assembled it all by myself perfectly on the first try, so it was well worth the time and effort spent."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this chair for my husband's computer, and it has been a great purchase. He uses it every day for work and says it is much more comfortable than the one he had before. The lumbar support feels great, the seat is cushioned, and the mesh back allows for airflow, making it comfortable for long periods. Plus, it was easy to assemble, looks sturdy, and has a modern design that fits perfectly at the desk. We are very happy with the purchase and definitely recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this ergonomic chair for my home office, and it’s been a great upgrade. The mesh back keeps me cool during long work sessions, and the adjustable lumbar support really helps reduce lower back discomfort. The chair feels sturdy, rolls smoothly, and was easy to assemble. It’s comfortable enough to sit in for hours, and I like that I can easily adjust it to fit my posture. Overall, it’s an excellent value for anyone looking for a supportive and comfortable office chair."
    },
    {
        "review": "Here are my comments and concerns with model YX001 only.  The instructions have a few issues imho: black letters/words printed on a dark/darker background, I literally could not read them at times and had to go to another room with a spotlight to make sure I followed directions.  A box around the words are fine, but not a colored box.  The 6 star gear shims (piece I) on the arms really needs a better way to identify instead of “placed in the direction of the instructions”.  I am not having any issues with the arms so I assume I may have gotten it right.  There aren't any instructions when to tighten all the screws that you were told to leave untightened, that could lead to an issue if when you finally get the chair finished and see step 8 saying Done and try to sit in it.  Not impossible use the included Allen wrench (great it is included!) to tighten the screws from step 4 to Done because the T-handle will not fit in the now put together space.  We have a bunch of regular Allen wrenches so I was able to complete the tightening required.  Overall assembly was not that difficult and the time to accomplish it was not longer than expected.  While the above caused some delay, the chair is still fine after 4 weeks of continuous use.The chair itself: the lumbar support is very nice and easy to adjust.  The arms are attached to the back and the seat seemingly to give more support for them when getting in and out of the chair.  The arms lifting up and away is nice.  The seat, after a couple of weeks, seems reasonable, not too soft or too hard, the mesh back is nice, and the gas lift feels and sounds solid.  The chair would be worth 4.5 Amazon stars, except…  I’ve had a lot of office chairs (including work) over my 50+ years of sitting in front of a computer daily: cheap chairs, relatively expensive, and in between.  I have a glass floor mat and the chair does not roll freely.  There are flat spots on the wheels and it takes effort to get the chair to start to roll anywhere on my mat while sitting in it.  The description says they are soft to reduce noise and they do on my mat.  When on glass all chairs still make a noise due to the nature of the mat, so that’s not an issue.  Compared to the rest of the chair the wheels aren’t up to what I expected and I am concerned about their longevity being soft with a non-circular shape.  Perhaps on carpeted floors this might be hidden.  Lastly, be aware the description says Lifetime Warranty, however an included index card says 5 years IF you send them an email, which I did, but was ignored for a couple weeks.  Only after using Amazon to complain about them were my inquiries finally answered.  It is indeed only 5 years (NOT lifetime) which is still a decent amount of years for a chair.  I will update this if any issues appear within 5 years."
    },
