        "review": "Great!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Honestly I hate to write this review, one because I hate complaining and two I was super excited for a new gaming chair…… BUT after paying $160 for a chair that I would probably still be upset paying $50-80(but would expect for going the cheapest route) , the chair is super flimsy and POOR quality materials. All screws are super tight and the chair is still flimsy and moves around too much and also creaks. The back support is leaning to the side even after trying to adjust the T-bar support bracket, it’s the tilt mechanism that is causing it to lean, even after trying to reposition and tighten everything possible and the knob that the backrest T-bar slides into the tilt mechanism, it has too much play due to parts not fitting properly causing it to much free play to move around……. Also wouldn’t call this a massage chair with this super cheap non adjustable vibrating block (which you barely feel) that someone clearly ripped the backrest foam out with their fingers and it’s super uneven and crooked.(see attached images)Lastly, chair is on the smaller side! I’m 5’ 7” about 185lbs and the cushions are not too comfortable. I can feel the hard support under the seat cushion luckily the backrest and neck support pillows allow some sort of comfort for the backrest.I’ve sat in cheap $70-80 chairs that were 10x more comfortable and better quality, wish I knew the names and would have definitely purchased one of those instead, I figured spending double I would get a decent chair that I would enjoy ……. Lessened learnt, don’t expect a better quality because it cost more, and don’t purchase a gaming chair without actually sitting in it or at bare minimum having a 1st hand recommendation from a trusted source! Clearly the 4.1 stars, that magically dropped to 3.9 from purchase date to delivery date 🤬  wasn’t reliableDefinitely returning,"
