[
    {
        "review": "Given the price, this is a surprisingly good backpack - actually much better than the OEM Dell backpack it replaced.  The material is heavyweight and seems durable.  There are a wide variety of pockets and sections for organizing accessories.  Overall, the backpack has a lot of room - I've actually packed enough clothes for an overnight trip in addition to my laptop, charger, and all of my office road gear."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this backpack in early August and used it daily as a teacher.  Ten months later and at the end of the school year, this backpack is still going strong with little to no signs of wear.Style: This backpack looks sleek with a touch of vintage appeal.  The color is great, which helps if you want to maintain a low profile while using it.  There's a small pocket up front, a medium pocket behind that (with a separate zipper pocket inside for safekeeping valuables; and slots to hold several pens), and the main storage area has a separate laptop sleeve.  One of the photos has my school-issued 13-inch laptop.  It easily fits in the slot with plenty of room to spare.  The sides of the backpack have two mesh-like pockets that can hold small items.Comfort:  The handle on top along with the two straps have thick padding.  It's comfortable carrying the backpack whether you use one strap or two.Durability: My backpack is still in great condition after heavy use for the past ten months.  This includes tossing it on the rear seat of my car, placing it in my trunk, and having it rest many times on the carpeted classroom floor.  The back and bottom of the backpack still look great.  I will easily be able to continue using this backpack for at least another full school year.Cargo capacity:  My everyday carry included our school-issued laptops, plus a power cord, an iPad (with protective case), an external hard drive, about half a dozen pens, a pad or two of paper, and other assorted items.  Even with all that stuff I can fit more in there if needed.Overall value:  Excellent.  This is such a great backpack that I bought one for my wife, and she uses it at her school.If you're looking to save some money but still want a durable and useful backpack, do not hesitate.  Buy this backpack with confidence."
    },
    {
        "review": "Absolutely excellent!  I have been using this for over a year now at my job, and it is perfect -- of high quality and at a reasonable price.  It is stylish and tough with all the right compartments and strong straps that have not shown any fraying yet.  In fact, even after almost daily use for over a year, it still looks brand new!  I am thoroughly satisfied."
    },
    {
        "review": "Has lots of storage.  But if you put too many things in each pocket you may make the overall weight of the backpack seem a bit heavy.  Does seem to be fairly water-repellent though.  Many pockets for organization.  Shoulder straps are comfortable.  Fabric seems to be durable and will stand up to everyday use.  Seams are solid and zippers open and close  seamlessly."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm absolutely loving this backpack! I used to use a Nordace backpack that was supposed to have 2 laptop pockets, but one of them was very much not meant for laptops, and was disappointed so I looked elsewhere. I am so glad I found this one. It is far more lightweight than my Nordace one, plenty of pockets and zippers for organization, inner pockets and a back pocket for security (I personally keep my wallet in an inner zipper pocket since the back pocket is a wee bit small). It also looks exactly like the picture (which is very exciting to me). Here's a bit of a breakdown:Pros:- Large laptop pocket (fits my 16\" laptop)- Lots of pockets- Against-the-back security pocket- Very breathable- Very light- Feels high quality and durable- 3 bottle-holder pockets (2 outside, 1 inside)- USB charging for portable batteries- Strap for attaching to luggage- WaterproofCons:- Likely won't hold larger items like textbooks (at least, it doesn't hold my large ones)- Security pocket is small- Doesn't have 2 laptop pockets- VERY tight outer bottle holder pocketsI, personally, got this for both work and school so I can carry both laptops together. It doesn't have 2 laptop pockets, but the one that it does is MASSIVE. The strap is actually loose even after putting both laptops into it so it can easily fit larger laptops. I went on a work trip and it was perfect. Half the time, I forget how much stuff I have in my backpack because of how light it is and how well it disperses the weight. I also appreciate that it's slim. My previous backpacks have always been bulky and I always felt awkward while trying to squeeze down the aisles of a plane to get to my seat, but it wasn't a problem this time. I do wish the outer bottle holder pockets were a little looser and larger so that I can fit my larger water bottle into them, but it isn't too big of a deal for me since I like to carry my bottle for the most part.Overall, this backpack is AMAZING for the price that it's set at and I hope more people find this. This has honestly been life-changing after having so many poor backpacks. My back thanks you for your product, Volher. Keep making these backpacks to perfection."
    },
    {
        "review": "Just what I needed!Freelance sound guy here always on the go and often need to set up and get the show going quick.This backpack is just the right size to throw over the shoulder and hit the road.Has plenty of compartments and pockets I'm able to use for extra adapters, plugs, batteries etc.A padded compartment fornmy laptop and iPad, all my little essentials well organized and easy to grab when needed.Has held up great so far and even got dropped in parking lot with no damage to electronics inside.This has become a go to piece of gear for every gig, highly recommend."
