[
    {
        "review": "Eco friendly, anti-glare and anti-blur, the 27 inch Acer monitor was one of the best deals for our purpose. This screen has a full HD resolution (1920 × 1080). In general, monitors for screens display are TN, VA and IPS, which is the case of the Acer. The In Plane Switching is actually a LCD screen known for its superiorcolor accuracy, wide 178 degrees viewing angles, contrast (perfect for dark rooms), and response times as low as 1ms with refresh rates up to 1200 Hz via HDMI. This screen is the ideal choice for gaming or office task at a reasonable cost. One can hand it up on a wall, to save space for example (VESA wall mount compatible (100 × 100mm)), and it is tilt adjustable too (-5° to 25°). It was a good value quality/price and a good deal. Let's hope it will last a while."
    },
    {
        "review": "This monitor is huge, and the picture quality is amazing. The graphics are very crisp, and the colors are vibrant and vivid. I use it to connect my 12-inch laptop, and the larger HD display has made a huge difference in my daily use.I used to get tired from staring at my small laptop screen for long periods, but this monitor is much more comfortable and actually makes it easier to stay focused and productive while studying.I'm very happy with this purchase and would highly recommend this monitor to anyone looking for a larger, high-quality display."
    },
    {
        "review": "I picked this up as a secondary monitor, and it has been a great addition to my desk setup. The image clarity is excellent. Text is sharp, colors are clean, and it is easy on the eyes even after long work sessions. For email, documents, spreadsheets, and keeping reference material open, it does exactly what I need without any fuss.The 27-inch size is perfect for a second screen, giving plenty of space without overwhelming the desk. Setup was quick, the stand is stable, and it paired seamlessly with my primary monitor. For the price, this is a very solid option if you want a clear, reliable secondary display."
    },
    {
        "review": "My husband has an office job that requires monitors and sometimes he works from home so we needed these. He’s also in college and so it’s a nice benefit to have these when he does school work.We’ve had these for over a year, so here’s what I think: firstly, we thought these monitors came with audio which they do not. That is why I gave it 4 stars. Audio is really nice to have so it hummed us out when it didn’t come with audio. We didn’t return it because we didn’t notice until after the return window.Despite our original purchasing reasons, we use these heavily for XBOX Gaming and PC Windows Gaming. Xbox connects great through the monitors, the quality is nice, the speed is consistent and connectivity is stable though for older games like Sims 3 on Pc, the quality is really dark. It’s better to game on the computer alone than through the monitor. I believe we paid $108 for them at the time which for what we use and need them for is worth the money. They are great monitors for beginners, basic monitoring and basic gaming or tv. Though, if we wanted higher quality, we would choose a different brand.Some other notes: The appearance is nice. The screen is smooth and easy to wipe down if it gets dirty. They can also be swiveled to your preferred position. The adjustability is smooth."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this Acer 27-inch monitor for productivity and general use, and it has been excellent. The IPS display provides clear, vibrant colors with good viewing angles, and the large 27-inch screen gives plenty of workspace for multitasking. Setup was quick and easy, the picture quality is sharp, and the monitor feels well-built. Great value for the price and a solid choice for home office, browsing, and light entertainment."
