    {
        "review": "Picture quality is great for the cost. It’s exactly what it says it is. It is way more vibrant than the previous 75hz model I had bought. It’s lightweight, easy to mount. The sound quality from the built in speakers is terrible but most are. I’m not sure anyone is using built in monitor speakers as the default option. The only complaint I might have is that the spacing between the plastic layers on the screen is slightly gapped so at the very edge corners things look like they are running off the screen."
    },
    {
        "review": "One of my 24\" monitors I use as part of my work setup died and I needed a replacement. This Sceptre 27\" fit the bill nicely.  Not only was it a welcome increase in screen real estate, but it also has very nice image quality.  The picture is brighter than my older monitors and has great contrast. The whites are whiter and the blacks are darker. Text is sharp and clear running at 1920x1080 and colors are nicely represented. The VESA mount made it super simple to mount on my monitor arms. While I'm not using this for gaming, the high refresh rate and low response time provide a flicker free image that is easy on the eyes. I'm staring at three monitors for coding and web browsing all day.  I wish the other two in my rig were as nice as this one. The Sceptre monitor is a bargain at this price and I may very well snap up another one while I can."
