        "review": "High quality, easy to setup, affordable. Good colors, good contrast. Very convenient controls. It is about 1/2 thickness and 1/2 weight of my old LED Viewsonic display that I bought about 8 years ago. It can be mounted on the wall [there are 4 threaded holes on the back, but the mount is not included]. There are two drawbacks - 1) the stand is not rotating, which sometimes can be useful. 2) The sound is rather flat and does not have much of the bass. I guess you should not expect much from any build-in speakers. Overall I am very satisfied with the product."
    },
    {
        "review": "Rarely review anything until I have had it for some time, but making an exception here. This monitor would be a bargain at trice the price. It is excellent in all respects."
    },
    {
        "review": "8/1/25 been a week so far and satisfied with the quality of this BIG BEAUTIFUL monitor for the great low price. a few bits of advice/insights: for the price I paid for the monitor I got the extra Asurion coverage just in case it stops working after the Amazon return period. take into consideration all monitors can only go to the highest resolution offered IF your computer can go that high. if the monitor box says 4K but your computer can only go up to 1080 then that's what you will see = the better the graphics card and processor the better the resolution. do not touch the front screen at all since it is very delicate and can get damaged easily. adjust the monitor settings from your computer if it turns off to often. the built in speakers are not good so plan on buying great speakers if you want to listen to music at its best. all in all, i would recommend this monitor for those on a budget considering all i have mentioned in this review. i will update this review if there are any changes worth mentioning."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this monitor as a secondary display for my setup, and overall the installation was pretty easy. Everything worked right out of the box, and for general use like YouTube, Discord, or multitasking, it does the job without any major issues. The size is good, and for the price it’s definitely usable if you just need an extra screen.But... there are a few drawbacks I noticed right away. The BIGGEST one is the ghosting. Whenever I drag windows like Discord or scroll through darker content, there’s a visible trail behind moving objects. In games, the motion clarity isn’t very ideal compared to an IPS monitor and darker scenes smear more than I expected. The stand also doesn’t offer much adjustment. The 100Hz refresh rate is nice to have and better than 60Hz and the overall image quality looks okay but just a bit brighter compared to my ASUS monitor.My recommendation for this monitor: use DP and tweak the monitor settings to reduce ghosting. Just keep in mind that because this is a VA panel and some ghosting will always be there it’s part of the panel technology and can’t be fully fixedThis monitor is fine as a budget secondary screen but if you’re sensitive to motion blur or want better motion clarity you’ll definitely notice the limitations. It works, but it comes with compromises. If you want completely clean motion with no ghosting Id suggest going with an IPS monitor instead."
