    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using an old Sony 27” non-smart TV as third monitor for my workstation setup.  I recently upgraded my CPU by purchasing a Minisforum NAB6 mini PC (highly recommended and better than buying a laptop and a hub to support all your devices), I figured it's time to buy a real monitor. Since I am on a budget, I scoured Amazon reviews for a good monitor and found this Koorui brand.Given the price point ($129.99 on Boxing Day 2023), I am impressed by this monitor. I am not a gamer nor a content creator, but I use this monitor for work applications, streaming, surfing, and some video/photo editing.I like the following:1) I am satisfied with the brightness and colors of Koorui (rightmost monitor in the attached picture). The larger monitor on the left is 43-inch 4K LG monitor 60Hz with all its fancy features. Koorui held its own against a monitor about 6 times the price when it comes to video streaming.2) I have been using this monitor for almost a month now and so far, have not encountered any problem at all – no flickering, no dead pixels, no problem with latency, and no dreaded blue screen.3) Because of the plastic components, it is so lightweight it is almost like a toy, and I mean it in a good way. This means that when I travel and stay in a hotel, instead of bringing my laptop, I could just bring my Minisforum mini PC and Koorui.4) With my current workstation requiring attention on 3 monitors, Koorui’s viewing angle is ideally suited to my work needs.Adjusting buttons was a pain in the beginning but I got the hang of it, if ever I do need to make re-adjustment, it’s now a piece of cake.The seller was also quick to respond to my inquiry. I thought the unit I purchased came with built-in speaker. The reviews are for different models so make sure the review you read applies to the right size and model of monitor that you are about to purchase. Sure, I can always return the unit to Amazon and have it replaced with the model with built-in speaker. I did not do so because I find it unfair to the seller and Amazon to return something based on the specs that I completely overlooked.Whether it’s for extra or main monitor use, given this price point against branded competitions, this 27-inch 75Hz IPS monitor is a real steal. You won’t regret the purchase – 5 stars."
    },
    {
        "review": "Buy 2 for the best stream."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good screen, very good value for money. The sound is good, parameters adjustable with the keys under the screen (brightness, contrast, volume, etc.)."
    },
    {
        "review": "The **KOORUI 24-inch Gaming Monitor** is a great option for gamers and users looking for an affordable monitor but with solid features. With a Full HD resolution of 1920x1080p and a refresh rate of 100 Hz, this monitor offers a smooth and sharp visual experience, ideal for gaming, work or entertainment. Below I detail the pros and cons based on my experience:### **Pros:**1. **Image Quality**: Full HD resolution provides vibrant colors and clear details, perfect for games and movies. Additionally, Eye-Saver mode reduces eye strain during long usage sessions.2. **100 Hz refresh rate**: Although not as high as other gaming monitors, 100 Hz offers a smoother experience than the standard 60 Hz, especially in fast games.3. **Adaptive Sync**: This technology helps reduce tearing and stuttering, improving the gaming experience by synchronizing the monitor's refresh rate with the graphics card.4. **Ergonomic design**: The adjustable stand allows you to tilt the monitor to find the perfect angle, which is ideal for long work or gaming sessions.5. **Built-in Speakers**: Although not high-fidelity, the built-in speakers are useful for those who do not want to invest in external speakers.6. **VESA Mount**: The 75x75 mm VESA mount allows you to mount the monitor on a wall or an articulated arm, adding versatility to its placement.### **Cons:**1. **Limited Refresh Rate**: Although 100Hz is an improvement over 60Hz, more demanding gamers may prefer monitors with 144Hz or higher.2. **Basic Speakers**: The built-in speakers are functional, but do not offer high-quality sound. For an optimal listening experience, it is recommended to use headphones or external speakers.3. **Limited adjustments**: Although it includes tilt, it does not have height, swivel or pivot adjustment, which could be a limitation for some users.4. **Maximum brightness**: The brightness could be a little low in brightly lit environments, which affects visibility in certain conditions.### **Conclusion:**The **KOORUI 24-inch Gaming Monitor** is an excellent option for those looking for an affordable monitor but with gaming features. Its Full HD resolution, 100Hz refresh rate, and Adaptive Sync technology make it ideal for casual gamers. However, more demanding users might miss a higher refresh rate and additional ergonomic adjustments. Overall, it is a great purchase for its value for money. Recommended for those looking for a versatile and functional monitor!"
    },
