    {
        "review": "Great monitor, couldn’t have asked for more at this price point. Great picture quality, great color quality, great appearance. I’ve yet to test how long it holds up when mounting, but so far it’s been easy to mount and has held up for a short while. Responsive and high refresh rate. I would recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "Let's get straight to business with this review.This monitor has been with me since July of last year, and it's safe to say it's held up amazingly. I upgraded from a basic 1080p monitor from Sceptre (that I still use as a secondary monitor to this day), and while the color profile is different (until making adjustments on the monitor itself), the high refresh rate makes it a super smooth experience, especially for gaming. Not to mention, with a powerful enough graphics card (I rock a 4080 Super), the high refresh rate paired with high fidelity makes all aspects of gaming gorgeous, to the point where I'm considering getting a second one to have a triple monitor setup.One thing I should mention is the weight. It isn't heavy per se, but I would be cautious depending on what mounting bracket you plan to use with it, and the size paired alongside the weight makes it a bit cumbersome when mounting to a bracket/stand.Besides that, if you need a relatively affordable, high refresh rate monitor, this Nitro 27in model will do its job and more. Highly recommend."
