    {
        "review": "Absolutely awesome picture for the price.  Is it the be all end all of gaming monitors.  No.  It's a low cost 27\" 1080p monitor.  Yet the color, clarity, and build quality are on par with more expensive monitors.  Compared to my daily used work monitors built by LG it's just as good, or better. Actually it's oddly very very similar."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought 2 to replace my work monitors, easy set up, almost too easy. The quality of the screen is wonderful. You can adjust the tilt of the screens. Came with all the cords needed, took me less than 10 minutes to set everything up"
    },
    {
        "review": "Good things:1. Image is good. I bought two monitors and they're both connected to my laptop hub via HDMI. An HDMI cable comes with the monitor.2. Connectivity is very good. I like the rear USB connections, which have allowed me to declutter my hub.3. I like these monitors and they price is right for what you're getting. (I'm not a gamer. I use them for documents, spreadsheets, and graphics.  They're perfect for that.)What you need to know:1. You'll need to connect the monitor to USB. You'll need a cable with a USB type-B connector at one end and USB type A at the other.  (I also bought two from Amazon, $6.44 each.)2. Attaching the base went smoothly on one, but on the other it wouldn't go.  If that happens, you need to depress the tab while pushing the monitor in. (See the picture for where the tab is.)  I did that, and it went in and connected.  When it connects you hear a click.3. The button for on/off and control, in the back, is not intuitive, but once you understand it, it's ok.  I think front controls would be better.  But it adjusts everything you'd need to adjust.4. There's no information about registering the product for a the one-year warranty. I guess the fact that you can review your purchases on the Amazon site is proof of purchase.5. You'd better have lots of room on your desk.  That's a good thing though.6. The quality of the speakers is low, but can be improved with a free graphic equalizer tool that you can download.  But I use external speakers, so I didn't care.7. I'll never change the tilt.  It makes me nervous."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased two of these. The first one was damaged, not sure if it was shipping or me. So I purchased another one. The second monitor was different than the first. Same order number. However, this was a better monitor. Works great. Wasy setup. Excellent resolution and picture quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is exactly what I was looking for. I have two HP Series 3 Pro 324ph 24 inch (23.8) FHD monitors but I had to order my own third monitor for work. This Amazon Basics monitor looks and functions exactly like the two HP monitors, for a fraction of the price. The only difference I've noticed is the size of the monitor. It says 24 inch (23.8) but it's just a hair smaller than the HP monitors. It's not super noticeable, but I am kind of OCD about things like that. Most people probably wouldn't notice, honestly. It was super simple to set up. The base is plastic and felt like it wasn't going to support the monitor, but then I picked up the monitor and it's super light, so it works exactly as it should. I was going to knock off one star (since I can't do half a star) because the monitor tilts slightly forward and I feel like I'm looking down at the screen instead of straight forward, but I didn't because it's possible that it's just my OCD.  It's not adjustable, so I'll have to get another monitor mount, but that's just my preference. Overall, this is a perfect monitor for office work. I would most definitely purchase it again.*Edit* I actually used my paperclip holder to kind of prop up the monitor so it’s not tilted downward."
    },
    {
        "review": "A good solid monitor replete with desireable features like 4 port USB Hub, HDMI/Display Port/VGA (No DVI though, sadly). Great blacks, Good color depth, not overly intense saturation. Good control system for settings in a single toggle button that's kinda cool.Nevertheless, you can get higher res monitors for less money. For me, I didn't care enough about that to pursue it. I'm not a gamer. There is almost no bezel, it's crazy.What I don't like is my webcam has a hard time sitting on top because it is so thin.No review is complete with an over the time aspect, but I have no idea how long this will last. I hope it lasts 10 years, but we shall see. The size is ideal, I wouldn't want anyting wider or taller.Viewing angle is terrific.It's easier on my eyes than my 18 year old HP that died."
    },
    {
        "review": "An incredible 27\" IPS monitor that bridges the gap between old-school hardware and modern PCs.Features VGA, HDMI, and DisplayPort, a built-in 4-port USB hub, and crisp 100Hz performance. Absolute hidden gem for retro enthusiasts and daily users alike!I am absolutely thrilled with this Amazon Basics monitor. It delivers outstanding value and serves as the perfect display solution if you want to connect both classic hardware and modern systems to a single screen.A Holy Grail for Retro Enthusiasts (Amiga 2000 / 1200 + PiStorm)I mainly bought this to use with my vintage setups, specifically an Amiga 2000 and an Amiga 1200 equipped with a PiStorm expansion. Finding a modern display that plays nicely with legacy signals is getting harder every day. The VGA connection on this monitor is fantastic. Combined with the PiStorm, it outputs a crystal-clear, rock-solid picture. The Amiga Workbench and classic games look incredibly sharp, without any of the typical sync issues you find on other modern panels.Unbeatable Connectivity Across Generations.The port selection is a massive selling point. It effortlessly accommodates multiple computer generations at the same time:VGA: Perfect for classic retro computers and legacy systems.HDMI: Great for modern consoles, laptops, or streaming devices.DisplayPort: Ideal to hook up a modern desktop gaming rig.You can leave all your systems plugged in simultaneously and simply switch inputs via the monitor menu—no more annoying cable swapping!Smooth Modern PerformanceThis monitor doesn't just shine with vintage hardware; it is equally impressive as a modern daily driver. The 1080p FHD resolution on the 27-inch IPS panel ensures excellent color reproduction and wide viewing angles. With a 100Hz refresh rate and a 4ms response time, modern PC gaming feels incredibly smooth and responsive, with absolutely no noticeable ghosting or motion blur.Great Bonus Features:Built-in USB Hub: The 4 extra USB 2.0 ports are a lifesaver. I can connect my mouse, keyboard, or flash drives directly to the monitor, which keeps my desk clutter-free.Integrated Speakers: The built-in speakers provide clean and clear audio performance. It’s perfect for hearing those classic retro sound chips without needing bulky external speakers.Eye Care: Thanks to the flicker-free technology, my eyes don't feel strained even after hours of tinkering on the Workbench or playing games.Verdict:Finding a display with a 100Hz IPS panel, built-in speakers, a USB hub, and modern ports alongside a legacy VGA input is extremely rare at this price point. Whether you are a retro gamer, a multi-generation collector, or just need a solid everyday monitor, this is a highly recommended buy.It’s worth every penny!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent basic monitor including 2 speakers, 4 USB ports, 2 video inputs. The refresh rate and video capabilities amply do the job for everyday use (not purchased for gaming), screen size that allows you to comfortably work on two documents displayed. Very good value for money having been able to take advantage of a Black Friday discountAlmost perfect but: I bought this monitor to connect a mini PC with Windows 11 and a desktop computer with Linux Mint, two HDMI inputs would have been more relevant today than a VGA, especially on a monitor. One of the characteristics that appealed to me was the 4 USB ports included, I plugged my mouse and my keyboard into two of these and I use a USB switch to the USB-B power supply via the computer used, but there you go, I sometimes lose contact with these ports in the middle of a session, not very reliable for working with a device plugged into one of the two other remaining USB ports of the monitor. The on/off button which is also used to activate other elements such as brightness, contrast, etc. is rear mounted and difficult to handle. Control buttons on the front would have been more user-friendly. Small drawbacks that do not deserve to lose a star, I would have given it 4.5 if the options would have allowed it."
    },
    {
        "review": "A fabulous monitor. Easy to assemble. Painless to set up with your computer. Excellent color and clarity. Well worth the price ."
    },
    {
        "review": "At this price point, the monitor exceeds expectations. The built in speaker is a bonus."
    },
    {
        "review": "Does the job very well even if the microphones are not exceptional."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "great price and monitor is great.  Easy set up."
    },
    {
        "review": "Burnt out on me just after  the one year disappointing"
    },
    {
        "review": "Well constructed and very sharp, but terrible color balance that can be corrected with the included controls.The settings I came up with for natural skin tones and not having your eyes ruined by an extremely bright and blue screen output are these:Set it to theatre modeCut brightness down to 25 (!). Way, way down.Set red, green, and blue under the 'Color Temperature' to 65, 85, and 77, respectively.Your mileage may vary, but you can use these settings as a starting point and adjust for your personal taste.These settings work best in low to average room lighting; if in a brighter room, you may have to adjust more.I would have given the monitor a 5-star rating, but the default settings are not pleasant at all."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good monitor. Arrived fairly quickly. Priced reasonably. Useful as a secondary monitor due to the refresh rate. I would say if you use it for a primary, consider upgrading to a higher refresh rate screen.In my case the refresh rate is good since I don't want to overburden by GPU with too many refreshes on a high resolution monitor like this and it's used as a secondary screen.I use this as top monitor so i can see music tracks that are playing and view online wallpapers for leisure."
    },
    {
        "review": "Purchased for my wife's office.  It has been a significant improvement for her eyes, as they are noticeably less strained after a workday in front of a monitor."
    },
    {
        "review": "Really nice"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this monitor when it was $149 and while other options exist for a cheaper price and better refresh rate, this has the color saturation option. Basically, you can make the colors pop much more, which is a huge plus in my book as only a few monitor brands have it. It's a huge requirement for me. The 1440p is also a big upgrade compared to my other 1080p monitor, as games and other content looks way better while not being as resource intensive as 4k. However there are a few downsides to this monitor.First downside was getting the monitor to recognize the 1440p signal. When I first set it up, it only recognized 1080p from my mini pc. When I unplugged and plugged the HDMI cable back in, then the monitor discovered the 1440p. Not a huge deal breaker, as I rarely unplug my computers.Second downside however, is a very annoying one.  When auto switching from HDMI to Display Port, the monitor sometimes goes into sleep mode, or just bugs out. This is very frustrating as I constantly go from my mini PC (on HDMI), to my Desktop (on Display Port). It'll sometimes work without issue, and other times I have to power off the monitor via the back button for it to work again. But sometimes when powering back on from this issue, the monitor light will be amber instead of white, even though it's not sleeping and fully on. I have to physically unplug and replug the monitor in to fix this. (See the attached photo). Disappointing that this is an issue, given my other 1080p monitor from ASUS never had this issue.So ya, if you can get this for sale under $130 then sure it's a good monitor. If not, find something else that is less buggy."
    },
    {
        "review": "The unit was smaller than I expected. Returned it the next day"
    },
    {
        "review": "This monitor does sit at a very low level, below eye height, and that makes the user's head always in a low tilt position"
    },
    {
        "review": "Came with dead pixels out of the box, I asked for a replacement and the replacement was never delivered, it just caused me trouble. Maybe your will be ok."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I purchased this bottle just to try out in the summer of 2023. It is now the summer of 2026 and I still use it multiple times a week (only because I now have multiple Owalas and I have just ordered my third Owala FreeSip). I have used so many cups—Stanleys, Yetis, Hydrojugs, Hydroflask, etc—and the Owala is still my favorite. Here’s my favorite things about it:LEAKPROOF! This is the biggest one. I can throw it my bag and trust that everything will stay dry.THE SPOUT! Hands down the best spout I’ve ever used. I love that I can sip through the straw but then close the lid and keep my straw clean and not have any spills if it tips over. And then it also gives me the option to absolutely inhale water if I’m about to shrivel up from dehydration. I think this alone is why I now own three in different sizes.STAYS COLD! The 32 ounce holds ice for quite a while. It varies depending on how often I refill it but if I’m not constantly refilling it, it will hold ice for about 24 hours.THE SIZES! I love the size options. My original one was a 32 ounce and is a great middle ground for me. It holds enough water that I’m not refilling it every hour but it’s not huge. It’s great for work and this bottle will be going to live at my job. I just ordered the 40 ounce for home because I want a little more volume when I’m outside gardening but I can’t say much about the 40 ounce size yet. I also have a 16 ounce (kids size) that I use when I leave the house. It fits in a lot of my bags and it’s leakproof so I always have cold water with me. It’s perfect especially since I’m on medication that causes dehydration if I’m not careful.DISHWASHER SAFE! This one is self explanatory.It’s amazing and I love it. There are a few cons though. The first one is that the 32 ounce doesn’t fit in my cup holder. Not a huge deal since it’s leakproof—I just keep it on the passenger seat. But Owala does have cup holder friendly options now if that’s something you want.The bottle also does dent and scratch fairly easily. I dropped it getting out my car one day and it’s a little beat up now. Kind ugly, but it’s still my fave. It’s kinda disappointing because I have Yetis and Stanleys that have been through far worse and still look new. Just be mindful of that and baby it a little. Still 100% worth it though.Long story short, it’s a great bottle that will keep your water cold and everything else dry. As someone who has used this bottle regularly for years, I highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I freaking love this thing. I'm not a trend person, I go for function. And when my STB SIL got my fiancé a shiney new Stanley I decided it was time to replace my beat up Rtic with the mismatch lid and straw.I may not follow trends, but I didn't want my fiancé's cup to put mine to absolute shame!First off, can we all agree that the marshmallow is gorgeous? THIS cup is spectacular. Strange to say that about a water bottle, I know. But  since I never jumped on that train, I didn't know what I had been missing out on. Let me tell you what!The most important things to me is taking care of my service dog. She keeps me safe so her care is paramount to me. This enables me to pour my water into her bowl on the fly, without having to open my bottle past what I would do to drink from it. Quick and easy. That right there was the selling point for me. But as it turns out, there was even more benefit than that.I don't chug my water but if I did, the chug hole does works fine.The straw portion is ready to sip from, and it doesn't stick up tall like other water bottle straws. It's JUST tall enough to get the job done.  No worry of toppling over because the straw got knocked over by the cat. (Because that happens.)The \"handle\", which is generally the locking feature unless you're using it as a handle, is well placed and comfortable for my sized hands. Not to small and not clunky and large. STB SIL likes to talk about how great the Stanley handle is, which I don't really get. I like that this doesn't have a handle. I have one to carry it if I need it, and not if I don't.The seal is completely water tight. I occasionally put a drink mix in it and shake vigorously. No leaks whatsoever. In fact...It fits in a car cup holder upside down. That's how I transport it in the car. It doesn't fit butt down, so I put it top down. I've been known to do this with various bottles, so I tried it with this one and it fits ok. It's not ideal but it's better than nothing. Try it in yours! Since it's completely leak proof there's are no worries about spilling. (Just be careful when you remove it that it doesn't unlatch.)Another bonus of the covered straw is that germs don't get in the straw. Perfect because people in public often don't cover their sneezes. Ugh. And the coolest part? Lipstick messes are concealed with a flip of the lid! Easy peasy!I have noticed that the inside of the straw stains a little, which was disappointing. I don't like that I look at it and it looks dirty when it isn't. But I guess I shouldn't have used drink enhancers then. Also, my top color is very light. Other colors might not show that. Another thing that want fun was that when it fell, it dented! Oh no! So beware of that.It keeps my water super cold and I don't go anywhere without it. I love it so much that I'm thinking of getting another so I don't have to limit myself by style! Definitely worth the price since I use it constantly, every day.This one is so chill and Zen... The next one shall be colorful and crazy! One for every mood!I simply can't say enough about this darn water bottle... Does that mean I'm on trend now? Who knows! I just love my Owalla! I'm definitely a fan!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Owala water bottles for the win! These are hands-down our favorite water bottles. We have tried just about every popular brand out there—Yeti, Stanley, Hydro Flask, and others—and the Owala is the one that everyone in our family consistently reaches for.I absolutely love the versatility of the lid. You can use the built-in straw when you want to sip, or easily flip it open and drink straight from the opening. Having both options in one bottle is incredibly convenient, especially when you're on the go.The color combinations are also so fun! There are so many options to choose from, and the colors and designs make the bottles feel a little more personal and fun to use.Durability is another huge selling point. These bottles get used constantly and have been dropped and knocked around, yet they hold up extremely well. They seem much less prone to denting than some of the other brands we've tried, which is especially important when they're being used by kids.And, of course, they keep drinks really cold! We can fill them with ice and water, and they stay cold for hours. The lid also seals extremely well—we have never had an issue with them leaking in a bag.After trying so many different water bottles, Owala is definitely the winner for our family. They're durable, versatile, attractive, keep drinks cold, and don't leak. I honestly can't think of another water bottle brand we've liked as much!"
    },
    {
        "review": "As my first Owala I am so pleased with this water bottle. Keeps ice and water cold for hours, doesn’t leak, and love that you can use straw or spout. Great quality and liked the price. Only complaint is that it doesn’t fit in the car cup holders"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am absolutely thrilled with my Owala FreeSip stainless steel water bottle as it has quickly become my absolute favorite for every day use, and it is easily the best insulated bottle I have ever owned. The best part for me is the built- in straw. It allows me to sipupright or I can drink from the widemouth opening. The push button lock lid locks securely so I can toss it in my tote bag without worrying about any spills. The stainless steel keeps the water ice cold all day even if I leave it in my hot car! It has a convenient carry loop. It can be filled with large ice cubes, and it’s easy to clean. You will love it!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "We love this Owala! The 16 oz size is perfect for kids—big enough to hold plenty of water without being too heavy or bulky for them to carry around.The FreeSip design is probably my favorite part because they can sip through the straw or tilt it back to drink normally. It doesn’t leak all over the place, keeps water cold for a long time, and the covered spout stays cleaner than an exposed straw. The Read My Lips color is super cute, too.It’s held up really well to everyday kid use, which says a lot. Definitely worth the 5 stars!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this Owala for my son and really like it so far! My favorite feature is that you can drink from either the built-in straw or use the chug opening. It gives him both options without having to switch out lids or pieces, which is really convenient.The bottle itself feels sturdy and good quality, and the lid closes securely and has a handle that makes it easy to carry. The colors are also really fun and vibrant.My only concern is the coating on the outside. It feels like it may be somewhat easy to scratch, especially since this is going to be used by a kid and tossed into bags, taken to school, etc. We’ll see how it holds up over time!Overall, though, I’m really happy with it.I’ll update my review once I find out how sturdy it is."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love Owala bottles and I have several of the 24 oz.  I decided to get a larger size (32 oz.) this time to take to sporting events to hold more water.  Water stays cold all day like the others, and it never leaks.  The only downside is that it doesn't fit in my car or chair cupholders by just a fraction.  I kind of suspected that might be the case going in, so it doesn't bother me too much.  At games I just have to set it on the ground instead of my sports chair.  It just won't be my everyday bottle - I will continue to use the 24 oz for the car since it fits perfectly in the cupholder.  But Owala still gets 5 starts for the great design, easy to carry, and staying cold all day."
    },
    {
        "review": "Let's go, firstly, I LOVED the bottle, I was super excited for it to arrive and I don't regret buying it at all. It keeps the water cold for a LONG time (if you're like me and curious to know exactly when, a great example was that I put water in it WITHOUT ICE at 4 pm and the next day at 8 am when I woke up it was still cold as if it had just come out of the water filter, remembering that my filter has ice water). Her straw is amazing and super practical, but I also recommend buying one of those little brushes to clean. Plus, it's really beautiful and big. I bought the 945ml one and it's perfect for me, as it has a handle and the external material of the bottle is not slippery to the touch. Now talking about the negative points, the only negative point I have to mention here about this bottle is the delivery. I saw a lot of people complaining about the delay in delivery and it actually happened to me too, the shipping time is HUGE, I believe it's because of the number of people who buy this bottle, so it took a LONG time for them to ship, approximately a month. The delivery itself after shipping took a week +/-, so I believe it's actually a stock thing. The problem is that the bottle should come in a cardboard box, lined inside and everything. But in fact it came in a bag with nothing on it, just the bottle, wrapped in a small package with a DUBIOUS layer of bubble wrap. I even believe that this was the reason for the scratch in the photo (it's small, very small, and it's on the bottom, you practically can't even notice it, especially after I bought that silicone mold to put on the bottle). Anyway, the product is perfect, but they're quite wrong in the way they sent it, and it's not even because of the delay, but because of the damage caused to the products, since more people here had the same problem."
    },
    {
        "review": "Did not include the green ”cover” as shown.Other than that, I adore this bottle!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Really nice and holds so much water and keeps it cold for a really long time. The quality is worth it for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "A little expensive compared to average, but worth it! It keeps the temperature very well, but above all the possibility of drinking by suction thanks to the straw makes it easier to use even while driving! The colors are fantastic!"
    }
]

