    },
    {
        "review": "As my first Owala I am so pleased with this water bottle. Keeps ice and water cold for hours, doesn’t leak, and love that you can use straw or spout. Great quality and liked the price. Only complaint is that it doesn’t fit in the car cup holders"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am absolutely thrilled with my Owala FreeSip stainless steel water bottle as it has quickly become my absolute favorite for every day use, and it is easily the best insulated bottle I have ever owned. The best part for me is the built- in straw. It allows me to sipupright or I can drink from the widemouth opening. The push button lock lid locks securely so I can toss it in my tote bag without worrying about any spills. The stainless steel keeps the water ice cold all day even if I leave it in my hot car! It has a convenient carry loop. It can be filled with large ice cubes, and it’s easy to clean. You will love it!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "We love this Owala! The 16 oz size is perfect for kids—big enough to hold plenty of water without being too heavy or bulky for them to carry around.The FreeSip design is probably my favorite part because they can sip through the straw or tilt it back to drink normally. It doesn’t leak all over the place, keeps water cold for a long time, and the covered spout stays cleaner than an exposed straw. The Read My Lips color is super cute, too.It’s held up really well to everyday kid use, which says a lot. Definitely worth the 5 stars!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this Owala for my son and really like it so far! My favorite feature is that you can drink from either the built-in straw or use the chug opening. It gives him both options without having to switch out lids or pieces, which is really convenient.The bottle itself feels sturdy and good quality, and the lid closes securely and has a handle that makes it easy to carry. The colors are also really fun and vibrant.My only concern is the coating on the outside. It feels like it may be somewhat easy to scratch, especially since this is going to be used by a kid and tossed into bags, taken to school, etc. We’ll see how it holds up over time!Overall, though, I’m really happy with it.I’ll update my review once I find out how sturdy it is."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love Owala bottles and I have several of the 24 oz.  I decided to get a larger size (32 oz.) this time to take to sporting events to hold more water.  Water stays cold all day like the others, and it never leaks.  The only downside is that it doesn't fit in my car or chair cupholders by just a fraction.  I kind of suspected that might be the case going in, so it doesn't bother me too much.  At games I just have to set it on the ground instead of my sports chair.  It just won't be my everyday bottle - I will continue to use the 24 oz for the car since it fits perfectly in the cupholder.  But Owala still gets 5 starts for the great design, easy to carry, and staying cold all day."
    },
    {
        "review": "Let's go, firstly, I LOVED the bottle, I was super excited for it to arrive and I don't regret buying it at all. It keeps the water cold for a LONG time (if you're like me and curious to know exactly when, a great example was that I put water in it WITHOUT ICE at 4 pm and the next day at 8 am when I woke up it was still cold as if it had just come out of the water filter, remembering that my filter has ice water). Her straw is amazing and super practical, but I also recommend buying one of those little brushes to clean. Plus, it's really beautiful and big. I bought the 945ml one and it's perfect for me, as it has a handle and the external material of the bottle is not slippery to the touch. Now talking about the negative points, the only negative point I have to mention here about this bottle is the delivery. I saw a lot of people complaining about the delay in delivery and it actually happened to me too, the shipping time is HUGE, I believe it's because of the number of people who buy this bottle, so it took a LONG time for them to ship, approximately a month. The delivery itself after shipping took a week +/-, so I believe it's actually a stock thing. The problem is that the bottle should come in a cardboard box, lined inside and everything. But in fact it came in a bag with nothing on it, just the bottle, wrapped in a small package with a DUBIOUS layer of bubble wrap. I even believe that this was the reason for the scratch in the photo (it's small, very small, and it's on the bottom, you practically can't even notice it, especially after I bought that silicone mold to put on the bottle). Anyway, the product is perfect, but they're quite wrong in the way they sent it, and it's not even because of the delay, but because of the damage caused to the products, since more people here had the same problem."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good, doesn't leak, keeps the temperature."
    },
    {
        "review": "Did not include the green ”cover” as shown.Other than that, I adore this bottle!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Really nice and holds so much water and keeps it cold for a really long time. The quality is worth it for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "A little expensive compared to average, but worth it! It keeps the temperature very well, but above all the possibility of drinking by suction thanks to the straw makes it easier to use even while driving! The colors are fantastic!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I am obsessed with w/ the sway, I bought Daybreak/ Fig, they are gorgeous, the bottle design is sleek as well highly functional. It is matte vs  shiny the bottle isn’t slippery in hand, & there are different sizes to choose from.  It fits into my cupholders, it also fits into my couch cupholders, & have the 30 oz. I will be buying more for me as well for gifts as EVERYONE deserves to fall in love w/ this water bottle!  Oh, I have not talked about the lid functionality and I left the best for last because I never thought I would love love love the sip straw part as much as I do the chug part is very good as well. They’re right kind of like right next to each other, but you can definitely tell the straw area versus the chug area. I don’t usually use a chug type mouthpiece , but I did try it out because well it’s there and it’s very nice as well. With other brands, you either have a straw straight up you have a straw you have to flip up and this is more practice.  The sealing is  awesome,  I tested ice in the bottle and I put it in  @ noon 8/21/26 &  it’s 653am 8/22/26 and my water is cold with a lot of ice. I wanted to test it out because I know there’s some mixed reviews. I myself do not use ice in my drinks. I just use cold water so the ice retention for me is really not huge on whether I buy a bottle or not.. and let’s face it if you put water and ice into any water bottle you’re gonna have some weight, but I don’t think it’s that heavy and I have arthritis and some other issues. I love the handle on the sway. I don’t usually like cups that have the side handle. I just find those to be bulky, but I love the handle on the sway because even though I have small hands, sometimes I have to carry it versus putting it into my bag because I have a lot of things as being a teacher if you know you know. So I’m an advocate for cleaning your entire bottle and when I say entire bottle I mean take the little part and I don’t like 1 million gazillion pieces and I’m one that’s very thorough. I don’t just take a little brush through it. I take the seals off I take my watch a video first on it on TikTok and then because sometimes I don’t know how to clean the bottle lid and then of course I repeat that and I find this one to be extremely easy to clean even the piece that sits in the lid. I don’t know depend on the color you get mine is gray. I will just pop that out, clean it with the brush clean it however let it dry then put it all back together so you don’t get any type of mold because any water bottle you have you’re gonna have mold if you don’t clean your bottle and again I love this bottle and I did purchase it with my own money as I have no deal with them at all I’m not even vine reviewer( I wish)."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this water bottle for many reasons.  It checks off all of my requirements!  My list was particular and I didn’t think I’d find exactly what I wanted.The body is stainless steel and is quite sturdy, it keeps my water cold for about 24 hours and the 30 oz. size is perfect. It’s neither too big nor too small. It fits in my car’s cup holder, has a convenient carry handle, features a lock and unlock switch, has a dual spout with a straw and also a regular spout to drink out of, the mouthpiece is covered by a pop up lid that opens at the press of a button and protects the mouth area from dirt and germs. Last but not least is the pretty color. I bought the Out of the Blue color.Durable, sturdy, leakproof, easy to clean. The lid, straw and gaskets are dishwasher safe. The bottle itself should be hand washed so the finish doesn’t get ruined in a dishwasher.One point to consider is that this bottle is for cold liquids only, not for use with hot beverages. It’s by far the best water bottle I’ve had because it has so many great features.  Since it’s easy to carry around by the handle, I am finding myself taking it wherever I go in the house and I’m actually drinking more water because of it!Try it and you’ll fall in love with it just like I did!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Solid water bottle!!!. Not a water bottle person nor I do I really review anything but I like this is it a lot. Buy it. It’s worth it. Cool colors. The cherry one I got has a candy paint sparkle. simple ergonomic design. So far spill proof. Fits in cup holder and yea. Don’t get a Stanley get this instead."
    },
    {
        "review": "I didn't get into the Stanley craze-I've had too many accidental spills with the whole cup & straw set up. So when my kids started insisting I get an Owala, I was skeptical. But then I saw the TikTok of that one guy using his Owala as a weapon to fight off the men who attempted to break into his house, and not only did he stop them, his Owala survived with just a dent (and a broken handle, if memory serves me right)! Then Owala does the of the best PR stunt/customer appreciation ever, and not only sends that man a safe, but filled that safe with several Owala bottles! I admire a company that can back their products up; but I will support a business who listens and recognizes their customers too! So I started looking for one; I got to thinking as a woman who often does her errands alone, \"you know, I can always use it for defense and I can't be accused of carrying a weapon, because technically it's a water bottle.\"When Owala came out with this Amazon exclusive color, I knew it was kismet! I put it on my cart, but before I checked out, my kid saw what I was doing and she stopped me. She said, \"lady, I already bought that for you. It's coming next week.\" LOL I guess she got tired of telling me to get one, and just grabbed it for me, knowing that burgundy is one of my favorite colors!I've had it for 5 months now. It's a little dinged up on the bottom-nothing too bad. I just dropped it one or two times (maybe more). I love that the mouthpiece is covered up and can be locked so 1)it will always be clean; and 2)it won't accidentally spill if it tips over, or you know, you accidentally drop it. It keeps me accountable-I fill that 40 oz 2-3 times a day to make sure I stay hydrated. I love that it's insulated so I can keep my drink cold or hot-depending on what I fill it with. I love that it's easy to clean-there are no nook & crannies that can't be cleaned or reached! I just love it. Period."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love, love. Love this Owalla water bottle! It’s big enough to supply my needs and the body has flat side., just a tiny indented surface that makes it much easier to hold. I enjoy the sipping it allows so the beverage doesn’t come in an uncontrollable flow. With that you get a face wash ! But the open top allows for larger portions faster on days you’re really hot. I like the style of the bottle and the colors to choose from are so varied and stylish. In using this bottle it performs beautifully in keeping my beverage cold, even on the beach. I highly recommend this item👍‼️"
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been really happy with this bottle. The 30 oz size feels like the perfect middle ground—big enough that I'm not constantly refilling it, but not so big that it becomes a pain to carry around. It also fits in a standard cup holder, which was a must for me.It's surprisingly lightweight, and the bucket handle makes it really easy to grab and go.The only downside I've noticed is that ice doesn't last quite as long as some other insulated bottles because the lid isn't fully insulated. That said, it's not a dealbreaker for my use. It still keeps my water plenty cold throughout the day, and the convenience and design more than make up for it.I got the Dreamy Fields color and it looks even better in person. Overall, definitely recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very versatile, keeps water icy cold all day.  Has a built in straw, great colors offered and the lid also has a lock feature.  No worry about spills!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this Owala water bottle for a couple of months now, and it’s quickly become one of my favorites. I love the color, and the large handle makes it really easy to carry around throughout the day.One of my favorite features is the option to either sip directly from the spout or use the built-in straw. It’s nice having both options depending on what I’m doing.The only downside I’ve found is that the sip area can be a little tricky to clean thoroughly because of the design. It’s not a dealbreaker, but it does take a little extra attention when washing.Other than that, I’ve been extremely happy with it. I’ve run it through the dishwasher several times, and it still looks brand new. The finish has held up beautifully with no noticeable wear. Overall, it’s a well-made, durable water bottle that I’d definitely recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "EXCELLENT BOTTLE OF APARA AGUA"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Owala FreeSip Tumbler in Light Roasted exceeded my expectations. The color is stunning: a beautifully understated light beige with a subtle milk tea undertone. It feels warm, muted, and elegant, making it look far more refined than most tumblers out there.Its minimalist design looks clean and polished, whether on a desk or in a car cup holder. The carry handle is easy to use without compromising the lid’s locking function, making it secure and convenient for travel. Cleaning is straightforward thanks to the wide-mouth opening, which also makes it easy to add ice.If you’re looking for a tumbler that combines visual appeal with everyday practicality, this one is an excellent choice."
    },
    {
        "review": "Chugga chugga sip sip tech cannot be beaten. Colours are lovely, doesn’t spill. Good investment"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great quality! owala is truly the best.love the color."
    },
    {
        "review": "Aesthetic and functional! This Owala thermos is perfect, large capacity, keeps the liquid cold for many hours, its handle allows you to easily carry it anywhere and the best thing is its anti-spill system is completely safe!! I would buy it again."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Really happy with this water bottle. It’s a great size for everyday use, fits nicely in my car cup holder, and the 2-in-1 lid is convenient depending on how I want to drink. The insulation works well and keeps water cold for hours, and I haven’t had any issues with leaking. It also feels sturdy without being overly heavy. Overall, a well-designed bottle at a very reasonable price. Would definitely recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been really impressed with this POWCAN insulated water bottle. It keeps my drinks cold for hours, even in Florida heat, and the insulation works exactly as advertised. The build quality feels solid, the lid seals tightly, and the bottle is easy to carry around. I also like that it doesn’t sweat or leak, which makes it perfect for work, the gym, and travel. Overall, it’s a reliable, well‑made bottle that performs better than many more expensive brands. Highly recommended."
    },
