    {
        "review": "This definitely kept my drink called the entire day at the beach in 95 degree sunny weather. I was at the beach for 6 hours and the ice was still the same as it was when I filled it up that morning. Definitely a great buy ! Highly recommend! And the color was like a blueish purple which I absolutely loved !"
    },
    {
        "review": "Performance & Insulation:The Stanley IceFlow 2.0 Flip Straw Tumbler is a standout for anyone who needs their water to stay cold during long shifts or outdoor activities. Thanks to the double-wall vacuum insulation, it keeps drinks chilled for up to 12 hours and iced for a staggering 2 days. Unlike the popular Quencher, this model is designed specifically for cold liquids, making it incredibly efficient at maintaining temperature without the bulk of a multi-purpose lid.Design & Portability:One of the best features of the 20 oz size is its tapered base, which fits perfectly in standard car cup holders. The integrated folding handle makes it much easier to carry while walking or commuting compared to side-handle models. It’s also built with sustainability in mind, using recycled stainless steel and materials sourced from discarded fishing nets, so it feels as good to use as it looks.The Flip Straw Advantage:The leakproof flip straw is the highlight of the design. When snapped shut, you can toss this tumbler into a backpack or gym bag without worrying about a single drop escaping. The built-in straw allows for quick, upright sipping, which is much safer and more convenient while driving or exercising than tilting a traditional bottle. It’s also fully dishwasher safe, and the newer 2.0 version features a removable spout for even deeper cleaning.Verdict:If you want the durability and style of a Stanley but need something that is truly portable and leakproof, the IceFlow Flip Straw is the superior choice. It’s rugged, easy to carry, and fits into a busy, on-the-go lifestyle perfectly. A 5-star essential for anyone from students to outdoor enthusiasts."
    },
    {
        "review": "The ice inside lasts so long. I work where it gets very hot. It keeps my water cold for I want to say two days if I needed it to. The straw kinda sucks. You have to make sure you jammed the straw in tight, or it will fall out and can’t use the outer part of the straw.For being 40oz it’s not super heavy or bulky.The last gripe I have about this is the handle. It’s awkwardly shaped, so it can be hard to hold at first. You have to relearn how to hold a handle.My final note it’s that it doesn’t break or dent on concrete. I have dropped it about 1 1/2 feet off of the ground and it didn’t dent. I used to have a another brand of water bottled , and that would have destroyed it."
