[
    {
        "review": "I purchased this bottle just to try out in the summer of 2023. It is now the summer of 2026 and I still use it multiple times a week (only because I now have multiple Owalas and I have just ordered my third Owala FreeSip). I have used so many cups—Stanleys, Yetis, Hydrojugs, Hydroflask, etc—and the Owala is still my favorite. Here’s my favorite things about it:LEAKPROOF! This is the biggest one. I can throw it my bag and trust that everything will stay dry.THE SPOUT! Hands down the best spout I’ve ever used. I love that I can sip through the straw but then close the lid and keep my straw clean and not have any spills if it tips over. And then it also gives me the option to absolutely inhale water if I’m about to shrivel up from dehydration. I think this alone is why I now own three in different sizes.STAYS COLD! The 32 ounce holds ice for quite a while. It varies depending on how often I refill it but if I’m not constantly refilling it, it will hold ice for about 24 hours.THE SIZES! I love the size options. My original one was a 32 ounce and is a great middle ground for me. It holds enough water that I’m not refilling it every hour but it’s not huge. It’s great for work and this bottle will be going to live at my job. I just ordered the 40 ounce for home because I want a little more volume when I’m outside gardening but I can’t say much about the 40 ounce size yet. I also have a 16 ounce (kids size) that I use when I leave the house. It fits in a lot of my bags and it’s leakproof so I always have cold water with me. It’s perfect especially since I’m on medication that causes dehydration if I’m not careful.DISHWASHER SAFE! This one is self explanatory.It’s amazing and I love it. There are a few cons though. The first one is that the 32 ounce doesn’t fit in my cup holder. Not a huge deal since it’s leakproof—I just keep it on the passenger seat. But Owala does have cup holder friendly options now if that’s something you want.The bottle also does dent and scratch fairly easily. I dropped it getting out my car one day and it’s a little beat up now. Kind ugly, but it’s still my fave. It’s kinda disappointing because I have Yetis and Stanleys that have been through far worse and still look new. Just be mindful of that and baby it a little. Still 100% worth it though.Long story short, it’s a great bottle that will keep your water cold and everything else dry. As someone who has used this bottle regularly for years, I highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I freaking love this thing. I'm not a trend person, I go for function. And when my STB SIL got my fiancé a shiney new Stanley I decided it was time to replace my beat up Rtic with the mismatch lid and straw.I may not follow trends, but I didn't want my fiancé's cup to put mine to absolute shame!First off, can we all agree that the marshmallow is gorgeous? THIS cup is spectacular. Strange to say that about a water bottle, I know. But  since I never jumped on that train, I didn't know what I had been missing out on. Let me tell you what!The most important things to me is taking care of my service dog. She keeps me safe so her care is paramount to me. This enables me to pour my water into her bowl on the fly, without having to open my bottle past what I would do to drink from it. Quick and easy. That right there was the selling point for me. But as it turns out, there was even more benefit than that.I don't chug my water but if I did, the chug hole does works fine.The straw portion is ready to sip from, and it doesn't stick up tall like other water bottle straws. It's JUST tall enough to get the job done.  No worry of toppling over because the straw got knocked over by the cat. (Because that happens.)The \"handle\", which is generally the locking feature unless you're using it as a handle, is well placed and comfortable for my sized hands. Not to small and not clunky and large. STB SIL likes to talk about how great the Stanley handle is, which I don't really get. I like that this doesn't have a handle. I have one to carry it if I need it, and not if I don't.The seal is completely water tight. I occasionally put a drink mix in it and shake vigorously. No leaks whatsoever. In fact...It fits in a car cup holder upside down. That's how I transport it in the car. It doesn't fit butt down, so I put it top down. I've been known to do this with various bottles, so I tried it with this one and it fits ok. It's not ideal but it's better than nothing. Try it in yours! Since it's completely leak proof there's are no worries about spilling. (Just be careful when you remove it that it doesn't unlatch.)Another bonus of the covered straw is that germs don't get in the straw. Perfect because people in public often don't cover their sneezes. Ugh. And the coolest part? Lipstick messes are concealed with a flip of the lid! Easy peasy!I have noticed that the inside of the straw stains a little, which was disappointing. I don't like that I look at it and it looks dirty when it isn't. But I guess I shouldn't have used drink enhancers then. Also, my top color is very light. Other colors might not show that. Another thing that want fun was that when it fell, it dented! Oh no! So beware of that.It keeps my water super cold and I don't go anywhere without it. I love it so much that I'm thinking of getting another so I don't have to limit myself by style! Definitely worth the price since I use it constantly, every day.This one is so chill and Zen... The next one shall be colorful and crazy! One for every mood!I simply can't say enough about this darn water bottle... Does that mean I'm on trend now? Who knows! I just love my Owalla! I'm definitely a fan!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Owala water bottles for the win! These are hands-down our favorite water bottles. We have tried just about every popular brand out there—Yeti, Stanley, Hydro Flask, and others—and the Owala is the one that everyone in our family consistently reaches for.I absolutely love the versatility of the lid. You can use the built-in straw when you want to sip, or easily flip it open and drink straight from the opening. Having both options in one bottle is incredibly convenient, especially when you're on the go.The color combinations are also so fun! There are so many options to choose from, and the colors and designs make the bottles feel a little more personal and fun to use.Durability is another huge selling point. These bottles get used constantly and have been dropped and knocked around, yet they hold up extremely well. They seem much less prone to denting than some of the other brands we've tried, which is especially important when they're being used by kids.And, of course, they keep drinks really cold! We can fill them with ice and water, and they stay cold for hours. The lid also seals extremely well—we have never had an issue with them leaking in a bag.After trying so many different water bottles, Owala is definitely the winner for our family. They're durable, versatile, attractive, keep drinks cold, and don't leak. I honestly can't think of another water bottle brand we've liked as much!"
    },
    {
        "review": "As my first Owala I am so pleased with this water bottle. Keeps ice and water cold for hours, doesn’t leak, and love that you can use straw or spout. Great quality and liked the price. Only complaint is that it doesn’t fit in the car cup holders"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am absolutely thrilled with my Owala FreeSip stainless steel water bottle as it has quickly become my absolute favorite for every day use, and it is easily the best insulated bottle I have ever owned. The best part for me is the built- in straw. It allows me to sipupright or I can drink from the widemouth opening. The push button lock lid locks securely so I can toss it in my tote bag without worrying about any spills. The stainless steel keeps the water ice cold all day even if I leave it in my hot car! It has a convenient carry loop. It can be filled with large ice cubes, and it’s easy to clean. You will love it!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "We love this Owala! The 16 oz size is perfect for kids—big enough to hold plenty of water without being too heavy or bulky for them to carry around.The FreeSip design is probably my favorite part because they can sip through the straw or tilt it back to drink normally. It doesn’t leak all over the place, keeps water cold for a long time, and the covered spout stays cleaner than an exposed straw. The Read My Lips color is super cute, too.It’s held up really well to everyday kid use, which says a lot. Definitely worth the 5 stars!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this Owala for my son and really like it so far! My favorite feature is that you can drink from either the built-in straw or use the chug opening. It gives him both options without having to switch out lids or pieces, which is really convenient.The bottle itself feels sturdy and good quality, and the lid closes securely and has a handle that makes it easy to carry. The colors are also really fun and vibrant.My only concern is the coating on the outside. It feels like it may be somewhat easy to scratch, especially since this is going to be used by a kid and tossed into bags, taken to school, etc. We’ll see how it holds up over time!Overall, though, I’m really happy with it.I’ll update my review once I find out how sturdy it is."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love Owala bottles and I have several of the 24 oz.  I decided to get a larger size (32 oz.) this time to take to sporting events to hold more water.  Water stays cold all day like the others, and it never leaks.  The only downside is that it doesn't fit in my car or chair cupholders by just a fraction.  I kind of suspected that might be the case going in, so it doesn't bother me too much.  At games I just have to set it on the ground instead of my sports chair.  It just won't be my everyday bottle - I will continue to use the 24 oz for the car since it fits perfectly in the cupholder.  But Owala still gets 5 starts for the great design, easy to carry, and staying cold all day."
    },
    {
        "review": "Let's go, firstly, I LOVED the bottle, I was super excited for it to arrive and I don't regret buying it at all. It keeps the water cold for a LONG time (if you're like me and curious to know exactly when, a great example was that I put water in it WITHOUT ICE at 4 pm and the next day at 8 am when I woke up it was still cold as if it had just come out of the water filter, remembering that my filter has ice water). Her straw is amazing and super practical, but I also recommend buying one of those little brushes to clean. Plus, it's really beautiful and big. I bought the 945ml one and it's perfect for me, as it has a handle and the external material of the bottle is not slippery to the touch. Now talking about the negative points, the only negative point I have to mention here about this bottle is the delivery. I saw a lot of people complaining about the delay in delivery and it actually happened to me too, the shipping time is HUGE, I believe it's because of the number of people who buy this bottle, so it took a LONG time for them to ship, approximately a month. The delivery itself after shipping took a week +/-, so I believe it's actually a stock thing. The problem is that the bottle should come in a cardboard box, lined inside and everything. But in fact it came in a bag with nothing on it, just the bottle, wrapped in a small package with a DUBIOUS layer of bubble wrap. I even believe that this was the reason for the scratch in the photo (it's small, very small, and it's on the bottom, you practically can't even notice it, especially after I bought that silicone mold to put on the bottle). Anyway, the product is perfect, but they're quite wrong in the way they sent it, and it's not even because of the delay, but because of the damage caused to the products, since more people here had the same problem."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good, doesn't leak, keeps the temperature."
    },
    {
        "review": "Did not include the green ”cover” as shown.Other than that, I adore this bottle!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Really nice and holds so much water and keeps it cold for a really long time. The quality is worth it for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "A little expensive compared to average, but worth it! It keeps the temperature very well, but above all the possibility of drinking by suction thanks to the straw makes it easier to use even while driving! The colors are fantastic!"
