[
    {
        "review": "I didn't get the stickers for some reason but I'm not too worried about those.I absolutely LOVE this bottle. Its exactly what i wanted and the value for money to me is worth it.Its capacity of 64 oz is really good, it's just right for me. I love the appearance, the gradient colors are something Im a big fan of. So far, I've been using it for a week. Its sturdy and holds well. Keeps cold so long as you put enough ice inside. I use the straw primarily, and like the handle on that. Hydrating is easy with this giant thing, and I can add whatever flavors I like. Its stable and easy to use. I really recommend it. Im even considering getting one for my partner for their birthday, its worth it. (:"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this for $16. Absolutely the best deal around. There's not a lot to say beyond the fact that everything the manufacturer says is true. There's no catch for it. You're not going to order it and then find out that it's really just a picture of a water bottle or something crazy like that. You really get a 1/2 gallon insulated stainless steel bottle with a nice holder, alternative mouthpiece, and cleaning tools. If you get the two-tone effect, the colors even blend together very nicely.I just don't have anything to critique about this product. It's everything it claims to be and it does it very well. I haven't performed any scientific experiments regarding temperature retention, but so far, it seems  to keep water cold for at least as long as my more expensive 32oz \"Beast\" bottle. So...As far as the weight is concerned, it's exactly as heavy as you would expect a large double-walled steel bottle to be. That is to say, it ain't light. There's a reason it comes with a holder you can hang from your shoulder. But really, if you're looking at this item, you don't care about the weight. Why? Because even if the bottle were weightless, the weight of 64oz of fluid is going to be heavy. Go pick up a half gallon of milk. That's how heavy it will be. Making the milk jug out of steel doesn't change how heavy that feels in any significant way. ."
    },
    {
        "review": "I couldn’t be happier with this 1-gallon jug. If you struggle to drink enough water throughout the day or just need a massive supply for outdoor trips, this is exactly what you need.​The double-wall insulation is no joke—I’ve filled it up with ice water, left it out in the hot sun all day, and still had solid ice chunks hours later. The build quality is incredibly rugged and durable. It comes with two different lids (a straw top and a spout top), which is awesome because you can customize it to how you prefer to drink.​The carrying pouch is a game-changer. It has a heavy-duty shoulder strap that makes lugging a full gallon around much easier plus the built-in zippered pocket is perfect for holding small items. As a bonus, the included cleaning brushes make scrubbing a breeze, and the stickers let you customize it right out of the box. Highly recommended for anyone who works outdoors, hikes, or hits the gym hard!"
    },
    {
        "review": "What's not to like?  It keeps my water cold on a hot summer day in South Carolina--even in a parked car!  It has a sturdy paracord handle, the top unscrews but still stays attached to the bottle so you don't lose it, it has a carrying case that makes it easy to carry and still be hands-free, has extra accessories like a carabiner and stickers, and it looks great!  I came to buy another one for my husband! (I can't speak to the funtionality of the straw because I don't use that option.)"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got the 64 ounce and I really like it. I like the insulator and shoulder strap because I take this with when I go work at my farm or workout and it has a small pocket for my inhaler and other related items. The only thing I was missing was the straws. And sometimes it does leak if everything isn't put together just so. It comes with a lot of extras though and I really appreciate it. It also stays cold for a very long time."
    },
    {
