[
    {
        "review": "I've been using this water bottle for everyday use and have been really happy with it overall. It keeps my water cold, and the size is great without feeling overly bulky or difficult to carry around. I also haven't had any issues with leaking, which is important with a bottle like this.The straw works well most of the time, although I've noticed that it can occasionally be difficult to use. It's a minor inconvenience, but it's something I've experienced with the lid.Overall, I really like the size and insulation, and it's been a good everyday water bottle for me."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this water bottle! It actually keeps my water cold for a long time, even after carrying it around all day. I love that it has two different ways to drink from it. It also doesn't leak, feels really good quality, and the pink color I got is super super cute. Definitely worth buying!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased this bottle hoping it would keep my water cold throughout each day as we traveled in hot environments in our car.  So when I received this bottle, I did a \"cold test\" in my home.  I totally filled the bottle with ice, then finished it off by filling the remaining spaces with water.  The ice was still there that night.  The next day (Day 2), I checked it in the morning:  still a lot of ice.  I checked it again that night (still a very large \"clump\" of ice).  The following day (Day 3), I again checked in the morning to find there were still a few little ice cubes still floating in the bottle.  WOW!  When I will be traveling in a hot environment in our car for an upcoming trip, I expect the bottle to at least keep the ice and water cold throughout each day of travel.  I will do the same thing every day of our trip to ensure I have something cold to sip.  Good job, Encool!  I am very pleased!  So pleased that I immediately purchased a 2nd bottle for my husband!  It feels like it is made of great quality.  The handle is wide enough for my four fingers to grasp.  Something I hadn't noticed is that the handle area closest to the bottle lid isn't just a 90-degree angle; it is made with a 45-degree angle at each side so your fingers rest more comfortably when holding the bottle.  The lid has both the straw-sip and the chug options, and work great.  I turned the full bottle on its side all night and there were no leaks.  This may just be the perfect water bottle for us!Update after 1.5 weeks of hot environment travel:  These water bottles were the only ones among our group of travelers that kept the water cold,  They worked so well, we didn't even have to fill the entire bottle with ice and then fill the remaining spaces with water.  Instead, we were able to put about 1/3 of the space as ice, and the rest as water.  Still, by the end of the day, ice remained--even after drinking all the water.  I ended up leaving the chug and straw features open through the day to try to melt the ice on the first few days before I began changing the ice to water ratio.We love these bottles.  They are perfect for us!Also, the \"boots\" we purchased from Amazon fit perfectly and worked perfectly:  https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D7D4MYYK?ref=ppx_yo2ov_dt_b_fed_asin_title&th=1"
    },
    {
        "review": "I LOOOOOVE this water bottle. It never leaks. The straw suction is perfect. The handle is sturdy. And it stays cold for a long time (indoors). I like that it has the regular drinking spout option but I rarely use it because the vacuum it causes makes it hard to chug water. But would 10/10 recommendations this bottle!! Way better than Stanley and Arctic"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love these bottles.  The 26oz is perfect size.  Fits car cup holders, the handle is very convenient, the can key water cool for a day.  The only critique I have with the Indian Kaki color and the Pewter Blue (returned) is that the color of the cap and the bottle is not a perfect match and that’s bothersome.  That’s why I didn’t give it a 5-star review.  The Cotton Candy color doesn’t have that problem.  I ordered a 24oz charcoal gray color of this same brand.  If it fits my cup holders I’ll be returning this one (Indian Kaki) unused.MACARON CAT- Beautiful!!!!  It was a gift for my cat-loving daughter.  She loves it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Easy to clean. So easy to use that my youngest has no issues using flip spout for now. I love that once she is more coordinated, she can use the other spout as well. She loves that it is bright pink and mommy loves that it has survived several drops already with no dents. No leaks when closed. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a great water bottle. I needed a small one to carry when traveling. This bottle fit my needs. It’s just the right size, easy to clean, and keeps my water cold. It doesn’t hurt that it’s so cute too. I highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "Awesome little bottle; just finished a vacation and it was the perfect size for staying hydrated throughout the day while not being too big to carry around. Amazing insulation, too! If I put ice water in this overnight, usually there will still be unmelted ice in it by morning. Cleans very easily and I really like the lid options; I use the twist-off cap for pouring electrolyte mix or flavor packets, while I use the small spout for drinking.After one month of use, it has one dent (shown in photo) but that’s from the bottle accidentally being dropped on a concrete floor. Thankfully it doesn’t affect how it sits or anything. This thing is still very durable without being heavy.The only issue I’d bring up (shown in photo) is that the plastic of the drinking spout is kind of rough on the edges of the hole. It almost cut my lip the first time I used this (I wasn’t very careful inspecting it the first time I used it), and I have to pull off tiny flecks of plastic from it once in a while to make sure I’m not drinking any of the flecks. Really not ideal, but I prefer a plastic spout to a rubber one that could break. Even so, I figured it was worth mentioning, especially since a water bottle this size is often purchased for kids to use. (Also! Be sure the drinking spout is empty before you close it; if you don’t, the spout will leak a tiny bit of water when moved.)Having said all this, I still really like this water bottle. I wanted something small but durable for travel that kept cold water cold, in a bottle without a lot of loud branding on it. This one is super sturdy, with amazing insulation, in a convenient size, and in a really lovely neutral color! Recommended, if you can look past the rough plastic bit. Be sure to inspect it before using it!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Nice color! I got this for my husband's birthday since he's a big pickleball player. It worked perfectly; no leaks, and he said it keeps his drinks cold. He loves that it fits in his truck's cup holder. I'd totally buy this again, it's great for everyday use or sports. The handle is a nice touch too, I noticed that's how he carries it. Overall, I think it's a good, solid water bottle, probably one of the better ones. It's a bit pricier, but my husband isn't exactly gentle with his stuff, so I think this can handle him dropping it or whatever he does with it during pickleball.😄"
