    {
        "review": "Fits in my cup holder which is a big win for me. I like the handle, and I can also drink from it while holding from the handle, which I wasn't sure I would be able to do at first, but I am happy to say that I can. That would've been a deal breaker for me if I wasn't able to, but so far this cup has been a great addition to my cup collection. I don't think it's quite 40 oz, it doesn't hold as much water as my 40 oz. Owala. I can easily put two 16.9 water bottles in here and it's about a 1/2\" from the lid threads. That puts me at 33.8 ounces. I wish it was actually 40 for my water tracking, but everything else makes this a win. I also like that there are flat indents on each side, which makes it easier to grip the wider upper portion when drinking that way. Sometimes I also grip it from the thinner bottom area, especially when it's not full. Color is perfect for me. The only slight complaint that I might have is that the straw is a good size, but I wish it was just the tiniest bit wider. I tend to wait until I'm extremely thirsty and then chug. My Owala suits that just a tad better, but it doesn't fit in a cup holder so I find myself reaching for this one more"
