[
    {
        "review": "Time and time again a continued purchase. No need for fancy water. Or toted as best. This water which is just water is straight forward and has a refreshing and clean taste in the mouth. Our family uses this for refreshing taste and reliability in exceptional pricing."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have always trusted Amazon for offering top-notch products, and their own brand, Happy Belly, is no exception. From my experience, I can confidently say that the Happy Belly Purified Water delivers exceptional quality and has become a staple in my household.First and foremost, the taste of this purified water is clean and refreshing. It lacks any unpleasant aftertaste, making it perfect for drinking on its own or using as a base for beverages like tea, coffee, or smoothies. The water is crystal clear and has a pleasant mouthfeel, leaving me feeling hydrated and satisfied.One of the aspects that impressed me the most about Happy Belly Purified Water is its commitment to quality and safety. The bottle is made from durable and 100% recyclable plastic, ensuring the water remains uncontaminated until consumed. Additionally, the water undergoes a meticulous purification process, removing any impurities and leaving behind a pure, crisp taste.The pack size, containing 24 bottles, is ideal for my household needs, and the compact design allows for easy storage in my pantry or refrigerator. The bottles are also convenient to grab and go, making it perfect for keeping hydrated while on the move or during outdoor activities.Moreover, I greatly appreciate the affordability of Happy Belly Purified Water compared to other brands in the market. It offers exceptional value for money without compromising on quality. The subscription option offered by Amazon also ensures that I never run out of water, as it can be conveniently delivered right to my doorstep.Lastly, I commend Amazon for their commitment to sustainability. The Happy Belly Purified Water bottles are easily recyclable, and Amazon actively encourages customers to recycle them responsibly.In conclusion, I highly recommend Happy Belly Purified Water to anyone seeking a reliable and refreshing source of hydration. With its excellent taste, commitment to quality, and affordability, this Amazon brand has become my go-to choice for purified water. Stay hydrated with Happy Belly and enjoy the convenience of having it delivered right to your doorstep!"
    },
    {
        "review": "What a deal! The price is right. There is a “purified” water taste to these found in all purified bottled water no matter the cost. I’ve been mixing in propel powder and xtend powder and even drinking them with no enhancement. They’re a bargain and make adding water easy to my hydration  strategy. I photographed a bottle with 3 other 16.9 oz bottles to see the size differences."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been really impressed with the Amazon Grocery brand bottled water. It tastes great—clean and refreshing—and honestly we prefer it over several of the name-brand waters we’ve tried. It’s also priced really reasonably, which helps a lot for a busy household.I have several kids who are involved in sports, and while we do our best to remember reusable water bottles, that doesn’t always happen when everyone is rushing out the door. I like keeping a case of these on hand for practices, games, and last-minute needs.It’s a simple product, but the quality and value make it a great staple to keep around. Definitely one we’ll keep buying."
    },
    {
        "review": "I DO NOT like or will drink tap water. which means i have tried many kinds of bottled water. Compared to other bottled water not only is this a low price but the taste is great and fresh. I don't get any plastic after taste and it gets delivered on schedule to my door."
    },
    {
        "review": "Amazon Grocery Purified Water is honestly a solid and affordable option for everyday drinking water. The water tastes clean, purified, and refreshing, and I haven’t had any issues drinking it regularly. It does not leave a strange aftertaste, and overall it feels like a reliable product for daily use.One thing I would like Amazon Grocery and Amazon to improve is making the plastic bottles a little stronger and more durable, especially during delivery and carrying multiple packs.I would also love to see more quantity options available, such as 30+ bottle boxes, along with larger bottle sizes like 1L purified water options for people who drink a lot of water throughout the day.Another great improvement would be expanding the variety of water choices, including spring water, alkaline water, flavored zero sugar water, and specialty water options designed for people managing diabetes or healthier lifestyles.It would also be nice to see Amazon Grocery continue expanding affordable water options for SNAP users, low-income individuals, and families who rely on grocery delivery and budget-friendly products.Overall, this is still a really good purified water product, and I appreciate Amazon Grocery continuing to improve and expand their grocery selections."
    },
    {
        "review": "Quality"
    },
    {
        "review": "If you want no-drama drinking water for the house, car, gym bag, or emergencies, Amazon’s purified water bottles do exactly what they should: taste clean, stay sealed, and not cost a fortune. It’s the kind of neutral, crisp water you don’t think about—which is the whole point.What I notice (and why I keep rebuying)Clean, neutral taste: Chilled, it’s refreshing with no plasticky aftertaste. Because it’s purified (typically reverse osmosis) with a touch of minerals added for taste, it doesn’t have the “salty” edge some spring waters do.Grab-and-go size: The 16.9-oz (500 mL) bottles fit cup holders, treadmill holders, and backpack side pockets perfectly.Consistent seals: Caps twist off with a clean pop; I haven’t hit leakers or half-sealed bottles.Value: Case price per bottle is hard to beat, especially for keeping a few packs on hand for guests or a go-bag.Where it shinesDaily hydration: Easy way to track intake—four bottles gets most adults near their daily goal.Workouts & errands: Neutral flavor is ideal when you’re sweaty; it doesn’t fight with electrolytes or mixes.Coffee machine/steamer safe: Purified water reduces mineral build-up vs. hard tap (still descale on schedule).Emergency stash: Two cases on a shelf = peace of mind for outages/boil advisories.The honest nits (no sugar-coating)Bottle thinness: They’re lightweight by design. Great for portability, not meant for multiple refills. If you squeeze hard, they’ll crinkle.Shrink-wrap case: The plastic wrap can tear if you grab from the side—lift from the bottom to avoid the cascade-of-bottles moment.Taste preference: If you love the mineral “snap” of spring water, purified can feel a bit “flat.” That’s normal—this aims for neutral, not terroir.Tips to get the best out of themChill them. Purified water tastes best cold; keep a rotation in the fridge.Store smart. Keep sealed cases in a cool, odor-free spot—water can absorb nearby smells.Freeze hack: Half-drain a bottle, freeze it upright, then top with fresh water before heading out for a long day—instant ice pack + cold water for hours.Recycle everything your local program accepts (bottle + cap + label where allowed). Day-to-day, use a reusable bottle and lean on these for travel/emergencies.Bottom lineIf you’re after clean taste, reliable packaging, and real value, Amazon’s purified water bottles deliver. They’re an easy “set it and forget it” staple—perfect for stocking the pantry without overthinking it."
    }
]

