[
    {
        "review": "Nalgene bottles just work.The Nalgene bottle is perfect for those who enjoy outdoors activities. As funny as it is to say it \"just works\" when it's as simple as a bottle, it absolutely does.For starters the material. Not only is it BPA-free, the Tritan material is perfect for a drinking bottle. It's extremely rugged, in fact Nalgene has gained a reputation for how long their bottles last. It also doesn't leave much of a taste! A lot of my experience with plastic bottles is that you can taste the plastic, the problem persists with metal as well. Nalgene bottles have a fairly neutral taste. It's also very resistant to trapping odors and tastes. My problem with alternatives is that if you hold coffee in them for a long time, then your water tastes like coffee even after a clean.1L is a perfect amount of water to hold in my opinion. It's enough to be usable, but not overkill to where it's not a functional bottle. It's great for day to day use as well, I find myself finishing a Nalgene just fine. The size is great in this aspect, it doesn't waste space with insulation. I find a lot of metal bottles and other plastic bottles can only ever hold 500ml and some change because of their shape.The leak proof seal just works. A lot of bottles are finicky, if you screw the cap from an angle it still leaks. I've tried to do it from an angle but it always screws on properly, I've never had a problem with it spilling.Overall the Nalgene is the perfect bottle. It's a good middle ground of everything while having its strengths in durability, build quality, and price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this bottle. Cute color, hardy and stands up to drops and dings perfectly. Fits 32oz and then some which is perfect if you’re trying to drink more water in the day. No leaks, easy to clean and easy to clip to a bag or just carry around. Highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like the simplicity of this water bottle! No straws, no complicated lids, no weird tiny parts that are impossible to clean, this is just a simple water bottle that you’ll actually end up using every day. I got it in the color “cotton,” and it’s honestly such a nice neutral shade, knd of a soft beige that looks way more expensive than it is. The wide mouth is one of my favorite features because it makes cleaning super easy and also makes it easy to add ice. I also really like the ounce/milliliters markings on the side of the bottle, it became surprisingly helpful to me for keeping track of how much water I’m actually drinking throughout the day. This is actually my second Nalgene bottle, I bought this one to replace my older one because plastic bottles should be replaced once in a while, especially after heavy everyday use. My previous one lasted a long time though, which says a lot. The only downside is that because there’s no straw and the opening is pretty wide, drinking from it while walking or moving around can be a little awkward unless you’re careful.Overall, really happy with it. Simple, durable, lightweight, and super practical, which honestly matters more to me than trendy designs ;)"
    },
    {
        "review": "The best and most dependable water bottles out there. No need for janky o-rings. The build tolerances are so tight that you just twist the lid snug and it won’t leak. Great color and the wide mouth is easy to clean.Only drawback?  When you put cold stuff in it, the condensation will get on stuff."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is the perfect water bottle for those who want to get their daily water intake. It has the measurements and a wide mouth opening that makes cleaning easy. No straws to wash just the bottle and attached lid. Nalgene products are also very durable and affordable."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using Nalgene bottles for years, but this Sustain 32 oz. Wide Mouth Water Bottle in the clear finish is my new absolute favorite. I love being able to see exactly how much water I have left at a glance, and it makes measuring out hydration mixes or tracking my daily intake incredibly easy.The biggest selling point for me is the new Sustain material. It is made from 50% recycled plastic, but it retains the legendary toughness you expect from the brand. I have already dropped this bottle onto solid concrete while getting out of my truck, and it didn't crack, shatter, or leak a single drop—just a tiny, barely noticeable scuff. The classic wide mouth is fantastic because it easily accommodates large ice cubes, fits perfectly with most backpacking water filters, and makes cleaning out the bottle manually an absolute breeze. The leak-proof loop top is rock solid, and it attaches perfectly to a carabiner for clipping onto a backpack or gym bag. There are absolutely no weird plastic tastes or odors right out of the box, either. If you want a dependable, indestructible, and eco-friendly water bottle for hiking, camping, or everyday use, this clear Nalgene is an absolute classic that will last for years."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good water bottle for the price, love the colors. No issues with leaking but wish it fit in a cup holder"
    },
    {
        "review": "I've used a lot of water bottles over the years, and the Nalgene 32 oz Wide Mouth is still one of the best. Super durable, lightweight, and completely leak proof. I've dropped it multiple times and it barely shows any wear. The wide mouth makes it easy to clean and perfect for adding ice cubes. Great for the gym, hiking, work, and everyday use. Simple design, but built like a tank."
    },
    {
        "review": "Over the years, I've had about four of these in different colours. The only reason I've ever replaced them is because I appear to lose a water bottle every 2.5 years!Really nice vibrant colours that don't fade or chip like an anodised bottle would + it's dishwasher safe with no noticeable degradation to quality. The quality on Nalgene has always been exceptional and lasted many many hiking trips + every survives every day life. 1L is the perfect size for me.While some may say ~£20 is steep, I have had no problem ordering another without a second thought on price the instant I realise I've lost one."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent water bottle, the wide opening allows you to easily wash the inside."
    },
    {
        "review": "As good as any Nalgene, durable and I love the colour. Perfect for adventures."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using Nalgene bottles for a long time. There are so many colors to choose from, and they're all so stylish that it's hard to choose. I can see how much water I drink in a day, which is very helpful."
    },
    {
        "review": "Lovely colour, great bottle"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I'm in love. This water bottle is everything I could ask for. Its easy to clean, cute, and very easy to use. Nothing is so tight or stiff that it wont function properly or anything. I have the 24oz one so it's light even with ice in it and fits in my car cup holder without any issue. I'm able to even plop it into my purse without it taking up much room. In my experience so far, I've had no issues with leaking either. It keeps ice cold for almost the entire day. It has a slip proof silicone bottom that keeps it sturdy but doesn't catch fluff or animal hair on it.My boyfriend also has the same water bottle, but in a different color, and he's dropped it a million times. His still works properly, isn't dented, and is still leak proof."
    },
    {
        "review": "Title: Great Water Bottle for Sports and CampLandon has been using this water bottle for baseball practices and games, swim practice, and summer camp, and it has worked great. It’s a good size for kids, easy to carry, and holds enough water to get him through his activities without needing constant refills.The insulation works well and keeps drinks cold, even when it’s hot outside. We haven’t had any issues with leaks, and it has held up well to daily use. The blue color looks nice, and the price was very reasonable for the quality.Overall, we’re very happy with this purchase and would definitely buy it again."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a great water bottle for travel. I carried it all over the UK with me and it was very durable, no leaks, no problems. It kept my water cool and was a good size to fit in the side pocket of my bag love how many cute colors there are and the quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought two for my kids (9 1/2-years-old and almost 4-years-old) the Peach Purple and Frost Blue. They come looking exactly as described. I love that not only are they leak proof, but the texture of the bottle has a slightly bumpy feel to add friction so you are less likely to drop it. I also love that the spout is not a straw. It is molded at the top to act like a water bottle but has a piece that acts as a barrier to guide the water into your mouth rather than just pouring out. Will make drinking out of it immediately gratifying without being messy which is exactly what we need to survive our Disney vacation this August. Water stayed cold overnight with just a few ice cubes in each. The 18 Oz is perfect for kids or adults who need a more compact water bottle."
    },
    {
        "review": "My friends were trying to convince we to buy an owala, but the color I wanted wasn’t available in the 20 oz, so I decided to give this a try. I am so glad I did, because I actually like this one better! Looking at them both, they are very similar in design, but one main difference is that to drink from the o straw, you sip from the same opening where you free sip. This one has a straw piece that flips up behind the free sip area, which I like better. The cap seems sturdier, and the when the handle is down you can still press the button to open the cap to free sip. On the o, the handle prevents you from pressing the button, so you need to lift the handle to open the top to drink from it—I guess whether this is a pro or con depends on whether you want the button to be blocked or not. The button on this one is also easier to press to pop the top up. It does not leak at all, it fits in my car cup holder, and it kept my water cold for the 6 hours it took me to drink it. Even though I balked at spending $20 on a water bottle, it’s still cheaper than the other one by a fair amount, and I love the color—I will definitely be buying more in the other sizes!Edit: There are a few things I’ve noticed since I bought and have been using both the Encool and my Owala of the same size (35oz). The carrying handle is wider on the Encool, which I like better, and the bottom is rubberized, which is not the case on my o bottle. BUT one thing that this company needs to fix is that the top does not flip back far enough, so you are forced to tilt the bottle pretty far up when free sipping because it sticks into your forehead. I’m changing my review to 4 stars because this is pretty annoying, especially when I use the bottle to drink water, which I prefer to free sip.Dear Encool: Fix this problem and offer replacement tops to people who have already bought your bottles. They are perfect in every way EXCEPT for this incredibly annoying feature!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm really enjoying using it.It's really beautiful and I love the raised cats pattern and the color of the handle. It's very comfortable to hold.I mostly use it around the house, but I did take it out once or twice.I put it inside my bag because it's a bit too big for the side pocket. It was also too large for the cupholder in my car, but I still enjoy it.I mostly drink out the spout. I tried the chug top once or twice but the lid kept hitting my forehead, so not very pleasant.I do like how well it keeps cold. I have it by me now and the drink is still cold from last night, which is awesome.My black cat also approves. Photo attached"
    },
    {
        "review": "Best bottle ever!!!! It has a carrying handle andI Love that it has the straw and (open) lip feature . It HOLDS the temperature!!! Brought it filled with ice water to work one morning. Left it that evening. Didn’t get back to office until 2 pm next day… STILL had ICE!!!!! Love this bottle. It’s very strong and can be used to protect while hiking. lol. Gonna get another."
    },
    {
        "review": "Keeps my water cold for a very long time compared to other bottles I've had. It's also cute and a very good alternative to an Owala because it's cheaper."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great travel mug! Coffee stays hot for a long time!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "These are my favorite water bottles! I travel a lot for work and have a family always on the go. These bottles stand up to being knocked around, tipped over, thrown in bags, backpacks, purses, under airplane seats, thwon in the front seat, and they don't leak. They're durable and the perfect size for me (I get the 32 oz. size). I drink my water room temp so I don't need to lug around a stainless steel insulated cup, they're too bulky and heavy. My absolute fav feature is the free flow spout, I don't like water bottles that have a straw, this is free flow and I can take a big gulp or small sip. I'd love to see some bright yellow in the color lineup!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been through TOO MANY water bottles in my life. The plastic ones shatter when dropped, the metal ones dent when dropped, and they're all just so easy TO DROP. And the LEAKS! I can't even tell you how many puddles I've caused from toting my water bottles around with me on the daily.I bought this water bottle for one reason: the PRICE. I was not looking for a good water bottle at the time, I guess because I stopped believing they were out there in the world, so I bought a cheap one assuming that it would have some kind of design flaw or break when I dropped it in a couple of weeks. I was WRONG! This is, hands down, THE BEST WATER BOTTLE I HAVE EVER OWNED. I have had it for over a year now, and I tote it with me on the daily, always on the move walking from class to class on a large outdoor college campus.There are THREE things that make this the best water bottle in the world:1. It is HARD TO DROP, even for me! I just hook my finger through that little bendy hooky thing up top, close my fist, and that sucker stays on me! I walk everywhere with this thing, and when I'm holding it through the loop, it is basically UNDROPPABLE! When I'm drinking from it, the little hand indentation up at the top of the water bottle is a very comfortable fit, and even when the bottle is full and heavy, it feels very balanced.2. WHEN I drop it, it DOESN'T BREAK! Let's face it: I am forgetful and clumsy. There are times when I don't hold the bottle the undroppable way. There are times when the bottle is sitting on my desk and I accidentally swipe it off. There was even this one time when I threw it into the air and then failed to catch it. But through all these drops, this bottle has not cracked yet. And a couple of my drops have been when the bottle was fullish. That being said, I haven't had TOO many major drops (thanks to the bottles undroppableness) so I wouldn't try pushing your luck with this one. But alot can be said just from the fact that this bottle has survived a year of daily use with ME, a certified water bottle destroyer.3. IT DOESN'T LEAK! This bottle has something that's hard to find these days: A TOP THAT ACTUALLY WORKS! I have NEVER experienced a single leak with this bottle - NOT EVEN ONE! I throw my bottle into my bookbag all the time, with precious lecture notes and expensive textbooks, some of which are rented and must be returned, and I can do so with FULL CONFIDENCE that my water bottle will not leak on them! I'm not talking the side pocket of my bookbag, I am talking in the main zipper with all of my other stuff. I make ZERO EFFORT to be careful when the bottle is in my bookbag.  All day long that bookbag bumps into desks, walls, people, gets turned upside down, gets thrown on the floor, sat on, turned upside down, etc. This sucker doesn't leak.And that's it. THREE things that go into making the PERFECT WATER BOTTLE. This water bottle also has the added benefit of having a killer price (I was happy to pay the price I paid for it even when I was still assuming it was nothing special). It also holds 40 ounces of water, which is kind of a large amount of water compared to most water bottles. I bought this bottle with ZERO EXPECTATIONS, and it has turned out to be one of my favorite buys from Amazon to date. It definitely sparks joy in my life! Thank you, Pogo water bottles. You have created something of VALUE."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this water bottle. I had been lugging around a 64oz bottle that could barely fit in the side pockets of my backpack, and while it was nice to have during 12 hour shifts, I got sick of it.I got the purple bottle with the chug lid. The color is beautiful, the design of the bottle is very cute and elegant, and the actual hole you drink from is much more desireable to me than the straws/nips a lot of bottles use nowadays. Even though it is only 32oz, I find that I don't mind refilling it once a day to get in my 64oz. I actually prefer it to a 64oz bottle, since I know I'll be getting fresh, cool water after the first fill runs out.I've seen some comment that you can't actually \"chug\" with this bottle...well, of course you can't! The bottle isn't the thin, bendable plastic that you get with the water bottles from the store...it's sturdy!! And while you can't \"chug,\" you can most certainly get some big gulps in! I'm not a slow water drinker. I don't want tiny sips, I want to get that +64oz in! This bottle is definitely good for that. You can easily get 4oz, and even more, in a single gulp. Haha, I even did it now, just to be sure...I really love this thing. It is exactly what I was looking for, and the price is great. The lid is also very easy to open and close, but still very sturdy and secure. It also seems quite easy to clean, though I haven't had to do so just yet.For those who have seen mold growth on their water bottles...you must wash these things at LEAST once a week, if not more often, especially if you wear anything on your lips like chapstick, lipstick, etc. Even the slight bit of backwash from out filthy human mouths is enough to contaminate the insides of the bottle. If you live in a warmer climate, this is especially true and will result in the bacteria from your backwash contaminating the bottle resulting in the growth of things like mold. It has happened to me before and I was absolutely mortified. Another reason I prefer chug lids as opposed to straws...the things are a hell of a lot easier to clean. No hidden crevices harboring disgusting human bacteria...lol.I definitely recommend this water bottle for those of you looking to increase your intake. Very pretty, convenient, and simple to clean with the chug lid."
    },
