[
    {
        "review": "Actually holds cold all day, leak proof, the insulated 32-oz. size fits in the larger cup holes in a Ford Explorer and a 2014 F-150 (the cupholder in the middle closer to the floor), and best of all, there is NO plastic touching the water or tea or whatever you store in it - it's stainless steel all around, including the screw-on top.  There is a small circular seal of what appears to be silicone at the top of that screw-on top, but it isn't in contact with the liquid inside this insulated water bottle.  I also tested how well it would insulate hot liquids by boiling some water, steeping tea, and then filling the water bottle with hot tea - and it stayed hot all day.  It is stamped 304 in the bottom of the inside of the water bottle, indicating that this is supposed to be 304 stainless steel, which is supposed to be the same as 18/8 stainless steel - non-magnetic.  Feel free to comment below if you know of a water bottle with superior quality steel out there, but thus far it has held up well and it's the best water bottle I've tried.  The stainless steel exterior finish option still has a decent grip, I also bought one in green and it has a very good gripping surface as well.  These seem to be designed to be carried by the handle that is part of the screw-on top - which also doubles as a more ergonomic way to open the bottle at the end of the day.  As for the blue one, the color seemed a bit darker than it had appeared on my screen, more slate/grayish with some navy, so I didn't keep the blue one.  The green was very much the green as it appeared on my screen, and the stainless steel finish was my husband's favorite.  It's a great value, and I love how it can work for both cold and hot liquids.  I definitely recommend this insulated water bottle over their non-insulated model - the last thing you want is to return to your vehicle on a hot day and have your previously chilled water warm, or your warm tea cool when it's cold weather.  This insulated model works great outdoors and indoors, and if you're running errands or you're going to be driving and just want to leave your water bottle in the car, it holds up well."
    },
