        "review": "excellent product"
    },
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love these Gatorade 32 Oz Squeeze Water Sports Bottles! The new easy grip design makes them super comfortable to hold, whether I'm hitting the gym or out for a run. The size is perfect, holding just the right amount of water to keep me hydrated throughout my workout without being too bulky. They're durable too, which is a big plus for me as I tend to be pretty active. I also appreciate how easy they are to clean and refill, making them convenient to use every day. Overall, these bottles have become my go-to choice for staying hydrated, and I highly recommend them to anyone who's looking for quality and functionality in their sports water bottles."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great squeeze water bottle. Perfect for drinking on the go."
    },
    {
        "review": "For the price, I'd say go for it if you need a bottle that simply excels... at being a bottle. If you want something more consistent, I'd suggest looking for something different. However, this bottle works perfectly for me.Pros:For starters, it holds 1 liter, which is exactly what I need. Second, you can squeeze it for pressure, I personally like drinking water as fast as possible and the squeezing helps a lot! Finally, it's not over-complicated, it's easy to refill and carry with you anywhere you go.Cons:Don't expect the graphic to last, it's going to scrape off eventually, regardless of wether you are somewhat 'aggressive' with your bottle or not, but I'd say that makes sense especially given the price. Second, the lid can unscrew easily and it can be somewhat tedious to screw it back on, you won't believe how often I've had cases where the lid was screwed improperly, you can't screw it if you are on a rush. I've also had instances where I screwed on the lid properly and then the bottle unscrewed itself from the motion of my bag, that was really annoying, but it only happened once, so it might possible that I didn't screw tight enough. Finally,  the bottle doesn't have a conventional 'lid', it's just somewhat of an open 'nozzle' that opens whenever you squeeze the bottle. You don't have anything to close the nozzle with, so I wouldn't recommend this bottle if you plan on placing it somewhere tight where it might be squeezed and spill all over the place."
