[
    {
        "review": "I’m really impressed with this water bottle. The material feels very strong and durable; it has a solid, high-quality weight to it that makes it feel much more expensive than it actually is. For the price, it’s an amazing value.The Cotton Candy color is beautiful and exactly as pictured. It’s vibrant and fun without looking cheap.What impressed me the most is how well it keeps water cold. My water stayed ice cold for a full 24 hours, literally like it had just come out of the fridge.Overall, this is a well-made, affordable, and reliable bottle, and I would definitely purchase it again. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased this bottle so that I could keep it handy and increase the amount of water that I drink every day. However, it morphed into being one of my favorite buys of the year for many reasons.If you aren’t sure that you want to purchase one, here’s a few reasons that may seal the deal for you.The bottle comes with 3 lids, and they are all well made and easy to use. You can choose your preference. All of these lids work perfectly, depending on your drinking style. Of course, if one of the lids stops working correctly, you can replace it or use one of the others.I add ice and cold water to my bottle, as needed, in the morning and at night. The ice stays frozen throughout the day and overnight, even in the heat. In the seldom case that the ice melts, the water generally stays cool.The appearance is beautiful as well. You will enjoy using this water bottle and you can be sure that it will last. People will notice and ask you about it. As a bonus, it is hard to damage. If you accidentally drop it or knock it over, this isn’t going to be much of a problem.I didn’t want to spend the money that this bottle costs at first, but now that I have, I understand that I will be using it for many years to come, so I’ll be sure to get my money’s worth out of it.Overall, it is a quality product that is made well and looks absolutely beautiful. If you want one, go for it! Increase your fluid intake in a stylish way!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great quality flask! The liquid size capacity of 32 oz. is perfect for me. It is large in size but it enables you to carry enough fluid to help keep you hydrated. It is constructed of insulated stainless steel to keep your beverage ice cold. It also affords you the option to use a straw or spout to drink. I love the blue color! The only drawback is that it won't fit in my car's beverage holder. You may want to check out a tapered design if that is important to you."
    },
    {
        "review": "I paid only $15 for this and it's superior to other water bottles that we paid $20 or more for.  I love that it came with a metal lid; It's so difficult to find that these days.  I haven't fully tested how long the ice will last in this, but easily 24 hours.  I would guess that it would take about 48 hours or longer for all the ice to melt.  Also, it seems like a really tough and sturdy bottle.  I haven't had this one run over by our work truck like my last one was, but I think it would fare the same.  I also really like the little plastic doodad that keeps your lid attached to the bottle, even when it's open.  The fact that is comes with three different lids is also a really nice bonus.  Great Product, Iron Flask!  Keep makin' 'em like this and I'll come back for more, if/when I ever need them."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought for my husband to take when he's golfing.  He loves it!  Keeps his drink cold even after he comes home.  Definitely recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this bottle because I wanted a larger bottle that I would only need to fill up twice a day to get as many ounces of water as was my goal. I definitely got it in this bottle. I love this thing, and got a parachord handle to go with it, so when I go for walks or go to outdoor events it's perfect to take with me. I've dropped it more than a few times and while the paint will chip, it still holds up. What's a stainless steel water bottle without a few dings, anyway? It gives it character.However, I've learned that 32 oz is a little too beefy for me. First, it's a metal water bottle that holds water. It's going to be heavy, and heavy when you bring it up to your mouth to drink. But BE WARNED: don't drop this on your feet. It's going to hurt and you're liable to break something. Second, with how big it is, it doesn't fit in my cup holder in my car, and struggles to fit in any backpack bottle holder. Third, it will leak. Even before I dropped it it leaked if it was laying sideways, so when I use it and take it in my car, I'm careful to never let it lay sideways.All that being said, it's sturdy and keeps my water cold. I'd never heard of Iron Flask as a brand before this bottle but it's made me a loyal customer. And with it being easy to clean, it's fantastic. The bottle itself feels smooth but is easy to grip (I have small hands, but it's not slipping around in my hand). I have a Camelback bottle that has a similar paint, but it's more coarse and with my touch-sensitivity issues, I've had to get used to that. It made me appreciate my Iron Flask all the more because there was never that issue.I'm going to purchase a 24 oz Iron Flask so I can carry it in my cupholders in my car. I'm not one to follow brands, and the \"hype\" Hydroflask puts me off simply because it's so \"everywhere\". I'll stick to my Iron Flasks, thank you very much. Thank you for making a reliable product! Just please fix the leak issue."
    },
