[
    {
        "review": "I love this thing! After falling victim to 3 or 4 plastic water jugs that falsely claimed they wouldn't give water that weird plastic taste, this glass jug is the one that finally delivers. My water tastes completely fresh every single time, which is exactly what I wanted.This 64 oz jug makes it incredibly easy to stay hydrated. A single fill-up lasts me all day, and the built-in time markers keep me accountable to my hydration goals and activity levels. The protective silicone sleeve features clear cut-out windows, so you can easily track your progress and see exactly how much you have drunk.I put ice in my jug every morning to keep my water cold. Because it is glass, the bottle does sweat, but the silicone sleeve does an excellent job of catching condensation and keeping the exterior from becoming slippery. For hygiene, I periodically remove the sleeve to wash underneath it and prevent any moisture buildup or mold. Taking the sleeve off and putting it back on requires a little muscle, but it is ultimately not a deal-breaker.Maintenance is a breeze because Civago includes all the specialized cleaning tools you need—which is a huge plus since my hands don't fit inside the narrow mouth to scrub the bottom. It also comes with both a straw lid and a \"chug\" lid. I prefer the chug lid myself, but it is great to have options. I absolutely recommend this water jug!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this bottle so much! It comes with a scrub brush, two straws, and a straw cleaner, which is nice. The wide mouth makes it easy to clean/rinse and having two lid types makes it versatile and of good value. The legends on the sides are easy to read and help me more accurately keep track of my water intake. The fact that it’s glass gives me peace of mind. My husband recently got one after seeing mine. He really loves the sturdiness of the portability handle and the silicone sleeve that makes re-filling easier. The sleeves are gorgeous colors as well! I chose olive green and he chose navy blue. As it may matter to some, I do want to note that (1) a few of the color choices have sleeves that don’t match the lids, and (2) the lids must be factory screwed on because when unscrewing the chug lid, for both of our bottles, there is a bit of a discoloration chip in the center. It is slight, and doesn’t bother us, but is worth mentioning."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this glass water bottle.  I gave it 5 stars although one glitch is the removable straw is long and reaches the bottom to prevent it from coming out of the silicone hub in the lid. But, it cuts of the water supply when you try to drink.  I inserted the straw into the silicone hub in the cap at an angle which works for a few seconds, but when you tighten the lid, the straw straightens out again preventing water from being sucked up.  I just cut a small half moon shape into the bottom of the straw. All fixed!When full, this bottle is heavy.  It's not something to be walking around with at a theme park or shopping.  Although the glass is made extra strength and thick, if you drop it or bang/swing it into concrete, it probably will crack.  The silicone cover is thin so doesn't offer much protection, but is nice when you set the bottle down you don't get a sound.It comes with a pourable spout lid (hard to use with a heavy bottle), two plastic straws, a straw/lid mouthpiece brush, and a foam cleaning handle.I would hand wash all of it.  Not sure if the handles will withstand a dishwasher over time.  Although the silicone hub in the lid seems durable, I'm not sure of it's durability over several years.  No way to replace it.  Just go to the pourable spout lid.  Over this glass bottle is great 👍"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love that this water bottle is glass and comes with a silicone sleeve so it doesn't get slipper or break too easily. The glass is still very exposed. I love that it is dishwasher safe and the instructions even say that you do not have to remove the silicone sleeve in the dishwasher. Not sure how that will play out, I have only hand washed it so far. I love the 2 different style lids since straws can get nasty. The glass is great since it does not change the taste the way stainless steal can or soak up the dish soap taste."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really wanted to like this bottle, but the design makes it almost unusable.Straw Lid Issue: The little star-shaped piece on the straw cap constantly falls out every few seconds, or it wedges itself so you can’t suck any water through. Super frustrating; roughly 20 times a day.Twist Cap Issue: The twist top is just as bad — it doesn’t line up cleanly. You have to arch it, stretch it, and fiddle around just to get it to close, and half the time it cross-threads. Sometimes it eventually seals, sometimes not.The glass body and size are fine, but those positives are completely overshadowed by the lid problems. For the price, I expected much better quality control.Bottom line: Great idea, terrible execution. The caps make the bottle more of a hassle than a help. Wouldn’t recommend unless they completely redesign the lids."
    },
    {
        "review": "Oh this was wonderful, I love it! It's sturdy and secure the black plastic works wonders so the bottle won't slip out of your hands so easy, it comes with extra accessories, and I loved that it comes with its own pair of tool's to clean it. My family linked it a lot to so now everybody wants one."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love it - but I dropped and it shattered into pieces - so the sleeve didn't work and the glass isn't thick enough to withstand a clumsy event."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a great water bottle! The only complaint I have is that when you take the straw out of the top, it's difficult to get it back in. But is that a complaint? If it's difficult to get in, that's probably why it stays in. :) I love that I can just check the time and then look at the bottle and I know exactly how much I need to drink in order to stay on track with my water consumption for the day. The color I ordered is the color I got. I have not washed it in a dishwasher because I always wash it by hand. My water stays cool for a very long time. It is rather large, of course, so for portability... It definitely does not fit in the cup holder in my car, It's rather large to just carry around. But I don't really mind just leaving it on my passenger seat. as long as you're okay with the size, I would absolutely recommend this water bottle."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I've been very happy with this Stanley Quick Flip GO bottle. It keeps my water cold for hours, and the quick-flip lid is convenient for drinking on the go. The bottle is completely leak-proof, easy to carry, and fits nicely in my car's cup holder. It's also durable and easy to clean. Great quality and perfect for work, the gym, or everyday use. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased this water bottle in January 2026 and have been using it regularly at work ever since. Overall, I've been very happy with it.The biggest positives for me are that it is truly leakproof and does an excellent job keeping drinks cold throughout the day. I've never had an issue with leaks, even when transporting it to and from work, and my drinks stay cold for hours.The flip-top lid has worked well, and I haven't experienced any problems with it over several months of use. It's also very easy to clean, which is something I appreciate in a water bottle that gets frequent use.The only thing worth mentioning is that it doesn't quite fit the cup holder in my 2019 Volvo XC60. That's not a dealbreaker for me, but if cup-holder compatibility is important to you, it's something to check before purchasing.Overall, this has been a reliable, well-made bottle that performs exactly as I hoped it would. I would definitely buy it again."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great water bottle! My Stanley keeps my drinks cold for hours and is very sturdy. I like the design, the handle makes it easy to carry, and it fits well in my cup holder. It’s perfect for work, travel, or everyday use. I would definitely recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "These are the best Stanleys in my opinion. I like the easy open touch top for quick drinking. I also like that It latches shut for easy travel. I work with children so I appreciate the spill proof ability of this bottle. This keeps hot drinks hot and cold drinks cold even in extreme temperatures. I have left hot tea in a cold car (well below zero) while shopping all day and it is still hot by evening! I have also left ice in there on a 100 degree day outside in the sun and still have ice left the next day! Love these!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Stanley is a trusted company of mine for years. Way back when I worked construction. 30 years later I still know that I'm getting quality product. If you want the best, do yourself a favor and pick up one. Works as advertised, I fill it up with ice cubes and water and still ice cold the next morning."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been using this bottle for a few months now and I can't say enough good things about it!I've been having some health issues and need to keep myself hydrated, and can't stand warm water... I had another bottle that required the lid to fully screw off, which was ok, except the ice would melt halfway through the day and on long days my water would get warm (yuck!). This Stanley bottle not only keeps my water cold all day, there's usually a good amount of ice still in it when I get home.I love the 'quick open,' just hit the button and the lid pops up, ready to drink from, and the locking mechanism is nice also, so I don't accidentally pop it open. At 24oz, it's perfect for a 16.9oz bottle of water and enough ice to last all day. While it was twice the price of the other one I had ($25 vs. $12), it was well worth the money!!If anything happens to the one I have, I wouldn't hesitate to replace it with the same thing!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "4 and a 1/2 stars...Stanley quality in every way. Durable finish, clean stainless steel, no chintzy parts.This lid is not my favorite Stanley makes, but it's not terrible either. It has a spring so it does stay open as you sip. It does tap you on the forehead very lightly. But it's not like my no-name that I had to hold open as I sipped. That one kept my drinks cold, but the finish got scratched so easily and you had to exercise a lot of manual dexterity to hold it from landing on your nose as you took a drink - Annoying!I recently bought ice ball makers. The ice balls are 2.5 inches in diameter. Provided I give it a few minutes to thaw they'll fit. But I think the molds that make the 1.9\" ice balls will not need a few minutes to shrink minutely.  I don't use this Stanley for hot beverages, so can't speak to that.The lid is fairly simple and easy to keep clean and sanitary. The little metal handle on the back is a plus.I have a silicone boot on the bottom of mine to protect it from any potential dents or dings (heavens, no!)"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this water bottle! It literally keeps things cold or hot. And trust me this bottle does not leak AT ALL!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love these water bottles! We have 4 in total, and we've given them as gifts to several people too!Ice will last for nearly 2 days in these bottles, keeping your water nice and cold for h-o-u-r-s. The lids fit securely and do not leak, ever. They close well, and have the additional feature of a small flip wire-type thing that ensure the push-button opening won't trigger on accident. Even without that feature, the closure is very secure.The water bottles are weighty and a good size. The quality is excellent. This size (24oz.) fits perfectly in car cupholders - at least they do in ours (Subaru Outback).My only improvement suggestions would be to have a silicone grip, both for hand grip, and on the base of the water bottle. I have small hands, so I can be a bit dropsy with it (not at all a lot, I am just kinda clumsy - and on that front, even though I've dropped mine a few times, there's been no dings, dents, or damage of any kind). As well, they can be a bit slide-y on hard surfaces.Overall, though, love this product! (And I've tested so many water bottles over the years, my god! 🤣)"
    },
    {
        "review": "Size was ideal for travel in bag item."
    },
    {
        "review": "I had my doubts since it did not arrive with any protection or wrapping. After that I checked it and the lid looks like it doesn't fit well, however I think it is because of the packaging but even so it doesn't spill any liquids. It's 700ml, it's a bit long but easy to transport, it keeps things cold well, it arrived to me in just 1 day, it's very pretty and the best at a great price! I know that at that price I will not get a thermos from this brand again. I'll take it for my KickBoxing classes. 🤗"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "After 5 months of hard labor, I can attest to the genius of this water bottle.It's endured the hot sun in over 100 degree temps, weeks at sea under both sail and power, dusty/dirty construction sites, hundreds of miles of hiking and days of winter weather under 20 degrees.  In each case it just keeps operating flawlessly without fault or defect.The large removable top allows for easy cleaning of the inside, while being thoughtfully designed with a tethered hinge that holds the smaller drinking cap captive.  As a result, you can't lose this small cap and unlike other water bottles you aren't stuck needing two hands for hydration (i.e. one for the bottle and one for the cap).  The cap threads inside the small stub of a 'straw'.  This is perfect for cleaning purposes as the surface your mouth in in contact with is smooth and simple to clean.  The diameter of the drinking port is perfect for taking a swig and has proven to be dribble free.  The two removable seals on both threaded caps are easy to extract and install, making cleaning a breeze but also resulting in a leak free re-assembly process.  The bottle just doesn't leak.  I've tossed it into bags on it's side, upside down and every orientation in between.The bottle's diameter fits neatly in most vehicle cup holders and includes a rubber sleeve should you need to take up a little extra space for security.  I have not had an issue with insulation at all, but I've only used it for cold beverages.  The 24 oz volume is adequate for most day to day activities but I've found the need to refill it when used under more extreme conditions.After owning this for 2-3 months, we purchased the 64oz version for longer adventures where we don't have access to fresh water.  Ice in the that container lasts for days at a time while at sea.It's just a water bottle, but it's the best one we've encountered.  So much so that we're going to buy a couple more in the event we ever misplace or lose the one's we have."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is the absolute best water bottle I have ever owned.  Happened upon one in the thrift store, and was stunned at how long it kept my drink cold on a scorching hot day (freezing cold, with ice still in it, 24 hours later). Made of sturdy materials, which is great, because it gets used a LOT.  Love the spout - I hate cleaning the straws and the tops with tiny holes, and feel like there is place for ick to grow in them - but I feel like when I wash this, it's CLEAN. It's the right size (24 oz) for me, and easy to carry with the handle, even when I am also carrying a camp chair, a camera bag, a food cooler and all the rest of the detritus you bring with you to youth sports games.  Seal is excellent - it could be knocked on the ground at a baseball game by a 70 mph fastball and not lose the seal (do not ask how I know this).  The silicone seal does not seem to degrade with repeated washing, either - the thrift store one is from 3 years ago (and who knows how much longer it was used before that) and still going strong.  I loved the thrift store purchase so much, I did the research and found the same model online (albeit a new, different color), and could not believe they were so on sale (19.99, I think).  A true bargain. And now mine won't get stolen by my kid every time I put it down - we'll each have our own.  I'm gonna buy one for my mom and husband, too. Seriously - this is one of the few products in life that you will like even better than you thought you would."
    },
    {
        "review": "We bought some of these based on a Wirecutter review, and I was really impressed. Cold water with a lot of ice stayed ice-cold all day. The ice was still cold at the end of the day, or in the morning if I filled the bottle with ice water and set it on my bedside table to sip overnight. After graduating from 14-oz and 18-oz bottles, my kid now takes one of  these bottles in her school bag every day. If we put in too much ice on a cool day, the ice will stay so cold that it accumulates into a large chunk. It stays that cold! On hot days, we fill these bottles with more ice, and that helps keep everything cold even while this bottle sits in the direct sun at the beach or a park.The lids are dishwasher safe, and the small white gaskets inside the lid and the spout lid are seated pretty well, but we did lose one gasket. You can buy replacement gaskets directly from Takeya (they also run regular deals on these bottles, but in this instance I found them cheaper on Amazon and needed them really quickly). They have two different gasket styles; the better and I think newer ones have a small circular tab (almost a loop) that does double duty in helping you insert/remove the gasket and also seems to keep the gasket seated better. I say that because the one we lost did not have the tab.I check our gaskets regularly and they seem to be quite impervious to mold. I pull them out every 4-6 months to inspect and clean them, and they are always fine with no visible signs of mold.The one con to the bottles is that they get dented when you drop them. If you have a kid who swings their bottle around (and who wouldn't want to do that with the really great loop integrated into the lid of this bottle?), over time the bottom will reshape itself from flat to curved. Eventually my kid dropped the bottle or bashed it into one too many hard surfaces, and one of the dents broke full through. Then the outside of the bottle had a hole in it. The inside was still fine, but after hand washing the bottle, there was water inside the lining, and I don't want to risk that becoming a moldy mess. That's why I needed to replace a bottle.We had our bottle for about a year and a half before the r outside split. That's an expensive habit, so now I am making sure my kid keeps the bumper on the bottom -- and refrains from swinging the bottle around so much.We love our Takeya bottles! I liked their performance so much that I bought two for myself and rotate their use daily. Since we only put water in them, I put the lids in the dishwasher every day or every other day, and leave the bottles to dry in our dish rack nightly. I hand wash them with dish soap and a brush a few times a week. The only spot you have to be careful to catch is under the stainless steel rim below the lid, which is a narrow channel that can harbor some sand or dirt (and other gross stuff).The one on the left in the photo has been used for about 18 months, and the one on the right is brand new. I made large name labels for all of them with permanent vinyl, which you can see in the older bottle has scratched off in some places. I believe I re-applied the label on the left in the last six months, so keep in mind that Cricut \"permanent\" vinyl is not going to last forever on a curved surface like this that gets used and banged around every day."
    },
    {
        "review": "I usually end up hating every water bottle for one reason or another, but this one is perfect. Easy to clean and fill and it keeps my drink cold for several hours. Nice carrying handle. I especially like the removable rubber base. This is a keeper, highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I filled this up with cold water and only like 5 ice cubes. Forgot it in the car when we went out on the boat. Forgot to bring it inside that night. Next afternoon the water is still SUPER COLD. This is Florida where everything melts. Except this bottle. I only put 5 ice cubes because the ice doesn’t melt in one day - it stays THAT cold.I have a large yard (Florida panhandle) to take care of so I drink LOTS of water. I needed a bottle with a secure lid that won’t let bugs or grass clippings blow in AND keeps the water cold AND won’t sweat all over the place. Finally found one that checks all the boxes. AND this one fits in my cup holder - in my Honda CRV and the riding mower.Also. I bought in black because I saw reviews about lids breaking and replacement lids only come in black. Even with this black bottle sitting in the sun on the beach the water stays deliciously cold. And I am not having any issues with the lid anyway.I love this one so much I came back and bought the 64oz also in black. The lids can be swapped but the handle on the 24oz is on the lid. Handle on the 64oz is on the bottle. I think I prefer the handle being on the bottle, but I use the big one as my extra water and drink from the smaller one. It’s just easier to manage (short people problems) plus it fits the cup holder.Using both bottles, me (46F) and my daughter in law (28) and my granddaughter (<1) spent a couple hours at the beach and had all the cold water we needed. WAY easier than carrying a cooler or having a bazillion different drinks/cups/bottles.I’ll be buying the traveler bottle next for hot coffee season. Maybe I’ll buy another 24oz in a color to use for iced coffee. Other than adding more of these to my collection, I can’t imagine ever having to spend more money on water bottles or travel mugs. Probably all of my family will be getting their own as gifts this year. Takeya is this Florida girls best friend!!!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Keeps liquids cold all day. Wide mouth lets you use regular size ice cubes. Small drinking cap attached to the top so you won’t lose it. Nice handle makes it easy to carry and maybe attach to a backpack with a carabiner. I like it.Only cons: the top has a gasket you should clean every week. Otherwise easy to keep clean. Also the bottom has a rubber piece that comes off in my car’s cup holder so you need to watch for that.It’s a good water bottle that has lasted me a number of months with no problems.  Good product without the big price on some of the trendier stuff."
    },
    {
        "review": "Absolutely exactly what I needed. The color is so pleasant and gently blush pink. The capacity (40 oz) is perfect for my work day where I have it on my desk. I have another somewhat smaller one of the same brand that I use for travel.Extremely easy to clean compared to just about any other brand of insulated water bottles. Very few moving parts means it's a lot more durable and has fewer places for bacteria to hide. The rubber base is a great addition too, prevents a lot of spills and annoying sounds of the bottle being set on solid surfaces.The varying loop is fantastic, and the spout cap is easy to use and open with one hand (assuming you didn't over-tighten it). And again with the cleaning aspect: no straw, so it is really just the lid and the bottle that need to be cleaned. And the lid is dishwasher safe so just a simple bottle brush inside will do the trick.Drinks also stay cold inside for a long time even in warm conditions. I will put ice and water in mine at the start of my work day and often find there is still almost the same amount of ice left by the end of the day and I have to leave the lid fully off to let it melt down so I can finish it all. I don't really put warm beverages in it since I use it only for water, but I imagine it would keep it warm for a good while as well.All-in-all I don't have anything negative to say except I wish I had reasons to get more colors and sizes because they're great."
    },
    {
        "review": "I FINALLY found the perfect water bottle for my personal needs. I have POTS and hydration is kind of a big dill, iykyk. I've gone through many a water bottle, having a longer than average Goldilocks moment, but quite happy to finally find the one that's JUST right.What I love about it:-The handle isn't a silicone strap attached by cheap screws or whatever. I wasn't able to recover my Brita bottle after the strap decided to break one day. I can carry this all over with me comfortably with no worry about the durability.-Does an amazing job keeping the water cold.-You can unscrew the top to fill the bottle, but there's another spout to unscrew for the mouth. It's the perfect size for how I like to chug my water and haven't had any issues with leaking.-I'm a klutz and I've dropped it and ran into walls/various things with it - no damage done. Not to the water bottle at least.-24 oz is the perfect size for travel IMO - carrying around work, in the car, room to room in the house. I can't vouch for hiking yet but it seems like a decent size for a backpack. It holds more than the average plastic bottle, but not as uncomfortably hefty as hauling around 32 oz or more.-The removable silicone at the bottom keeps it from rolling all over a table if I accidentally knock it over, it stays put and it fits in my cupholder when I decide to slide that part off. HUGE PLUS!-Easy to clean. Get a bottle brush in there and throw the lid in the dishwasher if you want to take your bottle hygiene a bit further.Haven't discovered a single flaw yet. It just works. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "It's a very nice bottle, very easy to clean and it keeps my drinks cold for a long time. I don't have an issue with the seals getting moldy but I also let my bottle fully dry every week."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very happy with my purchase. Recently misplaced my owala bottle and wasn't willing to fork out for a replacement at the current price. I found this bottle on Amazon Marketplace, advertised as \"acceptable\" due to major cosmetic imperfections. I had to REALLY look to find any imperfections on the bottle, all I can see is this tiny dent - and for $15 instead of $70 I am absolutely fine with it! Fully functional and a great colour. Filled up this morning at 9am and at 11pm it's still lovely and cold."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've ben using this bottle for close to one year now and it's so good that I felt compelled to go back into my old orders and write a review.  Prior to using Takeya, I was using Contigo bottle with the same value proposition (double-insulated, easy pour spout etc).  Bottom line is this bottle beats all the rest hands down.  It not only delivers everything it has promised, it also seems to be unbreakable.  I've dropped it so many times that I'm seriously wondering how the double insulation is not cracked in the interior.  In fact it just continues to deliver as if it was new - I'm very impressed.  The other Contigo bottles I used would have interior cracks after big falls and although the exterior looked ok, it would no longer be able to maintain the cold temps over several hours.  So bottom line, Takeya is where it's at!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Something about the design of these products… the bottom sticky piece that helps stick the bottle to a surface fell off within a week. This is the second time this happened to me with your product. Also the balance of the 40oz bottle is not good. It is too tall and falls easily. I’d recommend a camelback or other brand."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this brand and will be very loyal to it as it's genuinely leak proof. It also keeps cold liquid cold, and hot liquid hot for hours.I have this one for water when hiking. I have a smaller one for hot drinks for hiking/ work. Both I put on their side in bags or flat in the car well, and they've never leaked. I've also dropped them several times from waist height onto tarmac, without hardly a mark sustained."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "For years I’ve purchased t’s based on price and there always seemed to be a combo deal that was cheaper than this company’s multipack.  Problem is those shirts would be stretched out at the neck and generally look and feel awful after a few weeks.  Clearly, these shirts are more than worth the few extra dollars because they look incredible and I’ve never had a better fitting shirt.  I often wear these under dress shirts so the neck shows and it’s snug and looks perfect - professional.  And, there are long options so they don’t ride up and show the torso.  I could easily tuck them into my pants if I wanted to.  Great color assortment, soft, fit perfectly.  Wish I’d found these sooner, highly recommend ."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'll start out by saying I rarely give five stars, t-shirts that fit well are difficult for me to find. I usually go through several Brands before I find one I like and then I have to try several sizes to settle on one. With all of that being said, the shirts are a great quality for the price especially, and they are true to size. The fabric, stitching, and packaging are great for the price you're paying. I would consider these right in between a muscle fit and a slim fit, flattering in the arms and chest but not too tight in the waist, and the length seems to be just right. I wasn't really sold by the pictures of people trying them on but when I got the shirts in hand they seem to fit way better and look much nicer. If I have one thing that I could point out that isn't a complete positive it would be that the neck could be just slightly tighter and a bit more sturdy but that's really nitpicking because the neck does not sag at all, after a wash this might tighten up slightly and all the shirts seem to be identical and well made whereas usually when I order there might be one or two shirts that just aren't up to par. I got a 12 pack of the black and I will be ordering more for my day-to-day t-shirts, including a 12 pack of the whites. For a little perspective in rating these shirts, I used to buy the Haynes that were on Amazon and (I've noticed that the quality had gone down a bit) but those shirts usually run anywhere from 8 to $12 a piece and these are right up there with them if not better.Uptdate- i would settle at 4 stars, after a wash on cold and a no heat air dryin the dryer, the neck did firm up. The shirts definitely retain a thinner cotton feel and appearance. Great for every day or gym but youll want a nicer T for other occasions.  Still great value but i would definitely see a xxl shrinking to a xl on heat in the dryer. Fantastic right out of the package,  good after a wash."
    },
    {
        "review": "My teenage son is growing like crazy these days, so I decided to order some basic comfy t-shirts for him to wear this summer. I came across these Gildan Men's Crew T-shirts, and decided to order them.I was really impressed by the feel of the material of these shirts; they feel durable and yet are breathable. These have been great shirts to have on these hot summer days, as the shirts don't cling to the body.These are sturdy shirts, but have a lightweight feel to them; my son likes to wear them when he's exercising, and also while he's just chilling at home. The shirts are very versatile, and could work in a variety of situations.I'm very impressed at how nice these shirts look, and they fit well. The shirts match many different wardrobe pieces, and the color combination of this set is great!I'm very happy with this set of t-shirts, and am glad I bought these. My son loves wearing them, and they've worked out really well for an everyday type of t-shirt.I think these are a great value for the price as well, as this set of 5 shirts is currently listed at around $22.99. I would highly recommend these shirts to others, and am considering ordering another set as I write this. I'm extremely pleased with these shirts, and am happy I ordered them."
    },
    {
        "review": "No tags-nice! Price per shirt-nice! Length-perfect! (I’m tallish), but thin. I do favor a bit thicker material and these are not too thin, but also not heavy, a good compromise. A solid 4 star item. I’ll buy more. I will be keeping an eye on the collar to see if it curls or gets all twisted after washing."
    },
    {
        "review": "Super soft. High quality. Fits perfectly and are the best white t’s I’ve found yet!!!! Lightweight but not too thin nor are they see thru. Just the right thickness. So soft. Definitely summer material. I bought them for my husband, but I’m getting some for my son and me too now haha!!! I love em’!!!!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Gildan Men’s Crew T-Shirts Multipack is a great everyday basic. The shirts are comfortable, soft enough for daily wear, and hold up well after washing. The fit is simple and reliable, and they work well on their own or as undershirts.For a multipack, the quality and value are very good. A practical choice if you want comfortable T-shirts at a reasonable price.Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "These have become my everyday T-shirts. They’ve held up extremely well over time with very little fading and very little shrinkage, even after plenty of washes. That’s something I really appreciate because so many basic T-shirts lose their shape or color after a few months. They’re comfortable, fit consistently, and offer excellent value for the price. At this price point, and compared to other brands I’ve tried, these really stand out. They consistently outperform many shirts that cost quite a bit more. I keep coming back to these because they simply work. If you’re looking for a reliable everyday T-shirt that lasts without spending a fortune, I’d definitely recommend these."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought the Gildan Men’s Crew T-Shirts multipack on Amazon for my 12-year-old son, who is on the heavier side and thus sometimes difficult to shop for. Pre-teen kids grow fast and go through clothes quickly, so I didn’t want to spend a lot of money on basics he’ll probably outgrow in a year. These shirts are really affordable, especially for a multipack, and the quality is surprisingly good for the price.The fabric is soft and comfortable, and my son says they feel good to wear all day at school. They’re lightweight and did not shrink after washing. I also like that the shirts don’t get stretched out like some cheaper T-shirts do.The fit works well for him too. They’re simple, classic crew neck tees that can be worn on their own or layered under hoodies and jackets. We’ve used them for school and just everyday wear.Another thing I appreciate is that they’re easy to care for. I just toss them in the wash and dryer and they come out looking fine every time.Overall, these are a great value. If you need affordable, comfortable basic T-shirts for a growing kid (or an adult!), this pack is definitely worth buying."
    },
    {
        "review": "Soft, affordable, and don't shrinking like the fruit ones or the ones that ryme with Baines.I used to buy the other brands but these are top notch quality5'10 190lbs size large"
    },
    {
        "review": "Nice quality T-Shirts. Will buy again."
    },
    {
        "review": "Best value ever, white comfortable tshirts that hold their shape, iron easily and comfortable to wear."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "During COVID I ordered some Hanes shirts that were the exact style that I already had and when they arrived they were extremely short and poorly sewn. This almost made me stop wearing Hanes completely but after wearing them for 20+ years it's hard to change, so I gave them another try recently.Seems to me that Hanes is back! These shirts are excellent. They fit perfectly and they look and feel l great. However, here are a few things people should know.1) They may actually be thinner than in previous years. For me, that is a good thing. I'm not wearing a t-shirt because I need extra warmth but because I want cotton between my skin and the outter. It's softer, cooler, and catches my sweat. Thick undershirts make no sense IMO, but not feels that way (as you can see in the other reviews).2) Out of the package, they feel kind of crusty. This made me worried at first, but I Googled it and learned that they should soften up after a few washes. Today they are on wash number three and they feel like a normal soft t-shirt (which is why I'm leaving this review now). So it may take a couple of washes for them to feel the way you want."
    },
