        "review": "Bought this for warm weather workouts and outdoor stuff because my other shirts get heavy once I start sweating. It’s lightweight and breathes well so it stays comfortable on runs, yard work, or just around the house. Fabric feels soft and doesn’t cling when I’m damp, plus it dries pretty fast. Fit is true to size with room to move without being baggy, and it’s held up fine after several washes with no shrinking. Only small thing is it can feel a little thin if the wind picks up, but overall it works well for what I need."
    },
    {
        "review": "Trying to think of a way to write a review for something that is so simple as a shirt is quite comical as I try to write this up. Hey, it's a shirt, you put it on, wear it and on you go is what you look for when buying clothing of this type. But, would like to get more in depth for others without boring you with a full blown essay!The fit is comparable to other brands and matches the description listed on the website. I use these shirts for coaching baseball during hot days, working out in the gym, and as a comfortable knock around shirt to wear at home. The length for the arms is better than most shirts as Under Armour does have shorter sleeve lengths than other shirts which is a lot more comfortable for me. It is breathable so if you are standing around on a scorching hot field, it is much better to wear this type of material vs. a cotton shirt. When sweating, the material does have some absorption capabilities, but not too much, will get into that later. The neck length does go higher than most, but it is not to the point where it is too high.Working out in the gym, I am able to do what I need to do and the shirt allows full range of motion and does not restrict when doing any workout types that I do. Now to get back to the absorption of perspiration. I do workout in a gym that has saunas, and when working out in a sauna you sweat, A LOT. The shirt can only take so much before it gets completely saturated. Not a deal breaker by any stretch, but if you use this shirt when exerting yourself in a hot environment for a long period of time, just know that if you sweat a lot, it will eventually feel like you jumped in a pool.Aside from that one con, the quality is unmatched vs. the price and is definitely something to have in your drawer at home as it is extremely comfortable and has multiple uses!"
