        "review": "Albeit stark white, they generally are resistant of stains provided they are washed correctly and not set in. I bought these preferring viscose and Tencel-like fabric. Not too stretchy, doesn't shrink, but they are very comfortable. Very lightweight and wick moisture far better than most shirts I own. They are a bit on the thin side (still thicker than Hanes), but I have yet to fray any seams. For the price, these are such a great value and with a better quality and fit than the Hanes SuperSoft product line. They are also roughly half viscose (bamboo) and polyester. As much as I wanted 100% viscose, the polyester gives it a great structure without it bunching up. Going forward, these are the only T-shirts I will buy for sleep or for wearing under my uniform."
