[
    {
        "review": "I don't wear this t-shirt as an undershirt. I wear as my only shirt. It's well made. Comfortable. Easy wash. The pocket is essential for any shirt I wear. Looks good in any casual setting."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought these for my hubby.  He likes the ones with the pockets.  So far they have kept their shape after washing and drying. And soft too sizing was great no shrinkage after wash/dry.  He is very happy with them"
    },
    {
        "review": "This 6-pack is a reliable choice for anyone needing basic, comfortable undershirts. After several purchases, I can confidently give them a solid 4-star rating, especially for the incredible value they offer.Pros:Nice Fit & Comfort: These tees offer a consistently good fit – not too tight, not too baggy, making them ideal for layering under dress shirts or sweaters, or even for casual wear around the house. The 100% cotton fabric feels soft against the skin and they're quite breathable, which is a big plus for all-day wear. A bonus is that they are tagless, eliminating any annoying itch.Excellent Bargain for the Price: You truly get a lot of bang for your buck with this 6-pack. The cost per shirt is incredibly low, making them a very economical option for stocking up on essentials without breaking the bank.Decent Durability: For the price point, these undershirts hold up surprisingly well. They withstand repeated washes without excessive shrinking (I wash in cold and dry on low) and maintain their shape and softness fairly consistently over time.Cons:Limited & Repetitive Colors: My main gripe, and the reason it's not a five-star review, is the limited color selection. While the classic black, white, and grey are versatile, these packs are typically only offered in these three shades. I really wish Fruit of the Loom would introduce more diverse and vibrant color options, even if just a few more muted tones. Furthermore, within a 6-pack, you often end up with repetitive colors. For instance, you might get three whites, two greys, and one black, rather than a more even distribution or unique shades. This can be a bit disappointing if you're hoping for variety within the pack itself.Overall:If you're in the market for comfortable, affordable, and dependable undershirts for daily wear, this 6-pack is an excellent choice. They're soft, fit well, and hold up to regular use. Just be prepared for the limited color palette and the potential for a less-than-diverse mix within the pack. Still, for the comfort and exceptional price, they're hard to beat for your everyday basics."
