[
    {
        "review": "Very light and comfortable to wear, especially in warm weather!  Not as heavy as many other T’s out there, but this is what you want when the weather is hot and humid.  The fit is perfect to size, too!"
    },
    {
        "review": "A little thicker material then what I was looking for but great fit and very minor shrinkage when washed.  I did decide to keep them for the cooler months"
    },
    {
        "review": "Soft and comfortable"
    },
    {
        "review": "Soft but runs small. More of a slim fit shirt."
    },
    {
        "review": "Awesome light weight shirt all cotten with pocket"
    },
    {
        "review": "Since I was in high school (which was decades ago), I've always liked Gap clothes.  They're usually a good traditional fit, and try to be fashion-neutral instead of fashion-forward.  For example: I typically don't go for shirts with pockets (like polos or tees), but don't find them too annoying especially if they're being worn as a base layer.This tee shirt is pretty much par for the course.  It's 100% cotton, which makes it very soft and comfortable.  I'm about a 37\" chest, and the small size fit me well. It's just the right thickness to work as a base layer under most circumstances, and the pocket isn't that obtrusive.However, the price of this shirt does not justify the brand name.  If all you need is a base layer, then this wouldn't be the best choice - there are more affordable options out there.  But, if you want a t-shirt you can wear that has a bit of style, then this may be good for you."
    },
    {
        "review": "Finding a basic t shirt sounds easy until you actually start shopping for one. So many either shrink after one wash, lose their shape, feel rough against the skin, or fit strangely. I ordered this for my husband and this one ended up being exactly what he was hoping for in an everyday shirt.The first thing he noticed was how soft the fabric feels. It’s comfortable right out of the package and doesn’t have that stiff feeling that some new shirts have before they’ve been washed a few times. It feels lightweight enough to wear comfortably throughout the day but still substantial enough that it doesn’t feel thin or flimsy.The fit is another big win. It has a relaxed, easygoing look without being overly baggy. It sits nicely through the shoulders and chest and drapes naturally without looking oversized. The pocket adds a little extra style while keeping the overall look simple and classic. It’s the kind of shirt that works whether you’re running errands, traveling, relaxing at home, or meeting friends for a casual lunch.After several washes, I’ve been happy to see that it has maintained both its shape and softness. The stitching appears well done, and I haven’t noticed loose threads or signs of wear. That’s something I pay attention to because basic tees tend to get a lot of use in my husband's wardrobe.What I appreciate most is how versatile it is. It pairs easily with jeans, shorts, joggers, or even under a lightweight jacket. It’s one of those grab and go pieces that doesn’t require any thought because it always works. Those are usually the items that end up becoming favorites.GAP has always done a good job with wardrobe essentials, and this shirt is a great example of that. It’s comfortable, fits well, feels durable, and looks good without trying too hard. If you’re looking for a reliable everyday tee that you’ll actually want to wear regularly, this one definitely delivers."
    },
    {
        "review": "There is a reason GAP's basic tees have maintained a loyal following for decades, and this crewneck pocket tee is a clean illustration of why. The fabric is soft and substantial without being heavy, hitting that comfortable weight that works year round as a standalone layer or under a jacket. The fit in small is well proportioned with a relaxed but not oversized silhouette, and the crewneck sits at a flattering height that works across a range of collar styles.The chest pocket is a small detail that adds just enough visual interest to keep this from reading as completely plain, and the construction is clean throughout with no loose threads or uneven stitching visible on close inspection. The black holds well after washing without immediately fading to a washed out gray, which is where budget basics often disappoint. For a foundational wardrobe piece that simply works and wears well, this is GAP delivering exactly what it does best."
    }
]

