[
    {
        "review": "I bought this long-sleeve construction shirt for my husband, and he really likes it. The material is lightweight, breathable, and comfortable to wear all day, even when working outside. The bright color makes him easy to see, which is great for safety. It fits true to size, washes well, and the quality is excellent for the price. I would definitely buy it again and recommend it to anyone who needs a comfortable work shirt"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is an excellent shirt for a bargain price, especially when bought in the 10-pack.  There are no side seams to itch you.  The back neck and shoulders are covered in fabric which is not always the case in undershirts.  The front neck, armholes, cuffs, sleeve seams, and bottom hem are not fabric covered, but they are surged with a very soft thread which is much more comfortable than the surging in some of my other shirts that scratches and itches my skin.  I was worried that the crew neck would annoy me since I don't like anything tight around my neck, but it is loose enough that I can get it over my head with my glasses on, plus you can stretch it a little both ways when the shirt is wet.  The cotton in this shirt is soft and surprisingly heavy, not like a typical men's undershirt.  It is more an outer shirt than an undershirt, but it could be worn under a roomy outer shirt.  It has cuffs, which is a very nice feature especially if the sleeves are a little long on someone.  The weight and texture of the shirt seems to be between a tee shirt and a very light weight sweatshirt.  I am using one for sleeping and it feels soft against my face at night and keeps me warm but not hot.  The arms are long on me which I expected since I am only 5 feet 4 inches tall and I ordered the size large shirt.  The size chart indicated I should order a medium or even a small if I wanted a snug shirt, but I went with the large for the comfort and I'm happy with the roominess.  The sleeve width is roomy enough on me, but not too roomy.  The construction of this shirt is excellent, in fact perfect except for a thread or two that was not cut off.  I bought my shirts in the 10-pack and they arrived with all ten shirts ironed and folded in half neatly, all in one big plastic bag loosely taped shut and inside a big box.  I didn't have a problem with the fact that each shirt was not individually wrapped, and in fact I can use the big plastic bag.  Some reviewers said there were holes, unsewn seams and stains on their shirts, but mine were all in perfect new condition.  I washed them and dried them in the dryer, but they do take a very long time to dry.  I ended up hanging them up to complete the drying.  The only negative thing I can say about this excellent shirt is that it has two very annoying scratchy tags sewn right into the back neck seam.  You can't tear them off without ripping the stitches.  I cut them out very carefully with tiny scissors.  Here are the approximate dimensions of size large after washing and drying:  underarm sleeve length 23\", sleeve circumference at shoulder 20.5\", sleeve circumference at middle of sleeve 15\", back width at top between sleeve seams 20.25\",  circumference around the bottom 45.5\", length at back middle 29\"."
    },
    {
        "review": "Buy a size up; these will shrink! Great fitting shirt for work, and the price point is perfect. But if you are looking for a long-lasting shirt, this may not be what you're looking for. This is not the Heavy Gildian stuff I usually buy. But I still like them."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love the Glidan products..I eas happy to see these long sleved Black tshirts came in a two pack..A great price too..I 100% recomend these tshirt and any made by  Gildan !"
    },
    {
        "review": "I highly prefer working out in cotton long-sleeve shirts, and these are exactly what I was looking for. The fabric is a high-quality, heavy cotton that feels incredibly soft against the skin, making it ideal for gym sessions.  They are a fantastic, breathable alternative to standard dry-fit materials. I liked them so much I bought them in several different colors. After multiple trips through the laundry, they hold up great in the wash and do not fade at all."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've owned a multipack of these Gildan G2400 Ultra Cotton long-sleeve shirts in black for about seven months now, and they've become my go-to shirts for cooler weather here (roughly November through March). I primarily wear them around the house or for casual errands like grocery shopping. Overall, I'm quite satisfied with them. The \"classic fit\" description is accurate – they offer a comfortable, loose fit without being overly baggy. The comfort is definitely there for everyday wear.The \"Ultra Cotton\" name isn't kidding – these shirts are genuinely heavyweight. The fabric is substantial, almost feeling like a very light jacket, which is perfect for the cooler temperatures I bought them for. What's impressed me most is their durability over the past seven months of regular use and washing. The black color has held up remarkably well with no noticeable fading, and I haven't experienced any significant shrinking either. All the seams are holding strong, and the construction feels sturdy, living up to the durability promise. The rib cuffs are a great feature – they fit comfortably and, importantly, have kept their shape and elasticity, preventing sleeves from getting soaked when washing hands. The neck opening is comfortable, not too tight or too loose, and I didn't have any issues with the tag.However, there's one key thing I discovered that potential buyers, especially pet owners, should be aware of: this fabric, particularly in black, is a magnet for pet hair. If you have cats or dogs, you'll likely find yourself constantly removing fur from these shirts. It's quite noticeable on the black color, so if you share your home with furry friends, you might seriously consider opting for a lighter color instead. Despite this one drawback, I feel these shirts offer good value for the money, especially when purchased in a multipack. They are well-made, comfortable, and durable. I would consider buying them again, particularly if I could find them at a price point around $5 per shirt, which would make them an excellent deal."
