    {
        "review": "Made in Madagascar of 56% cotton, 37 % modal, 7% elastine, shirts are pretty, stretchy, comfortably soft, and stitched neatly.  At approx. 5' 1” tall, 145 pounds, 38C, I carry extra weight in my stomach, waist, and seat. I usually wear med. to large or petite Lg jcp St. J T shirts. In 2024 I’d purchased 2 sets of Amazon Essential similar solid shirts in XL (coral/blue and lavender/navy). These are long and the shoulders too wide, but otherwise an OK fit. I recently bought the Amazon Essentials blue stripe/leopard in XL. They would best fit tall, slender persons. The leopard one had loose material in that back, fell to the bottom of my set and unattractively hugged it. I could have gotten away with wearing the blue striped one that size as it looked ok as a casual summer beachy oversized shirt. I liked both shirts so then tried them in Large. They were obviously too small, tight in the chest and arm-holes”. It’s odd that there’s so much size difference between sizes. As non-slender persons must go up one to two sizes, it results in shirts of excessive length and with too much looseness in the back. I’d also purchased the dark green/lilac animal print in Large which I’ll keep.  Although too small, they are a tiny bit looser than the set with the leopard print and can be worn with a very lightly padded bra or one with no padding. Basically, the quality of these shirts is excellent, but the fit leaves much to be desired. These shirts would be perfect for me if a little shorter and wider.  FYI: A white bra shows through the lilac animal print.  Also, this lilac print, while not a color match, looks nice against the Amazon Essential grape fleece joggers."
