    {
        "review": "I am a published author who writes poetry, fiction, and creative nonfiction, and I have already filled a good portion of this notebook. I genuinely love it. It feels as though someone actually considered how writers and creative people use a notebook instead of simply binding together a stack of identical pages and calling it a day.One of my favorite features is the table of contents. Do you know how useful it is to have an actual contents section in a notebook? I write many different poems, stories, ideas, and fragments, so having a place where I can record what I wrote and where I placed it is incredibly helpful. It makes the notebook feel organized without taking away from the freedom and spontaneity of writing.I also love the variety in the pages and their layouts. Not everything feels perfectly uniform, and I mean that as a compliment. The variation gives the notebook a creative, authentically human feeling. It invites experimentation instead of making every page feel like it must be used in the same way.The paper quality is lovely, and I appreciate all the additional details: the sticky notes, the included pen, the thoughtful thank-you cards, and especially the clear pocket or folder in the back. That pocket is one of my favorite parts because I can keep loose notes, cards, and writing materials with the notebook instead of inevitably losing them somewhere in my home.I was also happy to discover that the company has a business connection to Puerto Rico. As a Puerto Rican writer, that made the product feel even more special to me.I did have an issue with the included pen. The tip appeared slightly bent when it arrived, and the clip eventually broke off. I have arthritis and pain in my hands, so having to angle the pen a certain way made it difficult for me to use comfortably. I now use a different pen with the notebook. This was disappointing, but it did not diminish how much I enjoy the notebook itself.Now we must discuss the truly serious matter: there were not nearly enough mustache stickers.I loved the little mustaches so much that I began decorating the front of the notebook with them and drawing faces around them. I would happily cover the entire notebook in tiny mustaches if given the opportunity. Mr. Pen, please consider offering additional mustache sticker sheets—especially in different sizes or ridiculous prints. Zebra mustaches. Gold mustaches. Polka-dot mustaches. The world is ready.Overall, this is a thoughtful, well-organized, high-quality notebook that works beautifully for poets, authors, journalers, students, and anyone whose mind produces more ideas than they can reasonably keep track of. The table of contents, varied pages, paper quality, accessories, and back pocket make it especially useful for creative writing.I truly love this notebook and would gladly purchase another—preferably in purple, and preferably accompanied by an unreasonable quantity of mustache stickers."
    },
    {
        "review": "Wonderful quality notebook for an amazing price. The pen that comes with it writes well. The mustache sticker and thank you note where a great touch! I highly recommend this product."
    },
    {
        "review": "i LOVEEEE the cards are soooo sweet and i just love the details of the journal, the pen writes so amazingly and its just beautiful all together, exactly what i needed, thank you mr.pen🩷"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love love love this notebook. I wasn’t expecting much because the price was so low , but it honestly went beyond my expectations. It came with a cute little sticker and thank you card. I am going to order a few more to keep my notes organized at work."
    },
    {
        "review": "This journal is fantastic, love the sage green one. The note inside from the seller is also very nice and came with stickers ….mustaches... love them…..and the pen too.The price you cannot beat…it looks like it would cost much more…I will enjoy it for sure!!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Great notebooks. These are 100 pages and are thicker (more pages) than I expected. I suppose the standard one-subject notebook from Walmart must be only 70 pages, so these will obviously last longer. The cover is thick plastic rather than cardstock so it won't rip, tear, or wear at the corners. There is a sturdy sheet with pockets on both sides at the front of the notebook for storing documents. The variety of colors in this six-pack is nice, easy to differentiate which is which for different subjects.I wasn't sure what the dot matrix codes were at the four corners of each page so I had to research it. Apparently this is used to specifically work with the Five Star Study App. The codes printed into the corners of the page are used to flatten and square up the page when you take a picture of it to scan your handwritten notes into a pdf document. I haven't used this feature but it would be great for note taking in a college course."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love using these spiral notebooks. It is easy to flip through the pages. The coil doesn't smash easily, loose bits of paper are easy to remove when you take pages out.I like that the size of the paper is actually letter-size and not some odd size. I also like that you get a variety of colors on the cover. I work in an office where I need to keep track of phone calls, conversations where I have committed to doing something. I also use these for our weekly department meetings.I used to sort my tasks between many notebooks, but there's always that one time where you take down a phone message in the notebook set aside for meetings. I have ADHD and found it too hard to keep everything straight. Now I use these for everything. I put the date on the top of the page, and only write on one side of the paper. I used to use steno pads and would use both sides of the paper. It made for some difficult times retrieving notes when things were scattered.These are great notepads. The paper is nice and thick so you don't have to worry about ink bleeding through or using an eraser and having it tear holes in the paper.I just happened to come across these notepads at work. I liked them, so I keep using them. When they're full, I  attach a sticky note to the cover and write the dates covered on it, and then file them away together."
    },
    {
        "review": "This Five Star one-subject, college-ruled notebook is an absolute staple for both school and work in our house. My daughter uses hers daily for school, and I use mine for work, and they hold up incredibly well. They’re very durable—she’s constantly throwing hers in and out of her backpack, and it never gets bent, torn, or messed up.I love the built-in divider at the front with two pockets. It’s perfect for storing loose papers, graded assignments, handouts, or notes you need to keep organized without folding or losing them. Everything stays neat and in one place, which is a huge plus.Another great feature is the QR code that connects to the Five Star app, allowing you to scan and organize your notes digitally. It’s a really helpful option for staying organized, especially if you like having everything accessible on your phone.The paper quality is excellent, pages don’t tear easily, and it lasts the entire school year without falling apart. If you’re looking for a reliable, well-made notebook that works for students and professionals alike, this one is absolutely worth buying. I will continue to repurchase these every year."
    },
    {
        "review": "I picked up this 6-pack of Five Star’s Spiral Notebook + Study App edition, and I’m really impressed. Here’s why it stood out:Pros:The covers are durable and water-resistant, so my notes survived a few accidental coffee splashes without warping.Five Star+2Five Star Direct+2The paper is designed to fight ink bleed — I used gel pens, highlighters, and regular ballpoints, and the pages stayed clean on the flip side.Food 4 LessThe spiral binding is tight and doesn’t easily snag in backpack zippers or tear out when I flip pages.The integrated Study App adds real value — being able to scan notes, make flashcards, and sync to Google Drive was a game-changer for review sessions.Apple+1Excellent value for a six-pack: I now have a dedicated notebook per subject (or per semester) and don’t dread running out of usable materials.Cons (minor):Because each notebook is packed with features (durable cover, app compatibility, ink-resist paper), they are a bit more expensive than the basic spiral notebooks I used before.The colors of the covers are assorted, so if you’re hoping for specific colors, you may need to check or reorder.Five Star+1The Study App is awesome — but it means you’ll want to spend a little time scanning and organizing your notes in the app if you want to get the full benefit.Bottom Line:If you’re a student, professional note-taker, or just someone who writes a lot and wants better durability + digital backup, this notebook pack is a stellar choice. Durable build + smart tech + multiple notebooks = five stars in my book. I’ll definitely buy this again."
    },
    {
        "review": "This 6 Pack of Spiral Notebooks is a steal for back-to-school shopping.  I only have one child who's in 7th Grade, so sometimes those school supply lists are a pain because the only way to cheap it reasonable is to buy in bulk.  Thankfully, my kid doesn't care about name brands at all, *but thinks it's cool when we buy them*, but this 6 pack is really a much better deal than the other bulk paper deals on Amazon primarily because:*** You get 6 Notebooks that are all awesome colors suitable for boys, girls, women, men, etc and they have double-pockets in both the back and front of the Notebooks for extra storage for students (or yourself)***They are fully lined, very thick, and the covers are not paper.  They are the water-resistant plastic covers and also fit right into 3-Ring binders of any size, easily.***The price is fantastic for 6 of these.  And if you only have one student or two students, there's extra Notebooks left over for us adults (I don't know about you, but I need at least 2 or 3 Notebooks around the house for notes and lists)***They are good quality and durable and last a long time compared to buying \"other\" brands or buying them individually.  I've seen them as high as $5.50 for one notebook even as an \"add on\" item (only available if you spend $50 total on your order).I really love these and so does my son.  I was able to easily cover all of his teachers' requirements for lined paper Notebooks as well as keeping 2 of them for at home.  You can't beat the built in pockets and flexible, plastic covers that are so much better for being beaten up at school or work.  And for once, every color in the group is fantastic.  I kept the White and Pink for at home and my son has the rest for his classes.  Definitely grab this 6-Pack while you can.  Cardboard, cheapie Notebooks just don't cut it for lasting in backpacks and binders and these have the extra storage and quality covers, too.  One of the best Amazon deals I've found on branded, bulk notebooks (and I spend probably 8 hours shopping for each item on his school list).  Snag them while you can!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great for school. Holds up well."
    },
    {
        "review": "These notebooks work great for my college classes!  I like the variety in colors, and the pockets inside work well for holding a couple pages, like a syllabus!  They work well for taking notes; I use gel pens sometimes which do bleed through a little.  They have held up well to being stored in my backpack for hours at a time!When they first arrived, they were covered in little paper bits, which is probably to be expected, but it was a little annoying.  All in all, I'm satisfied with my purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Ordered these spiral notebooks for my daughter. These are great quality and an excellent price.. my daughter was also very excited about the different color options. Highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "These books are the best quality and they fit so much writing and they are so comfortable to write with ."
    },
    {
        "review": "Whetstone"
    },
    {
        "review": "I wish I got the blue one I was looking forward for that one but five star is my go-to best notebook brand EVER. I just love the quality of the paper, the size is big enough not to make me uncomfortable while writing you can flip the books on one side so it doesnt take much space of your table or surroundings. Plus, it has TWO pocketS at the beginning to place your loose paper. Lastly, the pages all have little holes to make it easier to tear the paper and let stay clean without the small pieces of paper hanging. I never used the app but I will try it this semester."
    }
]

