[
    {
        "review": "Really happy with these notebooks! The quality is great, the pages feel nice, and they’re perfect for school, homework, or everyday notes. They feel just as good as the ones I usually buy in stores, but this was much more convenient. Great value and definitely something I would purchase again!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got the Oxford Spiral Notebook 6-Pack for school and everyday notes, and it’s honestly one of the best basic notebooks I’ve used.Right away I noticed how solid the paper quality is. The college-ruled sheets are smooth, don’t feather with gel or ballpoint pens, and hold up well even with heavy note-taking. There’s minimal bleed-through, so I can write on both sides without fear of ghosting.The size (8 x 10-1/2 inch) is great — big enough for plenty of notes but still fits nicely in a backpack or under larger books. The spiral binding feels sturdy and doesn’t snag on other stuff in my bag. Pages turn easily and lie flat when open, which makes writing comfortable.I also liked the assorted colors. It helps me separate notebooks for different subjects without needing labels.A couple of honest points:• The pack doesn’t come with dividers or pockets, so it’s strictly notebooks.• Designs vary, so if you’re after specific cover styles you might not get the exact ones shown.Overall this 6-pack delivers great quality and value for everyday use — school, work, projects, lists, and general writing. The paper feels noticeably better than cheaper pads, and the binding holds up over time."
