[
    {
        "review": "I use these journals everyday for reflexion and prayer. The hardcover makes it easier to write in. It's easy to lay open flat. They function in the way they are supposed to. And very durable, I usually tear the covers on the flimsy covered ones. Also I'm bipolar, and keeping a journal is an important part of my therapy. The lines are college ruled which I like and the pages are a little thick which I also like like, there is no bleed through even with dark gel ink. I also like the color of the pages, it's easy on the eyes. The price is amazing. Most journals with all the pictures and frills on them might have 100 pages for the good ones and they are way more expensive. I don't need all of that. I like these and I've bought 5 now so far. Great for anyone who needs to write your feelings and thoughts down. Or if you just need a good notebook. These are great. I like the larger (B5) size but they do come in a smaller book (A5) that is also good. The bigger size is easier to hold for me and you can get more on a page. So far it's been very durable. The pages also don't feel like regular paper. It's soft to touch. I'd definitely buy more of these. And they're great gift ideas. They come in many colors, so you can give their favorite color. And put a nice pen with it. I use a UNI pen that's .38 in tip size because I write small. But they come in different sizes."
