[
    {
        "review": "I bought this Mead Composition Notebook 3-pack for my 5th grader, and it has been perfect for school use. The wide-ruled pages are great for kids who are still working on handwriting, giving them enough space to write neatly and stay organized.The notebooks are durable with a sturdy black marble cover that holds up well in backpacks. Even with daily use, they don’t easily bend or fall apart like cheaper notebooks sometimes do. The binding feels secure, so the pages stay intact throughout the school year.Each notebook has 100 sheets, which is a good amount for classwork, homework, and notes. The paper quality is solid and works well with pencils and pens without too much bleed-through or smudging.I also like that having a 3-pack makes it very convenient for different subjects. It helps keep my child’s schoolwork organized without needing to constantly buy replacements.The only minor downside is that the pages are fairly basic and not tear-out friendly, but that’s expected for composition books.Overall, this is a reliable and affordable school supply set that works very well for elementary students. I would definitely recommend it for everyday classroom use."
    },
    {
        "review": "This notebook is sturdy, reliable, and perfect for schoolwork, notes, and everyday writing. The wide-ruled paper gives plenty of space to write, and the durable cover holds up well in backpacks and desks. Pages are easy to use and the quality is exactly what I expect from Mead. Great value and a back-to-school staple! ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐📓✏️"
    },
    {
        "review": "First of all, the paper quality? Surprisingly good. I went in expecting “standard school notebook energy,” and instead got paper that actually respects your pen. Ink does not bleed through like it is trying to escape, and writing on it feels smooth enough to make you briefly believe you have your life together.Each notebook has 100 sheets, which means you start off thinking, “I will use this responsibly,” and end up halfway through with random lists, doodles, and one page that just says “get it together” written ten times. Plenty of space for both productivity and mild existential spirals.The size is perfect. Not too small where you feel cramped, not too big where it becomes a commitment. It fits in a backpack without drama, which is more than I can say for most things in life.Durability? Solid. These can survive being tossed around, shoved into bags, and opened aggressively when inspiration (or panic) hits. The classic composition cover also gives that timeless “serious note-taker” look, even if what you are actually writing is a grocery list and passive-aggressive reminders to yourself.And getting three in a pack? That is optimism right there. Three chances to start fresh, be organized, and finally become the person who uses notebooks properly."
    },
