    {
        "review": "Exactly as advertised, quick delivery and great price"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this Mead Primary Composition Book 4‑Pack for my 1st grader, and it’s been perfect for early writing practice! The wide primary lines give plenty of space for big letters, which helps him form his handwriting more confidently. The pages are sturdy and don’t tear easily, even with eager little writers flipping through.Having four books in one pack is great — there’s always a fresh one ready when he starts a new writing topic or story. They’re simple, school‑ready, and exactly what we needed for daily handwriting practice.If you’re teaching young writers and want a reliable, kid‑friendly notebook, this set is a great choice!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Mead's books  and other products are usually strong/durable for use by kids and adults.  That is the main reason I purchased this instead of the typical exercise books that are smaller and cheaper but easier to get damaged.  So that's not an issue here.I'm including below information I wanted to know BEFORE I purchased:1. This is the same product as Mead Primary Composition Book, Grades K-2, 100 Wide-Ruled Sheets, 9.5 x 7.5 Inch Sheet Size, Pack of 5 (72900)  ...it is just listed as one book here and a set of 5 books (comes in a small tight box) in the other listing.2. It is not actually like this picture - i.e. it is not black with white with blue designs; the picture of the back of the item is a closer representation of the coloring.  What I received from Amazon (seller) is the exact blue colored unit from the picture used for the Pack of 5 (72900) (By the way, that 72900 item number does not exist on the Mead website; what you get is 5 units of 09902).  My daughter is 7 years and did not want this black version with the Blue Palm Mascot as she said that was \"childish and the children would laugh at me in school\"...she requested the blue book and I bought one of these to compare.3. IT DOES NOT HAVE VERTICAL MARGINS!! This is the main reason why I gave it (and will be giving the Pack of 5) 4 Stars instead of 5.  At K-2 age and beyond, children need the guide of at least the left vertical margin to line up their work and write question numbers, etc.  It means that I have to go now and draw 3,000 lines (200 pages x 15 books) before school starts in September.  JOY...I'm typing this and thinking 3 stars. Sigh.4. The lines are \"narrow\" as they are actually 1/4 inch between the line pairs (i.e. the red and the dotted, the dotted and the high blue, the red and the low blue).  So the page holds 12 red lines; but the last red line is less than 1/8 inch to the edge of the page, so low dropping letters may be problematic on that line.  There is a larger margin at the top but to me it is not necessary - so this could be an improvement.5.  The pages are not bright white, but they are a comfortable white.  Not glossy - it is to write on after all.  I don't know how to technically describe it.  I'm satisfied with the color and thickness and overall page quality.So that's about it for now.  I'm off to drawing left hand margins."
    },
    {
        "review": "Thank you for delivering on time before first day of school. They came in perfect condition, they typically last half the school year but I bought 6, they are made with sturdy cardboard, and versatile if I have any left over they can also be used for drawings, notes, or tic tac toe."
