[
    {
        "review": "Super comfortable and perfect fit right out of the box!  These are incredibly comfortable, and the wide size is perfect for my big feet.  I like to ability to slip them on so easily!  Durability is something I will evaluate with time, but what a great first impression already!  For the price, I feel like getting more than anticipated!  These also look very nice."
    },
    {
        "review": "5 out of 5 stars: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐318 Days Later: Daily Worn as My ONLY Pair of ShoesI wanted to wait before reviewing these because I wanted to see how they'd hold up over time instead of writing a review after only a week.These Skechers became my only pair of shoes. I wore them every single day from September 14, 2025 until July 29, 2026 and beyond.That's: 318 consecutive days, my primary (and only) shoes, everyday walking, no rotation with another pair.I paid just under $50 after tax when I bought them. That works out to roughly 15.7 cents per day (about 16 cents/day) over their lifespan.I've attached a photo collage showing exactly what they look like after those 318 days so people can judge the durability for themselves.Comfort: The Air-Cooled Memory Foam was easily my favorite feature. They were comfortable right out of the box and stayed comfortable for most of their life. The Hands Free Slip-Ins also worked exactly as advertised. Being able to step into them without bending over never got old.Durability: Considering these were my only shoes, I'm impressed.After 318 days,The uppers are still intact: CheckNo holes in the toe mesh: CheckStitching has held together: CheckSoles are still attached: CheckThey still have usable traction: CheckThe main wear is exactly where I'd expect it: Heel lining has worn through. The insole covering has rubbed away in the heel area. The cushioning isn't as fresh as when they were new.The outsole has gradually worn from everyday walking. Nothing unexpected happened. They simply aged from daily use.Would I buy them again? Yes.In fact, I'm planning on buying the exact same pair again today. Not because these completely failed, but because I got almost 11 months of everyday use from them for about 16 cents per day, which I think is excellent value.I'll will keep this pair as backup shoes for rainy days, yard work, or quick errands.If you're looking for an everyday walking shoe that's comfortable, convenient, and can hold up to nearly a year of constant use, I think these are a solid choice.Would I recommend them? Absolutely!"
    },
