[
    {
        "review": "These are the classic white high tops that I have liked for a few decades. Glad to be able to still get them. Good fitting, comfortable shoes that hold up well. I waited for the price to drop below $50, because I see no reason to pay more than that. For no more than I wear them, they will last me for a few years."
    },
    {
        "review": "These Reebok BB4500 Hi2 high tops are a solid throwback-style sneaker, but they definitely feel more like a lifestyle shoe than anything performance-focused.First impression is good — the design has that classic high-top basketball look and they’re easy to wear with jeans or casual outfits. They look better in person than I expected, especially if you like retro styling.Comfort is decent for everyday use, but not amazing for all-day standing or heavy walking. The cushioning is fairly basic, so after a few hours you can start to feel the lack of support compared to more modern sneakers.Fit runs a bit narrow for me, especially in the toe box, and there’s a short break-in period before they start feeling more comfortable. Once broken in, they’re fine for casual wear, but not something I’d choose for long walks or sports.Build quality feels okay for the price — not premium, but not cheap either. The leather upper holds up well, and the outsole seems durable enough for regular street use.Overall, these are good for style and casual everyday wear, especially if you like the retro basketball look, but they’re not a comfort-heavy or performance shoe."
    },
    {
        "review": "Beautifully comfortable and very stylish. Trust me you won’t regret the comfort… if you got “Frodo” feet like me, get you the Wide size… long toes? A half size longer. Ommggg you won’t regret it. But for my Morton’s toe and wideness the W size was just perfect. Thank you."
    },
