[
    {
        "review": "I am going on vacation and was looking for a comfortable sneaker for daytime activities where I would be walking alot. Sadly I order two pair at the same time these and a pair over twice the amount I paid for these. The Project Cloud came first and I tried it on my right foot first because of my ever returning pinkie corn. Not only was there enough toe space, the level of comfort was undescribable. I tried them on with a thicker sock I already had on thinking It would be too tight or I wouldnt get a proper fit. I was wrong, they fit perfect so I can only image when I have on my proper sneaker bootie sock. And the color was just as shown, spot on and beautiful I plan on making additioal purchases in other colors."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought these for a weekend trip to New York City and Philadelphia, where I knew I’d be doing a lot of walking. On the first day alone, I walked over 13 miles (including lots of subway stairs and walking between stops), and these shoes held up great.I did wear them every day for about a week before my trip to break them in, which I think helped. I also used blister prevention bandages just to be safe, and I didn’t get a single blister.Overall, I think these shoes are absolutely worth the money. They’re comfortable enough for long days on your feet and stylish enough to wear with just about anything. I’d definitely recommend them if you’re planning a trip where you’ll be walking a lot. The picture below is AFTER the trip."
    },
    {
        "review": "These Project Cloud shoes are cute and super comfortable. I am a true size 8 and I would say these run TTS, maybe slightly large. They are very easy to slip my feet into. In fact I may need to tighten up the stretch laces or wear a thicker sock with these because they are pretty roomy. They feel very soft and cushiony, and they're definitely comfortable to walk in.I am dubious of the claim these are made with 100% genuine leather though. I ordered the dark brown and the \"leather\" parts have no nap whatsoever. When you look closely at the product photos some of the colors definitely look like suede but the dark brown ones look and feel synthetic to me. There is no leather smell. There is also no labeling on the shoe itself indicating these are made with real leather. Up close they look cheap to me. I ordered these on sale so they were under $35, and they are comfy so I'm keeping them. I think they are worth the price I paid but would not pay any more for these shoes. I saw the next day the price went up to around $50 and that's too much, at least for the dark brown ones."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been searching for quite a while for sneakers that do not look boring. I decided to buy these because of the style and colors.  The double color laces made the sneakers very attractive. They were delivered quickly. I normally wear an 8-9. The 9 fit great except a little tight.(no half sizes). So, what I did was  remove the Memory Foam Insoles.... this then allowed additional space for me. Now i am happy with my walking sneakers.."
    },
    {
        "review": "I loved the looks and feel of the shoe. BUT, my ideal 7w was snug in this shoe 7.  Felt too narrow & tight width wise.  Even though they look like a comfy casual shoe, they are not.  The sole was too thin.  I could feel everything under my foot and there is no firmness anywhere for the bottom.  Disappointing because they are cute.  Looking for a Cloud feel with memory foam…this is not it."
    },
    {
        "review": "GREAT little shoe! Comfy and so cute! Very lightweight and yet just the right amount of support. The design is super cute and I have had SO many people ask me where I got them. They look expensive. I love that they slip on but look like they're tied. I got the off-white  with the extra striping but they do go well with actual white outfits...very high-end and unique looking. I plan on getting another pair so that when these wear out I'll not be out of luck! Am planning on getting the black, pink and red ones. Don't under the negative comments stating poor fit. For me, they're great although I do have a narrow foot so that may be it. I really do love them. They are so versatile, too. I wear them with jeans as well as cute dresses. Did I say that I love them?!!!😄"
    },
    {
        "review": "Perfect fit and style for me!  Well made, easy to slip on (i have to hold the tongue, but no big deal).  True to size.  I love that the toe area is a little wider but not too loose.  Easy wear for daily use but I don't think , for me, they would be comfortable to walk all day in them.  Not a real thick sole, but that's what I wanted.  They came perfectly packed.  Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I like the design and general feel of this shoe. It looks good and seems well made. Prior to this athletic shoe, I bought two pairs of Project Cloud sandals that were dreamy in terms of cushioning and fit. However, these shoes surprised me because it did not have the same heel cushioning. As I walked in them, the heel felt like a \"thud\" followed by the ball and toes being fabulous. I'm not sure how this will play out in the long run. I'm glad a purchased them, but I am leery to purchase more \"shoes.\"  Also, if you wear a 9 1/2 in a shoe, the 9 will not fit, and the 10 is a bit roomy, but easy to adjust."
    }
]

