[
    {
        "review": "I never usually buy shoes online, since I have had serious problems with my feet. I can only buy a wide width and trying to find a comfortable and cute shoe is very difficult. I decided to try this shoe and it is so comfortable and feels so good I can’t believe it. I tried on one that looked like this that was much more expensive and was not comfortable at all. It comes in so many colors. I will probably buy another couple of pairs. You should size up. I normally take an 8  1/2 wide. I ordered these in a 9 wide and they fit perfect. I feel like I could walk anywhere all day in these. They feel like a light to medium weight and good support, not flimsy at all."
    },
    {
        "review": "I wanted to wear these for a few days before giving my opinion. Overall these are great shoes. They are comfy and fit almost perfect. They are wider than I am used to. I usually wear narrow shoes. So for a few days I had to learn to walk in them properly. However, now they feel normal on my feet. The souls are stiff as others have mentioned. And the arch support is very minimal. So if those things bother you don't buy these. However They feel a good quality and over all I think they are a great buy for the price. I will be buying other colors in the future!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I wasn't sure how these would be for me, but I'm surprised and mostly very happy.Pros: I got the deep pink and it's as gorgeous as I hoped.Bonus: I normally wear an 8.5WW size, but saw the recs to size up so I tried a 9. These aren't shown as wide shoes, but they are only a smidge too narrow to fit perfectly properly, but I\"m keeping them because they fit well enough.Cons: these are VERY slippery on my kitchen linoleum floor, so \"no slip\" is quite a stretch. These are fine on pavement, but I really wouldn't wear these if it was raining or if I was going somewhere with very smooth floors. But mine are also suede-ish, so I wouldn't wear those in the rain anyway. The insole padding is...adequate, but I am not 110lbs, and as they are these are a 3K step/day shoe, not a 10-20K step/day shoe. That is, I wouldn't take them on vacation when I average 15-20K steps per day. I already know that would be a painful world of hurt. Though the insoles do seem to be removable, so replacing them with something more formidable could help a lot. The bump/bone below my big toe, which is at about the second lace hole, that's a bit narrow for my feet and will be a hot spot until I stretch it out, but I also have rather wide feet, so someone with narrower feet shouldn't have that concern. The back of the heel seems soft enough that it won't cause blisters, but that's yet to be seen -- these arrived yesterday and I've been wearing them around the house today.Overall, I really do like these, though I'll probably get better insoles so I can wear them for more than an errand or two. These are a great deal for the $30 I paid for them, even if they just become low-step day shoes."
    },
