        "review": "Great shoes, great product"
    },
    {
        "review": "Don't get me wrong, this is a great shoe.  Skechers are renowned for their comfort, and this shoe is no different.  It has an incredible cushioned sole.  My main gripe here is that I'm just not a fan of the whole slip-in / slip-on / bungee laced shoe.  Skechers, why, why, why are you doing this?!!  You don't have to reinvent the wheel here!  Lace up shoes have been working pretty well for centuries now, but these days they're getting harder and harder to find.  Don't know if we've all just gotten fatter and we can't bend over to tie our own shoelaces anymore, but it's almost like they're trying to faze out laces altogether.My main thing about shoes is that I don't want to feel any pressure on the TOP of my foot, even if it's a little pressure, and these shoes feel like I have a couple of little pug dogs sitting on top of my feet.  The tongues on these are attached, stitched in, all the way to the entry point.  With a loose tongue, and regular laces, the customer could more easily adjust the \"breathing room\" up top.  But these, with their rubber band laces, lock your foot in.  It just gives me an uncomfortable, claustrophobic feeling. I get it, some people like to feel like they're \"locked\" into their shoe, especially if they're playing sports, or engaging in some kind of physical activity.  And others, like myself, like to adjust my shoes and leave them a little loose, for my big Hobbit feet.  With old-school fabric laces, the person has the option to go tight or loose, depending on their own personal preferences.  These laces, and the design of the tongue, gives you ZERO options in this area.Again, I love the shoe.  It looks great and the soles really are like walking on air, but I think for my next pair I'll get a gool ol' \"Go Walk\" lace up shoe.  In fact, I think I might cut the bungees off of these and lace them up with regular laces-- this may relieve some of that upper pressure.UPDATE:  Cut the bungee laces out of there and laced it (loosely) with 32\" flat white laces, only looping through the first three rows.  Difference is NIGHT and DAY.  It's like a whole new shoe!  This released the pressure I was feeling at the top of the shoe, and I think it looks better IMO.  I like how the white laces compliment the white outer sole.  Keep in mind, there's still no tongue, it's all one, continuous piece of netting, but the material is pretty flexible once you lose the bungees.  Highly recommend doing this if you have big, ol' wooly mammoth feet like myself.  So much better!"
    },
