        "review": "Great shoe. Fits well. Grips wet pavement and tiles well but there's minimal to no arch support. You will probably end up investing in a set of insoles."
    },
    {
        "review": "Historically New Balance only makes certain shoe models with their extra wide sizing.  The retro/fashionable models haven't usually been included in that bucket.  So when I saw these new 515's on my BIL's also wide feet and saw them being offered with this many colorways, on Amazon, for less than $100, it seemed too good to be true.I know I'm writing this like I'm about to bring up a big \"but\" with these shoes...  But I'm actually not.  They're actually extremely well made, breathable in the summer heat and surprisingly comfortable, even with just an EVA midsole and thin hard rubber outsole.  I'm also one of those weird goth kids from the 90's who proved it wasn't just a phase, so the minimalist blacked-out colorway also gave me a bit of the fizz.  The wider 4E fit and footprint is also identical to what I'm used to with my other New Balance faves (the 410v5 dark Trail Runners) but the materials feel even more substantial and quality.  Though I will admit that the sole response of the 515's is less springy and athletic-feeling than those kicks.That said, I've been wearing these shoes a LOT this summer and they haven't disappointed yet.  The leather has held up and stayed clean with no fraying at the seams or obvious signs of wear inside or out.  The midsole has well broken into the shape of my foot and toes, providing a decent amount of support and grip without looking agressively athletic.  Which seems to leave the 515's striding a happy line between looks and functionality that have made them my go-to running around town shoes going forward.If you have wide feet, you could do a lot worse."
