[
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love these shoes and find them so cute and comfortable. I bought these shoes for work 3 weeks ago and have worn them every shift since. I am an ER nurse who is constantly on her feet at work for 12 hours. This is actually the second pair of new Balance shoes I have bought. I was so impressed with the first and I wanted a different color. I normally wear about a 6.5 to 7 in women’s depending on the brand. I bought a size 7 in the slate gray metallic silver color. These shoes fit me well and are true to size. The toe area is roomy enough to allow me to spread my toes out some. They also leave enough room to accommodate thicker socks, or foot swelling during shifts. I do have arches in my feet and they feel well supported while wearing them. They feel lightweight on my feet during my entire shift and my feet never feel heavy.When I first wore them they were a little stiff, but they never once hurt my feet. I was surprised because usually new shoes have to be broken in. Of course my feet do get tired since I worked 12 hour shifts, but they have never once hurt like they have with other shoes I have worn in the past.The sole of the shoe is cushioned and has not compressed after use. I have never once slipped while wearing them on polished and tiled flooring, so they provide traction. The mesh on the side is breathable. They are a little harder to keep clean because of the fabric near the lace toe and heel. After three weeks of use, I have not noticed any loose stitching and they have held up very well. Additionally, there isn’t any noticeable wear to the outsole.These shoes are good for casual wear, work, travel, and light exercise."
