        "review": "Great early '90's movie with Sidney Poitier, Robert Redford, River Phoenix, David Strathairn, Mary McDonnell, Ben Kingsley, Dan Ackroyd--what a fantastic cast. This is one of those great early movies that focused on the computer hackery skillset as the central theme incorporating spy tech, the mafia, big tech, the little guy, betrayal, the feds, and so much more. But the story is centered on relationships which are built well across the movie, along with enough humor, and a sense of discovery to keep it interesting. Very entertaining from start to finish, and a good ending. This was one of those truly successful ensemble pieces where you have big names, but doesn't feel like big egos. Definitely some scene chewing, but not aggressive of distracting. Another 90's gem."
