    {
        "review": "They are as nice as they look online. Very comfortable and love the look."
    },
    {
        "review": "I was looking at a model of a New Balance shoe that looked very similar to these (and I have since learned there is a similar Steve Madden shoe as well). The new balance shoe was pricier and the way the rubber on the shoe came up over the toe was not an ideal look for me. I could not justify the price if I was not completely happy.  I thought if they went on sale, maybe, but that happened and I still could not do it.  It was actually in my search for those shoes on sale that I came across these.  I thought about it.  The reviews were good, covered all the things I needed to know, but the price made my wonder, are they really as good as most reviews said? Well, I finally took a chance and I am happy that I did! Since taking that chance I now own 2 pairs - black and grey.I am an avid walker and runner too.  I do both everyday.  I am about comfort and quality. I would not run in these shoes as I have heavier duty runners for that.  I think these would be okay, but I am not sure how they would hold up to that kind of activity.  But walking in them a minimum of 7 kms a day, they are perfect. This is my experience anyway.  They are comfortable, stylish and the quality seems alright.One thing though is that the tongue does not stay in place, it would shift to the side of my ankle after a few steps, which I was not crazy about.  Most shoes of this style, a runner type, have a slot that the laces fit through to hold the tongue in place. These do not. There is material on the tongue though that, with some magivering, I was able to create slots by removing some stitches and adding others.  I am a sewer.  I have done this to both pairs and it works perfectly.  Also, for the grey shoes, I replaced the grey laces with the same lace style, but in white.  I much prefer them this way."
    },
