    {
        "review": "Bought these Project Cloud kids tennis shoes for my daughter because she’s constantly on the move—think less “child” and more “tiny tornado in glitter.” I wanted something that could keep up with her, and these shoes absolutely deliver.The quality is impressive. Solid stitching, durable materials, and they’ve survived recess, a spilled juice box, and a surprise game of backyard mud tag. So far, not a single tear or complaint (from the shoes OR the kid).As for comfort, my daughter says they feel \"like jumping on marshmallows,\" which I take as a glowing endorsement. She wears them without whining—which is the gold standard of children’s footwear reviews in my house.Value-wise, they’re a total win. They look and feel like they should cost a lot more than they do, which is great because kids outgrow things faster than I can say “I just bought those!”BUT—and this is important—they run small. I had to return the first pair and size up, which was only mildly frustrating because my daughter had already emotionally bonded with them. Cue the tiny dramatic meltdown. Once we got the right size, though? Smooth sailing.TL;DR: Buy them. Just go a size up, and prepare to hear the words “these are my favorite shoes EVER” roughly once a day."
