        "review": "I am an avid candle lover! I decided to pick this up because it reminded me of Voluspa candles. The scent is STRONG. Even taking it out of the beautifully wrapped packaging (which was a wonderful surprise btw, it felt like unwrapping a present), I could already smell it. The glass container is weighty and I can imagine using this for other things after the candle is finished. Taking off the lid, you can still pick up some of the scent through the area. It is light but the throw is there. When lit, the wick crackles prettily. And the throw is even further. I only have to light this for 30 minutes or so to have a nicely scented space. I’ll be going back to this brand. I’m so impressed!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I sent my mother-in-law a candle from this company for her birthday. I think it was an amber scent, or something like. She said she could smell it as soon as she opened the box, and that her whole upstairs smells marvelous with the candle just sitting on a table in the hallway unlit.I am a candle lover (collector) so after hearing her rave over it I purchased one for myself. I bought the rose noir & oud, and o.m.g......what a gorgeous floral scent. It’s light and strong - but not overpowering. It’s just wonderful.The wick burns clean - no black smoke. The all glass design is very feminine. The lid just sits atop the jar - no rubber seal. You do not need to blowout the candle - just place the lid on top and it will go out in seconds on its own. Every time.I’ve had it lit everyday for a week - roughy 2 hrs - and have barely made a dent. I think it may last longer than the other more expensive well-known candle brand(s).Don’t hesitate and just splurge a little.I am buying ALL my candles from the company from now on!"
    }
]

