[
    {
        "review": "I bought these specifically for running, and they’ve been perfect. They’re lightweight, comfortable, and stay securely on my face even during longer runs without slipping. The polarized lenses make a huge difference by cutting down glare and making everything look much clearer, especially in bright sunlight. They also feel well made and more durable than I expected for the price. If you’re looking for affordable running sunglasses that perform well, I definitely recommend these. Great purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The QALLY Polarized Sports Sunglasses turned out to be a fantastic surprise. The lenses are genuinely polarized, which makes a big difference when driving, cycling, or spending long hours in the sun. They cut glare extremely well, and the UV400 protection gives peace of mind knowing your eyes are fully shielded.The frame feels lightweight but sturdy, so you can wear them comfortably for hours without pressure on the nose or ears. TOverall, these sunglasses deliver great clarity, strong sun protection, and reliable comfort at a very reasonable price. If you’re looking for stylish, durable sports sunglasses that perform well outdoors, the QALLY pair is definitely worth it."
    },
    {
        "review": "These sunglasses are very stylish and lightweight. It doesn’t keep pressure on eyes for a long-time use. It can be used for driving, cycling, running and it cuts glare to a great extent. It provides full sun protection and the material of this sunglass is farm and solid. If you want both comfort and value for money, I will recommend buying this one."
    },
    {
        "review": "Not bad overall, can't complain with the low price. True polarized, and you are getting 3 identical glasses with different lens colors. Simple and straightforward.The glasses wrap around pretty nicely, and the nose piece and arms are fairly comfortable during long runs or fast intervals (haven't tried them with any sports yet).My main complaint is they sit too high and you can't adjust the nose piece up. So if it was just raised slightly, the glasses themselves would sit lower in your face. Maybe some people wouldn't like that if the bottom of the lens is touching their cheeks, but I have a very lean and long face so I would prefer them to sit lower.Plenty of protection and vision above and to the sides; there's a slight blond spot in the upper right corner where the lens is notched and you can notice it when wearing them. And once again the lower part of the lens doesn't cover enough...so on windy days, dust can still come through the sides and top. (I'm not saying sunglasses will have a perfect seal, but the gap is bigger than other sport glasses I've tried)Besides that, you really can't beat the price. Great for Spartans/Trail runs/ beach days/field sports, anything you want the overall protection, but also don't care of they get damaged cause you'll have 3 ans they're so cheap."
    },
