[
    {
        "review": "The KALIYADI Polarized Sunglasses are a remarkable blend of style, functionality, and affordability. I've already purchased two pairs, a testament to their quality and my satisfaction!One of the standout features of these sunglasses is their unisex design. Their sleek semi-rimless frame is effortlessly trendy, fitting both me and my partner perfectly. It's a versatile accessory that adds a fashionable edge to any outfit.While the black rim version has its charm, I found the spotted version exudes a slightly more premium feel. However, this doesn't detract from the overall quality of the sunglasses.The functionality of the KALIYADI sunglasses is impressive. They've proven to be excellent in blocking sunlight, even on the brightest of days. Despite their light weight, they are effective, enabling me to fully enjoy my time outdoors without any glaring disturbances.But the most compelling advantage of these sunglasses is their affordability. They offer similar, if not better, protection compared to high-end brands like Raybans, without breaking the bank. It provides a sense of ease, knowing that even if they are misplaced, they can be replaced without causing a dent in your pocket.In a nutshell, the KALIYADI Polarized Sunglasses are a great buy. They are stylish, practical, and accessible – an absolute steal for their price. It's no wonder they've become my go-to sunglasses!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought the two pack on amazon prime day at a great price. I’ve got a bag full of sunglasses to chose from but went ahead and got them anyway. I’m so glad I did because they’re awesome. They are big and cover the eyes very well. I have a small head and the unisex style I think is the cause of them seeming a bit big, but they are very good sunglasses and I think that you’ll love them as much as I do so yes, “I do recommend them.” 4* due to size and fit, otherwise I’d give them five.*OkAy, it’s been over a year that I’ve had this pair, not that I didn’t get two when I purchased them more than a year ago, but the black ones, which were my favorite pair got stolen away from me. Aside from that which is a bummer I have to admit I want to say that after more than a year of having this Pair of sunglasses that I upgraded my four star review to five stars because of how well they have held up over this year. I also want to say that I bought them on prime day that July prime day, and I got a really good deal for two pairs of glasses on the other hand when I’m reading reviews about the glasses, I noticed that some people say that the lenses are great but the frames are cheap, well I am here to tell you that I am taking good enough care of my sunglasses that I know that if you bend them they’re going to bend, you know you can force them to bend you can do that on  a pair of $300 sunglasses too, but my point is people should not put a review on that is solely to say the frames are cheap or some of the photos I see that obviously, they were stepped on okay, they didn’t break by their self like that, something happened. I don’t live in a house that doesn’t have normal things going on and you drop stuff or you have a toddler. But please be honest, if you tank it.  I think that a lot of the pictures I am looking at are just accidents where people broke their sunglasses and then post a picture trying to get the seller to give him a new pair, at least that’s what I thinks going on, and it’s wrong, that is wrong people if you step on your sunglasses, they didn’t break by themselves, you stepped on them, just admit it, don’t be a Fraud or a phony or are just trying to get the seller to give you something for free, at their expense, that’s just not the American way or is it just your way and maybe we’re different, but I don’t do that stuff because I think it’s wrong. I was raised better, I teach my children better, And my grandchildren know better; so for all you people who broke your own sunglasses and posted that they broke, like just fell apart, yeah they just broke. I don’t believe you and you shouldn’t do stuff that you know is wrong, just saying. Okay, lecture over.Anyone else out there if you want to get a really good pair of sunglasses that fit your face and hold on please remember that they’re unisex, as stated in the description, so they might be a little bit bigger on females than they are on a big headed man, which is what they are, bigger than us, so if you’re worried about that then go find yourself a pair that are not unisex or don’t complain if they are a little bit bigger than you expected and then write a review that they were bigger than you expected. Just sayin... duhh......."
