    {
        "review": "Love these glasses! I’ve got them for my husband after his surgery on his eyes. He was told he had to wear dark sun glasses, as the light really bothered him. These do the job. They are comfortable, durable, very lightweight, and he wears them every time he goes outside. He said it’s like he’s not wearing anything, the material is good. It looks high-end.  I bought them cause I thought it was a good value for the money."
    },
    {
        "review": "Fantastic! Lightweight, comfortable and polarized. Health reasons need me to have wraparound glasses and these fit that bill. I am female, tall, slender with short hair and the shape/style fit perfectly. They come with hard and soft cases plus a cleaning cloth. Great price so I bought two. Nice choices and colors. I highly recommend these glasses and seller."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased the red tinted lens set. They are light on my face. Now my face is narrow and long, oval really. These sunglasses grip the sides of my head firmly. It's not uncomfortable, it feels secure. But, I would question just how comfortable they would be on someone with a round face or wide head. Take that into account.They are brand new, so the clarity is sharp and clean. I wore them out earlier it's not really the sunniest day out, and the red lenses are specifically supposed to be most effective on bright days. Half the sky had towering thunderhead building and my vision was pretty dark. I don't mind that. I spend most of my time inside and intense sun can be physically painful.The company says that there is a scratch resistant coating on the lens. I'm not about to test it for you. Waste your own $30 on that! My advice is, treat these glasses gently. They are injection molded plastic frames, plastic lenses, and silicone non-slip padding. There are no reinforced hinges or other built in design features.They are definitely polarized. The wrap around design warps my sense of peripheral vision as opposed to a standard pair of eyeglasses.Value for money? Well, that's kind of on you, right? They are cheap to buy, but if you are going to abuse them, they will be destroyed quickly. And the more pairs of cheap glasses you buy, the less value for your money you are getting. In that case, buying a more durable product would save money in the long run.In my case, I don't abuse my eyewear. I use microfiber cloths to clean them. I keep them in the case if they aren't on my face. And I keep them safely away from the animals and kids. I am confident that these will last several months at least.The microfiber cloth is quite large. That's nice. The hard cover case is more of a 'medium cover' case. It will protect your glasses, but it won't stand up to abuse either. Oh, it also comes with a neck strap holder for the glasses too. I hated the way that felt on my neck and tossed it away. But it looked to be a fair quality one. I don't use them, so don't trust me on that."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought these for being out on the water and on my motorcycle...Love them! Def worth the money and super cute. Very lightweight, made well, and I love the color!"
    },
