        "review": "I had dropped and cracked my favorite pair of sunglasses that I had bought 2 years ago.  They were not repairable and not as durable as I had expected.  After much research for a new pair, this suoso Sports Polarized Sunglasses pair was the winner. They fit great and it was even better at fighting glare than the pair I previously owned.  I love all of the extras that came with it (great case, soft cloth and glasses holder) It was everything I hoped it would be!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I like these.  They are comfortable and stable in use.  I have used them during running, jumping rope, and vigorous calisthenics.  The blue lenses, nose bridge, and temple pieces trim look good."
    },
    {
        "review": "Rating: 3.5 / 5 StarsI'm keeping these sunglasses for biking and expect I'll adapt to the fit, but they do have a few specific pros and cons.The Cons:Fit issues: The nose bridge is too narrow, which holds the frames too far from the face. This creates distracting dark \"pillars\" on the inside (nose side) edges of the lenses.Light gap: There is a gap at the bottom that lets in a sliver of light.The Pros:Great value: Low cost, lightweight and comfortable.Nice extras: They include a hardshell case and a generous amount of accessories.Optics: They are definitely polarized, and I really like the slightly lighter tint.Bottom Line:My main issue is the nose bridge; it's just too obtrusive. Having an option to adjust, widen or remove it altogether would have been a great feature."
