        "review": "I like the sunglasses for what they are, they are $10-20 shades that reduce sunlight and have polarization, if you select a model that does have polarized lenses. These are not very expensive and still have a good build quality to them. I gave it a 4/5 for scratch resistance because at the moment i have yet to scratch the lenses but that's because i have not really abused them like i normally would do to a set of glass lens sunglasses and would expect them to get scratched when pocketing with keys against them. These are better than any pair of gas station sunglasses that i have looked at in the past few years and you actually get to choose style. They are lightweight and still maintain rigidity.They are oil magnets, i typically wear some sort of sunscreen when out in the sun and these like to hold onto any fingerprint or oil from them as possible when compared to my previous glass lenses sunglasses. It takes a lot of effort to make them wearable through wiping them off to clean the lenses compared to glass would be. I also don't 100% love how they fit on my face with them fitting rather small for a pair of Women/Men glasses to fit. I think it is because the bridge is too narrow and the lenses are not wide enough for my face. This results in a gap on either side of my eyes that are prone to dust flying into compared to glasses that i have had previously that fit tighter to my face. This is also the reason that i knocked the sun protection down to 4/5 because it leave a space for sun to hit my eyes while driving as well. Your mileage may vary.Summary:Pros:-Affordable-Good build quality-Fun color options-Lightweight and sturdy-Company is responsive by emailCons:-Smaller than expected, depends on person-Oil magnets, annoying to clean off oil smudges and get clear again-Plastic lenses, haven't scratched yet but imagine they would through use, I plan to report back later-Sun and dust can get in due to smaller size"
