[
    {
        "review": "I have tried a genuinely impressive number of phone stands over the years. Rigid plastic ones that only work at one angle. Bulky ones that take up too much desk space. Flimsy ones that tip over at the slightest provocation. None of them quite covered every scenario I actually needed.These do.The silicone and aluminum construction gives them something no rigid stand can offer: genuine flexibility in every direction. They lie completely flat for storage or travel, slim enough to slide into a pocket or bag without any bulk whatsoever. Then you bend, fold, and shape them to whatever angle or configuration the moment requires. A comfortable viewing angle on a desk? Trivial. Wrapped around a tray table on an airplane to hang your phone hands-free during a flight? Done. Hooked over the top of a monitor so your phone sits visible alongside your screen for cross-reference note taking? Also done. I keep discovering new ways to use them that I hadn't even anticipated when I ordered.The soft silicone is gentle on whatever surface your phone rests against, with no scratching or slipping. The internal aluminum strip holds whatever shape you bend it into reliably, even after repeated adjustments.Two stands for under fifteen dollars is genuinely exceptional value. One is orange, one is black, which makes them easy to distinguish and means you can keep one at your desk and one in your bag without thinking about it.One small note worth mentioning: in the first week, the metal bar on the black one came loose. It popped right back on cleanly with no fuss, and I genuinely can't tell whether it's a design feature or a minor hiccup. Either way it hasn't affected performance at all, and I'm not taking a star off for something that fixed itself in seconds."
    },
    {
        "review": "These are about as simple as a phone stand can get, but they work. They're made from a flexible rubber like material that holds my phone securely while still allowing me to adjust the angle pretty easily. I've been using one on my desk, and it's been convenient for watching videos, video calls, or just keeping my phone upright while I work.My only hesitation is the value. While they function well, they're also a very simple design, so the price feels a little higher than I'd expect for what they are. That said, they've worked exactly as intended, they're lightweight, portable, and easy to toss into a bag, so overall I'd still recommend them."
    }
]

