[
    {
        "review": "The Pyle Complete 40\" Beginner Guitar Set is a fantastic choice for anyone just starting their guitar journey. This set comes with everything you need to dive right into playing, including a gig bag, capo, guitar strap, extra nylon strings, and three picks.The guitar itself boasts a beautifully handcrafted all-wood build, featuring a linden wood body, birch headstock, and a dyed maple fretboard, which together create a warm, resonant tone. Its traditional classical body style and full scale make it versatile enough for lessons, recitals, and casual practice. The soft nylon strings are gentle on beginners' fingers, helping to ease the learning curve while producing a crisp and clear sound.With a total length of 40 inches and a scale length of 25.6 inches, this guitar is perfectly sized for players of all ages, making it an excellent choice for kids, youth, and adults alike. The inclusion of protective binding and chrome machine heads adds durability and a touch of elegance to this well-rounded package.Overall, this set is a great value for newcomers eager to start making music."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been playing the heck out of this 1/4 size classical nylon guitar and it's time for my review. I am no beginner. I call myself a guitar hack, as my technical knowledge of music theory is um, spotty. I am a full sized 71 year old adult 5'8\" with average sized hands. I enjoy playing the smaller sized guitars and never expected this little guy to boom out like a 41\" dreadnot guitar. It has a 20\" scale and is 30\" end to end.It arrived quickly and I saw no visible damage. As for tuning it? I need to say we live on the big island Puna District. We leave our windows open always. The climate, humidity, etc make it impossible for any hollow body acoustic to stay in tune overnight. Ever. Tune it in the early day, and it will go sharp overnight.  Having said that, the tuners are just okay. They do the job. The guitar has a decent finish. I am going to add fret markers on the side of the neck just like on my steel string acoustics. Classical guitars have few fret markers, and I need the full set. It comes with a bare minimum gig bag with no real padding and a storage pocket. Spare set of strings, A capo, and a strap. Has a strap pin in the end of the body and none at the top, but the strap has a string to tie that end onto the neck. No tuner came with it.  Too bad because I have bought four Pyle acoustics and they came with great rechargeable tuners that I love. The neck seems straight and does not have a truss rod. Many classical guitars, even full sized ones like Yamaha do not have truss rods. This one has no \"kerfing\" inside. My Pyle 34\" steel string acoustic has full kerfing. This 30\" is tuned to standard guitar tuning, EADGBE. I'm quite sure, with the right strings, one could tune it down five frets to A and call it a guitelele, like my Yamaha GL-1. I plan to leave it  standard tuning. It developed a bit of a fret buzz caused by the 3rd fret. When pressing down the D string the second fret it would buzz. The harder you picked that string, the worse it was. I agonized whether I should send it back or not for a couple weeks. Then, after a particularly hot dry spell here, the buzzing quite. I have played this every day. I like to grab my guitar whenever I want and I may pick it up and play 10-15 times a day. I have grown to really love this handy little classical and enjoy the nylon strings and sound it gives me is very nice! I am going to install a piezo pickup inside the body and will have to drill a small hole for the input jack. I could see myself playing one or two of my original songs at an open mic night using one of my amps. I'm a blues oriented player. I like I play slide, and I often use a slide with this guitar. I tune the high E sting down 2 frets to a D, as it really gives a fuller sound with a slide. I love this little bugger and would buy it again. My kitty liked it too!"
    },
    {
        "review": "My son loved it. Easy to follow instructions."
    },
    {
        "review": "We bought this for the grandkids who have yet to play It. I've been playing guitar for 50 years and it's not bad for a beginner guitar. It has a pretty good sound.  This is for nylon strings only!!  Do not put steel strings on this or you will pop the bridge right off the body.  It took a bit of time to stretch the strings to keep them from going out of tune. You just have to be patient play it and stretch the strings and retune."
    },
    {
        "review": "Action is about an inch high (string height).  Intonation is about an inch off (cannot be tuned).  Frets are painted.  Coming from a past instructor, this is closer to a toy than an actual \"beginners instrument\" as the description claims.  Not worth its price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very nice guitar it is smaller than a regular guitar easily handled by 18 or child plays nice comes with all the stuff you would need basically it’s really pretty guitar"
    },
    {
        "review": "Seems well built for the cost.  Great starter for my 6 yr old"
    },
    {
        "review": "This guitar is amazing! My son is just starting out learning guitar and this was perfect for him. The black color is super shiny and looks great, plus it comes with everything you need. Extra strings, a capo, picks, even a strap and a case so he can carry it around. We didn’t have to buy anything else. It sounds really good for a beginner guitar too, wasn’t expecting that.Honestly, couldn’t have found a better deal for the price. My son loves it and plays everyday. It’s a great size for him to handle and he’s learning fast. I would recommend this guitar to anyone looking to start out, especially for kids. Can’t go wrong with this one."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought from returns. Came absolutely brand new all good, very good value"
