[
    {
        "review": "Just wanted to write a quick review on these strings! I'm a huge fan of Yamaha Guitars in general, and recently bought a new FG800 in matte finish. Wonderful sound, as I believe is has a bit more open sound without the thick poly finish. Upon changing the strings to my go to, Elixir Nano PB lights, I noticed that the guitar lost a lot of what I liked about its initial sound. I searched the web and found that these are the original strings from Yamaha, and that they are coated as well. I bought a set and after installation, there's that wonderful sound again. I next swapped out the strings on my Guild DS240 sloped shoulder, and again a much improved sound! I know sound is subjective, so here's my take. These strings would be great for a player that is looking for a less high and brassy sound. These would be a combination of an Elixir and a Martin Retro string to my ears. More of an emphasis in the mids to lows, and less on the top end. The strings seem to last a long time and have a great feel to them. Will definitely be buying more."
